{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas","id":860617,"title":"1001 interesting character ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-06T15:59:06-07:00","id":860617,"title":"1001 interesting character ideas","content":"Let's compile character ideas for either storytellers or for player inspiration. Please try to put one idea per post to keep the ideas and post numbers in line. <br /> <br /> 1) Vampire who was a chef in life and maintains his humanity by cooking and eating incredible meals (eat food merit). Of course, in the end it is futile as the food is all disgustingly vomited up; but hey, that's just a metaphor for humanity in the body of the beast. As the character loses humanity, perhaps they start experimenting with including human blood in some of the courses...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11579-lazarus","name":"Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T16:04:27-07:00","id":860619,"title":"","content":"2) Tzimisce elder who fancies himself a god and has a deep seated need to be worshiped and loved. Embraces and blood bonds fledglings and uses Vicissitude to turn them into bloated, immobile vitae manufacturing monstrosities that continuously bleed into the local water supply, blood bonding thousands of morals - which then worship the Tzimisce as a prophet/ deity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11579-lazarus","name":"Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T16:14:15-07:00","id":860626,"title":"","content":"3) Malkavian conspiracy nut who uses Dominate to make the people he feeds on think they were abducted by aliens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T16:43:18-07:00","id":860636,"title":"","content":"4) European Gentleman (or lady) born hundreds of years ago. Through an unfortunate series of events, he fell into torpor shortly after his embrace. After rising from torpor in modern nights, he must deal with modern society and technology, as well as his vampiric nature and the fact that the world he used to know is dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11579-lazarus","name":"Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T17:10:26-07:00","id":860652,"title":"","content":"5) A Gangrel who, one lonely night, pricked his finger and watched the spiders and ants drink his blood. Fascinated, he kept feeding vermin in his haven, taking care of them, playing with them like pets. Years later, he has amassed swarms of blood bound vermin (mice, scorpions, spiders, etc) that have lived long beyond their natural lives, grown substantially larger due to the effects of his vitae, and (though not truly intelligent) they can sense anything threatening their master. Be careful if you speak with him when the swarms are around - they would die to protect him from any perceived threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11579-lazarus","name":"Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T19:17:50-07:00","id":860722,"title":"","content":"6) A Malkavian who works as a professional Anti-Witness Protection assassin. Uses his Contacts to find and dispose of witnesses before they testify in court, on behalf of organized crime interests and wealthy patrons. Has a quirk about collecting the eyes of his victims, believing them to be the key to insight into their visions (Auspex 3 helps in this). Amassed quick a collection of eyes, as well as a collection of secrets and blackmail material on his clients. Suffice to say, this Lunatic dances on the knife's edge of discovery or reprisal, for multiple reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T20:17:03-07:00","id":860748,"title":"","content":"7) Lasombra <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/5-essential-tips-to-becoming-a-successful-vitaephile-vampire-the-masquerade/\" target=\"_blank\">Vitaephile</a> with a fascination towards the ocean (as is common in the Clan). Has taken to experimenting on vessels, to capture the essence of the sea in their blood. Feeding them fish and seaweed, extracting blood under greater degrees of barometric pressure, exposing them daily to ocean air, and making them drink sea water (not too much obviously; the saltwater could overpower the blood's taste, in addition to wasting/killing the vessel). All of these experiments are performed on the Lasombra's private ship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T19:04:15-07:00","id":862948,"title":"","content":"8) A beautiful Assamite vizier who poses as a newly embraced bimbo Toreador sexpot (think Kelly Bundy level). That way everyone underestimates her as being too dumb to know anything other than following orders while her sugar daddies and &quot;manipulators&quot; take the blame for everything she has done. For bonus points, give her the merit, unbondable.<br /> <br /> 9) A Caitiff with Vicissitude and a specialty in special effects make-up has managed to get some grudging respect in the Camarilla thanks to her talents in making her unaging kind look like they can and designing realistic masks for Nosferatu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T19:00:19-07:00","id":863427,"title":"","content":"10) A Tremere who got a brain injury (either through an accident, battle wound or botched spell) that has dropped his intelligence score from 4 to 1. How does he handle this new turn in life with a clan that values intelligence?<br /> <br /> 11) A Ventrue antitribu who can only drink from animals. Due to her clan curse, she just can't drink from humans.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T15:40:50-07:00","id":879054,"title":"","content":"12) A Ghoul who was left paralyzed due to his master's foolishness has managed to expertly play upon the Vampire's guilt. To the point that the Vampire is now his broken-spirited caretaker who performs his personal political schemes for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":1834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","user":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","date":". 04-30-2016, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T22:44:06-07:00","id":891003,"title":"","content":"13) A Tremere who hunts Vampire hunters. Thamaturgy, rituals and vampiric abilities rolled into one vengeful package.<br /> <br /> 14) A cruel, sociopathic Mortal is turned into a Malkavian. While the embrace has cured his anti-social disorder, it has now been replaced with all-consuming guilt over all the horrible things he's done. So when his guilt doesn't leave him in a depressed state, he is on an obsessive quest to set things right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":1834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","user":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","date":". 05-15-2016, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T15:36:11-07:00","id":893674,"title":"","content":"15) A Setite who made a personal challenge to himself only to tempt mortals and vampires towards behaviors they wanted to do anyway. He refuses to introduce any new temptations or encourage courses of action the person hasn't already considered. To him, these people are obviously prevented from fulfilling their true desires by the machinations of the Aeons. Pushing them towards actions alien to them would be no better than doing the Aeons' jobs for them. But if some mortal is suppressing a desire to lay with children - or a vampire is suppressing their desire to diablerize their sire - the Setite should help them overcome this hindrance to their wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T16:59:40-07:00","id":895143,"title":"","content":"16) Travis: Born during the 50's, you were a rebelious teenage. Kicking the trashcans and breaking the laws. Everything Changed when you meet John Lydon, Steve Jones , Paul Cook And Glen Mantlock. The high speed, the violence and everything else made sense, The world changed as Travis became the Sixth Sex Pistol...Until every one figured out he was an Arsehole (Charisma 3, Apparience 1, intelligence 1 and ADHD) . He was soon embraced, Due do this he had to quit the band (or rather the band fired him since he was only aviable by night, he played no instruments, he constantly got into fights and the band constantly gave him wrong addresses of shows so he would never arrive).<br /> Travis is So Fucking Stupid that he doesnt care about telling people he is a vampire -But he is so ugly that everyone believes he is just drunk saying bullshit- He is considered a Court Fool or Jester. He is ALWAYS horny -And he NEVER Gets LAID-. Being a Brujah doesnt helps either, specially since his Berserker button involves talking about Sid Vicious (since Sid replaced him after he was fired)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T22:20:01-07:00","id":895302,"title":"","content":"17) A Nosferatu elder (whose been patron for the PCs) has been watching over the descendants of a blind man who showed her kindness when she was a neonate. Over the centuries, the family believes that they have a guardian angel watching over them. It seems that her Dark Fate flaw is kicking in and she knows that the dark forces she's been fighting her entire unlife will finally destroy her. All the party has to do is deliver her final message to the family (who once they found out what's happening to her, decide that they need to protect their angel as thanks for all that she has done.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:43:02-07:00","id":899031,"title":"","content":"Daughter of Cacophony metal-singer (think Otep or Walls of Jericho level growler) with heavy Fortitude and medium Melpominee. Her actions in the musical industry are slowly changing the way people view heavy metal and her travels to Eastern Europe to discover the origins and holy land of Death Metal led her to meet with the Sabbat. Her connection to the ancient Sabbat of Europe led her to view the Camarilla as rather antagonistic to music and progress, giving her the reason to fight them. She does underground style tours and has her eyes set on Nashville, TN to make it the mecca for the other Daughters and Sons while also staking out the Buckle of the Bible Belt as land to raise the USA's first Black Cathedral. Just imagine those mosh pits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Debating between ghouls and hunters PbP","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11874-melora","name":"Melora","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T11:27:21-07:00","id":928827,"title":"","content":"19) A Ventrue who has a loyal-to-a-fault identical twin brother who performs his brother's plans and job during the day to uphold the Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T13:31:12-07:00","id":932612,"title":"","content":"20) A Lasombra Antiribu has discovered the last remaining descendants of her pre-embrace Mortal family. Desiring a way to bring them back to their ancient glory and to give herself a challenge, she has decided to start with the youngest who is a child prodigy. By posing as the little girl's imaginary friend that is made of a face and mass of swirling shadows, the Vampire hopes to guide her to glory.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For extra fun, have the Nosferatu from #17 be an old rival and thorn in the side for this character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":1834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","user":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","date":". 07-16-2016, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T13:46:49-07:00","id":932618,"title":"","content":"21. A Giovanni of mixed European and Chinese descent who basically has decided to adopt a kind of mad scientist Bond villain mystique to himself. He uses a combination of Dominate, Presence, Necromancy, and the wealth of his family to live the dream of being a criminal mastermind as well as mad scientist. The other members of his clan find him quite queer but vastly entertaining. Double points if he's ninety years old and inspired Ian Fleming (A NWO acolyte) from the time they lived in Jamaica together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T13:47:34-07:00","id":932620,"title":"","content":"22. A handsome Thin Blooded woman or man who just survived losing their entire crew to other vampires and has been barely surviving from night to night. They've decided to offer themselves to one of the PCs in hopes of getting their protection. This includes, explicitly, the option to feed on them and use them as their faux concubine and servant. They'll even willingly blood bond themselves to the PC in desperation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T13:53:23-07:00","id":936224,"title":"","content":"23. Elzbieta Checinski always trained hard. Since she was a little girl in Wloclawek, Poland, she was always at the gym before dawn. She attended school as usual, albeit with advanced classes and advanced pressure. Then she returned to the Youth Athletics Centre in the afternoons. Whether on the mats, the parallel bars, balance beam, it didn't matter. Always perfect. Always agile. Always strong. Or else. Her mother, her coach, and most of all, she herself would allow nothing else. Training, training, training. Competitions both thrilled and terrified her. Finally, there were other gymnasts as gifted as she, but none were as driven. She beat them all, right up until the Olympic trials at Warsaw.<br /> <br /> The competition was nearly over, and she was well ahead. Elzbieta swung herself around the uneven bars as precisely as a ticking timepiece, but as fluidly as silk sliding down a staircase. Perfect swing, perfect flip, big smile, in the air, soaring like a cloud... and &quot;Gwsno!&quot;, she screamed aloud. She hit the mat at a bad angle, stumbled three whole steps to the left and hit the floor. She didn't notice the fracture until she tried to stand. It was a compound fracture. This wasn't just the end of her Olympic dreams, but the end of everything. Of who she was. Of what she was. She was 15 years old.<br /> <br /> Elzbieta went on to study medicine at Jagiellonian University. She specialised in sports medicine and biochemistry. When the soviet bloc fell apart, she moved to London to teach biology, chemistry and coach phys ed at a school for over-privileged girls. She despised the Sloane Rangers in her classroom and on her playing fields. They were weak, lazy, overfed and undisciplined. So she pushed them until they either failed or improved. In twenty years of teaching few improved.<br /> <br /> For one girl it was too much, the constant criticism, the veiled disdain. She cracked completely and killed herself. She mentioned Elzbieta in her note. This was bad enough, but her mother was an MP of the governing party, a backbencher, yes, but still... Elzbieta found herself unemployed. She was lucky not to be prosecuted.<br /> <br /> She had failed again and was crushed. The family of the girl had an old alliance, though, who in payment for a debt accrued in the court of George IV had promised to look after them. He approved heartily of Elzbieta's style. This ancient aristocrat was a vampire. And now, so is Elzbieta.<br /> <br /> This concept can go a couple of directions. She could now be a Ventrue who feeds exclusively on weak, lazy girls, while training the creme de la creme to serve the Camarilla. She could as easily be an Old Clan Tzimisce who takes on proteges who she pushes either to personal perfection or destruction, working on techniques to improve the human race as a whole. She could be a Toreador obsessed with gymnastics, now freed from the limitations of her ruined knee, but while ironically immortal, appearing too old to compete. She could also be a Tzimisce, using her fleshcrafting skills to create the perfect athlete, whether they want to be &quot;perfected&quot; or not. Personally, my favorite option is for her to be embraced as an Assamite. She would make an excellent trainer of foot soldiers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T15:07:59-07:00","id":936263,"title":"","content":"24. Oh, Bob Krebsbach is a heckuva a nice guy, dontchaknow? He was born in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, to an insurance salesman and a school nurse. Bob had two sisters. All three of them were above average in school, though nothing to get full of themselves over. He named his dog Bilbo and earned a trophy for participating in youth league softball. He played oboe in the Concordia College orchestra, and earned a degree in accounting. He married his wife, Joanie, bought a three-two craftsman in the Kenwood section of Minneapolis, and they had two kids. He works at the Lutheran Brotherhood, managing a pension fund for hospital employees in St. Paul. Joanie is a regional manager for the Minnesota DMV. Every Sunday they went to church at St. Luke's ELCA and sat in the second to back row. Joanie always made Krumkake with snickerdoodle filling for the Christmas Eve coffeehour, and a red, white and blue Jello salad for the July Fourth picnic.<br /> <br /> Bob's a modest guy, always averts his eyes when he says hello and doesn't go for a lot of hollering or whooping it up, but that night... when those three ruffians showed up at his door? Well, the family had just sat down to a tuna hot dish and the Vikings were on their second down when the door burst open. Bob jumped up and ran for his gun cabinet. One guy, the big one with the weird eyes, threw Bob down and started biting at his neck! Can you imagine? Well, Joanie raced for the gun cabinet herself. Bob felt cold and slipped into a sludgy semi-consciousness. Joanie loaded the deer rifle with trembling hands, flipped the safety and pulled the trigger as a second biker charged towards her. His skull exploded across the stenciled ducks on the kitchen wall. The last thing Bob remembered from his breathing life was feeling empty deep inside and seeing Mister Weird Eyes explode inches from his face.<br /> <br /> Some of the blood from Joanie's shot must have gotten into Bob's mouth, because he came to a few seconds later and entered a frenzy. He tore the third guy limb from limb, and when Bob finally calmed down, they all tried to figure out what had happened.<br /> <br /> It took a few nights of trial and error, but the Krebsbach's quickly figured out their new reality. They met up with some local anarchs who pieced together what had happened. The Sabbat pack that attacked were wanderers looking for food and short term shelter. Bob had been accidentally embraced by a Brujah antitribu. The Prince accepted him quickly, hoping Bob's mild manner would help quiet down some of the more raucous Brujah. For Bob's part he doesn't like that the &quot;Prince&quot; has such an outdated, anti-democratic management style, but figures that, really, it's none of his business. It's been two months now and the local Brujah have accepted Mr. and Mrs. Krebsbach grudgingly because they are tremendous help with the minutiae of nightly existence, like filing taxes, paying the utility bills on hang outs, and procuring fake IDs. They attend all local rants, when they can get a sitter for the kids. They don't really fit in, but they also don't actively offend anyone. They just stand there in the corner, looking like a page from the Lands End catalog, smiling as mildly as they can.<br /> <br /> Clanmates who know their story all think of Joanie as the real badass and assume she is ghouled; she is not. Bob is afraid to do so because, for one they never went for that kinky stuff and for another, Joanie is pregnant and it might be bad for the baby. She is just starting to show, and un-life in the suburbs is about to get very complicated, indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T14:05:57-07:00","id":936710,"title":"","content":"25. Dr. Gabriella Williams was born in the Germantown section of Philadelphia, the daughter of a dentist and an HR manager for PSFS bank.<br /> <br /> She always got good grades at Philadelphia's Friend's Select School, and her parents hoped she would become something dependable and practical, like a physician or possibly a lawyer. After earning a BS in Biology from Temple, though, instead of applying to medical school, she entered the University of Pennsylvania's Anthropology graduate program, with an emphasis on the early development of religion in the Eastern Mediterranean. Her doctoral thesis involved a new translation of inscribed hymns from Egypt, Phoenicia and Judea showing parallels in early fertility cults dealing with the intrusion of Indo-European Tiwaz sky god figures. Only one person has read it since she wrote it ten years ago: a Setite elder on a recruiting swing through Philly.<br /> <br /> Gabi had gone on to earn an MDiv from Harvard, and an associate pastor position with a Unitarian church on the Main Line. One evening, while locking up the rectory she was approached by her eventual sire. She assumed he was a homeless immigrant until he started chatting about early Levantine history. They talked all night, switching freely from English to French, from Aramaic to NT Greek. When he asked her riddles in Hebrew, she countered with dirty jokes in the Noban Tamen language. They discussed the cosmology of proto-Egypt and the mathematical correspondences of poetry written in Hebrew during the Babylonian captivity.<br /> <br /> They were both impressed.<br /> <br /> He ghouled her, then eventually embraced her. She resigned her ministerial position, of course, but taught some night classes at the Community College of Philadelphia. Meanwhile her sire taught her the basics of Setite religion. On a particularly sacred night he invited her to a ritual at the Setite Temple in Reading, PA. She was not impressed. Half way through a particularly torturous translation of an early Cushitic hymn she cleared her throat and raised her hand:<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, for God's sake! Set was not a snake god or a god of corruption, he was thunder and foreigners and typhonic beasts. Snakes were a whole other god, Apophis or Apep. You've read too much Conan! And, while we're on the subject his entire character changed within recent historical times. Hello! There was no actual Set! Oh, and these so-called ancient garments we put on are from at least three different eras of Egyptian history, and the priest is wearing a polyester Turkish nun's habit from the fifth century CE. The opening prayer could only be performed in front of a congregation of at least 700, and was definitely not meant to be posted on the wall in a torn out piece of notebook paper! Do you people know anything about Egypt other than what you saw in the Mummy movies? And turn on some damn lights. Yeah, yeah, sunlight burns, but you can't see nothing in here, which is good since that banner of hieroglyphics, translates as &quot;Our Lord Set ate celery but enjoys a nice beer once in a while if he doesn't have to work the next morning&quot; You people have been played!&quot; She hastily pulled on her jeans and Temple sweatsuit, flicked on the fluorescent overhead lights and stormed out.<br /> <br /> The entire congregation of five sat stunned, broken and not knowing what to do next. Her sire met her at the street corner, laughing like a hyena. She has spent her time since as an avowed Setite atheist, interpreting her clanmates' faith in purely modern sociological, anthropological and psychological terms. Somewhere along the way, though, something strange happened. Her sire started teaching her Setite sorcery and it works, of course, and when she rationally dissects the rituals to strip them down to the thaumaturgical essentials, they still work. But the strange part is that when she only performs the &quot;extraneous superstitious parts&quot;, she suffers horrible nightmares for days afterward. They are always similar. A terrifying man is chasing her on a large boat. It can be a yacht, a ferry, a paddle boat or a 19th century slave boat, but the man is always the same. He's a foreigner with red hair, swings a mace and when he screams there is thunder. Inside of Gabi's soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T14:26:37-07:00","id":936720,"title":"","content":"Gabriella is now in my campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T08:08:27-07:00","id":937607,"title":"","content":"26. He was born Frank Harold Simmons, but his fake ID says &quot;Francis Harriman Simmons IV&quot;, even though his father's name was Jim.<br /> <br /> Frank wasn't born poor, exactly, his family was downwardly mobile upper middle class. He reached back to his great-grandfather, &quot;State Senator Francis Harriman Simmons III&quot; when he changed his name to something more impressive. FHS IV, on the other hand, is the scion of a wealthy, if little known, political dynasty.<br /> <br /> Frank attended PS 81 in the Bronx, while FHS IV studied at Deerfield, or in some versions Exeter. Frank took a few classes at CUNY, in Metallica t-shirts and riding the MTA. FHS IV claims to have attended Middlebury College, full of alligator shirts and BMWs.<br /> <br /> Everything about MHS IV is a lie. A lie that was believed just long enough for him to be embraced as a 9th generation Ventrue, during the fight for Manhattan. He had a very brisk agoge, but took to Dominate well.<br /> <br /> He spent most of the campaign hiding out in a bodega on 103rd street, but he did manage to Dominate several other fledglings into remembering some valiant act or another.<br /> <br /> After the &quot;battle&quot;, having earned his blood, FHS IV decided a quieter domain would take the mortal out of immortal and moved to Wichita. There were only 9 other Camarilla kindred there, 3 of whom rarely attended Elysium. He BSed his way into some status, ingratiating himself with the Princeling, who was 10th generation and therefore manipulable with discreet use of Dominate. FHS IV spent five years building up his image as the oldest money on the Great Plains and a strong blooded asset to the Camarilla. FHS IV dominated every kindred in town at one point or another into spreading to their respective clans outside Wichita highly exaggerated tales of his prowess.<br /> <br /> Then the Sabbat came to town. They roared into Elysium at the Orpheum Theater on motorcycles, swinging chainsaws. FHS IV slipped right back into Frank mode. He dominated a dozen mortal passersby to throw themselves into the fray. This created enough confusion that both sides utterly destroyed one another while Frank hid in the basement. Frank realized that as the sole survivor there would be an investigation. It did not look good that an ambitious Ventrue may have sold out the domain.<br /> <br /> He tracked down the three semi-autarkis who escaped the carnage and Dominated them into testifying they were, in fact, there that night and saw FHS IV use powerful disciplines to pound the Sabbat into the ground, and then sob openly at the loss of his beloved fellow Kindred.<br /> <br /> Frank breathed a sigh of relief that he wasn't caught in his cowardice, again, but then something far scarier than the Sabbat came to town: a Justicar with full retinue arrived. To Frank's surprise and unending terror FHS IV was named the new Prince of Wichita.<br /> <br /> Running a domain through an Alternate ID is not for the feint of heart. Neighboring Princes from Tulsa, Kansas City and Topeka have all visited and seemed mildly suspicious, or maybe Frank is just paranoid. He keeps seeing mortals on the street who might kind of resemble one of the witnesses from the Battle of the Bodega, having regained their memories. He needs to rebuild the local domain through embraces, but anyone he chooses would eventually see through his lies. Frank's Humanity has take a beaten. The Masquerade in Wichita is stretched paper thin. He keeps running out of blood as he ghouls half the city. Oh, and the Sabbat are still circling.<br /> <br /> Frank is in waaay over his head.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T09:32:49-07:00","id":937641,"title":"","content":"1) &quot;Environmental Services Engineer&quot; that has been cleaning the University's library for 30+ years. No one seemed to notice the amount of time he spent late at night reading in the rare books collection and in the archive, and no one has ever seen the &quot;tricks&quot; he learned as a result. Except for his sire, who stumbled across him levitating his mop one night while on the hunt for a particular piece of lore.<br /> <br /> 2) Homeless vet living under the highway interchange downtown, a metal plate where an IED took part of his skull and night terrors where the war took part of his soul. Something's been watching him for weeks, following him as he forages for supplies in the streets and alleyways. That something introduced itself the night he killed a feral dog for food, and it knew his name. Now the foraging is easier, but there's a new war to fight.<br /> <br /> 3) The family's golden boy, fresh from a year spent abroad celebrating his graduation from an Ivy League university. Some cash flow problems ended his first business before it even began, but an attorney claiming to represent a new investor has offered a very appealing deal that will fund his next venture for years, if not longer. The only catch: he will have to cut ties with his family and focus on the work, at least for a &quot;little while&quot;.<br /> <br /> 4) She was tired. Tired of a life that did nothing but beat her down, tired of a shit job that paid her just enough to keep going but not enough to have hope, and tired of running from mistakes she should never have made. And she wasn't even 30 yet. When she thought she was dying the that back alley she was relieved. Now that she's upright again, she's angry. Angry that peace was taken away from her, angry at the wasted years, and angry at whatever did this to her.<br /> <br /> 5) Her great uncle was a legend among the family. 103 years old, still working, and making sure they never wanted for anything. No one had seen him in at least 50 years, not since he went overseas and made his fortune, but he kept writing letters to everyone without fail. When the plane ticket with her name on it arrived in his latest letter there was no way she could refuse. Her parents are sad to see her go, but they know that he has big things in store for her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10796,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","user":"Dismas","date":".  Autocorrect screw-up. 10-25-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","name":"Dismas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T09:42:31-07:00","id":937646,"title":"","content":"I have to say 26# probably has all of his secrets known by the Ventrue but they admire his Flashman-esque chutzpah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T09:56:21-07:00","id":937652,"title":"","content":"27) the kinfolk who is now a high humanity vampire (usually Gangrel) who still try to stay in contact with the &quot;furry side of her family&quot; and wants to keep the peace between Garou and Cainites (results may vary)<br /> <br /> 28) The Lasombra Antitribu who was opposed to the Diablerie of [Lasombra], made some enemies in the future Sabbat and decided to basically disappeared from vampiric society. A few centuries later everybody either forgot about him or think he's dead, but he is still hiding somewhere, paranoid, pretending to be from another clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12015-elstren","name":"Elstren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T08:23:24-07:00","id":938126,"title":"","content":"CTPhipps: I'm not sure which is scarier for #26, that the Justicar knew Frank was a brilliant liar, cheat and thief and figured he would fit in well on the Camarilla team; or that the upper echelons of that team were so incompetent as to not realize the scam. Either way, Frank is Prince of Screwedtown.<br /> <br /> Dismas: I really like your #3, which would be #29 overall. If the Golden Boy is desperate to gain approval from his family and the only way to do so is to cut all ties to his family it creates a classic dilemma. Lots of possibilities!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:08:05-07:00","id":938160,"title":"","content":"#34 Judy Campanelli was born in the usual way, in the usual town of Rockford, Illinois. But everyone said she was not a usual girl, though she never had any idea what they were talking about. Sure, she was a bit lanky, and dressed exclusively in sweaters or t-shirts and ankle length dresses from the Goodwill. She loved the works of L. Frank Baum and Anne McCaffrey, Pablo Neruda and Bill Sienkiewicz. She learned to play every Beatle song ever published on her zither. She won the scrabble competition at her local Mensa chapter eight years running. Judy attended role-playing game conventions in the 80's when she would often find herself in a room with 300 other people, all men. Somewhere along the line she earned a Masters in Medieval Studies and adopted four cats, whom she named Frannie, Larry, Stu and Harold. She knew she was quirky and self-actualizing, but why did people treat her like an escaped mental patient?<br /> <br /> She suspected that no one would think she were strange if she were a man, hrumph. Her sire saw something in her, though, and sat her down one night to explain the pluses and minuses of the embrace. It was especially risky because his clan was Malkavian and all Malkavian fledglings go insane, sometimes a little and sometimes a very, very lot. It was a choice he left to Judy. She accepted the embrace and it went seamlessly.<br /> <br /> She felt no difference at all. Her sire warned her of the impending craziness and explained the basics of vampiric existence for a few weeks, then left her to fend for herself. She did well, having read more vampfic than most, but there was one problem. She felt exactly the same, mentally. Oh, there was the Beast, frenzies, some sensory overload from Auspex, and the Hunger and she had to give up her cats when they kept hissing at her, but felt no crazier than ever. She decided she must be a Caitiff, but she had taken to the Malkavian disciplines with gusto, so she figured she was, ummm, a Malcaitiff?<br /> <br /> The other vampires she met at Elysium just roll their eyes and laugh when she explains that she's a Malcaitiff because she's not crazy. &quot;Not crazy? Oh, honey...&quot;, as they take her hand in a condescendingly empathetic way.<br /> <br /> What do they see that she doesn't see?<br /> <br /> Is she having fugues and acting crazy then forgetting it? Couldn't be, because she installed a high end video system in her haven to observe her own behavior. Maybe it's an aspect of her affect she can't see. So, she took some night classes in abnormal psychology and theater arts, but all seems to check out there. Maybe a nervous tic or verbal pattern problem, but she recorded 1000 total hours of her social interaction with cameras a ghoul set up everywhere she went and saw nothing unusual when reviewing the tapes.She had a theory for a while that it was a taint in the blood of Malkav, so she cycled through starving herself, then feeding only on the blood of people others identified as highly sane. She accidentally torpored twice from this experiment, but it convinced her either the blood wasn't tainted or couldn't be cleansed. It remains a mystery.<br /> <br /> She received the blood of Malkav and feels entirely the same as ever. What does that mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T09:17:24-07:00","id":938893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=938126#post938126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dismas: I really like your #3, which would be #29 overall. If the Golden Boy is desperate to gain approval from his family and the only way to do so is to cut all ties to his family it creates a classic dilemma. Lots of possibilities!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I realized that I screwed up the numbering about half an hour after I made the post. All of them were pulled from games I've played in (and only one was mine). The Golden Boy was a Tremere played by a friend of mine, whose first business was intentionally ruined by his Sire in order to manipulate him in to accepting the &quot;investment&quot; offer. The local chantry needed someone to help improve its financial situation, and he was their man.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10796-dismas","name":"Dismas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10796_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:15:40-07:00","id":939127,"title":"","content":"#35 Simon Billinghurst-Mumford had always vaguely known there was more to life. Some vast universe just outside his limited perception, and perhaps an even vaster one inside. His friends, family and teachers thought him an aimless daydreamer, obsessed with books about magic and fantasy. The more he read, though, the more he researched real world history, the more it seemed like magic must be real. Waiting there, just outside of his high pressure world of a student passing multiple A-levels, including Computing (A*), Further Math (A*), Physics (A), History (A), Classic Studies (A), and Latin (B), was a world of magic.<br /> <br /> His parents thought him mad for studying Philosophy at University. Why not something more practical like Engineering or, at least, Philosophy, Politics and Economics? His family had some social connections to some Tory back-benchers who could turn one of those into a career, but Philosophy? They may have posh connections, but little inheritance beyond the double barrelled name. At least he passed the entrance exam at Oxford and was offered an exhibition at Magdalen. He excelled in his coursework, earning a BA in Philosophy with first class honours.<br /> <br /> About this time he caught the eye of a powerful patron. His mentor explained the situation one night, over dinner, which the patron did not eat. He could offer him great power, but it would require tremendous commitment. No, it's not in government. No, not business. It's something bigger. A secret world, a very long-term commitment. Interested?<br /> <br /> Simon spent seven years studying Hermetic magic, while maintaining a cover as a minor civil servant involved in importation of art objects from India. His awakening was a polite affair, a ritual arranged for Lammastide, cloaks and sigils and all that. Finally, he had all he wanted, the world of magic layed bare for him. He excelled in the study of Spirit and Correspondance, with a minor interest in Entropy. He never knowingly met a technocrat or other enemy of the Order of Hermes, but then he was a minor scholar, really, organizing the libraries at the Chapter House, on weekends and evenings.<br /> <br /> At his day job, he became involved in a tariff row over the importation of a certain sarcophagus. Was it simply a dead body being transported for the grieving family or was it an art object in it's own right? Legally it fell into a grey area and had to be kicked up the chain of command. It became a minor scandal, with the PM of India accusing Britain of stealing India's cultural heritage and descendants of the Indian Raj in question saying they simply wanted their great-great-great, etc grandfather buried where belonged, in Hounslow with them. Preferably in a modern coffin, thank you. The fact that Sotheby's was involved was irrelevant, they said.<br /> <br /> One night, while reviewing paperwork in the warehouse, the sarcophagus in question and who stepped out but the Raj in question, looking far too fresh for someone so old. Simon threw up some basic defensive rotes, but the Raj started asking him questions. The evening ended with Simon driving him to a Tremere chantry and being embraced.<br /> <br /> Simon will never, ever forgive his sire. All real magic left him. Once, he could mumble a few words in Enochian and touch a clay tablet to his forehead and listen to any conversation in th world, or other worlds. He could spend his evenings listening to Bach, the actual Bach, play the organ either through past viewing or by asking his Wraith to do him the honour. He could apport to Mykonois for a quick holiday or turn base metals to gold. And, now? The rituals are so basic a random child off the street could do them.<br /> <br /> He held the power of a god in his hands, and the Tremere took it from him. He knows he must be obedient for now.<br /> <br /> But he will have his revenge someday. These stunted freaks will pay, and pay dearly!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T12:43:00-07:00","id":939714,"title":"","content":"My favourite character concept is a female Russian Brujah anarch who was a Bolshevik revolutionary in her breathing days and still looks, walks and talks the part. She wears the revolutionary paraphernalia such as a <i>telnyashka</i> and a commissar hat (worn backwards) mixed with more modern Brujah biker/punk fare, to look less out of place on modern streets. Her weapons of choice are the Mauser C-96 Broomhandle and an old Rdultovsky engineering grenade, and her speech and mannerisms of choice are something that can be found in a Soviet Ostern movie character. She's also an expert on creating blood-based concoctions spiked with alcohol and/or cocaine that have the effect of corresponding drugs on any Kindred (this is a reference to the practice of use of the &quot;trench cocktail&quot;, a vodka-cocaine mix, among the real Bolsheviks).<br /> <br /> You guessed it right, the sire of this character was Antonin Zilkha himself, detailed in Victorian Vampire.<br /> <br /> Another favourite, though less original, character concept from mine is a counter-cultural Toreador. Rather than delighting in mainstream culture, this Toreador is crazy about subcultures and counter-culture, things like punk and metal music and lyrics; this character is more poor and unglamorous than the stereotypical Toreador, and likely to be an Anarch as well.<br /> <br /> There is also a villain I will someday unleash onto someone when I'll be Storyteller: a serial diablerist Caitiff inceptor who invented the Discipline that mimics the effects of other Disciplines, and founded a bloodline called the Mimicrians. This inceptor and the whole gang are hated by both Camarilla and Sabbat (the former because of the diablerie thing, the latter because the founder once served the Sabbat as a Pander but defected). But they still exist because they can successfully imitate normal vampire clans, and there's no easy way to identify a Mimicrian (they are also minor Viss users and can use it to steal identities of others). All Mimicrians, not only the founder, are serial diablerists, because diablerie is necessary to &quot;unlock&quot; mimickable Disciplines, but they all have Hidden Diablerie. So, in this chronicle, anyone not showing the telltale stripes after diablerie is under suspicion of being a Mimicrian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12156-the-caitiff-antediluvian","user":"The Caitiff Antediluvian","date":". 07-29-2016, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12156-the-caitiff-antediluvian","name":"The Caitiff Antediluvian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T19:38:58-07:00","id":952934,"title":"","content":"#36: A trio of Elder Tzmisce hedonists and artistic flesh-crafters have long grown bored over the centuries. So when a lone Caitiff (knowing he would get his ass kicked) suggested that their boredom comes from thinking only of themselves and that perusing a more virtuous path would help them expand beyond this, they took the advice. So now they challenge themselves with elaborate games of punishing the wicked and rewarding the virtuous. The thing is when it comes to ancient Fiends, their take on the advice was not what anyone expected. Think along the lines of Hellraiser: Inferno for the punishments. The virtue rewards are odd, but makes things better in a messed-up way. Example: A virtuous old bag lady is given a job as a live-in maid for a very wealthy family and eventually become an unofficial member of the family and later, a down-to-earth, charitable matriarch. Which was achieved by major amounts of dominating every member of the main and extended family (including some personality changes).<br /> <br /> As for the Caitiff, he was let go, but he does receive recordings of their latest achievements, thanking him for this more rewarding pursuit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T21:23:32-07:00","id":952972,"title":"","content":"Is this supposed only to be Modern Nights or are Dark Ages welcome as well?<br /> <br /> #37: A Malkavian who escaped his tyrannical Sire and knows the Sire is still there, looking for him. The Malkavian can have periods of depression when greeting the sun seems like a good idea to avoid further suffering at his Sire's hand, mixed with periods of intense, frenzied activity when the Malkavian makes ready for a confrontation with the Sire, building relations, ghouling and getting hands on arms, only for all of it to fall out of his hands in his periods of depression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T02:51:33-07:00","id":953068,"title":"","content":"#38: She's a rumor among the street gangs of the city, or even several cities, for after the fighting is done and sometimes before the guns are silent, she appears from the dark to raise the most worthy into everlasting life on the streets. Like a modern day Valkyrie the Gangrel seeks out the modern day warriors, violent gangbangers, brutal police officers and more among the American cities and there give them the chance to keep fighting forever.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhile some may Think that she's ancient Brunhild was born as Maria back in the early 1900s and influated with the ancient Norse myths seeks to gathered a small army for one reason or another. And when its done, there will be hell unleashed. But until then she adds to the folk lore and urban legends while granting the Embrace to the most violent and brutal members of the human race. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:44:24-07:00","id":955100,"title":"","content":"<b>Dark Ages: Vampire[39] (Death of Wings)</b> In the Omen War of Eastern Europe, horrifying magics are unleashed, careless of the consequences.<br /> <br /> Such is the case of the Angel-Maiden of Warsaw, a most...<i>unusual</i>...Gargoyle. (8th-generation [thanks to diablerie], to be precise.) Though originally a hideous monstrosity, she partook in the diablerie of a Cappadocian aide to a Tzimisce warlord, during an attack. The change was slow, barely noticable---at least at first.<br /> <br /> The soul of that Cappadocian had <i>changed</i> her; though he did not overtake her mind, his soul still brought far more with it than 'mere' power. The Angel-Maiden's features became beauty incarnate---the sweet lure of death---and she began to hear...<i>something</i>...whispering to her.<br /> <br /> The blood oath to her Tremere master too faded away, and the Angel-Maiden made her escape. There, the whispers grew stronger, and now, she was <i>seeing</i> things...and those things now told her <i>secrets</i>, hidden things.<br /> <br /> She needs to know more. She <i>must</i> know more!<br /> <br /> [In game terms, she swiftly gained mastery of Auspex, despite it being an out-of-clan Discipline... Furthermore, her stolen powers drive her instinctually to learn Mortis, though, sadly for the Angel-Maiden, she CANNOT learn it without a Cappadocian teacher.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-14-2016, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:45:05-07:00","id":955420,"title":"","content":"I'll throw on a couple concepts I've worked up lately.<br /> <br /> - A blue collar, complete schlub, knucklehead (think Ash Williams level and flavor of stupidity)...Ventrue. With Charmed Existence, Lucky, and a few choice social flaws to accentuate the dumbass nature of the character. Why would a Ventrue embrace a person like this, and why would they suffer him to love, you ask?<br /> <br /> He embraced...himself. His soon-to-be sire was drinking him dry, and as a last, desperate act of self self-preservation...bit him right back, and ended up with enough vitae in his system to turn once the Ventrue dumped the body. His sire doesn't know what really happened...yet.<br /> <br /> - A burnout hippie Toreador, who happens to be a medium. Along the way, they learned Animalistic because they wanted to talk to and befriend all the beautiful animals of the world. So you have a Torrie of all vampires, who can communicate with and manipulate people, spirits, and animals. So, basically, the ultimate spy master and information broker...if they could stop being a hippie long enough to put their skill set to productive use.<br /> <br /> - (my favorite). A restaurateur. Famous restaurateur. As in &quot;multiple Michelin starred restaurant&quot; restaurateur. He's also a nosferatu, much to the local Torries' chagrin, and tends to put &quot;extra special&quot; ingredients in the meals of those he deems worth taking down a notch or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-22-2016, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T14:11:51-07:00","id":958410,"title":"","content":"#42: Bob McCrory grew up in Huntington, West Virginia. In high school, he bagged groceries at the Save-A-Lot and played varsity football. He fixed up an old truck and dated Debbie, the actual girl next door. He and Deb weren't the most popular couple in town, but they were the best looking. They had known each other before they looked good, so it didn't really matter. And he loved her. Really, truly, deeply. So much it hurt. So much he was terrified to tell her how much. Then, they had a pregnancy scare their senior year, but she had a miscarriage two days before they were named Prom Queen and King. After that, it wasn't the same. Debbie went off to college in Ohio. Bob got a job changing oil at the local garage.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, when he was sitting at the corner bar, listening to some old Journey song on the jukebox, he'd just sit and think. &quot;Life had been great. It really had. I can't say exactly when, but it had. Now, it's just life.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bob worked on his Camaro. He dated pretty girls, but nothing really solid. He played softball with a local team, and worked out at the gym to stay solid. He rented one of those little apartments out by the strip mall, and no one but him ever went there. As the years went by, his old buddies all got married and got a paunch. The girls all dressed up every Saturday night, until they only dressed up for Sunday mornings. &quot;Bobby,&quot; they'd all say, &quot;When are you gonna grow up and get a real life? You're gorgeous. You could marry any woman you want.&quot; He'd just smile and ask how their kids were doing in school. He knew they talked. Maybe he was gay, or depressed or a secret drunk. But he wasn't any of those things. He just never met a woman who looked at him like a person and not Mr. September from the pinup calendar.<br /> <br /> By the ten year reunion, he had had it. He didn't want to go, but the old gang made him. Then Deb walked in, with her husband. She was a math teacher in Cincinatti and her husband, was, umm, something with a suit. Bob almost lost it right there in the gym. He made his apologies and left.<br /> <br /> Driving home, a six pack between his feet, he came round the bend and saw a crashed car by the side of the road. It was a Jaguar. As he got out and walked toward the high beams shining up from the ravine, the horn was blaring in the night. He thought, &quot;Amazing the first Jaguar I've seen with a working electrical system and it's crashed in a ditch.&quot; Only the front of the hood was visible, but as he shimmied down the slope, he saw a woman at the wheel. She looked dead. Like days dead. There was no blood anywhere, but she could not possibly be alive. Her head was at a right angle to her neck.<br /> <br /> He looked inside to see if there was anyone else and jumped when she moved. Her head swiveled around and he could hear her say, &quot;Open the door. Now lean in. Now turn your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> He hadn't realized it, but he had done those things. Then he began to die as the blood flowed out of him. But he didn't, well not exactly.<br /> <br /> Seems even the Toreador prince of Columbus can hit an oil patch and skid out. She had planned to just drain him dry, but at the last moment, she looked at him. Those powder blue eyes. The soft blonde hair. The flawless skin and chiseled jaw. He was simply the most beautiful man she had ever seen. And considering the circles she moved in, that was saying something.<br /> <br /> She embraced him, and took him to Columbus. He hung out in Elysium for a few months, but it just all seemed so fake. Yes, he was good looking, but that was it. He didn't care about the things her friends talked about. It was all post-deconstructionist poetry and cinema verite re-montaged installations and this and that. Bob probably could have understood it if he wanted to, but what was the point? He would never fit in, and he knew it. Art was meaningless, there was just survival. Blood. Or not, and take a walk in the morning sun. Whatever.<br /> <br /> They called him a poseur, but posing as what? A NASCAR fan in a roomful of Edith Heads and Dandy Warhols? &quot;This is just me, not a pose&quot;, he'd point out. So, they called him a burnout. But had he ever really flamed. Well, prom night, but that doesn't count. His sire grew impatient and dropped hints that he should leave, and maybe not mention his lineage. They talk every once in a while, on the phone. He thinks she's afraid he'll go anarch or sabbat or something, but he wouldn't. She calls him a blue-collar, burn-out autarkis. He always tries to sound chipper on the phone, but usually cries afterward.<br /> <br /> He moved back to the apartment in Huntington. He works the night shift on a tow truck for spending money, but uses his supernatural charisma to pay the rent. He feels bad about cheating the landlady, but she doesn't seem to mind.<br /> <br /> Nights off, he sits at the corner bar, some old Journey song on the jukebox, and pretends to drink a beer. He thinks, &quot;Life had been great. It really had. I can't say exactly when, but it had. Now, it's just life.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:57:06-07:00","id":961223,"title":"","content":"#43 Gavin Charbonneau MacCullough; BA, MFA, MA, PhD, EdD, was a professor studying literary theory at Concordia University in Montreal. He was well known for his novels, mostly focusing on middle class professionals trying to survive in a world that ignored their emotional and spiritual life. He won multiple awards, including the Writer's Trust, the Governor General's Award and Scotiabank Giller. He was a regular contributor to MacLean's, writing a column about popular culture and the arts. He was a regular at dinner parties at Margaret Atwood's summer cottage. He was quickly climbing the academic ladder, some predicted an administrative post or even a seat on the board.<br /> <br /> In 1979, though, the local Liberal party committee asked him to stand for election to the Canadian Parliament. He had never had a strong interest in politics, but was assured that he was unlikely to win against the local Bloc Quebecois MP, a popular deputy party leader. The Liberals just didn't want the riding to go uncontested. Then the Bloc MP was caught with three under-age prostitutes in a van behind Tim Horton's at three in the morning. They weren't eating donuts.<br /> <br /> Gavin entered parliament expecting to serve a short term, then turn things over to a successor. But an odd thing happened, he became really fascinated with the politics of the Centre Block. He delved into the interpersonal relations of the senate, examined decades of funding data on nearly every MP and became personal friends with the Governor General. He approached this research with the dispassionate detachment of a scholar, of course, which most members took as polite reserve. Gavin became a regular guest on several political panel shows, and a go to interviewee on internal parliamentary affairs for the National. He developed a reputation for calm, trans-partisan even handedness.<br /> <br /> The elections of 2005 elected a hung parliament, with the Liberals in coalition with the NDP only able to form a minority government if several Bloc Quebecois MPs crossed the aisle and joined the coalition. But the Bloc was only willing to join the coalition with large concessions, such as a new independence referendum, abolition of the Senate and a Canada-wide referendum on becoming a republic without the British Monarchy. Wasn't gonna happen. The other parties in the coalition would collapse in the RoC, if they conceded to the Bloc's demands. Meanwhile, the Tories were short of a majority, but no other party would work with them. No one was able to form a government and the Governor General feared a constitutional crisis was brewing. Both the Liberals and Conservatives held angry party conferences with backbench revolts threatening to oust the party leaders.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Liberal and Conservative Party leaders, meeting with the Governor General at Rideau Hall, agreed to a stopgap deal until new elections could be held. But under only one condition: Gavin Charbonneau MacCullough become the new (and temporary) Prime Minister, leading a multi-partisan caretaker government. He had remained a confirmed bachelor and had no children, so he moved into 24 Sussex Drive with four tweed suits, his briefcase and his toothbrush. He only served for three months, but had done his part in maintaining peace, order and good government. As part of the coalition agreement, he did not stand for election in his riding, rather retiring from government service. He also agreed to forego a senate seat.<br /> <br /> Gavin entered a genteel semi-retirement and writing short stories. He spent New Year's Eve 2007 at his winter home in Charleston, South Carolina. It was quiet evening, watching television and catching up on some correspondence. But then a visitor arrived who offered him the embrace. Gavin agreed, and the deed was done.<br /> <br /> His sire faked Gavin's death by creating a home invasion gone wrong. As an American, the sire assumed this would the most plausible story, but the safety of traveling Canadians became a cause celebre in Canada, dominating headlines for weeks. Gavin passed quickly through the agoge, taking a small domain at a local college. He feeds exclusively on handsome undergrads. He is working on a new book, co-edits a literary journal, and very much wants to go home to Canada. That is, of course, completely impossible. Here in the States, no one recognizes him, but in Canada he is a household name. He occasionally runs into Canadian tourists and expats, and has had some close calls. He figures in four or five decades he can go home.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, elder Ventrue who don't grasp how clueless Americans are about Canadian politics are apoplectic. They are pleased at Gavin's skill set and demeanor, of course, but embracing such a public figure is not advisable. Not advisable in the sense that they consider Gavin a walking threat to the masquerade and have discussed a bloodhunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T15:00:02-07:00","id":961260,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11558_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11558\" data-vbnamecard=\"11558\">Nosimplehiway</a> I have to say I've loved your entries in this thread. Well, except one...<br /> \u200bColumubs with a Toreador Prince? Really? Given this town, it has to be a Malkavian.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T11:30:17-07:00","id":961795,"title":"","content":"<b>A Follower of Set</b> who models himself after the Serpent of Eden. He offers resources and knowledge to the underprivileged so they can rebel against their oppressors. Most of the time, they aren't wise enough to use his gifts responsibly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Sabbat Gangrel</b> who's suffering the affects of dysmorphobia, causing her to feel uncomfortable in human form. She spends the majority of her time in animal shape, growing increasingly hostile when forced to take human form for extended periods of time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A Ventrue Anarch</b> who prefers to lead by example, rather than by force. Unlike most Lords, he is actually much beloved by his followers, which makes it harder for enemies to buy their loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T06:14:09-07:00","id":963187,"title":"","content":"Livewire: Thanks. I really enjoy writing them. Good after-work therapy.<br /> <br /> The Toreador prince is not the best fit, frankly. From the times I've been in Columbus it struck me as a straight forward Tremere sort of place, maybe Ventrue.<br /> <br /> But for storytelling purposes, I wanted Bob to be from Huntington because I needed a blue collar city in Appalachia, large enough to barely support just one vampire, but not so rural that Garou would be thick on the ground. I needed the Prince to be Toreador from a city that could be driven to in a few hours. Pittsburgh seems too Sabbat-ey. Cincinnati and DC have poor road connections to Huntington. Roanoke is on the wrong side of the mountains, since I wanted the Toreador's snooty court to clearly be in Mid-America and not too Southern. That brought it down to Columbus or Lexington, KY. I was leaning toward Lexington, but decided it was too small to host both a full Camarilla court and an insular Toreador clique. If the general Camarilla population overlapped with the Toreador too much Bob would have fallen in with the Brujah, Gangrel or Anarchs. Columbus is in a more densely populated part of the country. This allows having larger and more exclusive Toreador functions.<br /> <br /> And I never said the Toreador Prince of Central Ohio was *secure* in her position. Based on how she is presented in the character sketch (distracted by clan parties, siring profligately, and driving around other states unattended) I'd say she delegates nearly all of the actual administration of the city, and her days are numbered. Bob could very well wind up with someone crashing on his couch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T08:14:12-07:00","id":964301,"title":"","content":"Hell, I'll also throw in the single darkest, most awful, character concept which I have actually been banned from <b><i>ever</i></b> playing in my local group, I've ever come up with, too. And, considering I've played Baali, Tremere <i>antitribu </i>serial diablerists on the Path of Caine on the Red List, and Angellis Ater before, that's no light comment.<br /> <br /> The character was a Setite. Her entire schtick was using Obfuscate and Presence to seduce mortals of power and influence, having kinky, totally fucked up sex with them, surreptitiously video recording the whole thing...and using those tapes as blackmail material, selling them on the black market, or even just sending them to the local news depending upon mood, profitability, potential recruitability to the Cult of Set, and/or whose pawn that mortal was. Pretty typical, bog-standard, Setite shenanigans, except for a certain three-point physical flaw which at this point is probably easily enough figured out by yourselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-06-2016, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T09:44:03-07:00","id":964343,"title":"","content":"I had a version of that setite, a nosferatu PC with the &quot;false reflection&quot; merit so &quot;Mask of a Thousand Faces&quot; worked on camara. It's very easy to fabricate blackmail material with a bit of effort this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11224-mjensen","name":"Mjensen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:18:54-07:00","id":964519,"title":"","content":"#49 A Cathayan Primogen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-19-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:16:33-07:00","id":965034,"title":"","content":"#50 Ronnie Hampton came from a large and loud family, eleven brothers and sisters. He was the youngest, and the only one with no memory of their father, who died in world war two. His mom remarried in a few years to a widower with four kids of his own. Ronnie often stayed on the outer edges of the family, a quiet, awkward boy, with few friends outside his siblings and step-siblings. When Ronnie graduated from high school, and went off to Texas A&amp;M, he reluctantly joined a fraternity. He was terrified of being around so many strangers, but three of his older brothers had joined and graduated, so he was a legacy. The chapter had a large endowment and the house was like a palace compared to the residence halls, and cheaper to boot.<br /> <br /> The house was intimidating at first, with scores of rooms and multiple wings, many of which seemed to be tacked on at random angles. There was a pool, a wine cellar and a library bigger than some junior colleges. Construction was making it even bigger while Ronnie was there, as the A&amp;M's administration expanded the student body drastically, including admitting women and some minorities. (Neither of these would ever be admitted to the frat, obviously.) Ronnie majored in civil engineering and earned several scholarships. While his frat brothers didn't dislike him, they also didn't exactly know him. He was so quiet and bookish, they would often forget he was there. That is until they needed tutoring in any field of math or the physical sciences, then they kept him up late. Oddly, Ronnie started studying outside his major so he could better tutor his house brothers. He developed a working knowledge of anthropology, psychology, sociology and veterinary science. By his final semester, he realized he could breeze through a second degree in mathematics in a single year, so he stayed on.<br /> <br /> This attracted the attention of a kindred out of Houston who wanted a childe capable of building secret warrens into the growing industrial sector of that city. The sire came Thanksgiving weekend figuring he could snatch Ronnie from his room while pre-game festivities were going on. She embraced Ronnie and took him a storage room for old furniture to wait for the change to come upon him. She arranged plenty of blood for his first meal, but once he fed he was flush with emotion and frenzied. He staked her with a table leg and ran toward the nearest large source of blood: the annual bonfire. Along the way, he drank a townie passed out on a lawn, and, not used to so much alcohol, remained in the frenzy, albeit in a deep stagger. When he got there he ran toward the light, grabbing at undergrads. The vast crowd buffeted him away from each intended victim, finally maneuvering him near the fire itself. At that moment, the bonfire collapsed onto him. Bystanders grabbed him and pulled him onto the lawn, extinguishing him with coolers full of ice.<br /> <br /> By the next night he was in the city morgue, seemingly killed in the fire. He awoke horrifically burned, but &quot;alive&quot;. His sire freed him from the meat locker and took him back to the storage room. Her ghouls had removed the stake and hidden the body of the townie. Next they would arrange for Ronnie's &quot;remains&quot; to be cremated and transferred to his family. She stayed around for a few weeks teaching him the basics of vampiric existence, and holding his hand through the Nosferatu change. Perhaps predictably, he looked like a burn victim. She left him, there, though, deciding he was too unstable to work on the sort of large scale projects she had in mind.<br /> <br /> The campus, of course, was aghast at his death. People who had never looked twice at him claimed to be close friends. For Ronnie's part, he was too scared to leave the frat house except for short periods, and has not left the campus at all since his &quot;death&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ronnie has become a local legend, known as the Thirteenth Man. The guy who died, some say willingly throwing himself onto the bon fire as a sacrifice to school spirit. It reinforces the legend when he feeds on the members of his old fraternity, and keeps a haven in an obscure corner of the house. Ronnie spends his nights observing his brothers, following their interpersonal intrigues the way an old woman follows her soap operas. He has watched them dodge the draft, get girls pregnant, run a pot ring, campaign for Carter, campaign for Reagan, get involved in a hazing scandal, admit their first black member, lose one of their own in Iraq and elect the first openly gay greek chapter president on campus. He has been, watching passively, the whole time. Sometimes he goes months at a time without speaking to single person. He has, also, never actually met another vampire.<br /> <br /> He has kept a cordial correspondence with his sire, and she keeps him filled in on the gossip around Houston's court. Now, he thinks he may need help. A national ghost hunting show is scheduled to film on campus. They have not been given permission to film in the frat house, but it's just a matter of time. They probably won't find anything, but he is still worried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T14:50:25-07:00","id":965276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=958410#post958410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#42: Bob McCrory grew up in Huntington, West Virginia. In high school, he bagged groceries at the Save-A-Lot and played varsity football. He fixed up an old truck and dated Debbie, the actual girl next door. He and Deb weren't the most popular couple in town, but they were the best looking. They had known each other before they looked good, so it didn't really matter. And he loved her. Really, truly, deeply. So much it hurt. So much he was terrified to tell her how much. Then, they had a pregnancy scare their senior year, but she had a miscarriage two days before they were named Prom Queen and King. After that, it wasn't the same. Debbie went off to college in Ohio. Bob got a job changing oil at the local garage.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, when he was sitting at the corner bar, listening to some old Journey song on the jukebox, he'd just sit and think. &amp;quot;Life had been great. It really had. I can't say exactly when, but it had. Now, it's just life.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Bob worked on his Camaro. He dated pretty girls, but nothing really solid. He played softball with a local team, and worked out at the gym to stay solid. He rented one of those little apartments out by the strip mall, and no one but him ever went there. As the years went by, his old buddies all got married and got a paunch. The girls all dressed up every Saturday night, until they only dressed up for Sunday mornings. &amp;quot;Bobby,&amp;quot; they'd all say, &amp;quot;When are you gonna grow up and get a real life? You're gorgeous. You could marry any woman you want.&amp;quot; He'd just smile and ask how their kids were doing in school. He knew they talked. Maybe he was gay, or depressed or a secret drunk. But he wasn't any of those things. He just never met a woman who looked at him like a person and not Mr. September from the pinup calendar.<br /> <br /> By the ten year reunion, he had had it. He didn't want to go, but the old gang made him. Then Deb walked in, with her husband. She was a math teacher in Cincinatti and her husband, was, umm, something with a suit. Bob almost lost it right there in the gym. He made his apologies and left.<br /> <br /> Driving home, a six pack between his feet, he came round the bend and saw a crashed car by the side of the road. It was a Jaguar. As he got out and walked toward the high beams shining up from the ravine, the horn was blaring in the night. He thought, &amp;quot;Amazing the first Jaguar I've seen with a working electrical system and it's crashed in a ditch.&amp;quot; Only the front of the hood was visible, but as he shimmied down the slope, he saw a woman at the wheel. She looked dead. Like days dead. There was no blood anywhere, but she could not possibly be alive. Her head was at a right angle to her neck.<br /> <br /> He looked inside to see if there was anyone else and jumped when she moved. Her head swiveled around and he could hear her say, &amp;quot;Open the door. Now lean in. Now turn your head.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> He hadn't realized it, but he had done those things. Then he began to die as the blood flowed out of him. But he didn't, well not exactly.<br /> <br /> Seems even the Toreador prince of Columbus can hit an oil patch and skid out. She had planned to just drain him dry, but at the last moment, she looked at him. Those powder blue eyes. The soft blonde hair. The flawless skin and chiseled jaw. He was simply the most beautiful man she had ever seen. And considering the circles she moved in, that was saying something.<br /> <br /> She embraced him, and took him to Columbus. He hung out in Elysium for a few months, but it just all seemed so fake. Yes, he was good looking, but that was it. He didn't care about the things her friends talked about. It was all post-deconstructionist poetry and cinema verite re-montaged installations and this and that. Bob probably could have understood it if he wanted to, but what was the point? He would never fit in, and he knew it. Art was meaningless, there was just survival. Blood. Or not, and take a walk in the morning sun. Whatever.<br /> <br /> They called him a poseur, but posing as what? A NASCAR fan in a roomful of Edith Heads and Dandy Warhols? &amp;quot;This is just me, not a pose&amp;quot;, he'd point out. So, they called him a burnout. But had he ever really flamed. Well, prom night, but that doesn't count. His sire grew impatient and dropped hints that he should leave, and maybe not mention his lineage. They talk every once in a while, on the phone. He thinks she's afraid he'll go anarch or sabbat or something, but he wouldn't. She calls him a blue-collar, burn-out autarkis. He always tries to sound chipper on the phone, but usually cries afterward.<br /> <br /> He moved back to the apartment in Huntington. He works the night shift on a tow truck for spending money, but uses his supernatural charisma to pay the rent. He feels bad about cheating the landlady, but she doesn't seem to mind.<br /> <br /> Nights off, he sits at the corner bar, some old Journey song on the jukebox, and pretends to drink a beer. He thinks, &amp;quot;Life had been great. It really had. I can't say exactly when, but it had. Now, it's just life.&amp;quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12326-slick-willy","name":"Slick Willy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T21:43:08-07:00","id":965485,"title":"","content":"<b>#51</b> A Nosferatu who's embrace physically aged him to the point of being an invalid... supposedly. He is almost never seen outside of the company of his female attendant who serves as a nurse, body guard and mouth piece. Unlike most Ghouls, he has given her a thorough education in the use of disciplines, making her far more powerful than a common thrall. He doesn't like having to personally engage in combat, but when he does so, he flips out like Yoda and proves himself inhumanly powerful for a 109 year old man!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-09-2016, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T06:35:12-07:00","id":966172,"title":"","content":"<b>#52</b> A caitiff who was embraced from one of the low born street trash as part of an experiment by their sire. They wanted to see which blood was the source behind the Venture's talent for power. Was it the result of good breeding, proper education and mentally sound behavior? Or was it simply a boon granted to them by the languid vitae in their veins? The caitiff isn't a thin blood, but his sire refuses to acknowledge any connection to him. That would obligate him to take responsibility for the childe's education, which would ruin the experiment and destroy his reputation in the process.<br /> <br /> No, he must remain at a distance while he observes his childe's progress. Now, if only the gutter spawn wasn't making bedroom eyes with the Anarchs!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>#53</b> They call him <b>Kinky Pete</b>, an eccentrically charismatic Malkavian who counts himself among the ranks of the Sabbat. While most of his clan scare the shit out of other vampires, Pete has made himself invaluable to his pack and the Sabbat as a whole due to his knowledge of Thaumaturgy. As a self proclaimed <i>Punks Sorcerer</i>, Kinky Pete's knowledge of blood magic gives his pack a fighting chance against any Tremere they come across. What they don't know, however, is how Kinky Pete came to learn his craft.<br /> <br /> In truth, Kinky Pete is a Diabolist who obtained his power by bargaining with demons, and followers the Path of Pain, respectively. His Malkavian insight makes him very good at hiding this secret from Sabbat inquisitors. Most people just chalk it up to him being a crazy son of a bitch; nobody wants to pry too deeply into a Malkavian's personal affairs, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T11:15:17-07:00","id":966837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=952972#post952972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this supposed only to be Modern Nights or are Dark Ages welcome as well?.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be used in any setting you like.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:03:06-07:00","id":966876,"title":"","content":"#54 Linda Kay Keegan's parents were pleasant and fairly well-adjusted. Her dad owned a hardware store, her mom was a nutritionist at a hospital in Cleveland. It was all very double knit and Republican. At 19, Linda took a week off from her job as a secretary at an aluminum siding manufacturer and went on vacation to San Francisco. Six days later, on October 24, 1974, she drank two and a half Grasshoppers at a fern bar on Fisherman's Wharf, saw her mood ring had turned pink, and went to the payphone. First she called her boss and quit her job. Second, she called to cancel her flight. Then she called her mom and was told she had gone insane. And was asked if she had joined a cult? Then she walked all the way to Pacific Heights, where a guy she knew in high school was living with his boyfriend. The whole way there, she looked like Tricia Nixon Cox running away from home, with nothing but three avocado green hard-side Samsonite bags and a clear plastic snoopy umbrella.<br /> <br /> Linda lived with Barry and Dave for ten years. Well, Barry and the handsome boyfriend du jour for ten years. Living with them was fun, but sometimes the gay thing kind of freaked her out. Partying all weekend wasn't really her thing, but if that's what they were into, whatever. She'd rather just read the old People magazines at the laundromat on a Saturday night. Everyone always said she was uptight, but really she was just a little shy. She went to UCSF, got a Bachelor's in nursing and worked at Presbyterian Hospital. She dated some guys, but nothing really worked out. Gary was married. Tom went off with the People's Temple. Cliff became a woman. Doug was too depressed all the time. She just wanted someone normal. Her mother pointed out, &quot;you don't catch lobsters in a bathtub, honey. Come home, Linda!&quot; Linda always just replied that this was home.<br /> <br /> She was generally happy, and looked on the bright side. She figured the universe gives you what you give it. If you act all dark and broody, the universe will oblige. If you do your best and keep the right attitude things will work out. Then, in March 1983, Barry got sick. It started small, with night sweats and a series of colds. It seemed like he had a low grade cough for two months, and just couldn't shake it. She figured he was just working too hard. But then, the first tiny lesions appeared. She, being a nurse, noticed it first. They went to the doctor and got the diagnosis. His creepy boyfriend who only ever saw Barry at the clubs disappeared, the turkey. She cut back on hours at work to help Barry when it got really bad. By Christmas, Barry almost went into hospice, but suddenly the creepy night time boyfriend reappeared. And just as suddenly Barry was all better. He only went out at night, now, but he seemed great otherwise, if a bit pale. He had a new circle of friends and went to a new set of clubs, and had kind of left Linda behind. They got together for drinks once in a while. He was healthy, just like Linda had hoped, but she missed him.<br /> <br /> By the summer of '85, Linda had moved out to her own place on Russian Hill. She started to freak out about getting older. She had turned thirty and was starting to show it. Nothing huge, just some little lines, and a few extra pounds. But she could see the difference. She went on a vegetarian, macrobiotic diet and took up yoga. She jogged on the weekends. She dated some cool guys, but nothing fantabulous. If she just kept a positive attitude, though, she knew it would be fine. Then, Barry introduced her to his sire, and he offered her the embrace before he and Barry moved to LA. She thought about it for a few days, arranged to change to a night shift, and then said yes. A new adventure!<br /> <br /> People always talked about vampires like they're so dark and gloomy. It was nothing like that, though. Oh, her sire told her lots of stories about dark gods and aeons and stuff, but what was the big deal? Oh, she couldn't go out in the day, but San Francisco had lots of nightlife. She worked as an IV nurse, so never was short on blood. She's immortal, more or less immune to injury, and can heal anything that does hurt her. She dates lots of new guys and hangs out with some of the other neonates. Some of them are very political, and a little too radical for her taste, but that's San Francisco. Sometimes, they're sad and gloomy, but she does her best to cheer them up. Just look on the bright side, she says! She's gotten really good at doing super-accurate horoscopes and slips in all kinds of encouraging messages when she does them.<br /> <br /> She's learned how to turn invisible and how to become supernaturally alluring. She can even do some snake type tricks with her eyes and tongue like her sire, but snakes are creepy, so she doesn't do it unless she really has to. The local elders require her to attend a party at the Palace of Fine Arts once a month, just to keep in touch. It's sweet of them to want to hang out so much. even though they don't like her sire's ancestors or whatever. <br /> <br /> When she RSVPs for Elysium, she always signs her name with a little happy face over the &quot;i&quot;. She genuinely hopes it makes them smile. She can't understand why the elders are so down all the time. Being undead is awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:25:02-07:00","id":966950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slick Willy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=965276#post965276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is gold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much all of Nosimplehiway's contributions to this thread are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T07:41:03-07:00","id":967301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=966876#post966876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#54</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Soooo, is she a Setite? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:02:57-07:00","id":967349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=967301#post967301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Soooo, is she a Setite? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Setites can't be this cute","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12326-slick-willy","name":"Slick Willy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:07:57-07:00","id":967352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slick Willy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=967349#post967349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setites can't be this cute</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They'd have to be. How else would anybody let them into their home?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T12:22:42-07:00","id":967459,"title":"","content":"After repeatedly hearing that Caitiff are treated like 3rd class citizens among vampire society, I thought a character like this might be fun to try out. Even if his life expectancy is shorter than most of his kind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>#55</b> </span>Being a caitiff in the world of vampires sucks, it sucks pretty hard. But when the most hated clan and the most inhuman clan both have a vendetta against you, you don't have to suffer final death to know what hell is like. Such is the unlife that Harold Tippens has found himself in when he was left sireless with only a remedial education on being a vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> At some point after his embrace, Harold began to manifest the disciplines of Auspex, Thaumaturgy and Vicissitude. He claims to have no idea how he obtained these powers, something just clicks in his head one night and he gains the knowledge spontaneously. Clans Tremere and Tzmisce, however, are not buying it. They accuse him of thievery, stealing their most sacred powers and bastardizing their use. As a result, these two mortal enemies have both declared a bounty on the caitiff, offering rewards to anyone who can capture him for interrogation. Once they've extracted what they want from him, they will almost certainly execute him, which means Harold can not afford to let his guard down.<br /> <br /> <br /> Prior to his embrace, Harold was a middle class, white suburban bachelor of 22 years. He worked as a carpenter, with some of his best work being hand crafted. Life may not have been fancy, but it was a comfortable life, none the less. That all changed the night he received a request for a custom order. An anonymous customer wanted him to fashion a coffin for a funeral that would be held later in the week. They even sent him a list of measurements to make sure he did it right. Harold was curious why the customer would choose to remain unknown, but agreed to take the job and started work on the project.<br /> <br /> <br /> Harold wouldn't receive payment for his efforts, because after he finished building the coffin and was ready to deliver it, he was jumped from the shadows by an intruder who had snuck into his workshop. He was stabbed, things went black, and the next thing he remembers was waking up inside the coffin he had just built... six feet under the earth's crust!<br /> <br /> <br /> The climb back to the surface was indescribably horrific. Harold was forced to draw upon reserves of power that he never knew he possessed, and would later find out he never had until that moment. Bursting out of the soil like a raving lunatic, it took two minutes for him to finally regain his senses to the point where he could take in his surroundings. He was in a graveyard, alone and without even a tombstone to mark where he had been buried.<br /> <br /> <br /> Harold never knew who his sire was, as they had been chased off by Camarilla agents before he had time to climb out of his grave, and Harold was already gone by the time the agents circled back to check on him. But ever since that terrible night he's been on the constant move. Never being allowed to sleep in the same spot twice, for fear of being located. After encountering both the Tremere and the Tzimisce, Harold would shock both clans (as well as himself) by being able to replicate their abilities after only a brief demonstration of their uses. Immediately declaring him a threat to their secrets, both clans deployed agents to hunt him down.<br /> <br /> <br /> Harold's knowledge of Thaumaturgy and Vicissitude is novice level, but it is enough to draw attention from their respective clans. The supernatural senses granted to him by Auspex have proven to be a greater boon than sorcerous alchemy. With it, he can sense his pursuers before they get too close, although he does come across as overly paranoid to those who don't understand what's happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-04-2017, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:48:19-07:00","id":967510,"title":"","content":"Thank you. For the Linda Kay Keegan idea, I owe a huge debt to Armistead Maupin.<br /> <br /> Yes, she is a Setite. Think about what she's been through. The sudden, impulsive break with her parents, the challenging of her conservative upbringing, the revolving door of impossibly dramatic break-ups... I mean, a transexual <i>and</i> a guy who followed Jim Jones to Guyana? A best friend nearly dying of AIDS? And through it all she coped with aplomb.<br /> <br /> The Setites have cults built around Vikings, Aztecs and Indian demons, why not one built around the power of positive thinking? Sure, the holy symbol is a happy face, the ritual hymn is the theme from Greatest American Hero, and the theology is cribbed off of Course in Miracles. But, how does any of that disagree with Setite teachings? Sometimes the best evangelist for a faith is someone who just seems so darn happy that everyone wants to be like them. Linda's been <i>fantabulous</i> for thirty years, and isn't snotty about it. Lots more people take advice from her than from any prophet of doom.<br /> <br /> Maybe the scariest part is that orthodox Setite thought can be so seamlessly expressed through modern, pop culture idiom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T10:21:25-07:00","id":968595,"title":"","content":"#56 By 1975, Mary Lawrence had made a comfortable life for herself. She used her MFA and MEd teaching art at Woonsocket High School. Her husband, Edward, managed a successful trucking company. Their daughter, Debbie, won the county wide spelling bee in the seventh grade division, then came in fourth in the spelling bee against students from all of Rhode Island. They lived in a pleasant ranch home with a dog named Moxie. Mary loved teaching, but wanted to expand her horizons, so she enrolled in the PhD program in Art History at Brown.<br /> <br /> Two years into her studies, at the age of 41, she thought she was going through early menopause, missing periods and feeling tired all the time. But, her doctor explained she was pregnant. How could she possibly balance all of this? She sat down with Ed to figure it out. He reassured her he would help as much as he could. Debbie was getting her driver's license, so she'd be more independent. He suggested Mary take a sabbatical from work to get in as much work on her thesis as possible before the baby came. Her advisor agreed to the changes and she entered a frenetic period of research and writing.<br /> <br /> In early 1978, Mary gave birth to the most beautiful little boy she had ever seen. She and Ed named him Michael. However, there were some physical abnormalities noted by the doctors at birth, and Michael was eventually diagnosed by the doctors with Down Syndrome, and a related heart defect. Mary and Ed rearranged their plans, Mary taking a leave of absence from the doctoral program to help his development with as much individual attention as possible. After graduation in 1981, daughter Debbie, who had wanted to attend NYU, instead attended a commuter college so she could help out. By 1983, Mary had completed her thesis and her presentation to the committee went well. Her thesis was filed in a dusty file cabinet in the Brown library. Mary taught a few classes at the local community college, but mostly focused on being a fierce advocate for the mainstreaming of students in the local school district.<br /> <br /> In the back of Mary's mind was a creeping fear, though. What would happen to Michael (who needed constant care) when she and Ed were gone? Neither of them were getting any younger, and Michael, like any child, was sometimes a real handful. He had wild mood swings, one minute being quite pleasant and happy. The next he would become frustrated with some task and throw a tantrum. Debbie and her fiance said they would care for Michael if anything happened to Mary and Ed, but that struck Mary as unfair. She wanted Debbie to be happy, too, and didn't want such a young couple to carry such a responsibility. It broke Mary's heart to realize how relieved she was that Michael's heart defect might mean he would pre-decease her.<br /> <br /> Then the unthinkable happened. While driving home from a Christmas party in 1988, Debbie and her fiance skidded on the ice and crashed into the frigid waters of the Blackstone River. Mary and Ed were understandably devastated, but not like Michael. They had a frame of reference with which to grieve, but Michael didn't know how to express his loss. He became even more difficult to handle, and his academic progress came to a near standstill. Mainstreaming at school was out of the question. Michael's earning money at a job-coached job and living in a group home when he grew up seemed less and less plausible.<br /> <br /> Debbie and Ed's marriage suffered. How could they admit their greatest fear to one another when they could not admit it to themselves? That they, alone, would be left caring for Michael, even as they someday lost their spouse to old age and were themselves declining. Stony silences and a numb routine became the order of the day at the Lawrence home.<br /> <br /> In 1991, when Mary was 55 and Michael was 13, a Toreador ancilla from Boston was browsing the Brown library and came across Mary's thesis. He was very impressed at Mary's interpretation of the intersection of psychology and art history in creating a predictive model of artistic productivity in later life, with special emphasis on sculptors of the Harlem Renaissance who had retired to upstate New York. The Toreador believed that with further research Mary could predict which young people would go on to be artistically productive after ghouling or the embrace.<br /> <br /> He approached Mary and offered her the embrace, without fulling exploring her life circumstances. Mary jumped at the chance to retain her last vestige of youth and to be able to care for Michael for years to come. She was released a few months later into Providence's small kindred court. She ghouled Ed before realizing the psychological dependency it would cause. He is a shell of his former sense, worshiping her, but in a distinctly unnatural way.<br /> <br /> It's been 25 years since she was embraced. Michael, at 37, has survived longer than any of the doctors thought he would. Mary has refused to ghoul him, either out of fear of losing the authenticity of his relationship with her, or for fear of having... it kills her to say this... but fear of having him with her forever. His blood pressure is terrible. His heart is worse than ever. It's just a matter of time before she will have to say goodbye. But can she actually bear to let him die when he's on his deathbed? Or... and it's nearly unthinkable... but there is one way she could save him without blood bonding him. But, the Prince would never stand for that. Not under the Third Tradition anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:42:27-07:00","id":968648,"title":"","content":"Can Obeah cure Down's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12326-slick-willy","name":"Slick Willy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T13:31:12-07:00","id":968704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=967510#post967510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. For the Linda Kay Keegan idea, I owe a huge debt to Armistead Maupin.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThought I recognized a bit of Tales of the city there...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T13:37:35-07:00","id":968708,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Mary would not consider it something to be &quot;cured&quot; exactly. Trisomy 21 (aka Down Syndrome) is one component of who he was meant to be, from birth. You wouldn't cure someone being left-handed, or unusually tall, or having a birthmark. That's all just part of who a person is. If he woke up tomorrow without that extra copy of the chromosome, he would no longer be Michael.<br /> <br /> Besides, Mary is not aware of any of the more obscure bloodlines and disciplines. She didn't even know ahead of time the emotional toll ghouling would have on Ed. Ghouling would presumably freeze Michael in time as far as his cardiac condition's progression goes; but then most ghouls sooner or later frenzy and that can't be good for someone with a weak heart.<br /> <br /> Copore sano (Obeah 3) heals wounds, which might help in the moments of cardiac arrest, but is not a long term solution. Mens sana (Obeah 5) soothes madness, but Down Syndrome is definitely not madness, though it might help when he is in emotional turmoil, just as with anyone. In theory, Biothaumaturgy or Vicissitude might be able to stabilize or even fix his cardiac issues, if the practitioner has enough mundane knowledge of cardiac surgery to touch the heart without killing Michael.<br /> <br /> Possibly mage intervention, but his DS is integral to his natural pattern and making him not have DS would cause serious pattern leakage and draw paradox like little else.<br /> <br /> The only long term fix is probably the embrace, but that raises a <u>lot</u> of other issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:02:29-07:00","id":968915,"title":"","content":"56) The local Prince learns that two rival Vampires both want to embrace the same person. Being the sick-humored bitch she is, the Prince meets with each one separately and gives them the same time and place to embrace the Mortal. As the Prince hoped, one of the Vampires came in just as the other was about to put his vitae into them. Thanks to the bloody fight between the two, both of their blood got into the Mortal. Since both Vampires are the same generation and clan, it's hard to tell who the fledgeling's sire is.<br /> <br /> Now the poor childe is torn between two &quot;sires&quot; who are in a passive-aggressive relationship to raise her together. All while the Prince is secretly laughing at them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":1834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","user":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","date":". 09-13-2016, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T04:08:32-07:00","id":969130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=968915#post968915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">56) The local Prince learns that two rival Vampires both want to embrace the same person. Being the sick-humored bitch she is, the Prince meets with each one separately and gives them the same time and place to embrace the Mortal. As the Prince hoped, one of the Vampires came in just as the other was about to put his vitae into them. Thanks to the bloody fight between the two, both of their blood got into the Mortal. Since both Vampires are the same generation and clan, it's hard to tell who the fledgeling's sire is.<br /> <br /> Now the poor childe is torn between two &amp;quot;sires&amp;quot; who are in a passive-aggressive relationship to raise her together. All while the Prince is secretly laughing at them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maury by Night","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12326-slick-willy","name":"Slick Willy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T08:08:19-07:00","id":969234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slick Willy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=969130#post969130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maury by Night</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says V:TM can't have a bit of a sense of humor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:16:16-07:00","id":969368,"title":"","content":"<b>57) [Larva]:</b> Larva is a Nosferatu (13th-generation) who shriveled and mummified to such an extent he has shrunk down to the size of a horrid, undead infant. His jaws are too deformed for speech and he has virtually no strength in his body. Normally, Larva would be doomed, such is his physical helplessness...but Larva has...a 'mother'.<br /> <br /> Larva's ghoul has been with him for over a hundred years. Despite being quite male, the ghoul responds to the name 'Mother'. Wrapping him in diseased swaddling-clothes, Mother carries Larva about, hunting food for him, a silent butcher with a 'baby' in one hand and a gore-encrusted meat-cleaver in the other.<br /> <br /> Intellectually, Larva has regressed to a mostly feral state (Humanity 2); Mother is hardly any better (Humanity 3). But they are a family, and nothing can ever tear them apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-14-2016, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T14:26:24-07:00","id":969450,"title":"","content":"#57 Larry Khoury grew up tough. He was the oldest of seven boys from the side of town good people rolled up their windows when they drove through. His father came home late from the plant every night. Some nights so drunk he could barely walk. Other nights, the bad nights, he was just drunk enough to get angry. At what? It didn't take much. Anytime he was about to go on a tear through the boys, splitting lips and blacking eyes, Larry's mom would put herself in the line of fire. A few jibes about dear old pop's manhood, and she got the beating, not the kids. Even with mom running interference, by the time it ended, the seven brothers had had four broken arms, three broken legs, twelve dislocated shoulders and six cracked ribs between them.<br /> <br /> When Larry was sixteen, in 1946, his father got it bad. His brothers were all out. Pops had mom cornered on the third floor of the rowhome they lived in and was just slamming and slamming and slamming. She was bent backwards out the open window, woozy, with blood flowing down her scalp, dodging his fists. Pop lifted his fist one last time, loading up a haymaker, and the iron doorstop came down on the back of pop's head. Larry's mom gasped, swooned for a moment and recovered her balance in time to see Larry holding the doorstop. It was in the shape of a small bulldog, and was solid iron. It was dripping a foul liquid, grey and oozing. His father was on the floor, his skull split open, brains clearly visible on the rug. She never knew a person had so much blood in them.<br /> <br /> She sat there, on the radiator below the windowsill, numb, still bloody, not knowing what to do. Larry went immediately into action. He had planned this moment for sixteen years. He gathered a shovel, a heavy blanket and some lime from the outhouse. He slung his father over his shoulder and staggered down three flights of steps to the dirt floor basement. As far as Larry knows his father is still there.<br /> <br /> He went out that night with his friends, got drunk and got a tattoo: &quot;Mom&quot;, in hearts and flowers on his shoulder. He got a job at his dad's plant (there was suddenly an opening), and moved out three weeks later, after hand concreting the basement.<br /> <br /> He worked at the plant until 1950, when he joined the US Army to go fight in Korea. He was an infantryman, and saw a good bit of frontline combat. He was a quiet, grim eyed soldier and though his the officers couldn't quite find anything to criticize in his service, they didn't trust him. He was brave, but a little foolhardy. He was a good leader within his unit, and the men respected him, but somehow when things went south he never seemed to be around. If the COs were able to admit it to themselves, they would have seen that every time Larry dropped an enemy combatant he would suppress an ecstatic shudder. He kept careful count of the enemy he killed. Anytime he got leave, he would add to his collection of tattoos. One for each kill. By the time he rotated home, he had 14 new tattoos. None of them larger than a few inches, and all easily hidden under his clothes.<br /> <br /> Stateside, he joined the Detroit PD. He gained a reputation as an honest cop, but one who pushed the edge of acceptable violence. He always slammed his knee into perps' backs a little too hard, and pulled runners off the fire escapes into the concrete with a little too much enthusiasm. But if he seemed to enjoy it a little much, so what? No one in the department ever complained, of course, who would you rather have watching your back, someone a little too rough or not rough enough?<br /> <br /> In 1966, Larry, service weapon drawn, cornered a drug dealer who had been cutting his product with dangerous chemicals, killing at least a dozen druggies. His hands were up and he was begging for his life. Larry took a deep breath, shuddered a bit and pulled the trigger. The dealer's brains exploded across the floral wallpaper. Larry felt the greatest release of his life. He was on desk duty for a few weeks, while the paperwork was processed. By the time he was back on the street, he had gotten his sixteenth tattoo.<br /> <br /> The downtime was too much for him. He had tasted blood and he wanted more. He started wandering the worst neighborhoods on his nights off. Dressed well, and acting drunk. Muggers picked him often, but they never mugged anyone again. He developed a source for body disposal; local organized crime, the Detroit Partners, was happy to oblige. In exchange, he just had to keep the other cops away from &quot;victimless&quot; crimes like prostitution and the numbers racket. By the time he retired from the Detroit PD in 1986, he had exactly 427 small tattoos covering his body from his toes, up to just below the &quot;V&quot; neck of his t-shirts, down to the caps of his shoulders. Not one line of ink showed in uniform.<br /> <br /> His last day on the force, the Detroit Partners threw him a retirement party at a fancy restaurant Larry could never have afforded. It was a small affair, a dozen guys, mostly from the Lebanese family that handled clean-up for the Italians. One of the big wigs Larry had never met before invited him back to an empty banquet room behind the kitchen. Charlie was a small man, but looked very athletic, the sort of guy who could rip you in half with one hand. His eyes were a vivid blue, but his skin was a dusky grey, the color of the streets after they put down cinders and the snow starts turning to slush. He asked Larry to tell him the story of his tattoos. Larry was confused. How did this strange looking man know about his tattoos?<br /> <br /> Larry told him the story of every tattoo. He began with the most recent, a pair of dice in flames he got on the back of his knee, after killing a man who beat his wife and gambled away their money. Showing the collection and recounting each victim's sins took hours, working backwards. The last, of course, was Pops. Charlie said nothing, asked no questions, but just nodded gravely. Charlie placed his hand sympathetically on Larry's bare shoulder and offered him a job, as a ghoul providing him with &quot;security&quot;. In 1993, after seven years of good service, Larry got a promotion.<br /> <br /> By then, he was tattooed from his fingertips and palms to his jawline, and it crept up onto his scalp and down onto his temples and forehead. Only the center of his face remained blank. Otherwise, his tattoos were packed as tight as a rainbow bramble. Finally, now, upon his embrace, he could begin hunting, judging and executing even more vile monsters, those who can only rightfully be judged by the Banu Haqim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:42:03-07:00","id":971024,"title":"","content":"<b>#58</b> Alexis Gourdon is a victim of one of the worst embraces, one performed out of spite, rather than any real interest in recruitment. Even worse than that, she was embraced into the Toreador, which means her sire had a taste for the theatrics!<br /> <br /> <br /> Alexis' father was a hunter who kept his double life a secret from his family. She had no idea that every night, he would sneak out of the house to go slay monsters and be back home in time for breakfast. But one night, Mr. Gourdon chose the wrong prey, which lead to the tragic circumstances that came after. A pair of vampires (twins even before their embrace) had been stirring up trouble in the city, and Gourdon was determined to see them exterminated. He managed to locate them, but was only successful in destroying the sister, while the enraged brother escaped into the night, rather than stay behind and risk final death. Gourdon decided to call his victory there and headed home. He arrived just three hours before dawn, enough time to slip into bed and get some much needed rest after a successful hunt. But just as he finished placing his gear in its passcode protected storage containers, the door to his house exploded off its hinges and a pack of Sabbat poured into his home, lead by the brother who had escaped that night.<br /> <br /> Mr. Gourdon didn't have time to retrieve his gear again, because the lightning quick Toreador was already up the stairs and slammed him against the bedroom wall, momentarily stunning him. His wife was startled awake and began to scream, before a clawed hand was clamped over her mouth and a gun pressed against her temple. One of the brother's packmates had followed him upstairs and was now holding Gourdon's wife hostage.<br /> <br /> Most Sabbat would have been able to just slaughter the family and be done with it, but no self respecting Toreador would have passed up an opportunity to bask in their victory, and so they spent the better part of an hour beating the hell out of the furious hunter. All the while, Mr. Gourdon didn't give him the satisfaction of surrender, until two more packmates entered the room, dragging the 16 year old Alexis by the shoulders like she was a toddler. That seemed to break her father's stoic front as he demanded they leave her alone. The vengeful brother turned to Gourdon, flashed him a fanged smile and then fell upon Alexis, embracing her on the spot.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alexis would awaken the next night in her own bed, stripped of her clothing and with another man spooning her from behind. With a startled shriek, she jumped out of bed and turned to see the man who attacked her laying on his side with the same grin on his face. <i>&quot;Welcome to the Sabbat.&quot; </i>he said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since then, Alexis' life has been one of passive aggressive torture. Her sire (now known formally as Richard) considers his abusive mistreatment to be his way of striking at her father even in death. When he isn't coercing her into acting like a blood thirsty monster, he uses her as a slave for all manner of sexual fantasies. It's blatantly clear he has no regard for her as his childe, and it's entirely possible that he plans to drive her into a draugr state and then cast her aside. But what is she supposed to do? Alexis knew nothing of this world when she was mortal, and her sire hasn't exactly been the best teacher, forcing her to learn about vampire society through personal experience and second hand mentoring by other vampires. If it weren't for the fact she knows her clan lineage, she might be considered a caitiff!<br /> <br /> <br /> As it currently stands, Alexis has neither the knowledge, nor the courage to abandon the Sabbat. Alexis has seen more than enough evidence to know that attempting to run would result in a painful death. And as if that wasn't bad enough, being forced to partake in the Vaulderie allows Richard and his friends to toy with her emotions, making it even more difficult to resist giving into their demands. Her only hope is that somebody arrives to show her a better way, hopefully before she's too far gone to be recognizable as anything other than another shovel head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  fixed some typos and phrasing 09-18-2016, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T05:03:55-07:00","id":971887,"title":"","content":"My favorite part with Alexis is that she, herself, now has the Toreador antitribu weakness. If she ever gets the upper hand over Richard, he will pay for what he has done. Classic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T06:18:09-07:00","id":971901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=971887#post971887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite part with Alexis is that she, herself, now has the Toreador antitribu weakness. If she ever gets the upper hand over Richard, he will pay for what he has done. Classic!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, hadn't thought of that! Maybe take the &quot;created your own monster&quot; route for her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:39:05-07:00","id":972608,"title":"","content":"Here's one with which I came up just last night, which I plan to use as one of the PC's fellow city-dwellers when they move into Kronstadt in my TC game. Details omitted because I haven't thought that far ahead yet:<br /> <br /> In the city, there is a particularly noteworthy brothel. Noteworthy because all the women there are clean, exceptionally beautiful, devoted to their matron with a near-religious zeal, and never seem to age. Needless to say, the matron is a vampire, equally exceptionally beautiful, but also quite mad. No one is quite sure what clan she is -- she has the disposition of a Malkavian, but the refinement and taste for beauty of a Toreador.<br /> <br /> She is obsessed with...babies. She pushes her prostitutes (her herd) to get pregnant, as often as they can, forces them to carry to term, and midwifes for them. After they give birth, she takes them as her own, fawning over them by night in her haven which doubles as a creche, as a chosen ghoul runs the brothel itself. The only time she leaves her brothel is to buy, or even steal, others' babies according to her own inscrutable standards. She even goes so far as to wet nurse her babies, feeding them drops of blood from her own breast but never enough to lock them into the stasis of ghouldom (i.e she stops short of feeding them a full blood point at a time), and even apply the Kiss (but not feed) to quiet upset babies.<br /> <br /> Of course, once they grow past infancy, she quickly loses interest in most and shoves them out the door to be cared by the prostitutes or whoever will take them. Those she keeps, continue feeding at her breast until adulthood, and go on to be the next generation of exceptionally-beautiful, long-lived prostitutes.<br /> <br /> Because she's a Zantovich, and and out raw insanity or misguidance is breeding her own family of revenants (albeit not doing it very well, as her methods don't include inbreeding). She fleshcrafts the <i>dogshit</i> out of the babies, and keep them blood bound, as they grow into adulthood and beyond. Likewise, she fleshcrafts her prostitutes regularly to prevent them from becoming physically marred from repeated childbirth. Her &quot;babies&quot; are her territory, and she <i>is</i> obsessed with them and their welfare...at least, until they stop being babies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:09:48-07:00","id":972704,"title":"","content":"I got one for a NPC in one of my games<br /> <br /> #59<br /> <br /> Pete Schaffer life was taken before his time and in the worst of ways<br /> <br /> Pate was a smart kid at school and was like by his friends and peers about school because of his neutral talent of making anything, he favorite lesson was arts and crafts where he would amazed everyone with more and more complex stuff but there was one thing loved to make out of anything and that was flower bombs for pranks that he and his friend was doing and they were mostly harmless... until the April 1st flower bomb incident. He had miscalculated the how much flower he had put in and instead of taken out just the class room half the school was covered in flowery DOOM as he put it.<br /> <br /> his parents were called in of course but his where different as they loved him and defended him over it saying it was just a harmless prank and no one got hurt. he was taken out of school the following day to his parents anger. for the next two months his parents would look for a new school but he was already plotting his revenge on his old one...<br /> <br /> but it never happen because something would change anything for him and it all started on his 12th Birthday on June 5th when he woke up early in the morning when he heard something from the living room. as he came down he say saw someone standing in the middle of the room and it would be the most horrifying thing he had ever seen. he described it as some demonic cactus man. what happen after that becomes more blurry but this is what we do know, his parents were killed, he house destroyed in a fire, and pate was left for dead and they dumped his dying body on the side of a road in a ditch.<br /> <br /> but he was not dead far from it he just laid there straying at the star above as he waited for death... it came but not as he was expecting it because a kindred saw him and for one reason or another decided to embrace the kid and then just left the neonate to defend for himself and after that a police car just happen to be passing by and saw him walking down the road in a daze. poor cop try to help the kid but little did this guy know Pete was hungry and the beast was in control. he would of rid the guys head off drinking his blood if a pack of anarchs where not passing by.<br /> <br /> they took Pete to there place as the reality of his situation started to set in... he wasn't human and more... he was something from horrer movies... that when the whispers came to him and spoke... he had to find somewhere anywhere HE HAD TO... after that he was not seen for sometime until the The Sabbat started getting hit hard by a unknown assailant who had it out for them.<br /> <br /> it was little old Pete and he had set up shop in an abandoned house or like he called it the Funhouse and he had made it his personal vendetta to take out every Sabbat in the area and he did it using his knowledge of explosives. he was using hit and run tactics to disseminate them and became a rebel without a cause<br /> <br /> after he had pretty much force the Sabbat out of the city he was pick up by the Camarilla and they let him in with open arms and was praise by the prince for his work<br /> <br /> but when ask why he did all of it he said &quot;they took everytHing from mE so i TooK everythiNg from them&quot; and he just smiled like any 12 year old would<br /> <br /> it was later found out he had been embrace by a malkavian but no one know who his sire was but he did not care. after a while, after the prince allowed him to stay in the city he want back to his F\u200bunhouse and set up a small &quot;legitimate&quot; business<br /> <br /> so if you are in need of something the makes a big KADOOM he the kid to go to and he is always open and he may seem childish but dont let that fool you he a born again survivor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12439-the-vampire-fish","user":"The Vampire Fish","date":". 09-19-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12439-the-vampire-fish","name":"The Vampire Fish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12439_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T18:35:41-07:00","id":975322,"title":"","content":"#62 David Dawson is a practical man raised by practical people in the very practical town of Pottstown, PA. His parents are retired, a general contractor and a home ec teacher. After high school, he earned a bachelor's of science degree in Engineering Technology in Construction Management Technology from Temple University. He married his high school sweetheart, Aayisha, who had gotten an accounting degree from Temple.<br /> <br /> He used his degree to help run his father's growing contracting and construction business. Aayisha kept the books. His three brothers, an electrician, a plumber and an HVAC guy, all worked at the business. Aayisha and David had three kids: David, Jr., Alana, and DeShawn. In the twenty years, since graduation the business grew. They mostly did re-models on older homes and re-purposing of large, old homes into commercial offices. They did some new construction, too, like the big apartment complex over by King of Prussia. David was bidding on a strip mall rehab project in Norristown, when he met his sire.<br /> <br /> More exactly, David was standing by the side of his truck just before dawn, eating a Wawa breakfast sandwich and waiting for the client, when his sire pounced upon him. She had destroyed a Sabbat pack in direct combat inside the abandoned strip mall, and she was badly wounded, low on blood and nearly a goner. She found David, dragged him back to her haven, a 1960s era bomb shelter in the midst of suburban tract homes. She closed the hatch moments before dawn. She pounced on David in a desperate bid to avoid torpor, and drained him to a husk. Then, realizing she may have been trailed, she fed him her blood and hid in her usual crypt, an old 300 gallon water tank. As she locked the hatch, she saw David rouse. Anyone who disturbed her rest tonight would find a frenzying young vampire first.<br /> <br /> He strained against the zip ties she had bound him with and began screaming, then frenzying. He bit wildly at the air. Any who entered would surely have been destroyed. Then, he slept his first day.<br /> <br /> That night she arose to find David in full frenzy, starved for blood and slamming against the walls. She wrapped him in the tarps she usually used to carry bodies, threw him in the back of her van and started driving up and down alleys until she found what she needed. It was in the back of a row-home fronting on Lafayette Street where she saw a Labrador Retriever doing it's business in the yard. She rolled down the window, whistled and the dog jumped in the driver's side window. She pulled the tarp off David's face, and he fed for the first time.<br /> <br /> That took the edge off. He felt the van jostle and bounce on rough roads and heard the river nearby. She pulled into a gravel parking lot and explained that they were on an island in the middle of the Schuylkill River, used for power transfer stations. She told him, &quot;You're a vampire. Feed on animals, not people. Ever. Don't tell anyone what you are. Ever. The Sabbat are a vampire cult. If you meet one, run like hell. Don't make other vampires. Ever. Respect your elders. Don't trespass on another vampire's turf. Ever. The Camarilla are the good guys. Forget what I look like. Good luck, you unlucky son of a... &quot;<br /> <br /> She cut the tarp open and kicked him out of the side of the van and the final words were drowned out by the sound of gravel spitting from under her tires. He saw her toss the dog out the window into the river.<br /> <br /> He doesn't remember how he made it home to Pottstown or the next few nights. Aayisha helped him figure out most of his condition, He learned how to flush his skin and look human, he learned how to increase his strength and speed. He was feeding on cows from the dairy farms a few miles away. He accidentally ghouled Aayisha during sex, but after some testing they realized she hadn't caught the full vampire virus.<br /> <br /> After a few weeks, a press gang showed up at his door, demanding he appear before the Dux Bellorum of the Five Counties, who held court at a State Police Barracks in West Philadelphia. David only had one question for them, &quot;Are you Camarilla or Sabbat?&quot; The Dux Bellorum was impressed that a seeming Caitiff knew that much, in addition to the rudiments of the Traditions. David's company has been working for them ever since. No one respects him, of course, or invites him to the parties, but he was used to that.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Dawson and Sons has more business than they know what to do with. They build havens and fortified meeting spaces. They light-proof safe-houses and concrete over Sabbat Gangrel while they sleep in the soil of abandoned lots. Mostly, though, they provide practical services, like unstopping the plumbing at a mass house for the herd, or rewiring an interrogation chamber. It's been five years, now, and the Camarilla is close to a break through (they always are...) and David has been quietly instrumental.<br /> <br /> David Dawson is still a practical man doing practical work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:22:18-07:00","id":975550,"title":"","content":"NSH does it again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12326-slick-willy","name":"Slick Willy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T13:37:35-07:00","id":976710,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>#63 Egidio Giovanni:</b> Life in the mob is never easy, especially not when you're part of the family and expected to make them proud from day one. Fortunately, Egidio seemed to have the knack for doing just that, and once he was old enough to enter the family business, he began to establish legitimate business fronts for the Giovanni family. Businesses that allowed them to make large sums of cash while they secretly worked their occult rituals away from the public eye. Yeah, Egidio was related to <i>those Giovanni</i>, the necromantic vampires who spend their nights raising corpses and fucking their cousins!<br /> <br /> Perhaps if things had gone differently, Egidio would have been accepted into the inner circle, receiving The Kiss and becoming a true vampire. But tragedy struck when the family did a little digging into his geneology reports. Egidio was not a Giovanni by blood, his mother had an affair, making him a bastard. Well, needless to say, the Giovanni did not like that, and decided to take action against them.<br /> <br /> His mother, they simply killed in her own home, but Egidio (who had seen more than enough of what went on behind the scenes), they decided to make an example of. They dragged him down to one of their underground cemetaries, filled with reanimated corpses, and tossed him into a dirt filled pit to be eaten alive. Perhaps he would have been, if the Giovanni had tighter security measures in place. Something had managed to infiltrate their cemetary, something that bore a deep grudge against the blood drinking necromancers living just a few floors above them.<br /> <br /> Seeing a potential ally in Egidio, the creature lunged at him before the shambling corpses could notice his presence, draining him of his life's blood and then reciprocating the act. With the now limp body of Egidio slumped over its shoulder, it slipped through its secret escape tunnel, the Giovanni none the wiser.<br /> <br /> Egidio awoke the next night to find himself in a terrible state of decomposition, he had been embraced by one of the Samedi, a bloodline of zombie-like vampires hailing from the Carribean. His sire's rotting form had allowed them to blend seamlessly with the rest of the shambling dead. The Giovanni had a spy within their organization and never even noticed!<br /> <br /> Egidio was pissed at his sire for what he did to him, but he was even more enraged at the Giovanni who would cast him aside for the simple reason that he wasn't a blood born Giovanni like the rest of them. He had given 30 years of hard work and dedicated service to their operations! Reluctantly, he agreed to partner with his sire and use what resources he could to bring them down. Most of his assets were seized by the Giovanni with his presumed death, but he still managed to scrounge together the contacts to establish a shipping operation, smuggling things in and out of the country. His hope is that he can eventually smuggle enough Samedi into the country to battle the Giovanni in force, but such an operation takes time and precision to carry out successfully.<br /> <br /> He may not be privy to the secrets of Giovanni Necromancy, but he finds the art of Thanatosis to be a satisfying replacement!<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps the worst thing out of all this, is that Egidio has no idea their sire is his biological father, having received the embrace shortly after his conception and forced to sever contact with his mother. If his sire is aware of their familial bond, they have chosen to remain secretive about it, probably for good reason.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-06-2017, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:47:17-07:00","id":977310,"title":"","content":"#64 Once upon a time, in a faraway land called Dolancourt, there was a little girl named No\u00eblle, who lived on a farm at the edge of a deep, dark forest. No\u00eblle's father had hair the color of midnight and her mother had hair the color of noon. So, naturally, No\u00eblle's hair was redder than the sunset.<br /> <br /> No\u00eblle's father and mother had many students they taught to sing and play the piano. Every morning No\u00eblle was awakened by her parent's music and every night they sang her a lullaby.<br /> <br /> No\u00eblle had two problems. First, she was very scared of the deep, dark forest where the villagers all said an evil witch lived, who ate children. Second, the adults were fighting a war, and everyone was very scared. Because of the war, three of her mother's students came to live with them. No\u00eblle's mother explained that these boys were now her brothers, and if anyone asked, No\u00eblle should say they always had been.<br /> <br /> One day, when No\u00eblle and her mother were in the barn, soldiers came to their farm and pounded on the door of the house. No\u00eblle's mother became very scared. She gave No\u00eblle a cabbage, a barn jacket and a bucket of water and told her to run, as fast as she could into the deep dark woods. No\u00eblle refused at first, of course, and cried and begged her mother not to make her go there alone, for the woods were very large and very dark. But, her mother put her hand over No\u00eblle's mouth and held her close. She said, &quot;Now, now. Do as I say child. Run as fast as you can. Go through the woods, to the village on the other side. Tell the preacher at the church what happened. If you get scared, just listen, and you will hear me singing to you. And always know that I love you.&quot;<br /> <br /> And her mother began to sing softly as she shoved No\u00eblle out the back door of the barn: &quot;Au clair de la lune, Mon ami Pierrot, Pr\u00eate-moi ta plume, Pour \u00e9crire un mot. Ma chandelle est morte, Je n'ai plus de feu. Ouvre-moi ta porte. Pour l'amour de Dieu...&quot;<br /> <br /> No\u00eblle ran as fast as she could, and ran and ran and ran, all day until it was night and she grew very tired. Late in the night, she woke, thinking she heard her mother singing, and climbed over a rise to see a tall white tower, glowing in the moonlight. No\u00eblle began singing her mother's lullaby, hoping she would be found. &quot;...Ouvre-moi ta porte...&quot;, she sang and the door on the tower opened. An old, old woman beckoned No\u00eblle to the tower and took her inside.<br /> <br /> No\u00eblle was very scared at first, but the old woman was not a witch. For many years, No\u00eblle stayed with her, the only food she had, the thick broth the woman gave her. The woman was strange, she slept all day and was gone all night, but No\u00eblle and the old woman came to love one another very much. They sang beautiful songs together and played many games with people they found in the woods.<br /> <br /> One night, the old woman asked No\u00eblle if she would like to hear music all the time. No\u00eblle, thinking of her mother's promise, said yes, very much. And so, the old woman held her tight, and for a few moments, she saw her parents and they said they loved her very much. As they faded away, and No\u00eblle awoke, they were singing that lullaby. And they have never stopped singing since.<br /> <br /> No\u00eblle hunted alongside the old woman for many years. First they hunted bad men like the ones that came to No\u00eblle's house. Then hunters and hikers and lost travellers. It was easy because if they wanted to, they could make themselves very beautiful and could use their songs to lead the men astray. <br /> <br /> Finally, after many more years, the old woman said she was growing weak and needed to sleep. No\u00eblle, of course, begged her not to, but the woman said she had no choice. So she climbed into the cellar of the tower and went to sleep, leaving No\u00eblle with no one for company, except the lullaby she always hears.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, No\u00eblle gets lonely in the woods. She sneaks into town and hears little children being told the story of the witches of the woods. It's about an old woman and a little girl who will eat you if you go into the woods. No\u00eblle wishes with all her heart that the story weren't only half-true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:25:01-07:00","id":977968,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>#65</b> When you're the prince of the domain, it pays to have some informants who aren't quite as, shall we say... mercenary... as the Nosferatu. It's not a terribly well guarded secret that the Haunt's only true loyalty is to the clan itself, and that kind of neutrality can be dangerous if left unsupervised. But who would possibly be crazy enough to run surveillance on the masters of subterfuge?<br /> <br /> Madeleine Harrer, that's who! Despite her prestige of being one of the more high functioning Malkavians of the city, she still suffers from intense paranoid delusions that drive her to obsessively keep tabs on her associates. Fortunately, the prince has manipulated her to spying primarily on the Nosferatu, promising that no harm will come to her so long as she is operating under his orders. Of course, she still needs to be discreet about her activities, or the Nosferatu will feed her misinformation at best. Worst case scenario is they retaliate against the Prince, who will likely throw Madeleine under the bus to appease them.<br /> <br /> As a paranoid schizophrenic, Madeleine's security measures are beyond excessive. Her own haven is wired with explosives while she spends the day inside a reinforced bomb shelter with its own escape route! Her files are triple encrypted and she has no less than seven computers with seven IP addresses that she cycles through every night. Two of her computers are just decoys filled almost to capacity with German pornos. Combining this with the fact she sleeps with a butcher knife in one hand and an uzi in the other means that nobody is getting access to her information without the fight of their lives!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-28-2016, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:47:50-07:00","id":978681,"title":"","content":"Here's another NPC from my TC game, which I just introduced during the last game session:<br /> <br /> Klauss Gottfried von Schaffhausen, childe of Malgorzata, Tremere conspirator envoy; embraced 1111 AD (intentionally; stupid Hermetic numerology)<br /> <br /> While most Tremere busy themselves waging the Omen War directly, or indirectly via outreach to other clans and playing prestation, Klauss Gottfried von Schaffhausen has methods and intent entirely his own. As childe of Malgorzata and member of Goratrix's conspirator faction, while his efforts benefit the Tremere as a whole, Klauss ensures the favor, influence, and boons he gains go to furthering his sire's and grandsire's interests in Hungary first and foremost. However, his methods and expertise are founded solely within the realm of <i>logistics</i>, an art largely lost since the fall of the Roman Empire, and in increasingly higher demand as the War of Princes looms.<br /> <br /> As a thaumaturge, he has mastered <i>Transitus Velociter</i>, and has secondary expertise in the newly-adapted Path of Mercury, as well as in Weather Control. He commands significant allies, contacts, merchant influence, as well as a spy network made of those very same merchants, caravans, and guides, as well as having a strong working knowledge of not just trade routes but back roads and hidden passageways that allow he and his companions to travel with a minimum of risk from lupines, hunters, bandits, and marauding Cainites. He busies himself as a courier and merchant guide, to see messages between cities carried, and other, more prominent, Cainites' pawns escorted safely.<br /> <br /> Klauss has no taste for, nor skill in, battle, and at first hint of trouble he will teleport away, care of his own knowledge of Path of Mercury, or by using Escape to a True Friend in the direst of emergencies. This has been of use to House Tremere on more than one occasion, as while neonate Tremere may fall to Tzimisce fangs, word of the attack and the best-possible measures for reprisal never fail to reach elders' ears. Luckily for Klauss, this fate has yet to befall customers outside the clan, but should it his prestige and influence will fall greatly, as he would be considered at best an untrustworthy guide, and at worst a coward and oathbreaker (not that either are necessarily false).<br /> <br /> Of late, he aided a group of Cainites contracted by Vencel Rikard to build a keep in Tihuta Pass to travel from Budapest to Mediasch well ahead of schedule. Choosing for his own reasons to meet with the Prince, Nova Arpad, later, he notices her unusual behavior and seeks to investigate. He will play a role in the rescue of the real Nova Arpad and ouster of her imposter, Ruxandra, and will secure a place for himself among the ruling coterie of Balgrad, which he will exploit to establish a chantry in the city in the dawning years of the 13th Century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-29-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T21:39:29-07:00","id":978847,"title":"","content":"<b>#67</b> Muffled dialect and hazy images are the only clues Slate has about his past since the five years he was embraced. The last memory he has before rising from the dead includes horrified screaming, and that's not much of a surprise. Slate is a Gargoyle, a free Gargoyle who was naturally embraced, not the byproduct of some Tremere's magical experiment. His sire made sure to instill one vital lesson into him early on; do not trust the Tremere, ever!<br /> <br /> The Tremere wanted to shackle him, leash him, compel him, enslave him, command him, enthrall him, break him... destroy him! The Tremere were slave masters who eyed his kind with greedy ambition. Slate would not allow himself to fall under their spell, he would fight to the death, rather than be caged. And so with his sire's guidance, he joined the Anarchs, a collection of like minded kindred who seemed to hate the idea of slavery just as much as him, possibly even more so!<br /> <br /> As a certified amnesiac, Slate is the nickname given to him by his Anarch brethren, and references the stony appearance commonly associated with Gargoyles. Piecing together the memories of his past is one of his constant goals. During the last five years, Slate has made it his mission to recover his memory and learn about the man he used to be. But it's only been five years since that night, and he doesn't even know where to begin looking for answers. Regardless, he is convinced that a vigilant search will begin to reveal clues about his past.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Role Playing:</b> As a Gargoyle, Slate has the potential to bring some dry humor to the table. The mental image of a statuesque monster barely fitting into the back seat of a car while two other vampires are scrunched against the windows is sure to entertain players, as is his <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drax_the_Destroyer\" target=\"_blank\">D</a>rax the Destroyer </i>style way of delivering unintended jokes. While his desire to find out about his past gives Slate something more to focus on than being the token bruiser of the group. Even better is if the ST decides to use his curiosity to lead him (and his coterie) into danger!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-20-2018, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T18:53:51-07:00","id":983067,"title":"","content":"<b>#68 A Bastet who was embraced by a Lamia but doesn't tell her sire until she has no choice but to.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12444-conaire","name":"Conaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T21:24:32-07:00","id":1078169,"title":"","content":"69) Take the Entrepreneur template in the Revised Followers of Set Clanbook and have it that he was found and taken in by the local Tremere Prince. In return for letting the Setite live, all he has to do is be the prince's personal toady and teach him/her how to use Serpentis. The truth is that he's fine with it since he knows he'll need all the protection he can get (what he's learned about his clan scares him).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T12:33:11-07:00","id":1092913,"title":"","content":"70) When Timothy was embraced and turned into a Gargoyle, his parents and two sisters had witnessed it. For the last two years they tried to track him down and when they finally found him, they were dismayed to discover that he lost him memories as a human. No matter what, he is still Timothy to them and even if his memory is gone, they are more than willing to make new ones with him. (His youngest sister admits she likes this new Timothy more since he was a bit of a dick in his Mortal days.) The family resides in Anarch territory (which Timothy is part of) and they provide him with a haven in their basement and let him feed on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T17:21:12-07:00","id":1093033,"title":"","content":"<b>71)</b> Every child inevitably goes through that angsty rebellious phase at some point in their life. They refuse to listen to anybody, because they think they've got the world figured out. For most people, this is simply a phase they grow out of, but others insist on clinging to their bitterness towards the world. So it was that the young and petulant Caleb Booth found himself a willing convert to the Baali. Originally embraced into the Bruja, Caleb's rebellious streak went beyond the standard hot bloodedness of the rest of the clan and bordered somewhere along the lines of asinine childishness and self destructive anger. Instead of the hardened biker gang banging style, he went with the more gothic demon worshiping outlook. At first, it was all bullshit, reciting false prayers and improvised rituals he found in a novelty bookshop. Caleb had no idea that somebody was watching him night after night. Eventually his own sire got sick of his shit and decided to cut him loose, leaving Caleb to bring about his own downfall, which is when Caleb's secret admirer decided to reveal herself to him. A few honeyed words and some revealed skin and Caleb was practically floating out the door with her in the lead.<br /> <br /> She took him to the beach, to an inflatable life boat and told him to get in. When he did, she began to row them out to sea; neither one of them were seen again until the following night, at which point Caleb seemed a lot more focused than before.<br /> <br /> <br /> Before his transformation into a Baali, Caleb already made an ass of himself when it came to demon worship and pagan rituals. Most people are used to it by now, so the occasional demonic activity doesn't draw as much attention as it perhaps should have when he's involved in the picture. Caleb has proven uncharacteristically skilled at using this to his advantage. He can act with more freedom than other infernalists; but even he is cautious about pushing his luck. He's only just started learning the powers his new existence grants him and revealing his cards too early would prove disastrous to say the least. Thankfully, he's got a smoking hot teacher to show him the do's and don't's of being the most hated clan / bloodline in kindred society!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:33:43-07:00","id":1094147,"title":"","content":"A few I recently wrote out for a similar topic on another forum:<br /> <br /> <b>72) Wake-Up Man</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">An archaeologist that didn't learn the meaning of those shadowy late night consulting jobs until he was embraced into Clan Nosferatu. Often enough he was better at figuring out what happened in the past than those that were actually around at the time. With the help of his Clan's information network this allows him to perform a unique function in Kindred society. For a price he tracks down the whereabouts of vampires lost to torpor.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>73) Serpent in Muslimah's Clothing</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Her years as a mortal Setite cultist had left her with some practical problems. The same devotion that eventually earned her the embrace made it very difficult to function in polite society anymore. With tattoos everywhere from her shaved head to her feet, covering up was the only option. Since she's become one of the most pious appearing members of the local Muslim community. Actually trying to undermine it at every turn, dodging True Faith keeps her pretty busy though.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>74) Camarilla Shovelhead</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">He's the lone survivor of a failed Sabbat raid. By the time he emerged from the earth the fighting had already ended. The only reason he wasn't executed on the spot was a familiar face. His uncle, who he had believed to be long dead was a Kindred with just enough clout to save his unlife. It's now up to him to make the best of it as a Lasombra Antitribu. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b>75) Rebel Economist</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A Ventrue chose a brilliant economy student for the embrace. Not the sure way to make a new fortune that he hoped for. The Childe in question had Marxist ideals that are quite incompatible with proper Camarilla society. He's in fact now secretly looking to bring the local Kindred business interests crumbling down. And simultaneously he hopes to instigate an Anarch takeover.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>76) Vengeful Widow</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As a young woman her parents coerced her into a marriage with a man of wealth. He turned out to be a horrible husband. One day she just snapped and killed him. The police couldn't prove anything, but unfortunately for her a Nosferatu wasn't going to let this slide. He was her late husband's distant ancestor, guiding his family to prosperity over the generations. Her having killed his favorite living relative, mucking up all his plans, he gave her the worst punishment he could think of; the Nosferatu embrace. Horrific as this may be, it hasn't cowed the woman. She is still not one to keep tolerating abuse, murder plans are in the works again.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T13:56:06-07:00","id":1102349,"title":"","content":"#77: Orson Pratt was brilliant, talented and gifted. Everyone said so. His parents, Clem and LaDeane Pratt, realized as an infant he would babble along in tune to the radio. His seven brothers and sisters would put on a show every Christmas, and when Orson was three he played a flawless &quot;Gloria In Excelsis Deo&quot; on the family's electric keyboard. Each Monday, when Clem and LaDeane would turn off the television and declare a &quot;Family Home Evening&quot;, the family would gather to play board games, read stories aloud, and sing along to Orson's playing the keyboard, from a songbook Grandma Young had given him for his birthday. When he was five he climbed up on the piano stool in the church social hall, and flawlessly played back, by ear, that morning's hymn, &quot;As Zion's Youth in Latter Days&quot;.<br /> <br /> As soon as the ward choir director heard him play, he was entered into a musical kindergarten program run by the Salt Lake City School District. Orson excelled, and the ward's bishop led a fundraising appeal to pay for a special piano tutor, pointing out to the congregation that music was clearly Orson's special gift. The tutor, a music professor at BYU, and Orson met five nights a week, using the piano in the ward social hall. In seventh grade, Orson was playing well enough to win first prize at the Utah Symphony Orchestra's Lyceum Music Festival, entering an original composition.<br /> <br /> Orson was, frankly, bewildered why everyone made such a stir over his music. It's not like it was hard for him. He just sat at the piano, and his fingers did the rest. The pieces he wrote weren't so much a labor of creation, rather more like remembering something from long ago, and then writing it down. To be honest, he would rather do something actually challenging. Once a month, his dad would take all the brothers up to Bear Lake, where Uncle Nephi and Aunt Odonna lived. Dad would load up the passenger van on Friday afternoon, and they would drive until night-time. The next morning, before dawn, all the guys would spread out along the lake and just fish. Breathing the thin, cool air of the high desert, as the morning insects buzzed and landed along the rocky shore, like a mirage on some alien desert, planet. Orson let his mind wander, pretending he was fishing on Tattooine or Dune. The swaying of the lake surface, shaded by the long dark reaches of the circling mountains silhouetted by the rising dawn would lead Orson to a deeper music, an older music. This music was like the vibration in the ground during a thunderstorm or the cramping of your stomach when you were sick. It was the natural music, the music of the flesh and leaf and antler and fin. A music too pagan for his family to hear or understand.<br /> <br /> Those trips to Bear Lake were what Orson missed most when he went on his mission to Madagascar. Oh, he enjoyed serving the church, and he really loved hearing Malagasy music, like polyphonic a capella, tsapika, and jejy voatavo. This was music which understood the music of Bear Lake better than any Utah hymnal ever could. When he returned and went to Julliard, he worked to fuse Malagasy music and other world music traditions with the vernacular music of rural North America. Oh, he played proper, classical piano impeccably, his hands wide, sinewy and precise, like soaring birds, but firm and insistent as a flash flood in a desert gully. He mastered Tchaikovsky's Violin Concerto in D Major and the Ligeti Etudes, but his heart was always in the simple and direct, but never simplistic or reductionist traditional music of the developing world.<br /> <br /> Orson entered the MFA program in Musical Composition at Carnegie Mellon in Pittsburgh. His senior piece was a full orchestral symphony which blended traditional American church hymns with the vibrant and often plaintive sounds of Malagasy music. When it officially debuted, played by the Boston Symphony at Tanglewood, NPR called Orson, &quot;one of America's most creative and fearless young composers. At turns sullen and vibrant, sadistically fast and lusciously maestoso. He is THE new voice to be followed. Expect to hear much more from him!&quot;<br /> <br /> Two weeks later, as Orson was driving back to Pittsburgh from Massachusetts, he was embraced by a Toreador fan. They faked his death in a traffic crash, but Orson was not sure if that was a lie. He had lost so much, for an art that mattered so little to him. Sure, he was gifted at music, but so what? Had he been gifted with a wrench, he would have been a plumber. It was, for Orson, just a job. Now, it was a job he was expected to never, ever retire from. And the rest of his clan? Gol, they were a mixed up bunch! Always going on about how decadent they were, but really they were just sad, having lost their free agency to the blood at the embrace. He was toasted as a prodigy by his peers and elders alike, but was simultaneously revolted by them and pitied them. He survived on animal blood as best he could, but knew he had to find a better environment if he was to preserve his humanity and his morality.<br /> <br /> Orson fled his sire, but didn't know where to go. He tried Utah, but to his great horror, vampires don't fare well in the shadow of faith cast by Temple Square. He suffered constant day-mares of being cast into the outer darkness whenever he closed his eyes. His apartment in Pittsburgh had been packed up by his parents. Madagascar? He loved that place, and maybe someday... but, the logistics were beyond him. So, for tonight, he just kept driving.<br /> <br /> He travels the country, mostly the western US and Canadian Rockies, in a light-proofed, white panel van. He pulls in at National Parks and roadside fishing camps for a few weeks at a time. He has met several Gangrel on the road who marvel that he has never run into a Lupine. But, then, maybe he has and didn't know it. His missionary training taught how to keep an upbeat attitude and a ready smile for anyone he met, and how to maneuver out of dangerous spots when necessary. The Gangrel just sigh deeply, shake his hand, and say it was nice meeting him.<br /> <br /> He doesn't get why they seem so worried. So what if there are werewolves; he's a vampire, right? So, he plans to just fish the most beautiful lakes and streams he can find for however long Heavenly Father sees fit to keep him here for his (im)Mortal Probation. If he has to die the final death, he'd like it to happen doing what he loves: in rubber waders, waist deep in the cold, deep water of a mountain lake, swinging a hand-tied lure over his head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T22:15:29-07:00","id":1103723,"title":"","content":"#78. A Salubri Warrior running a cult under the guise of a civil rights group. has learned a little bit of obfuscate and presence to pull it all together. has personally ghouled many of the towns authority figures and has all but in name claimed ownership of their home city","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T13:34:03-07:00","id":1122460,"title":"","content":"79) There are whispers of the mysterious Assamite called, &quot;The White Shadow&quot;. There are horror stories of kindred who have witnessed a blur of white emerge from the shadows before someone's life is ended. Some say The White Shadow will chop the victim's limbs off first, others say that its very touch drains them until they're a withering husk or that it used the powers from a diablorized Lasombra to break every bone in their body, but its methods are rarely the same for any long period of time. The only thing that is for sure is that it uses its clothing and title to strike fear and gain recognition for itself.<br /> <br /> If any of them were lucky enough to pull back the veil it wears, they will see that this 5th generation Vampire is not what they'd expect. After all, who would think that the Assamites would embrace an 11-year-old, tomboyish white girl with blond hair and blue eyes? Or believe that the fanatical White Shadow was embraced in 1970.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:52:07-07:00","id":1125363,"title":"","content":"<u><b>#80 </b></u><br /> <br /> Every night, little Denni Lou Jackson snuck out of her bedroom and climbed the tomato trellis up onto the shed roof behind her house down a little dirt road in Manning, SC. She would just lay up there, with her stuffed panda bear, Mr. Pibbles, asking him questions about the sky. Why are some stars kinda reddish? Why is that part of the sky lighter? How high can the birds fly? To the moon? She would drift off to sleep, paying no mind at all to the mosquitoes or her hard, corrugated-metal bed.<br /> <br /> Then the town siren would sound which meant everybody had to go inside, or at least be back on their own side of town. Denise's Mama usually waited until then to carry her off to bed. Mama would pretend to be annoyed at having to climb up there every night, but, honestly, with five kids and a long day of raising other people's kids, she was not about to complain about her quiet little four-year-old angel. Denni Lou may be peculiar, but at least she was peculiar in a way that made life a little easier.<br /> <br /> Denise did so well at school, her Baptist church raised money to send her off to a Catholic school in Orangeburg, near where her grandmother's people were from. She lived with aunts and uncles and no one minded, because she was polite, dutiful, smart as a whip (especially at math), always did her chores, and followed all their house rules... except one. Every night (if the sky was clear), there she'd be staring up, into the heavens.<br /> <br /> Denise graduated from high school at 17, and took some classes at South Carolina State, fulfilling all the distribution credits for math and science majors in one year, but couldn't afford to continue.<br /> <br /> She figured, with the federal government and LBJ pushing through civil rights legislation, the military would be a good plan for a black girl who already knew more math than most of her professors. She joined the US Air Force at 18, and excelled, as usual, despite the childish antics and hazing of many of the men. She made officer in 1970, but knew she could only go so far. Women weren't allowed to fly (or even serve) in combat, and she was more interested in the engineering side of things anyway. The USAF paid for her dual undergraduate degree in aerospace engineering and physics, with honors, from Stanford. Then it was back south to Georgia Tech for a Master's in Aerospace Engineering. She did her doctorate work in Monterey, CA, at the Naval Post-Graduate School, studying the mathematics of fluid dynamics in high temperature aerospace applications. All the while, she worked on engineering the next generation of jet fighters, whatever the next generation was that year.<br /> <br /> And, wherever she was stationed, every single night, she took a few minutes to stare up at the stars in wide wonder.<br /> <br /> She was eventually posted to a teaching position at Annapolis, from which she retired to civilian life in 1990. Her military pension allowed her to pursue her original passion: astronomy. She moved to Princeton, teaching calculus and engineering to undergrads while earning a second Master's in Astronomy, with a focus on what most of her colleagues thought was a crackpot field: exoplanetology.<br /> <br /> Denise didn't care what they thought, even when they would leave little Marvin the Martian toys and little-green-men stickers in her office mail box. She knew there must be other planets out there, after all, we've got nine. And she was fixing to find one. All it would take would be one jump in the radial red shift, one tug on the path of a star, just one unexplained sine wave in the chromatophotography, and she would have found a whole new world!<br /> <br /> Funding was hard to come by, so astronomers would send her their old data from other projects, and she would analyze it looking for anomalies.<br /> <br /> She found nothing.<br /> <br /> It was about this time she met Hans at the Midway Diner. He was a lawyer from Philly, and seemed to like her, but never actually flirted. They would sit every Friday night, talking for hours. About this and that, sometimes science, sometimes law, sometimes, they would just sit. Just spending time with him made her feel younger, like she would forever be on the healthy and spry cusp of sixty.<br /> <br /> This continued for years. Hans exulted with her when the data on 51 Pegasi B passed peer review. With the Hubble Telescope, whose propulsion controls she had troubleshooted, there was a cascade of new planets. A hundred. A thousand. Two thousand. Soon, four thousand would be in sight, in the one little patch of sky Hubble examined.<br /> <br /> When 451b, an Earth-like rocky planet in a habitable zone was certified, she was jubilant, and Hans was jubilant for her. Oh, he didn't understand the math, of course, but then she was vague on his legal theories. She had long resigned herself to their relationship being intellectually stimulating, if platonic. He seemed to genuinely come alive each night as they sat, talking in that diner. She had noticed years ago that he never ate, and had no reflection. But, he really seemed to understand her bittersweet joy at knowing... really knowing... that there were whole new worlds to explore, even if she would never live long enough to explore them.<br /> <br /> She knew he was older than he looked, but not how old until he told her the story of riding the prow of a ship at night. A ship captained by Ponce de Leon. Hearing breakers ahead, Hans saw the fires of the natives on the shoreline. He was there, in 1513, when Europeans first set foot on Florida. In a way, it was a whole new world... well, new to the Europeans, anyway. So, he understood what it was to search the abyss for a single point of light in the distance.<br /> <br /> Hours ago, she explained about the discovery of the Trappist-1 system. Seven Earth-like planets in the habitable zone! And, now, as she pulls herself up out of her shallow grave, she looks up at the stars and cries bloody tears of joy... 100 billion stars in the Milky Way alone... multiply that by ten trillion galaxies. Out there, looking back from the vast black void of the universe even the Antedeluvians must seem as small and insubstantial as neutrinos. Somebody has to be the first vampire to set foot on a new world, and see from that perspective.<br /> <br /> And that vampire will be a Lasombra. You can bet on it, or her name isn't Dr. Denise Louise Jackson; BA, BEng, MS, MEng, PhD, Capt. USAF ret.<br /> <br /> She's come a long, long way from that little dirt road with the segregation siren in Manning, SC, and she's got a helluva lot further to go!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T11:06:31-07:00","id":1125647,"title":"","content":"81) A newly embraced Tzimisc<i>e</i> has her infamous sire killed by the Camarilla before she could be sent to be buried and is brought in just to piss off the Sabbat. To rub the salt into the wound, they give her a mentor with high humanity, creating a humane and proud of it Fiend who uses her Vissicitude to help others. If the local prince and primogen could see how her grandsire frenzied at the discovery of his &quot;brainwashed&quot; grandchilde, they'd know they did the right thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T02:27:12-07:00","id":1138255,"title":"","content":"Dark Age characters :<br /> 82) Your great-grand mother was Saulot's childer. No, she isn't you great-grand sire! She is your human ancestor, a rare case of vampire-turned-human-again after she reached Golconda. Now you have a bunch of Salubri descended from her who believes that the sacred blood of Saulot runs into your veins and, well... now that he's dead, the value of said blood just sky rocketed.<br /> <br /> 83) Your Salubri Sire became human again and had children of her own. Now, you must protect them at all cost. The problem is that the one you are supposed to protect right now is a young, capricious noble human who fed on two much Amour Courtois and refuses to follow your kindly advices to stay safe and away from other Kindreds. You cannot goul or dominate her without comitting a serious sin against Saulot (or least, that's what you believe) and you are starting to believe that she may have a crush on you.<br /> <br /> 84) You are 82)'s bastard brother and the creepy salubri warrior who tries to babysit her doesn't know yet. You are still wondering if telling him would be a good idea or if there is still time to run away.<br /> <br /> Not-Dark Age character, but still a Salubri :<br /> 85) You don't know why, but one day, you just phased out and woke up in Ceoris with Etrius asking you why the fuck you walked into a Chantry <i>asking to see your father</i>. You spent a lot of time in torpor or as a subject to his experiments these past centuries, so your memories are a bit fuzzy, but you are now sure of one thing : Saulot wants to destroy the Salubri, and the only hope you have is for Tremere to save you. No one will convince you that you have been brainwashed or whatever, you are now the leader of your own small cult of Tremere-loving Salubri who believe Tremere will save the world from Gehenna by eating all the Antediluvians. Of course, Etrius is the only one who knows you and your group exist and had to seal your third eye to keep Saulot from seeing through you, and you may have to hunt the &quot;agents&quot; of your &quot;evil ancestor&quot;, but that's all for the greater good, isn't it?<br /> <br /> Dark Age character but not a Salubri :<br /> 86) You were a Saxon pagan back when Charlemagne decided it was out of fashion. You went south to witness his coronation and decided to have fun desecrating the tomb of a saint on your way... only to find that the saint was there. And pretty. Very pretty. You fell in love and decided to do everything in your power to have your very own love story with her. Some Ventrue lord linked with Charlemagne like that in you, and now, you are trying to climb the ladder in order to, <i>somenight</i>, be worthy of waking up your torpid beauty.<br /> <br /> 87) You were a monk and a most holy man with true Faith when someone murdered you. Luckly for you, a Brujah Embraced you as a &quot;reward&quot; for you unwavering faith and morality, arguing that your death would have been wasteful. Since then, you are doing everything in you power to be the perfect exemple that vampires are not damned. You only consume blood fort consenting and aware donors, you never use disciplines, in fact you DON'T have any discipline dot, have maxed all your virtues and willpower, preach for kindness, charity and forgiveness, and <i>know </i>that one day the power of Jesus Christ will turn you back into a human. The fact that a young lasombra priest is trying to persuade you of the contrary will not make you change your mind !<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T04:04:53-07:00","id":1138267,"title":"","content":"<b>88) Tremere musician without talent</b><br /> A young talented jazz musician is Embraced by his grandfather (who also was a musician in life), the regent of an unimportant Tremere chantry. Turns out the young musician is utterly lacking of any magical talent, meaning he has great difficulties at learning even the basic rudiments of Thaumaturgy. This is cause of great embarassment for his grandfather/sire amongst his clanmates. To make matters worse the fledgling has a frustrated and dickish personality, with self-destructive tendencies that drive him towards breaking the Masquerade...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T10:04:52-07:00","id":1138346,"title":"","content":"89. <b>The Feline Ventrue</b> (Optimist/Architect) She always felt a sense of <i>nobless oblige</i>, an abolitionist from a wealthy in the antebellum South (not unlike Mary Todd Lincoln) who firmly supported the Union. For this reason she impressed a rebellious Anarch who embraced her. What he did not realize was that she was Bastet Kinfolk, and the nature of her taste became to drink only from felines. Yet upon learning her heritage, she made an alliance with a certain group of the shape-shifters. In her Southern city, she would protect &quot;her&quot; people and their allies from other Kindred. In return they would give her some of their blood as tribute. In fact she's a charming, rather high-Humanity person rigidly true to her word but time is wearing away at her optimism and conscience. She can feel herself changing, very slowly, and intends to set up some method of countering herself should she lose her battle with the Beast. Yet at the same time she has plans to take the throne and reimagine her home city as an oasis of human dignity and peace. The fact she has fallen in love with one specific Bastet, who is now aging, both helps her preserve her Humanity while whittling away at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=David%20MacDowell%20Blue\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller Vault</a> </b>supplements. <img src=\"images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16204-davidmacdowellblue","name":"DavidMacDowellBlue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T04:21:11-07:00","id":1139142,"title":"","content":"<b>90) Sane Malkavian Primogen</b><br /> The Malkavian Primogen apparently is perfectly sane. No detectable derangements. He's a capable player of the city's web of intrigues and power struggles. He dismesses the Malkavian clan curse as an urban legend. He says he is not more mad than any other vampire he met. Many Kindred believe is not really a Malkavian, but he's credited as being the childe of a well known Malkavian elder and so there is doubt. He receives many phone calls and letters from a mysterious figure. From the looks of it the Primogen is a tool in a Methuselah Jyhad, and the player characters can learn about it. But plot twist: the old phone's cable is cut, and the paper of the letters is actually empty. The Primogen just imagines of being manipulated by ancient vampires. He's delusional about being a doomed tool in the legendary Jyhad. That's his Malkavian derangement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T05:30:01-07:00","id":1139150,"title":"","content":"<b>91) Those two Brujah you really don't want to meet (Dark Age)</b><br /> Coriolanus was embraced during the 5th century BC, a 6th gen vampire. A Roman general, he hated the Plebs and was ultimatly ousted by his own people. He turned against Rome, then decided against it when his mother convinced him to spare the city. He was then Embraced by a Brujah who felt that some good roman-hating guy could be handy. Coriolanus has since then been obsessed by betrayal; betrayal by your troops, your allies, your fellow officiers or your Lord. At the end of the 8th century, he embraced a young lord who was &quot;betrayed&quot; as well, Roland de Roncevaux, who would later inspire the Song of Roland and become a symbol of bravery.<br /> <br /> By the time of the game, however, Roland isn't exactly the hero of the song. Well, he never was this guy to begin with, but it's now blatantly obvious. Coriolanus has been at low humanity for centuries and Roland is now dangerously close to the beast. Both of them are too bitter and dangerous to be accepted anywhere, and both are ready to do anything to satisfy their fancy of the moment. They are dirty, they sleep in the ground, and Roland will feed on anything or anyone, and stop only when his sire commands him to stop his glutony. Coriolanus will frenzy at the first show of disrespect, and if you happen to own a red cloak, he will bully you until he can get it, like a sorry reminded that he was once Roman.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you met them my mistake. You were on this road, and they were on this road, and something must go wrong since one of them is a bitter, angry beast and the other one wants to eat everyone he sees. Perhaps one of your enemy promised to give Coriolanus a shiny, sadistic trinket to convince him to kick your ass. Or perhaps the enemy you killed was supposed to make a shiny trinket for him and now, he is anry at you because he won't get it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you have been betrayed, and that makes you Coriolanus's friend - a mixed blessing at best, since he is persona non grata with basically every other kindred.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you know of a way to save someone from the Beast. This may the only way to truly get to him; as degenerate as he is, Coriolanus would to everything to save his Childer.<br /> <br /> <b>92) The Tremere Caitiff</b><br /> You were a Chantry's regent faithful ghoul; not only faithful but useful, clever, agressive and brilliant. The Regent believed you were very promising, so on the day he was named Lord, he decided to Embrace you.<br /> <br /> But things didn't go as planned. You are immune to blood bonds and the Transubstantiation failed. Your Sire could not bind you, and if he could not bind you, then he had to destroy you. Yet he didn't; for decades you served him and House Tremere. In his eyes, you are <i>faithful </i>to the House, and an asset that doesn't have to be destroyed.<br /> <br /> Your hopes have been destroyed. You are alive, still serving your Sire, and he protects you, but you will never belong to the House. You will never have access to Thaumaturgy and you will never climb the Pyramid, and if anyone knows who is your sire... you may both die from this.<br /> <br /> <b>93) A Ventrue with a taste for Brujah</b><br /> You were a loyal, young Child of Hardestadt - that is, until he sacrificed you to the Inquisition to protect himself. You were bound to the stake and the sun was rising when you were unexpectedly saved by two Kindred. They slaughetered the churchmen and managed to hide with you and, as soon as the sun was down, you fled the city.<br /> <br /> One of them was very disappointed to discover you were a Ventrue. He was a Brujah anarch, and not very fond of your clan, but the other one had always wanted a Childe and apparently that was to be you. You have a very strict tastes, and can only feed from human and vampires of noble blood. Being on the run with tastes like that is hard; but lucky you, your two Brujah friends were noble-born, and you can find your preys by smell alone.<br /> <br /> By the end of the Anarch Revolt, the three of you were blood-bond to death, and you took a liking to Brujah blood. You like to feel the rage burn in your veins. You are still angry that Hardestadt betrayed you, and the Brujah rage is helping you keep that anger alive. Year after year, decade after decade, you gave everything to the Sabbat, not because you believe in everything the Sabbat says about the Antediluvians (that would be your Brujah pack mate), not because you despise the Camarilla (that would be your Brujah &quot;sire&quot;, who never joined the Sabbat and is still Anarch), but because <i>one day Hardestadt will burn</i>. Until then, well... that Brujah neonate just there really does seem super tasty, doesn't she?<br /> <br /> <b>94) False Ventrue, True Brother</b><br /> You were Embraced during WW2 because you have a twin brother. You two were always very close and your sire believed you two would make an interesting team. But the thing is: you aren't a Ventrue. You never developped the specific tastes and your Sire noticed.<br /> <br /> But you were lucky! Your Sire died in the last days of the war! Now no one will know, because you like... blonds. That's it, you feed from blonds, and no one will ever know you aren't a true Ventrue, and you and your brother will be safe.<br /> <br /> What you don't know is that your brother killed your Sire to protect you. What you don't know is that you aren't a Caitiff; you are a Malkavian, born of the vampire you Sire ate a few weeks before he made you. What you don't know is that your bond with your brother is far too strong. At first he was just &quot;you&quot; during the day, but for you, you are him and he is you; should he die, you will as well, and you are as &quot;blood-bonded&quot; to him as he is to you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T07:50:00-07:00","id":1139191,"title":"","content":"<b>95) Anark, True Climber of the Pyramid</b><br /> <br /> Once you were a powerful pontifex, one of the first Tremere and a 5th generation vampire. You ruled over Lords and Regents and Transilvania chantries were your domain. Then you fucked up. Etrius saw you as a rival and as a possible ally to Goratrix. His schemes got you a letter. You were called to a reunion with your elders to respond for a crime you did not commit. You didn\u00b4t understand but you were not a coward. Stoically, you traveled to your doom and were judged by the Inner Council of the Seven. Etrius wanted you dead but your past merits convinced the rest of the council otherwise.<br /> <br /> You were punished by the Ritual of Quenching the Lambent Flame which turned you into a 13th generation vampire. You were ordered to return to Ceoris were the mock continued. Your new &quot;status&quot; was a permanent job as &quot;The Guardian of the Gate&quot;, a mere sentry to announce newcomers to Ceoris. This position was reserved in the past for the lowest of the acolytes but you swallowed your anger and served the House as well as you could. You knew your time would come. Almost a century passed but finally Ceoris was under a new Regent and in dire need of powerful magi.<br /> <br /> The permanent attacks from Tzimisce and Assamite were the perfect opportunity. First as a battle mage at the frontlines and later as a leader of a small group you climbed again up the Pyramid showing the great abilities that turned you into a Pontifex the first place. You made clear your opposition to Goratrix when he defected the clan and you even hunted down some antitribu. It took centuries but you were again a Pontifex and a 5th generation tremere. Etrius thought he was wrong about you in the past and sure that you didn\u00b4t know who was the one which bring you down in the first place. So the Inner Circle left you on your way.<br /> <br /> But he is so wrong. You know it was his fault. His arrogance has made him forget that he sought your doom once but you are not going to fail to remember it. Your path is clear, now that you are in a position of power you will plan the fall of Etrius and all of his lineage. You will not attack directly. You are weaving a web and your enemies will be soon entangled in it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16177-zacharias-the-everliving","user":"Zacharias the Everliving","date":". 09-10-2017, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16177-zacharias-the-everliving","name":"Zacharias the Everliving","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16177_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T10:48:23-07:00","id":1143509,"title":"","content":"<b>96. The Tresombra </b><br /> Your &quot;sire&quot; is a high ranking membre of House Tremere, a Lord who got his rank due to his rare knowledge in Obtenebration and his work on Abyss mysticism. Isn't it nice to have such a prestigious Sire ?<br /> Only you sire <i>isn't</i> your sire. The truth is that you are a Lasombra by blood ; your reflection is a thaumaturgical construct by your &quot;Sire&quot; and you have been thoroughly dominated into believing your are his. Now the question is: why is he going through so much trouble to keep you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16128,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","user":"Kalendeer","date":". 09-29-2017, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16128-kalendeer","name":"Kalendeer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T16:22:24-07:00","id":1143619,"title":"","content":"97) A Giovanni with an impressionable streak had seen Flatliners and actually thinks this could work (the characters didn't have her clan's powers to do it right). So she's going to try her own version with some family Ghouls, outcast Caitiff and later herself...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T20:08:37-07:00","id":1152097,"title":"","content":"98) The Lore of the Bloodlines showed that the Kiasyd have a talent for making special mixed drinks. This one has found you can do the same hallucinogenic substances. Peyote fed with Changeling and Mage tears, snortable powder that has ground-up Malkavian bones in it, herbs grown in an umbral realm (he's got a Sorcerer to handle that), etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T04:10:55-07:00","id":1152754,"title":"","content":"99) Jonathan von Eisenberg<br /> <br /> Born in to a medium sized noble Prussian family way past its prime. You studied your families history and it had the perfect opportunity to become a major house in Prussian when they gained the rights to an iron mine some 220 years ago. But since then? No minor skirmishes, no duels out of honour, no ambitious marriages... Nothing just content and mediocrity.....you hated it.<br /> Even if you only were the 3rd born son and youngest child, this would not be your fortune. No you aimed higher.<br /> You found your passion in battle and commanding your troops after joining the Prussian military and fighting in the three German Unification wars before leaving the now German military with hounors in 1872. The state pension and your small allowance from your family allowed you to invest in new buisnesses. Initially with no success and even with a complete loss of wealth after a scam, which was initiated by your soon to be sire as a test of character. You learned, imporves and finally were able to succeed. In 1875 you were embraced and joined the ranks of the Ventrue.<br /> At the beginnig your were delighted and proud that you were chosen for your skills. But in the first 30 years you learned the harsh truth. Vampire society is feudalism all over again even harsher since nobody ever dies. For a time you found solice in the battle against the Sabbat and other monsters in the chaos of the Great War and even got some boons and status in- and outside of the Clan. But the strict hierachy was slowly but surely killing you. So you decided to something about it, you wanted more democracy and more rights based on merit instead of age and power.<br /> You started to secretly suppporting the growing anarch movement while keeping a loyalist apperence in the Camarilla. You created a network, where you were able to support them with money and more important information. To your surprise you whole-heartly supported the ideas and ideals of the movement.<br /> The last 80 years you played this dangerous game becoming a diplomat between the old and young in the process but its getting harder to sympathize with the ideals from year to year. For now you fight these thoughts as much as you the Sabbat if they are in town but if you're not careful you will become one of the beasts you loathe and that would be so....well mediocre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T15:48:38-07:00","id":1153821,"title":"","content":"100) <b>Silas Smith - Tremere Enforcer</b><br /> <br /> Description:<br /> Silas is 5'6&quot; and well built. Despite his century of undeath, his many years of riding and working under the Sun has left his skin tanned and with the texture of old leather.<br /> <br /> His body also sports several old scars (bull horn gouge on his lower left calf, knife, arrows and bullet wounds from bandits and indians weapon).<br /> <br /> <br /> Background:<br /> Silas Smith was born in 1809 in Asheville in North Carolina. Growing up he learned how to read, ride a horse/tend to animal and shoot. At the age of 16 he left with Dreams of making in in the West (he had a glorified view of the Colonization) and for about 5 years he worked as a cowboy/ranch hand, then worked a couple year to build the railroad. In 1832 he moved to the Iowa Territory to help remove the Indians/settle the Territory and fown in the Blawk Hawk War.<br /> <br /> In 1834 as he was in Cleveland, drinking in a bar, he got into a nasty barfight, with some pretty mean ruffians after knocking several out, he was himself knocked unconcious.When he work up, he found out that he was buried, after the initial panic, he quickly dug his way out...not realizing he was no longer breathing. He was one of 7 who got out of the ground before sunrise...5 more cooked to death and 1 never came out.<br /> <br /> His pack was composed of him (a Tremere Antitribu), of 2 Country Gangrel, 1 Lasombra, 2 Brujah Antitribu and a Kiasyd. Strangely enough, despite his Clan, he was never inclined towards Thaumaturgy and for several years his pack was pretty much Sabbat enforcers and raiders causing trouble in Camarilla cities as well as back West in the new colonies...several of the reported indians and bear massacres, were really just his pack having a bit of fun.<br /> <br /> in 1902 His pack and 5 others were sent to Chicago to liberate it for the Sabbat. It was a pretty bloody affair that lasted for most of the year, but at the end the Camarilla won and Silas pack was pretty much exterminate -John Cook (the Kiasyd) and himself were the last two survivor, caught by the Tremere for Experimentation (and in my case: Extermination).<br /> <br /> The Tremere were relentless...as they are usually with those of House Goratrix, but Silas will to live was solid and eventually (in 1905) he was send to the Main Chantry in Vienna. There he was interrogated some more and given a choice: Join or meet the Sun...so in 1910 he partook into the Blook of the Seven, becoming a clan member. From 1910 to 1935, he stayed in Vienna, working and protecting it and, at the same time, the Elders were keeping an eye on him for signs of Betrayal. in 1935, he was assign to the Chantry of Five Boroughs in New york, were again he pretty much work more menial work...not that he minded, he was always more agressive and prone to bash skull as oppose to the subtle use of Blood Magic favoured by his Clanmate.<br /> <br /> <br /> - My packmate mostly exterminated during the 1902 failed Chicago raid.<br /> Adam Preston - Lasombra - Pack priest - KIA<br /> Virgil Clark - Brujah Antitribu - Ductus - KIA<br /> John Walker - Brujah Antitribu - KIA<br /> William Johnson - Country Gangrel - KIA<br /> Ezekiel Johnson - Country Gangrel - KIA<br /> John Cook - Kiasyd - Capture/Experimented on - Unknown presumed Dead","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 11-08-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T12:57:00-08:00","id":1156137,"title":"","content":"<b>101)</b> A Malkavian who's multiple personality disorder manifests a psychic link between their IC persona and their OOC player.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8B6ChV7IpkM\" target=\"_blank\">How Not To Malkavian<br /> <br /> R</a><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s0STjReVW3s\" target=\"_blank\">evenge of the Malkavian</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-22-2017, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T15:14:15-08:00","id":1157136,"title":"","content":"102: AnnaMarie Librizzi was born in Sicily in 1899. Her mother was a simple cleaning woman for a rich family who lived in a villa high atop the nearest hill. Her mother was also a not-so-secret secret alcoholic. Their father was nowhere to be found, and her mother could just barely hold herself together enough to get up every morning to go scrub the marble floors of her boss's house. When Mama got home each night, she would retreat to her room and not come out again until the next morning.<br /> <br /> From an early age, AnnaMarie learned that anything she (or her twin brother, Alberto) needed they would need to provide themselves. The rest of the village called them &quot;bastardi&quot;, some of the children threw pebbles at them when they tried to walk the main street, and every few weeks AnnaMarie would have to scrub the word &quot;Puttana&quot; from the front wall of her family's little house. The only comfort they could find was from their Aunt Sofia, who was as poor as they, but did what she could.<br /> <br /> That was, until 1905, when Sofia announced she was moving to America with her new husband. AnnaMarie was heartbroken, but Sofia promised she would write. This only made AnnaMarie cry more, as she could not read. Sofia arranged for a local priest, a cousin of her husband, to help with the letters. (And, unknown to AnnaMarie, to check in on the children regularly.)<br /> <br /> AnnaMarie and Alberto got by the best they could, by the age of seven, they were picking through trash for rags, bones, and old bottles they could sell. She gathered wild herbs, mushrooms and ground bird eggs in the country-side to sell door to door. When they were twelve, Alberto snuck into a train station being built. He just smiled and kept his head down. He swept the floors and carried bricks, one-by-one. By the time any of the men realized he wasn't meant to be there, he had done a full day's work. He was hired on the spot.<br /> <br /> AnnaMarie was heartbroken when Alberto signed up for the army at fifteen. She was terrified to be without him. She was waiting tables at a restaurant, and taking in washing. But without Alberto's income, how could she make do? The day Alberto left, AnnaMarie decided to leave, too.<br /> <br /> She cut her hair short, memorized her Aunt Sofia's address in New York, and put on Alberto's clothes. She signed up with a freighter headed to America, using her brother's name. After months of wandering and diversions, caused mostly by the war, she finally arrived in New York harbor on 24 October, 1918. She jumped ship and swam ashore. It was after midnight when she knocked on her Aunt Sofia's door. Having spent the last of her strength climbing the fifth floor walk-up on Mott Street, AnnaMarie collapsed in the doorway and slept for two straight days.<br /> <br /> When she awoke, Sofia explained she had heard from Sicily. Alberto was missing in action and presumed dead.<br /> <br /> You might expect this is the part of the story where AnnaMarie collapses and wails and... well, she did all that, of course. But, as is the way of things, life went on. She married a man, a good man, Luigi. They started out installing carpets, then opened a little carpet store. There were children, of course. She learned to read from them, really. The Depression was hard, but to AnnaMarie, it felt like winning the lottery after her childhood. They worked long hours, opened seven carpet stores, and raised eleven children. She lost a son to the Japanese in World War II, had twenty-seven grandchildren, and moved to a little house out in Ozone Park, Queens, with a garden and a driveway.<br /> <br /> Luigi was shoveling snow during the Blizzard of 1960 when he died of a heart attack. The next day, she gave all of her clothes to the church, walked into the Gertz's Department Store on Liberty Avenue, and bought an entirely black wardrobe. She never wore any other color for the rest of her life. Other than that, she simply swung into action, organizing the funeral, taking control of the &quot;Happy Lou's Discount Carpet Mart&quot; empire. She expanded the chain from seven stores to twenty-three by 1974, when she finally retired, at the insistence of her children.<br /> <br /> She was in the hospital three months later. The doctor said it was diabetes, asthma, and heart disease, but she knew better. It was boredom and the frustration of having others do for her. She was a tired, sick, bored old woman. She was laying there, in the middle of the night, counting the holes in the ceiling's acoustic tile, when there was a knock at the door.<br /> <br /> She turned, and there stood Alberto. She crossed herself and clenched her chest. He must have been there to escort to heaven. But, if that's it, then why did her chest hurt so badly? And, though he was as handsome as ever, he was wearing modern clothes... corduroy bell bottoms and a cable-knit sweater? Shouldn't he be in his uniform? She tried to scream to make the pain in her chest stop, but couldn't and then there was just darkness.<br /> <br /> She awoke in Alberto's haven. He spent the next few months walking her through a brisk agoge. When the time came for her to choose a feeding preference, Alberto begged her to think broadly. He had ended up only able to feed on veterans of world war one, and times were getting hard. She found her ideal vintage was women with both children and a job. She completed her agoge by researching methods of changing a Ventrue's feeding habit.<br /> <br /> She practiced on her brother, and he now feeds on any veteran. She has traveled the world, and has gained quite the reputation (and a great deal of favors) around the clan for helping those clan-mates who find their tastes exceeding their means.<br /> <br /> She is known professionally by her clanmates as &quot;Nonna Vedova&quot;, and still dresses all in black. She appears to be a frail old woman, with olive skin and shoe-polish black hair, which she swears is not dyed, but is not to be trifled with. Alberto trained her well in martial matters, and she walks with a sword-cane, which no airline attendant would dare to ever take from the old lady on the red-eye flight. She has been using her travels, and her &quot;help with kitchen problems&quot;, to amass piles of favors and bigger piles of secrets about her clanmates.<br /> <br /> AnnaMarie is strongly considering returning to Sicily to establish a small domain. She already knows exactly the house on a hilltop she would like for a haven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T15:15:48-08:00","id":1157370,"title":"","content":"<b>103)</b> To say that Marshal Knight has commitment issues would be an understatement. Since joining clan Malkavian, he has found himself with a compulsive urge to side with the antagonist of any group he's faced with. When surrounded by the Sabbat, he favors Camarilla philosophy. When surrounded by the Camarilla, he favors the Anarchs, and when surrounded by Anarchs, he favors the Sabbat. His stance in such matters changes so fluidly that even Marshal can no longer recognize what he truly believes in anymore. In a desperate attempt to add some form of meaning to his existence, he has taken up the role of an 'agent of chaos'. He takes Malkavian pranking to an art form, in which nothing is considered sacred and all organized factions are a viable target.<br /> <br /> Oh how fun it was detonating that car bomb that took out the prince's newest childe and writing the phrase &quot;Beware the Sword of Caine&quot; in red spray paint at the scene of the wreckage. How widely he smiled when he tipped off the sheriff about the meeting place for a vaulderie he was invited to attend later that night. And how long he giggled to himself when he told a bunch of young Anarchs to meet him there under the pretense of having a late night party. Ultimately, the night concluded with all three groups blaming each other while Marshal sat back and enjoyed the show.<br /> <br /> Most of Marshal's pranks have been designed in such a fashion. The only way he can satisfy that antagonistic urge is to simultaneously piss off as many people at the same time as possible, usually without letting them know that he was behind it. He can't explain his reasons, only that it felt good to stir up chaos among the kindred population. Had he been left to his own devices, Marshal would surely have brought about his own destruction eventually. But there was one group who knew about Marshal's activities and decided he would be a perfect fit for their organization.<br /> <br /> The Followers of Set may not have been a perfect fit for Marshal Knight, but they were the best opportunity he had at the time. An entire cult dedicated to spreading chaos and corruption, it seemed that Marshal was finally surrounded by kindred spirits who felt the same was he did. In truth, Marshal still isn't too sure about the religious spin the Setites put on their motivations, but he can't deny that their assistance has greatly improved his survival chances. So for now, he's willing to overlook the cultist brainwashing. How harmful can paying lip service to a dead god be, anyways?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-22-2017, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T03:02:12-08:00","id":1161804,"title":"","content":"<b>104)</b> Ethan Barrett was a grizzled old detective with over 40 years of service on the streets of Detroit. Most people have probably heard the stories of what a terrible place the city had become over the decades, but Ethan had witnessed its decline first hand. And with retirement being just around the corner, there wasn't much the city could throw at him that the detective hadn't already seen. At least when it came to mundane threats, that is.<br /> <br /> Ethan's sire, a drifter from parts unknown and who would only identify himself as 'Mane' had rolled into the city and was looking for an easy meal. Seeing that Ethan was close to his 60's, he assumed the old detective would make for a light snack before he moved on to something more fulfilling. This did not prove to be the case, as Ethan was determined to make his attacker fight for his meal. By the time the vampire finally managed to sink his fangs into Ethan's neck, the detective had lost more blood through battle injuries than from the feeding process. Impressed by his fighting spirit, despite his age, Mane embraced him into clan Gangrel, before stealing off into the night to recover from the ordeal.<br /> <br /> Over the next several weeks, Ethan would be contacted by his sire every few days, who made sure to educate him about his new condition. The detective was forced to retire early, as he could no longer perform during the day shift and couldn't think of a proper excuse to be transferred exclusively to night shift on such short notice. But his transition into one of the undead has filled his aging body with renewed vitality. Shortly after quitting the force, he opened up his own office, where he now serves as a private investigator, utilizing his Gangrel abilities for something more positive than running around in the wilderness and picking fights with werewolves, or whatever crazy shit lurks beyond the city limits. Mane still contacts him about once every few weeks, but Ethan gets the feeling that his 'apprenticeship' is nearing its end. Soon, his sire will cut him loose completely, and he'll have to figure out the rest of this stuff on his own. Some nights, he almost feels like a fresh faced rookie again, stumbling into grizzly crime scenes that would churn the stomachs of most decent folks. Only this time, the crime scenes make a lot more sense, now that he knows what really prowls the streets at night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T11:15:35-08:00","id":1161923,"title":"","content":"105) Nosferatu Museum Director<br /> <br /> Phil, for want of a better name works for a very exclusive museum. The artifacts found within can originate from the grand gestures of the Jyhad or the small petty squabble of a backwood Domain. Every item within the museum holds a secret. Sometimes the secret is small, sometimes large. Some patrons pay Phil or the museums owner to keep an artifact locked away and hidden. Others pay Phil to highlight the item so to boost their fame or to spread the secret the item contains to all and sundry. <br /> <br /> Phil takes his role as curator of the Museum very seriously. He does not own the museum but he does care for it. No matter how mundane or insignificant the item Phil cares for them all equally. All are important for the history and secrets each items contains. Attempted theft or destruction of any of the Museums artifacts are met with a quick and deadly response. Phil has a love of history and a disdain for any who would destroy it.<br /> <br /> Although Phil is not the owner of the museum he has made a significant contribution to the collection. Phil is responsible for the Museums special collection of portraits and accidental snapshots of kindred and other supernaturals. The organization of the collection has been very lucrative to the Museum. Nosferatu, in particular are willing to pay large sums of money to see the living sculpture of Absimiliard created by an unnamed childe of Tzimisce. Most leave screaming. <br /> <br /> As the director and front man of the museum Phil is often the target of others who wish a secret destroyed or brought to light. As such Phil has become a little paranoid. Although outwardly gregarious, Phil is terrified of people. He wonders which one of them is going to try and kill him. Phil hopes one day he will be disappointed and he will meet someone who shares his interest in history without ulterior motive. So far that has never happened. <br /> <br /> 106) Toreador Art Forger<br /> <br /> Mary like Phil works for the mysterious owner of the Museum. Mary wanted to be a big name artist. She wanted her work hanging in the Louvre and other prestigious galleries. Mary's technical skills were superior to most but she had no artistic flare. Her embrace by her patron quickly lead to disillusionment and sire and childe drifting apart. The enigmatic owner of the Museum, however saw opportunity where Mary herself saw only failure. Mary currently works for the museum restoring very old paintings, some master pieces others not so much. Mary resents having to save the crayon drawings of some loopy Malkavian or crude drawn floor plan for a bank robbery gone wrong. When working on paintings of Masters she grows bitter that she will never be recognized as the great painter she thinks she could be. Mary's only pleasure are the forgeries she creates. For nearly half a century her employer has directed Mary to create copies of art from both classical masters and avant garde newcomers. Mary takes some small pleasure knowing that her work has fooled so many, both kindred and kine. Mary suspects that before her there was another &quot;Art&quot; curator who did pretty much the same &quot;job&quot;. No one is willing to speak of what happened to her predecessor. Mary wonders how much of the Art out in the real world is well... real. Mary is sure that the Mona Lisa is fake. How, the real one hangs in the vault of the museum. She wonders if she were to pass that info on to the Prince of Paris if he would favour her and her paintings. Other times she thinks the painting is a trap. A test of her loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T19:59:51-08:00","id":1164726,"title":"","content":"<b>107)</b> Tzimisce Justicar<br /> <br /> Quinton Delauny is a rare sight among the esteemed ranks of the Camarilla. When confronted about his lineage, he proudly confesses to being a member of clan Tzimisce, presumably undaunted by the horrific reputation of his Sabbat cousins. Any comparison made between Mr. Delauny and those of the Sabbat, however, does provoke feelings of disgust from him. In truth, Quinton is actually descended from Old Clan Tzimisce, those who scowl at the use of fleshcrafting as a blight upon their clan's once great name.<br /> <br /> Quinton may not have been raised in the old world, but he does come from old money, and his sire thought that was suitable enough to warrant the embrace. He was to act as his sire's agent in the new world, hunting down and eradicating the 'diseased' members of his clan who twisted the body with their perverse arts. The easiest way to do this, he learned, was to align himself with the Camarilla, who had frequent skirmishes with the Sabbat. Having already been exposed to the Machiavellian ways of the Camarilla due to his mortal upbringing, Quinton was able to rise through the ranks faster than most neonates his age and was eventually chosen to serve as a justicar, where he had nearly unlimited power to carry out his mission. Unfortunately, his station isn't as permanent as he would like. By Camarilla tradition, a justicar only serves for 13 years before a new group is elected. That means he's operating on a deadline, and his sire won't be pleased if they hear he's been dragging his feet on this matter. To that end, Quinton has exhibited an almost fanatical zeal since his appointment to office and hunts down the Sabbat with neither pity nor remorse for his actions. They are a plague upon this earth, and like all plagues, they must be cleansed.<br /> <br /> The Delauny family is one of French ancestry, though Quinton's branch resides in America. They made their fortune with the merchant industry, importing goods from their homeland to the colonies and gradually expanding from there. Today, Quinton runs a small shipping empire that delivers goods from all over the world. It has also proven to be most beneficial in assisting the migration of kindred across the continents, and a few members of Old Clan Tzimisce have even been customers of his in the past. His sire retreated back to his homeland a few years after Quinton's embrace, but promised they would see each other again once Quinton had paved the way for his return. And next time, he'd be bringing a retinue of soldiers and servants to help carry out his work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T04:38:06-08:00","id":1164756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1164726#post1164726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>107)</b> Tzimisce Justicar</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like the general idea a lot it wouldn't work with him being Justicar, because every clan alligned to the Camarilla nominates one and since Tzimisce aren't a member the dont have a Jusitcar and it will never happen because that would mean every bloodline with more than 3 members in the Camarilla would strive to get a Justicar.<br /> What will work though, is him being an Archon with privilege to hunt down Sabbaties.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T10:47:13-08:00","id":1164830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meldok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1164756#post1164756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I like the general idea a lot it wouldn't work with him being Justicar, because every clan alligned to the Camarilla nominates one and since Tzimisce aren't a member the dont have a Jusitcar and it will never happen because that would mean every bloodline with more than 3 members in the Camarilla would strive to get a Justicar.<br /> What will work though, is him being an Archon with privilege to hunt down Sabbaties.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I didn't know they were limited that way. I think the book just said they swap out every 13 years. Thank you for the advice, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T12:03:42-08:00","id":1164840,"title":"","content":"And the bonus of the Archon is that they are named by a Justicar, usually at the start of their tenure, and usually dismissed when that justices leave...but not always, so a character could technically by an Archon for more than 13 years.<br /> <br /> and I could see him as an Alastor (Hunter of the Red List), or a Doppelganger (spy/infiltrator).<br /> <br /> In V20, in 2011, the newly elected Justicars were:<br /> - Juliet Parr, Justicar of Clan Malkavian<br /> - Manuela Cardoso Pinto, Justicar of Clan Brujah<br /> - Geoffrey Leigh, Justicar of Clan Gangrel<br /> - Molly MacDonald, Justicar of Clan Nosferatu<br /> - Diana Iadanza, Justicar of Clan Toreador<br /> - Ian Carfax, Justicar of Clan Tremere<br /> - Lucinde, Justicar of Clan Ventrue<br /> - Kasim Bayar, Justicar of the Assamite Schismatics","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T02:34:35-08:00","id":1164993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1164840#post1164840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the bonus of the Archon is that they are named by a Justicar, usually at the start of their tenure, and usually dismissed when that justices leave...but not always, so a character could technically by an Archon for more than 13 years.<br /> <br /> and I could see him as an Alastor (Hunter of the Red List), or a Doppelganger (spy/infiltrator).<br /> <br /> In V20, in 2011, the newly elected Justicars were:<br /> - Juliet Parr, Justicar of Clan Malkavian<br /> - Manuela Cardoso Pinto, Justicar of Clan Brujah<br /> - Geoffrey Leigh, Justicar of Clan Gangrel<br /> - Molly MacDonald, Justicar of Clan Nosferatu<br /> - Diana Iadanza, Justicar of Clan Toreador<br /> - Ian Carfax, Justicar of Clan Tremere<br /> - Lucinde, Justicar of Clan Ventrue<br /> - Kasim Bayar, Justicar of the Assamite Schismatics</div> </div> </div> </div>Also don't forget that there maybe is a election every 13 years but some Justicars are in the office for centuries. I remember when it was a big deal in the metaplot when Karl Schreckt wasn't re-elected after serving somewhat over 400 years as Justiciar. So your mileage as an Archon may vary.<br /> <br /> I think the Justiciars who would get a kick out of employing a Tzimisce anti would be Lucinde and Ian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T06:13:56-08:00","id":1186624,"title":"","content":"I have to respond here because I think I've had a cool concept, but I'll never be able to use it.<br /> <br /> Marshal Williams (A.K.A. Marshal the kid, fastest gun in the east.)<br /> <br /> The fact that Marshal was embraced at a young age might matter if he weren't a Nosferatu. Marshal wears a cowboy get up like you might see children wear, but his badge looks like it might be real and is rusty, and his hat is pink with a (blood?) stained hole in it. Marshal loves cowboys and tries to be a heroic cowboy in every way. Although not from the west, Marshal calls everybody &quot;pardner&quot; and mixes in other &quot;old west&quot; terms as he's talking. His guns may actually be real, but he never uses them. He has a giant pet lizard that he calls &quot;spot&quot;.<br /> <br /> Unlike most Nosferatu, Marshal doesn't view his embrace with disdain. In fact, he almost views his change as being the end to trauma, rather than being a traumatic event itself. You see, when Marshal and his sister were playing &quot;cowboys and Indians&quot;, they found their father's gun. The gun went off in Marshal's hands and he ended up shooting and killing his sister. Marshal was inconsolable. He was a monster that had done the most horrible thing imaginable, and no one was going to convince him otherwise. That's why that Nosferatu decided to show Marshal what it REALLY meant to be a monster.. but things didn't go according to plan. The change hurt Marshal and made him as twisted and ugly as any Nosferatu, but in some way it was actually uplifting and healing for Marshal. He views his change as a sign that justice can exist in the world, but it sometimes needs to be helped along like the Nosferatu helped him.<br /> <br /> Marshal knows that his change doesn't mean he's been forgiven. It doesn't take away the past, it only allows him to carry on into the future. Now Marshal patrols the most violent slums he can find, trying to protect the innocent. (He keeps the brim of his hat low and pulls his bandana high to try and cover his features as he's crime-fighting). At night he creeps into abodes of criminals and takes their blood. (and sometimes he gives 'em a good whoopin') He particularly tries to protect children and targets those who would harm children a little more zealously than he does others.<br /> <br /> Even though Marshal isn't necessarily young, he has an allied Nosferatu who is like a school-marm. She looks out for Marshal and he usually does as she says, often complaining about it like a child complains about homework.. but anyone who gets to see Marshal's lair or his ability with scrounging and fixing things would probably figure out that Marshal has been around longer than he lets on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23753-gothik_knight","name":"Gothik_Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T11:28:58-07:00","id":1196866,"title":"","content":"109) A lady Tremere misses when she was a mother in the early 1940s has started to create rituals and charms related to motherhood, family and womanhood. Such as a ritual that allows a female Vampire to breastfeed (with regular milk) for one scene, ways to locate and watch over your mortal descendants and a charm that gives off a motherly aura that makes Kine more trusting of you. While her ideas were scoffed at first, seeing how her works have helped some of the local Vampires maintain their humanity, she might be on to something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T04:17:52-07:00","id":1197551,"title":"","content":"<b>110)</b> The Nosferatu have a long and proud history of spawning urban legends of monsters and witches who prey upon the foolish and the guilty. Most of these legends stem from their elders, who have been around for centuries and lost touch with the modern world. But now a newcomer has joined the party, in the form of an Autarkis named Ash Parrish. Embraced as an act of retribution, rather than reward, Ash did not appreciate becoming a hideously deformed monster, and rejected the ways of clan and sect in favor of doing things his own way. Separated from the vast information network of his clan, and unwilling to listen to the guidance of others, Ash found himself living among the fringes of society like some kind of wild dog.<br /> <br /> While initially humiliating and deplorable, Ash eventually began to find comfort in giving himself over to his more bestial nature. Coping with his inhuman actions became so much easier when he stopped perceiving himself as a human in the first place. One night, he decided that if this was going to be his existence from now on, then he might as well commit to it wholeheartedly. After slipping into a household one night and devouring a helpless child without alerting their parents, he cast aside the last of his attachment to his humanity and adopted the Path of the Feral Heart. Now, mortals and kindred alike have reason to fear getting too close to his territory, for Ash makes little distinction between them. He is like a wild animal, unfettered by the trappings of a civilized world. And to make matters worse, he still has a human brain, which makes him hyper intelligent compared to any natural predator.<br /> <br /> For now, Ash's preferred hunting grounds are low income, suburban neighborhoods. The kind that don't attract a lot of government attention and which don't have too many cops enforcing the streets. He is especially fond of feeding on people inside their own homes, and often uses his vampiric abilities to gain entry without being noticed. If his victims are lucky, they'll already be asleep by the time he catches them. But if they prove to be a bit of a night owl, then things are probably going to get violently messy.<br /> <br /> As both an Autarkis and one who follows the Path of the Feral Heart, Ash has absolutely zero interest in the political machinations of kindred society. If you wish to convince him to join your coterie, you must appeal to his more immediate concern of long term survival. The one who wears the crown is not as important as what they intend to do with said crown. And if they intend to make unlife difficult for Ash, then he may be willing to disrupt their plans. If, however, their goals do not directly inconvenience him in some way, then he is content to ignore the issue, regardless of who else gets hurt as a result of his apathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-20-2018, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T13:09:51-07:00","id":1197719,"title":"","content":"111) A Gangrel famer who has been breeding and experimenting on ghouled animals in hopes of creating ones whose blood can taste just as good as a human's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T19:34:05-07:00","id":1198211,"title":"","content":"<b>112)</b> One does not have to expend much effort to be repulsed by the research of those who dedicate themselves to the Path of Metamorphosis. But even they are rarely so dangerous as the ancilla who has come to be known as Dr. Gregor Steinhauer. Growing up in Germany, Dr. Steinhauer was an aspiring geneticist who was obsessed with transhumanism even before his embrace. He sought to unlock the secrets of the human genome and use it to achieve self controlled evolution. Intrigued that a mortal would harbor such a similar ideology to their own path of enlightenment, Steinhauer was targeted for embrace by a member of Clan Tzimisce, who fostered encouragement for his work.<br /> <br /> Now, Gregor's use of Vicissitude has taken a truly dark turn. While other metamorphosists focus on the the bones and muscles of their experiments, Dr. Steinhauer tries to shape them on the genetic level. The goal of his research is to create self replicating experiments who can pass their forms down through natural reproduction, instead of having to be manually sculpted. He prefers to create his experiments in pairs, consisting of one female and one male, before placing them into forced breeding programs to see if he can produce viable results. Thankfully for the outside world, his experiments have mostly been failures. No matter how much he warps them on the outside, their genetic makeup is still human (or whatever creature he used), which means they continue to produce offspring of that species. After regaining his composure from his latest failure, Gregor looks over what went wrong, before trying again with a new batch of test subjects. As for what becomes of the failures, that depends entirely upon how useful Gregor feels they can be in other fields of service.<br /> <br /> Unlike most of his clan, Gregor appears to be relatively normal looking. He's been too busy conducting experiments on other creatures to worry about his own modifications. He appears to be a German male in his late 40's with dark black hair and a handle bar mustache. He stands at a height of 6'2, weighing 173 lbs. His eyes are pale blue, and he wears a pair of circle rimmed glasses. As with many doctors and scientists, he prefers to keep himself in pristine condition, with his research facilities being cleaned to immaculate status before and after conducting his experiments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-28-2018, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T17:53:09-07:00","id":1201765,"title":"","content":"113) Not sure if this one will count. Since The Risen can sneak into Vampiric society with some work, this one has managed to make a home for himself among the local Giovanni (or Cappadocian if you want a Dark Ages game) who use his knowledge of the underworld, Wraith abilities and ability to walk in daylight to their advantage. (He poses as a Vampire to outsiders.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T18:18:40-07:00","id":1201776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1201765#post1201765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">113) Not sure if this one will count. Since The Risen can sneak into Vampiric society with some work, this one has managed to make a home for himself among the local Giovanni (or Cappadocian if you want a Dark Ages game) who use his knowledge of the underworld, Wraith abilities and ability to walk in daylight to their advantage. (He poses as a Vampire to outsiders.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it would be difficult for a Risen to walk among the Kindred for any length of time and not be noticed. Anyone with Auspex would spot them, whether through Aura Perception or simply by picking up on clues through their enhanced mundane senses.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say it'd be impossible, just really, REALLY difficult. Would probably require some heavy-duty sorcery to mask the Risen's aura, so it looked similar to the vampire's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T19:29:38-07:00","id":1201805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1164830#post1164830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah, I didn't know they were limited that way. I think the book just said they swap out every 13 years. Thank you for the advice, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It could work, a Tzimisce could be Fleshcrafted into replacing a Justicar or Justicar elect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T19:32:23-07:00","id":1201808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1201776#post1201776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine it would be difficult for a Risen to walk among the Kindred for any length of time and not be noticed. Anyone with Auspex would spot them, whether through Aura Perception or simply by picking up on clues through their enhanced mundane senses.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say it'd be impossible, just really, REALLY difficult. Would probably require some heavy-duty sorcery to mask the Risen's aura, so it looked similar to the vampire's.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could play that you are an Elder changing your aura to look abnormal if you are really clever.<br /> <br /> But in my headcanon the Camarilla permits Risen into their number as &quot;Kindred&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T18:35:41-07:00","id":1202088,"title":"","content":"114) A Malkavian who anthropomorphizes cars, always as women. Each car has a personality, a name, there's gossip about them. He uses spirit's touch on them to find out what they have to say about their owners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T19:23:09-07:00","id":1202106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1202088#post1202088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">114) A Malkavian who anthropomorphizes cars, always as women. Each car has a personality, a name, there's gossip about them. He uses spirit's touch on them to find out what they have to say about their owners.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that one as an example of Malkavian insanity!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 115) A Harbinger of Skulls who wishes to forget vendetta and madness and wishes to return to a semblance of humanity so she foregoes her mask and dons a tophat and monocle and poses as a member of the Samedi to join the Camarilla as a Houngan named Rich Uncle Skeleton.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T05:16:46-07:00","id":1202954,"title":"","content":"<b>116)</b> If one wishes to transcend the limits of the physical form, they must start by transcending its mental limitations. Such is the philosophy of Eliza Andrade, who's advancement on the Path of Metamorphosis involves modifications of the human brain. She claims to be seeking the perfect cerebral structure, which will provide the analytical capabilities to pursue other avenues of evolution in a more expedient fashion.<br /> <br /> Prior to her embrace, Eliza was a neuro surgeon who performed many successful operations on the human brain. In her current state, she would describe her work as being crude and ineffectual. Since becoming a member of clan Tzimisce, Eliza has implimented Vicissitude into her work on the human brain, modifying it in a way that she believes is properly suited to comprehend the secrets of the physical form. Her creations are as alien in their mindset as they are in their appearance. The 'useless' parts of their brains have been replaced by ones Eliza deems more suitable to the information she's trying to utilize, and their neural pathways have been almost completely remodeled. When it comes to her Szlachta, less is more, as the saying goes. Rather than churning out a bunch of drooling abominations, she devotes time into her work, producing creatures of wicked cunning and sophistication.<br /> <br /> Eliza has also gone so far as to perform modifications to her own brain as well. The first thing that stands out upon seeing her is the bulbous cranium atop her head. Nearly the size of a beach ball, her veins bulge beneath the surface of her skin, while the brown hair on her scalp looks like a poorly fitted wig, due to the proportions of her skull. Her arms, hands and fingers have also been modified into more spindly appendages that can perform surgery with greater precision than her former limbs ever could. Beyond that, she appears as a human female of Hispanic descent with brown eyes and a modest physique. She was embraced in her early 30's and still looks as such to anybody capable of ignoring her physical modifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-05-2018, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T21:51:00-07:00","id":1204427,"title":"","content":"<b>Some Tzimisce pics I found.</b><br /> <br /> <b>1st </b>- An old woman (?) who gave themselves a couple extra pair of eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>2nd</b> - Appears to have replaced his hair and beard with human intestines.<br /> <br /> <b>3rd</b> - This one molded their cranium to resemble a rib cage<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://cdnb.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/009/314/863/large/william-hoglund-mayer-tzimiscehex.jpg?1518283456\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:52:24-07:00","id":1204597,"title":"","content":"<b>120) Bad Dog (9th Generation, City Gangrel): </b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Grrrll... Bark, Bark!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Not many people know who Bad Dog was prior to his embrace. He's been a vampire for over 70 years now, so most of his connections to his former life are long gone by this point. In these nights, Bad Dog finds himself serving as an attack dog for Sabbat war parties, using his clan's abilities to track down their enemies and then tear them apart once he catches them. Because of his numerous frenzies over the past 7 decades, Bad Dog has lost the ability to verbally communicate in human languages. But those with access to the Animalism discipline or establishing a mental connection will find that he is still capable of holding a conversation if need be.<br /> <br /> As a Gangrel, Bad Dog is accustomed to surviving on his own. But as a member of the Sabbat, he's no stranger to working as part of a group. It's just that many of the packs he's joined over the decades haven't exactly survived longer than a few years before they do something stupid and get themselves killed. If a pack wishes to recruit him into their ranks, they're going to have to convince him that they're competent enough to survive, instead of rushing head long into danger like a bunch of shovelheads.<br /> <br /> As an Ancilla, Bad Dog has accumulated a permanent animal feature during his time as a vampire. Instead of having a human head atop his neck, he has manifested that of a doberman's. This head can only speak using barks, yips, growls and whines, lacking the biological components necessary for proper speech. Aside from his canine head, Bad Dog is a dark skinned man standing at height of 6'1 and having a decently muscular physique of 213 lbs. He is often seen wearing a crimson hoody, which he leaves unzipped to expose his bare torso underneath. The rest of his outfit usually includes a pair of tattered jeans and some worn out red and blue sneakers. He was embraced in his early 20's, leaving his body in good condition, as far as vampires go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-09-2018, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T13:40:24-07:00","id":1204965,"title":"","content":"<b>121) Silvain Bardin (8th Gen, Nosferatu)</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Lord taketh, and I taketh back!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In the Bible, when Job lost everything of value in his life, he realized that everything he had was given to him by the grace of God. So of course God would have the authority to take it all away if he felt inclined to do so. Unfortunately, for Silvain Bardin, he did not receive the same epiphany. Before his embrace, Silvain was what most people would consider a good Christian. He never performed any of the deadly sins, he gave his excess wealth to charity, he attended church every Sunday and he rejected the paganist heathens whenever he came upon them. So you can imagine his shock when he drew the attention of the Nosferatu, who embraced him for reasons that are yet still unknown to him.<br /> <br /> Over the next several weeks, Silvain would lose everything he ever loved or cared about. His friends, his family, his home, his job, his self respect and finally his faith. If this was how God rewards his faithful, then believing in God is worthless, or so Silvain had come to believe. In a fit of anger, Silvain pledged himself down the Road of Sin, vowing that he would indulge himself in death what he had denied himself in life. He now favors the Path of Pleasure, immersing himself in debauchery and opulence to distract from the hideous monstrosity he has become. He even became involved in the business of trading slaves, using the money to establish his own brothel and register it as a place of Elysium for the city's kindred to meet and socialize.<br /> <br /> Before his embrace disfigured him, Silvain was a Frenchman in his early 30's. Now, he is a haggard creature with a protruding overbite, completely bald, gnarled ears, long fingers and a sloping posture. His eyes have also become polychromatic, with the right one being a bright shade of blue, and the left being a dark green.<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Silvain is intended to be a Dark Ages character with a position as Keeper of Elysium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  Fixed several typs. 04-09-2018, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T14:56:04-07:00","id":1204983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1204965#post1204965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>131) Silvain Bardin (8th Gen, Nosferatu)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Silvain is intended to be a Dark Ages character with a position as Keeper of Elysium.</div> </div> </div> </div>shouldn't he be 118? (Bad Dog being 117).<br /> <br /> I do love some DA ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T14:59:29-07:00","id":1204984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1204983#post1204983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> shouldn't he be 118? (Bad Dog being 117).<br /> <br /> I do love some DA ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I counted the Tzimisce pics as 17, 18 and 19<br /> <br /> Which reminds me, I miscounted. He should be 121...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T19:23:31-07:00","id":1207120,"title":"","content":"<b>122)</b> <b>Bastion (11th Gen, Gargoyle):</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Oh, don't look so surprised. After all, you used me as a research subject for years. How could I not be expected to pick up a few tricks of my own?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Most people would agree that eavesdropping on somebody's conversation is considered rude and taboo. But for Bastion, it was his only means of achieving freedom from under the iron thumb of the Tremere. Created as a sentinel Gargoyle, Bastion spent his existence as the personal assistant of the Chantry's regent. It was his job to gather the necessary components, prepare the ritual chamber and clean up the mess afterward. His job to fetch the arcane tomes and record his master's notes as he rambled on into the night about ideas and formulas for his continued research. What the Tremere didn't realize, however, is that Bastion was doing more than assisting his master, he was also learning from him. It took a long time, about 20 years worth of grueling servitude, but Bastion slowly began to understand the fundamentals of Thaumaturgy, and eventually learned how to counteract their magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, Bastion is free of his master's control and has earned himself a modestly comfortable position among the Camarilla as an arcane scholar and adviser on matters of the occult. As one of the rare few outside of the clan who have the privilege of knowing Tremere secrets, Bastion's assistance has become invaluable to those who find themselves on the opposite side of the warlocks. Unfortunately, this also marks him as a target by the jealous Tremere, and it likely his knowledge of counter magic has been the only thing shielding him from their wrath in the time since he's escaped.<br /> <br /> <br /> While all knowledge of his past life has been wiped away, one can assume that Bastion was previously a member of clan Nosferatu. His appearance as a Gargoyle is truly hideous, with a stretched maw full of sharp teeth, A pair of short horns growing from his temples which curve around the side of his head, and sunken eye sockets that add a shadowy tint to his menacing glare. He's relatively small by Gargoyle standards, in the sense that he is able to fit into human clothing after modifying it for his new body type. He primarily wears elastic outfits, finding them cheaper and easier to get a hold of than ordering custom jobs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://www.compositeeffects.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/gargoyle_mask_clean_granite_01-443x600.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-14-2018, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T15:51:38-07:00","id":1207427,"title":"","content":"<b>Let's see what we've got in the old Loony Bin.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>123)</b> A Malkavian suffering from Megalomania has his sights set on becoming the next Prince. His hobbies include 3D chess, Lego kits, and an unhealthy fascination with puppetry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>124)</b> A Malkavian nihilist who allows most of her choices to be decided by the roll of the dice. Even she has no idea what she's planning to do next, until she sees what number comes up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>125)</b> A Malkavian who has taken up the art of training Revenants for use by others among the Sabbat. Unfortunately for those under their tutelage, the Malkavian seems awfully convinced they are literal animals of some kind and treats them accordingly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T19:54:19-07:00","id":1208685,"title":"","content":"<b>126)</b> An escaped Gargoyle who joins the Sabbat and seizes the rank of Ductus by destroying the previous leader of the now named 'Jailbreakers' pack. The amnesia caused by his transformation frees him of any distracting attachments he may have had to the world of mortals, allowing him to direct his full attention towards accomplishing the Sabbat's goals. His hatred of the Tremere is nearly as intense as the Tzimisce's and he never passes up an opportunity to destroy them when one presents itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>127)</b> A Toreador antitribu who serves as an agent of The Black Hand, using their skill in torture to root out and destroy the Sabbat's enemies. When not acting on official Hand business, they spend their downtime serving as the Priest of the Jailbreakers pack. It is said that they have become quite adept at stoking the pack's appetite for mayhem, most likely using their skill in Presence to stir the others into a full blown war party.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T08:07:03-07:00","id":1210960,"title":"","content":"<b>128)</b> A Nosferatu Cleopatra who's despair over their hideous fate drove them to commit the ultimate crime of diablerie. Hoping to steal the power of Presence from the Toreador, the hideous creature now finds themselves influenced by hedonistic impulses and seeks to distance themselves from the rest of the clan in favor of a more luxurious environment. The other Nosferatu warn them that they are drawing too much attention to themselves, but the Cleopatra refuses to listen to reason, instead basking in the supernatural charisma provided by their stolen soul.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>129)</b> A Giovanni meat baron who mixes addictive chemicals in with their products. In addition to greatly improving the taste, the chemicals have negative impacts on the physical and mental development of the mortals who consume them, thus making them easier to control over time. And should any pesky investigators try to expose the truth of what goes into their products... well, accidents can happen in a meat processing plant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>130)</b> A thin blooded Follower of Set who often finds themselves having to rely on less supernatural methods to expand the cult's influence throughout the city. While their condition would normally warrant scorn by lower generation vampires, their natural talent for manipulating others has earned them some degree of respect by the other Setites.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T08:30:31-07:00","id":1210965,"title":"","content":"<b>131) Allen Breck</b> is an unusual Gangrel with odd powers.<br /> <br /> In reality he is a Caitiff who was able to fly under the Ottawa Camarilla radar for about 5 years before being fortuitiously discovered by a Gangrel. A street gang member in life, he had turn the gang into his herd and his lieutenant into a dedicated ghoul. When brought to the Prince, rather then destroyed him, the Prince gave the responsability of properly educating him to the Gangrel much to the displeasure of the Malkavian Primogen, who saw in the young Caitiff precognition power and odd bouts of short-term amesia the mark of Malkav's Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 04-29-2018, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:49:50-07:00","id":1213076,"title":"","content":"<b>132) </b>Yasen Ivanov Peychinovich is an Old Clan Tzimisce Autarkis.<br /> <br /> A Bulgarian Boyar in life, he was embraced in the 1100s and to this day still hold dominion over his old domain. Skilled in his Clan's discipline and Kuldonic Sorcery, he has a strong disdain for the Vicissitude using upstarts that pollutes his once glorious bloodline.<br /> <br /> Through judicious use of Dominate, blackmail and bribery and proper use of lesser branch of the family tree, he has succeed in keeping the old ancestral domain within his grip. A strong believe of the old tradition of Hospitality, he will not tolerate any violence done upon his guest or from his guess. This trait has made his Domain a de facto neutral ground for his old coterie (a Setite, a Lasombra, a Ventrue and a Malkavian (A Dominate one in Modern Night, but knew Dementation in Dark Age)). A Greek Cappadocian doctor used to complete the lot; his death has made it such that Giovani are forbidden on his land upon penalty of Final Death...a faith even the upstart Tremeres managed to avoid.<br /> <br /> A true Lord, he is very protective of his subjects, which had as lead to a surprising outcome in the course of history. Deep in one of his domain's mountainous forest, there is a Caern historically maintained by Shadow Lord packs and their kinfolk, leading to a polite relation between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":"stupid typo 04-30-2018, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:02:51-07:00","id":1213096,"title":"","content":"133) Daniel thought the fighting was over. He\u2019d done his six years, two tours, and was planning on getting his law degree. Maybe become a judge.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat war party put an end to that.<br /> <br /> He survived his creation rites and bound to his pack by the Viniculum, took what he learned fighting terrorists to become Frighteningly effective. His humanity on a downward spire, his sire looked forward to teaching him the Path of honorable accord.<br /> Then his life changed again, as an encounter with a sole Lupine (what the hell was one doing in a Cam city anyway?) His pack, and the chains of blood bonding him to it shattered, he took an unfiltered look at his \u201clife,&quot; and was disgusted.<br /> <br /> Changing his appearance (thanks to a 'trick' learned from a pack mate), he went underground in the city, feeding on the homeless veterans while defending them from worse predators. After all who is going to believe a homeless crazy with PTSD who rants about blood angels?<br /> <br /> Other vampires, that is who. When brought before the (Ventrue) Prince and his story torn out of him, Daniel found something he had long thought denied to him, mercy.<br /> <br /> Now Daniel, Ventrue antitribu, is a member of the Camerilla, if not in good standing. He lays low, using his knowledge of the law, albeit limited, to help disabled veterans and build his herd as a result. He hopes that by helping others he can regain his diminished humanity. He knows that he\u2019s always one misstep away from Final Death, and tries to always have an escape plan ready. But he also knows the Sabbat would consider him a traitor of the worse kind, and has nowhere to go.<br /> <br /> (Ventrue antitribu, with one dot of vicissitude and the probationary sect member flaw, prey limitation is veterans though he tries to limit his feeding to veterans who have seen combat, so people under estimate him.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4034-the_livewire","name":"The_Livewire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4034_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T11:41:52-07:00","id":1213133,"title":"","content":"<b>134) </b><i>M</i><i>other gave us life, and we love Mother. Mother asked us to protect, we protected. Mother asked us to fight, we fought. Mother asked to leave, we left. Now Mother is gone, so I have return home to wait for her</i>.<br /> <br /> She has no name, yet she doesn't need one. An old gargoyle Ritually created in 1130A.D. to defend Ceoris, she did as the Mother of Gargoyles asked, never questioning, never faltering. Defeating enemy both during the Omen War, the Massasa War and the Anarch Revolt. Then came the Gargoyle Revolt and she fought the Tremere she once protected under her Mother's guidance. Once free she left with her mother and her brood. After a while some of her broodmates and herself left and starter to wander eventually returning to the ruins of Ceoris where they still live. Having parted early on, none of the possess any knowledge of Visceratika.<br /> <br /> Unable to embrace, and with none of them strong enough in Thaumaturgy to master the Gargoyle Creation Ritual, the quietly spend their life in the mountain, avoiding human, garou and the local Tzimisce, content in their simple existence, feeding off of animals or the occasional lost hiker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 06-09-2018, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T17:13:08-07:00","id":1213227,"title":"","content":"<b>135) </b>Vadzim Vasilyevich Jakavienka is a brilliant seismologist and geologist born in the Russian Empire's city of Minsk in 1913. Somehow surviving tge was he grew up in the Byelorussian Soviet Socialist Republic whee his keen mind and scientific acumen was quickly notice by his teachers which allowed him to study at the university where he was quickly notice. Once his study were done, he did some field work up until he received the invitation to join the Soviet Antarctic Expedition where his expertise would be welcome. Delighted he agreed.<br /> <br /> In 1953, On his way to Mirny Station, an encounter on the ship changed his life. One of the sailor was a Kindred, who found that life on the sea suited him better and was a good way to stay ahead of <i>them</i>. On that faithful night he become one of Malkav's Brood. He became a bit more excentric and focused, but nothing that caused more than the occasional raising of an eyebrow, but the time they landed at Mirny, he knew the basic of what it was to be Cainite as well as gain mastery of the basic skill in his Clan's Diciplines. His latent Obsessive-compulsive tenancies were accentuated by his Blood, but that actually proved to be boon more than a bane.<br /> <br /> To this day he still live and work on his study at the station, making judicious use of Dominate and Obfuscate as well as the ocasional bloodbond to avoid raising suspicion and the thick polar suit allows him to briefly and safely travel during daytime (help with a bit of Fortitude) which allows him to weather the Antarctic Summer more easily.<br /> <br /> On the Station he is known to be an excentric scientist, a bit disconnected with reality, still referring to the state and it's governmental organs by their old Soviet era names and often seen or hear signing the BSSR or the USSR Anthem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T18:24:18-07:00","id":1213997,"title":"","content":"136) A Molochim Baali who specializes in analyzing and &quot;sanitizing&quot; Dark Thaumaturgy, and other forms of Infernal blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> Any blood magician sufficiently familiar with Infernal sorcery understands that much of its methods and ritual components are, for all practical purposes, unnecessary. No one <i>needs</i> to sacrifice infants, draw circles in feces, desecrate holy symbols, or chant litanies to the infernal host. Other forms of blood magic get by perfectly fine without them. Rather, Infernalists do magic this way because it's the only method afforded them by their demonic patrons, who have a vested interest in ensuring both the damnation of their supplicant and the perpetuation of evil in the world. The way the magic is formatted is designed for this. And because demons don't explain why a spell must be cast a certain way, it ensures that 1) the supplicant is entirely dependent on their patron for all magic, and 2) that evil is done even if the pawn spreads their secrets around. If an Infernalist takes an apprentice or writes a spell down in notes, the knowledge passed down will be of spells and rituals that will Damn a soul just for casting them.<br /> <br /> This Baali knows this. As part of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, he makes it his mission to undo such activity.<br /> <br /> An experienced occultist and blood magician, with knowledge of multiple different practices, this Baali goes around collecting the notes of Infernalists. When he isn't capturing them and forcing the secrets out, of course. Once he's collected this knowledge, he carefully analyzes it from the perspective of a magical theorist. Excising redundant elements and making less morally repugnant substitutions. While the removal of Infernal texts (and Infernalists) is a good in and of itself, it's also important to extract genuinely useful magical secrets from tainted sources. If an Infernal Ritual can perform a feat otherwise unavailable to &quot;clean&quot; blood magic, this Baali will aim to correct that mistake. To derive a formula for safer consumption, while removed of as much atrocity, depravity, and blasphemy as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T11:30:40-07:00","id":1214230,"title":"","content":"<b>137) </b>Aristide Jean is a Haiti born Elder Samedi who left his land during the Duvalier era.<br /> <br /> Settle in his new home, the powerful Cainite has established a nice little vice empire based on drugs and prostitution. Very protective of the local Haitian population, and any Afro-American descendant of the slaves-trade when he feel so inclined, he doesn't tolerate if any other vampire dare to feed on them, poach or otherwise harm them. While he might be incline to simply warn or levy a light penalty on first time offender, recidivists or first time offending Samedi or Serpent of Light will not be granted such mercy and will be dealt with with extreme prejudice. Local and nearby Serpnt of Light actively go out of their way to either avoid his territory or to buy their way and remain in his good grace.<br /> <br /> An odd anacronistic quick of his, is that High Clan Vampire can expected to be received as a fellow ruler however they are expected to act accordingly and offer him the same treatment in return. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T10:29:10-07:00","id":1214670,"title":"","content":"<b>138)</b> William is at the bottom of the ladder, he knows it, yet in revels in it.<br /> <br /> A thin-blood (15th Gen) vampire sired by a Toreador, his extensive military background is the only reason reason the Prince did not give him Final Death. A Special Ops skilled in infiltration and demolition, he uses his skill and the weaken Curse of Caine to strike at Sabbat threat, sneaking into their lairs or safe houses during daytime and making great use of incendiary devise to wipe them out of the surface of the Earth. Although the opportunity to Diablorized has presented itself multiple times, he realises that his High Generation is what makes him such a great asset for the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T15:59:56-07:00","id":1214812,"title":"","content":"139) A Kuei-Jin from the Face of the Gods dharma has fleed to North America, taking on the idenity of an Indian immigrant. Picking the most downtrodden town he could find, he came in as a minister and with his beauty, charisma, and powers, he has now set up a faith around himself. With the town being in better shape than ever, the Godling hopes to influence the mayor he is advising to work his way to govenor in 10 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T12:42:27-07:00","id":1215873,"title":"","content":"<b>140)</b> <br /> <br /> <b>Quinn Wade (10th Gen Caitiff):</b> It doesn't matter what anyone says, when it comes to side effects of the embrace, Quinn is convinced that he hit the jackpot. But hey, you'd be glad to be a Caitiff too, if your sire was a member of the Nosferatu! At least he doesn't have to disguise himself as a damn leper when he goes out in public. But the true icing on the cake is that the circumstances behind Quinn's embrace were intended to serve as a punishment. It turns out that Mr. Wade was not a morally upstanding citizen in life, and the clan of sewer rats thought they could impart some much needed humility by turning him into one of their own. But when the first week passed by and Quinn exhibited no symptoms of turning into a hideous monster, they kicked him out of the warrens to fend for himself.<br /> <br /> In his mortal life, Quinn was a member of the city guard, who abused his position of authority over the peasant folk. His crimes at the time included extortion, police brutality, accepting bribes, tampering with evidence and even sexual assault. But at least his influence was limited by the fact he was a low ranking guardsmen. After his embrace, however, he began using his supernatural abilities to quickly escalate himself through the ranks and has now become the captain of his own night watch garrison, with a retinue of guardsmen under his control. Now it's not just mortals who need to fear him, because he's also been directing his corruption towards other fledglings who he feels are too low in status to attempt retaliation. <br /> <br /> Of course, this would have to take place in the dark ages, too. A time where the heads of state were largely unsympathetic to the plights of those beneath their station. Which basically means the Prince is content to let Quinn go about his business so long as it does not negatively impact his own schemes. Besides, having a kindred who's not affiliated with any particularly clan as a member of the city guard may prove useful in keeping the serfs and vassals under control.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mr. Wade appears as a young caucasian male in his mid to late 20's. He has short, chestnut colored hair and dark green eyes. He stands around 5'9 in height, with a moderately fit build of 162 lbs. He is rarely seen in public without his guard uniform on, which serves as both a symbol of his position in society, as well as constant protection in the event of an assassination attempt.<br /> <br /> <br /> Quinn Wade is a follower of the Road of Sin, on the Path of Pleasure. In the time since his embrace and rise to power, he has also taught himself the disciplines of Potence, Celerity, Fortitude and Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T08:18:40-07:00","id":1226080,"title":"","content":"<b>141)<br /> <br /> Marshall Blueburn (11th Gen Malkavian):</b><br /> <br /> At first glance, Mr. Blueburn would appear to be a healthy, functioning individual. But if one were to witness his feeding habits, his deep seeded madness becomes immediately recognizable. Even Marshall is not entirely certain why his hunger manifests in the way that it does, but the Malkavian can only willingly feed upon the blood of those who have been rendered physically powerless to resist his advances. Whether they have been forcibly tied down, rendered comatose, crippled for life, or suffering from severe brain damage, Mr. Blueburn is a sadistic predator who derives pleasure from knowing that he has absolute control over the lives of his prey. In a horrific effort to hide his appetites from public awareness, Marshall has imprisoned a few blood dolls within the confines of his Haven and has surgically amputated all four of their limbs to ensure they will never be able to escape on their own!<br /> <br /> Both prior to and after his embrace, Marshall Blueburn serves as a charity organizer who helps collect money for those with physical disabilities, or life long injuries. The big difference is that now Blueburn has decided to extract blood from his clients in exchange for the financial support he offers them. There's a poetic metaphor in there somewhere, but Marshall chooses not to dwell on it.<br /> <br /> Marshall has the appearance of a 31 year old caucasian man with chestnut colored hair and a full beard. His hair, both facial and that which grows from his scalp is trimmed short and neatly groomed into pristine condition. He dresses in modest, yet fashionable attire to showcase that he takes pride in presenting himself among others, without lording it over those who are less well off than he is. Marshall stands at six feet, three inches tall and weighs 152 pounds. He has bright green eyes which once exhibited a soft compassion, but now carry a sinister gleam behind them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Faction:</b> Anarchs<br /> <br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Caregiver<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Sadist<br /> <br /> <b>Flaws:</b> Dark Secret<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Natural Leader<br /> <br /> <b>Derangement:</b> ASPD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":".  Fixed Some Typos 06-16-2018, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T14:05:12-07:00","id":1227896,"title":"","content":"<b>142.</b> &quot;Franceso the Eskimo&quot; Giovanni made his money the old fashioned way: he stole it under direction from his 97-year-old ghouled father who abducted and brutally raped Frank's mother over a period of six weeks to punish her old-money New England family for getting too uppity around their betters, Clan Giovanni.<br /> <br /> The Milliners, understandably, held little esteem for the resulting bastard baby boy, but given his pedigree they couldn't kill him outright. They could, however, disown Frank's mother, force her to shame his father by naming the baby after him, and send her to be a common waitress at a diner in Perth Amboy, NJ.<br /> <br /> Frank grew up as a complete hellion. By grade school, he was beating up other students for their lunch money, or just for fun. By junior high, he was beating up teachers for their lunch money, or threatening them for grades. By sixteen, when he was 6'5&quot; and still growing, he was mugging old ladies and swiping car stereos for spending cash. Frankie would argue he just played the hand he was dealt.<br /> <br /> Exactly where he went bad is hard to say.<br /> <br /> His mother, broken by her torture and familial rejection, had taken up with a string of boyfriends and did more drugs than most Ramones. One of her boyfriends had lived with them for a few years in the late seventies, when Frank was a small child. Frank would never tell anyone why he was terrified every time the man came into his room late at night, what the man did, or that he was both relieved and crushed when the man just vanished one night while driving home from a drug-deal. One thing Frank did learn when the police came to question his mother about the man's car (which was found idling on the Pulaski Skyway, with the passenger door open) was that no one could ever actually love him. Something in Frank was broken. Wrong. Ugly. Furthermore, since everyone will always fuck you, you better fuck them harder and first. If only to prevent your own pain.<br /> <br /> Okay, maybe how Frank got broken isn't such a mystery. Not that anyone, including Frank, has ever figured it out.<br /> <br /> In any case, by the time Frank could be tried as an adult, he was robbing convenience stores and breaking knees for local loan sharks. He got the nickname &quot;Francesco the Eskimo&quot; because of how he dressed. It didn't matter what the weather was, or how much it made him sweat. Frankie always covered up: long sleeve shirts, long pants, a loose fitting jacket, and a knit cap pulled down over his forehead. Sometimes, he even wore gloves. The guys he worked with assumed it was a ploy to make him hard for witnesses to identify.<br /> <br /> This, as it happened, was true, but mostly it was that Frankie hated people to look at him. Anytime Frank saw himself in a mirror, he would fill with such self-loathing it gave him agita, driving him to eating Tums as a regular snack. He would shower with the lights out, and no photo exists of him after the age of eight. In fact, Frankie wasn't bad looking, and spent considerable time trying to look better. He worked out at the boxing gym for hours on end, he ate nothing but health food, and he jogged maniacally. He always wore expensive (if somewhat oversized) clothes and jewelry. He didn't just go to the corner barber shop, like his buddies. He went to an actual salon, with a stylist. Most people might even say he was a handsome young man. Still, Frankie remained convinced of his own repulsiveness.<br /> <br /> On New Year's Eve 1990, when Frankie was 19, he and his buddies robbed a liquor store in Carteret for partying money. It went bad. Real bad. The clerk and two customers were killed. One of Frankie's buddies was captured, and snitched within hours. Frankie was on the lam, and his name was all over the news. Frankie's father, now a neo-nate Giovanni vampire, took notice and tracked his son to a cheap motel room in Asbury Park. Frank, Sr. offered him sanctuary, if he would serve him. Frankie enthusiastically agreed.<br /> <br /> Frankie spent the next few years working out, and learning how to fight. He took boxing classes, and spent hours at the shooting range. He also did all the usual things a son does for an aged father: cooking, cleaning, and kidnapping runaways and hookers to eat for dinner. You know, like a good boy. Frankie knows he did a lot more (and a lot worse) than he remembers, since his father heavily edited his memory for most of those years. He does know that he's wanted for by the feds for a string of bank robberies from Nashua to Nashville, and his father is suddenly richer than Croesus.<br /> <br /> Eventually, the time came when Frankie was offered the proxy kiss. The catch? He would serve his mother's family, up in the leafy enclave of Duxbury, Massachusetts.<br /> <br /> Those years with his cousins were preppy hell for Frankie. Oh, they smiled and laughed all the time, in their LL Bean sweaters and khaki pants. They played touch football on the lawn. They spent summers on an island off the coast of Maine. Frankie slept in the fucking pool house, while they lived in a center hall colonial mansion. Oh, he drove a Mercedes, but as their chauffeur. Guess who had to pick up after their labradoodle when he shit on the putting-green-perfect lawn? Guess who picked up their dry cleaning and pruned their hedges? Guess who had to kill realtors and cops and assorted witnesses anytime the Milliner vampires asked him to, sneering through their perfect white smiles at the absurdity of having to talk to Frankie at all? He wanted to beat their blonde heads in with a shovel, and burn their bodies at noon.<br /> <br /> So, one sunny Thursday afternoon in September, he did.<br /> <br /> He expected to be killed for that, but, turns out this particular branch of the Milliners was skimming a tiny bit too much from their tributes to Venice, and Frankie was rewarded with the embrace. The Giovanni anzioni haven't told anyone who killed the Duxbury Milliners. They believe Frankie was the last survivor of a Sabbat attack, who was rewarded with the embrace for his valor in defending the family. Venice uses this secret for leverage to keep Frankie in line.<br /> <br /> Frankie has been sent to Phillipsburg, NJ, to handle gun-running and other business the clan has with the Sabbat. He's learned about the existence of Vicissitude, and desperately wants to learn it. Being undead has done nothing to diminish his body image issues. In fact, the knowledge that he is doomed to spend eternity looking like he does... 6'8&quot;, 400 pounds of muscle, with a square jaw and broad shoulders... depresses him deeply. He has a long list of things he wants to change: the shape of his eyes, the distance from his lips to his nose, the length of his limbs, the curl of his pompadour hair, a mole on his beefy neck, and the size of his... ahem. He would do anything, including selling out his family, to get his flaws fixed. He hasn't found a Tzimisce he trusts enough to actually ask. That, and his shame at this obvious weakness of his.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, Frankie is kicking ass, cracking skulls, and making big bucks for a Giovanni elder in Scranton. Frankie still turns out the lights when he showers, which makes it hard to get all the blood and gore out of his hair at the end of the night, but he's determined to play the hand he's been dealt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","user":"Nosimplehiway","date":". 06-16-2018, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T14:02:11-07:00","id":1228111,"title":"","content":"143) A Ghouled priest who performs religious ceremonies and church services for religious Camarilla/Anarch Vampires so he can help them maintain their humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T23:43:33-07:00","id":1229531,"title":"","content":"144) A promising Warrior Setite, who defended Setite temples since even before his embrace, and worked offensively to eliminate threats to the Clan. After completing a particular difficult and vital mission, he was rewarded by an elder with a potent honor: having his heart removed and left in his care. Immune to being staked and flush with honor, his future was looking bright.<br /> <br /> It all went wrong when his haven was burgled, and his heart stolen. It lay in the possession of an ambitious Ventrue ancillae, who seeks any advantage in his rise to princedom. Now the Setite Warrior has a new master, who literally holds the Setite's heart in his hands. Incensed and mortified, the Setite dutifully obeys, working towards the Ventrue's glory, rather than Set's. Another Aeon, another set of chains holding him down from transcendence. But he bides his time, for Set is a wily figure, and encourages subtly and patience. Set's will can still be done. For what sort of snake would the Setite be if he couldn't wriggle his way out of bondage? Or, rather, use his period of durance as an opportunity to corrupt his would-be master from below?<br /> <br /> Oh yes, the Warrior Setite will wait. He will play the role of the obedient hound, for now. Just long enough to find where his heart is hidden, and to turn the arrogant Ventrue into a pawn against the Aeons. The Serpent never balked from obstacles, and always relished a challenge. This merely serves as a different sort of challenge. He will not allow it to best him. Not in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T00:52:24-07:00","id":1229539,"title":"","content":"145) A Caitiff, her life was that of a modern business woman, working in a marketing firm. With her glasses and short hair, she had an attractive librarian-esque look. This and her social acumen apparently aroused the passion in her sire. During what was supposed to be a meeting to talk of an ad campaign for an art show, her sire was overcome by desire and drained her dry. Guilt motivated her to embrace the mortal, and then panic led to the pale woman fleeing. When the business woman awoke, the only sign of her assailant was a note tucked into her hand. &quot;I'm sorry. You are a vampire now. Run, or others of our kind will kill you.&quot;<br /> <br /> The newly embraced Caitiff discovered the full gravity of her undead state in the nights following, and so finally dismantled what remained of her life, making off with a briefcase full of cash and what worldly possessions she could pack. She tarried just too long, however, as other vampires attempted to murder her when she tried to give one last goodbye to her family. She leaped from a cliff in her panicked flight...and discovered that she could literally fly. It was the only thing that saved her from her attackers, who could not follow her rapid egress on the winds.<br /> <br /> For the next few years, she took refuge in a small town, where no other vampires took residence. She honed her powers of Flight, and further discovered more advanced senses and an ability to charm people. These allowed her to make a comfortable unlife amid scattered rural homes. Unbeknownst to her, her high Humanity allowed her to accidentally evade the notice of Lupines who made their homes nearby. It wouldn't be until later that she discovered, from talks with other vampires, just how precarious living in the backwaters had been. How close she might have come to death.<br /> <br /> Indeed, she didn't even know this danger before she decided to leave. She had been a young go-getter - an aspiring people person - in life. Living in isolation, in a place with no night life and no &quot;peers&quot;, was an enervating experience. Restlessness overtook her, until she resolved to return to the cities, in order to earn a place in vampire society.<br /> <br /> Her transition into larger Kindred society will not be easy, however. Caitiff and ignorant, she'll have to claw her way up just into tolerance, let alone acceptance. Still, as a woman who worked in business, she was not unused to glass ceilings. She cut her teeth on being persuasive, undaunted, and useful. And really, there's plenty utility that can be found in someone who can fly. As far as she's concerned, not even the sky is the limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 06-27-2018, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T03:10:55-07:00","id":1229555,"title":"","content":"146) In a certain Sabbat-controlled city, a Nagaraja maintains permanent residence. This is afforded by a standing agreement between her and the local Bishop, a pact struck after she did him a good turn some years back concerning a recalcitrant ghost. Much of the agreement revolves around local Sabbat using her as a convenient way to dispose of bodies inevitably created by their inhuman escapades. Their crimes get covered up, and the Nagaraja has a steady food supply. Win win, as it were.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the Sabbat is a churning vortex of atrocity and violence, so they produce not just corpses, but angry ghosts, in great supply. So they know who's services to hire when one of their &quot;tomfooleries&quot; comes back to literally haunt them. In return, the Nagaraja often asks packs to deliver messages to fellow scholars, as the Nagaraja is an adherent of the Path of Death and the Soul. She corresponds with a number of fellow scholars, in her quest to understand both life and death, and the history of the vampiric state.<br /> <br /> Unbeknownst to her erstwhile allies, the Nagaraja also works as a spy for the Tal'Mahe'Ra. Her allegiance to that sect is nominal, but it's good to keep on good terms with the rest of her bloodline. And the True Black Hand has much lore to share, in return for her surveillance. Since it's possible the Sabbat will eventually discover her duplicity, she suspects this comfortable state of affair will not last forever. Then again, she knows more than most that nothing ever does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T16:32:49-07:00","id":1231474,"title":"","content":"147) Joining that snake cult was meant to be ironic. His circle of friends heard about a cult, and decided to join as a joke. You know, because that's what you do when you're young, bored, and jaded with the world.<br /> <br /> Like his friends, he got initiated into this secret order that venerated snakes. When they got back from the temple, they all had a good laugh. So they kept going back. To make sure they weren't thrown out, they studied the material they were supposed to. Poking fun at the hokey texts together. As their membership in the order went on, though, his friends started reading the books on their own. So when he showed up to rites, he found that they all knew the material better than he did. He just figured they were really committed to the bit, so he worked to keep up. The laughs dried up some time after that; everyone was too busy studying and doing rites. But - idiot that he was - he presumed that the joke was still on.<br /> <br /> Then the rites and rituals became more...intense. His group's scholarship allowed them to advance to higher ranks of initiation. And the rites began to involve things like ritual blood letting, psychedelic drugs, and animal sacrifices to their snake god - Set. It was all starting to weird him out, but he couldn't say anything. One of his friends was advanced up a rank before anyone else, but disappeared soon afterwards. The order officials wouldn't talk about it, save to say that &quot;not all members have what it takes to handle the higher stages of initiation; pray to Set you are made of sterner stuff&quot;. The others seemed only slightly saddened by the friend's disappearance. He started to think maybe his friends didn't see this as a joke anymore.<br /> <br /> By this point, he didn't have the strength to pull out. After the next advancement, he realized why his missing friend had disappeared: the greater rites were actively dangerous. Harrowing leaps through over fire pits, walking across adder-strewn walkways, ritual near-drownings. All of his friends were willing to engage. When he privately tried to persuade one of them that maybe they were going too far, his friend - a buddy for years - snapped at him, and told him not to submit to weakness. &quot;The Aeons trap us with fear&quot;, he said, &quot;don't let yourself be chained down by them&quot;.<br /> <br /> That same friend died sometime later, in a rite gone wrong. One by one, they all did.<br /> <br /> He was left with his last old buddy at the gates of the final initiation, where the high priest would choose the one to receive the ultimate revelation. By some miracle, the poor sap had managed to make a mark for himself in the cult. It was just him and his last friend. And he'd faked it too well. Somehow, the high priest considered HIM the most worthy. He just wanted to fit in. Just wanted to go along with the joke. And he kept on keeping a straight face - an implacable mask of faux religious fervor - as he was given the &quot;honor&quot; of accepting Set's blood.<br /> <br /> Now he's a vampire - a Setite - and his position as a cult scion is a complete sham. His last friend - the only one to last as long as he did - got fed to him to slake his first thirst. Something about a sacrifice for the greater glory of Set.<br /> <br /> He's in a new city, expected to start his own cult. In truth, he's just trying to think of a way out of the nightmare his life - his unlife - has become. His initiation into the Followers of Set was a joke, alright. And the joke's on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T20:08:38-07:00","id":1233583,"title":"","content":"148) A Camarilla Malkavian whose insanity takes the form of a delusion that they are an undercover space alien. They believe that their &quot;native species&quot; are naturally vampiric (though they don't think of it in such mystical terms, preferring a &quot;scientific&quot; explanation for their blood thirst), and that all &quot;vampires&quot; are humans converted to the alien race. And that the entirety of Kindred society is an elaborate means of infiltrating Earth, so &quot;Homeworld&quot; can exercise subtle control. Hence why vampires spend so much time burrowing their roots into human society. The Malkavian thinks that they only know about this because their particular caste is designed to interface with the alien hive mind. Ergo, Clan Malkavian are the emissaries between the infiltrators and &quot;Command&quot;, while all other &quot;Clans&quot; fulfill some other purpose relevant to the infiltration (the Ventrue are obviously those given command, the Nosferatu ferret out secrets, the Brujah are muscle, the Toreador charm the Earthling populace, etc).<br /> <br /> However, this Malkavian decides that the Ventrue have done a poor job leading, since they've allowed &quot;Kindred&quot; to forget their purpose, and become distracted by politics and infighting. Large portions of the vampire population have even gone rogue, and now worship the &quot;First Sleeper Agent&quot; as some kind of god, rather than giving allegiance to their off-world alien masters. This Malkavian therefore takes it upon themself to get &quot;Kindred&quot; society back on track. But since their fellow agents have &quot;deluded themselves&quot; as to their ultimate purpose, they don't take talk of the True Masters in Space well. The Malkavian will have to be more subtle, and spread stability and unity of purpose through indirect means. This &quot;Jyhad&quot; is a waste of their time, but it's a tangle of conflict that must be worked within, since convincing &quot;agents&quot; of its folly is impossible. All the while, the Malkavian works to pursue what they think is the agenda of the alien masters, as told by visions and voices and impulses. Surely there must be some interference, if their connection to the masters is so garbled; nonetheless, the Malkavian must trust that they do their Masters' will.<br /> <br /> When not working, the Malkavian feeds their obsession with all things Alien. They visit UFO conventions and keep up with forums dedicated to sightings and abductions. They watch alien-related films and TV, read every book published on the subject, and has played Space Invaders, Destroy All Humans!, and X-Com hundreds of hours each. Their haven is filled with posters, alien plush dolls, and other extraterrestrial paraphernalia.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, they use Obfuscate to take the form of various classic depictions of aliens. In truth, they want to evolve beyond a mere drone, more human than anything. They want to change into a proper alien, like their masters in space. They don't yet know what the alien masters look like, but they are certain they will figure it out with enough research and experimentation. For this reason, they don't consider merely affecting the appearance of an alien to be enough. They want the physical form of one. As such, a long term goal of their's is to gain access to Vicissitude, to change their body, and more potent mental Disciplines, to perfect their mind.<br /> <br /> They also keep their ears to the ground concerning technology scavenged from UFOs. Both as a means of keeping tabs on how close humans are to stepping onto the galactic sphere (and thus how to stop them), and because they desperately want to be able to fly into space themself, to meet their masters. They have little hope of breaking into government bases or cracking into government mainframes looking for what they know, but the Malkavian does pay attention to those informal and underground attempts to obtain and understand alien tech. They are currently investigating leads into the Thal'hun and the Star Council.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T22:01:39-07:00","id":1233609,"title":"","content":"As a follow-up to the previous entry:<br /> <br /> <br /> 149) A Malkavian Ancillae who has similar delusions of alien origin. Except his ethos derives from older tales of otherworldly people, from when people still believed that the Moon and Mars were populated. The century or so of time has allowed him to invent an elaborate fictional history. About a Martian colony planted on Earth's moon, from which the Martians would stage infiltrations of Earth, as prelude to invasion. (He vehemently believes the Orson Welles hoax was a genuine broadcast, that was covered up by one party or another).<br /> <br /> However, whereas the neonate above is a loyalist to alien powers, the Malkavian ancillae is a rebel. He believes that the lunar colony rebelled against their Martian masters, and now work to influence Earth to their own ends, rather than the ends of Mother Mars. The ancillae is ardently in favor of this rebellion, and privately swears allegiance to the Lunar cause, which favors freedom and lunacy (naturally) over everything else. He opposes Dominate Malkavians as a matter of course, whom he sees as pawns of the Martians. He also is suspicious of hawks within the Camarilla, for he sees the warlike Martians behind them.<br /> <br /> Because of this division between loyalist and rebel, the ancillae will become the above neonate's enemy as soon as they become aware of one another. To him, their adherence to alien authority makes them sworn opponents. Moreover, unlike the neonate, the ancillae has nothing to learn from pop culture and current UFO theory. They are all based on a scientific consensus that says both the Moon and Mars are barren; &quot;obvious cover-ups&quot;, in his mind. He does subscribe to the theory that the moon landing was faked, but not because the US never went there. Rather, because the footage needed faking because Buss Aldrin et. al. clearly met the Lunar rebels, who forced them to hide the truth of their presence. Moreover, the ancillae is under the opinion that the US government made an alliance with the Moon, while the Soviet Union had a clear and obvious alliance with Mars. Since the fall of the USSR, the Martians now make deals with red China. Because of course they do.<br /> <br /> It's because of this latter Cold War delusion that the Malkavian ancillae despises the Brujah, because the latter tried to control the USSR. That Clan are the ultimate traitors against their own ethos - a Clan of rebels siding with the ultimate Martian authoritarians - and thus are not to be trusted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 07-14-2018, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T20:22:38-07:00","id":1235160,"title":"","content":"150) A True Brujah who acts as the Keeper of Elysium in a Camarilla city. As part of a social experiment, he has endeavored to find out how long he can go and how far he can drop hints before anyone realizes he's not a normal member of Clan Brujah. As such, he's surrounded himself with clues that could lead to someone realizing he's True Brujah. He goes by the name Justin Thyme, and the Elysium he keeps has an impressive collection of antique clocks, which he is constantly adding to. He makes no effort to disguise his dispassion, nor does he interact with &quot;regular&quot; Brujah to any degree in excess of what is required to perform his duties. He won't come out directly to say he's True Brujah, nor overtly display the powers of Temporis. That would be too obvious. But in every other way, he's baiting the Kindred of the city into making the connection.<br /> <br /> As of yet, no one seems to have done so. He presumes that the Nosferatu may know, but if they do they are keeping it to themselves. Plenty of people have made jokes about his name being a pun, but they see it as nothing more than an eccentricity. It's not like Kindred society is lacking in licks who take on assumed names. So he continues to wait, and wonders if he's been too subtle...or if the Camarilla is just filled with ignorant, willfully incurious people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T15:39:34-07:00","id":1239461,"title":"","content":"151) A historian and archaeologist, who got the attention of Clan Nosferatu when he began to dig (for figuratively and literally) where vampires would rather he not. Certain Nosferatu were impressed, however, by his refusal to both die and give up seeking the truth. Realizing this kind of stubbornness, intellectual acuity, and survivability could be assets, he was given the opportunity to continue his world for eternity and gain access to information no mortal is privy to, provided he abandon the sun forevermore. He accepted.<br /> <br /> For decades afterwards, this Nosferatu sought answers about ancient subjects. But, time and again, the subject that gnawed at him - that compelled him to study - was the origin of vampires themselves. For this reason, he pursued that oft verboten field: Noddism. So great was his resolve that he abandoned the Camarilla entirely - who did not publicly acknowledge Noddist theory or tolerate its study - in order to further his explorations among the Sabbat Nosferatu. Given the Clan has greater ties between its &quot;Main Clan&quot; and &quot;Antitribu&quot;, though, he is often consulted by researchers on both sides of the divide.<br /> <br /> His current project - worked on between research trips - is the construction of a mural rendition of the Book of Nod, carved into the granite walls of tunnels beneath a major Sabbat city. To preserve the text in base relief - complete with illustrations - against the ravages of time. The underground complex of tunnels would, upon completion, serve as a new and vibrant center for Noddist research. At least, that's what he hopes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T17:17:06-07:00","id":1240643,"title":"","content":"152) Gangrel are nomadic and solitary by nature, so it's a self-evident Big Deal when another vampire can inspire loyalty in one that isn't induced by Discipline or the Blood Bond. Even rarer are those who inspire loyalty in a Gangrel, who is not also a Gangrel themself.<br /> <br /> That's the sort of situation this Gangrel saw himself in. An Elder vampire managed - through nothing but word and deed - managed to earn his undying respect and eternal service. How tragic was it, then, that this Elder eventually fell to Wassail. The Gangrel staked his beloved master quickly, but could not bring himself to deliver Final Death. Their shared history was too great, as was the veneration - hell, the outright <i>Love</i> - the Outlander held for the old one. There had to be a better way. That night, he vowed to find a way to cure Wassail and bring a vampire back from cognitive oblivion. No matter how long it took.<br /> <br /> So ever since, the Gangrel has traveled the world, with the staked Wight in tow. Sometimes placed in a proper coffin, more often stuffed in a crate or large suitcase. It's a treatment the Gangrel regrets, but he doesn't feel secure letting his master's torpid body out of his sight. His master was a low generation vampire, and so makes a tempting target for Diablerists. Unable to afford leaving the old one alone for extended periods, he has to bring him along when he travels from city to city, territory to territory. He only deposits his master in places well fortified against intrusion, and even during extended stays the Gangrel will sometimes change the storage location.<br /> <br /> For now, he moves around, chasing leads about possible ways to bring a Wight back from over the edge. Dutifully bearing his heavy burden, like the good dog he is. One night, he WILL meet his master again, in an intellectual capacity. To finally talk to his <i>Friend</i> again, and have him talk back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T21:26:49-07:00","id":1243112,"title":"","content":"153) A Setite that acts as a professional extortionist. Experienced in stealth, infiltration, investigation, and technology (mainly spy tech), he grows and maintains a long list of people who pay him to keep their secrets secret. His haven is full of filing cabinets and hard drives, stuffed with incriminating evidence. His night doesn't really start until after he's made a stop around any of a number of drop-off points, to collect his cash. His burner phone has dozens of numbers on speed dial, for when he needs to get in contact with his &quot;clients&quot;. And he's quite difficult to track, as he sees to his collection duties wearing a different face every time, when he doesn't have some of his blackmail targets work off their &quot;tab&quot; by collecting stuff for him (which they don't dare steal).<br /> <br /> To his credit, he's not exactly rolling in dough from this gig, even with all the extortionist irons in the fire. Because, despite blackmailing people, he makes sure to keep the financial or &quot;favor&quot; burden on his victims light. Constant, but light. One hundred dollars a month here, an errand run there. Sometimes he'll wave payment entirely for a week, if the person agrees to come to a place so they can &quot;chat&quot; (read: sit still long enough for him to sneak up and feed on them). From this Setite's perspective, the key to a successful extortion is to make the burden of blackmail less than the price of letting the truth come to light. To make it so the cost is mild enough that it fades into the background of everyday expenses. Paying out the blackmail should be on the same cognitive level for the person as the payments they give to the power company or the grocery store.<br /> <br /> For his part, the Setite sees himself as a secret keeper. While keeping tabs on his clients, he looks for signs that their secrets might come to light, or if they come under the attention of a rival extortionist. Dispensing with those threats is, of course, the Setite merely looking out for his own self-interest, but he likes to think that solving such problems is part of his &quot;services&quot;. That his &quot;clients&quot; ought to feel grateful for him looking out for them, and only asking for a little in return. Sometimes, the people he extorts even seem to believe that. These people could make for valuable tools down the line.<br /> <br /> However, if a person he tries to extort decides they won't be blackmailed, it garners a measure of respect from him. After all, if they are willing to let the truth come out, that means they have the will to accept the consequences, if it means being free. That means they won't allow things like reputation, jobs, or &quot;the law&quot; shackle them. As he follows through with his threat to expose them, he can't help but smile at the fact that they've shrugged off another snare of the Aeons. Which means, after the fallout of the exposure, they might just be the most useful of all. It depends on how well they come out on the other side. If they seem truly exceptional, he might pull strings to have their far pulled from the fire anyway...courtesy of a Setite cult, who are always looking for new members. <br /> <br /> He knows for a fact this is a valid strategy. How do you think he got embraced in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T22:49:05-07:00","id":1243410,"title":"","content":"154) An Assamite Vizier that is also a skilled and knowledgeable combatant. A rare sort, the Vizier caste embraced her specifically because their caste tended to lack people who could fight. While on paper, it may have been for the purpose of better coordinating with Warrior Assamites, in truth her embrace was motivated by a desire to bolster the fighting ability of the Preservationist faction within the Children of Haqim. With the Web of Knives growing increasingly belligerent and extreme - and scooping up the lion's share of Warriors - the part of the Clan that seeks schism and alliance with the Camarilla needs all the muscle they can get.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say this Vizier isn't also a scholar. Indeed, she was a scholar first, before a fighter. She sometimes thinks her sire overestimated her prowess.<br /> <br /> An academic and historian, her living days were largely sedentary. Growing self-conscious of her poor physique, she hit the gym to get in shape. Having done her thesis on Medieval history, she was fascinated by western martial arts, and so added these to her training regiment. Her desire to master these skills was half utilitarian, half academic. Coincidentally, the night school she trained at had another student, a Middle Eastern woman of dark complexion and a similarly scholarly bent. This fellow student was, of course, her future sire, taking lessons to shore up the Vizier caste's abilities. Their shared interests made them fast friends, eventually leading to the older Vizier embracing her.<br /> <br /> Since the embrace, the new Vizier's obsessive nature (a product of her caste) has only deepened and broadened her interest in learning. From lessons on European grappling techniques, she's moved on to brawling, then knife fighting skills. Then her current focus shifted again, this time to the knives themselves. She's collected dozens of them, and studies both their practical forms and the artistry put into them. Despite the dangers, she's having a forge installed in her haven, so she can attempt to start making her own sharp art pieces.<br /> <br /> To her, becoming &quot;immortal&quot; was the best thing that could have happened to her. Now she has all the time in the world to pursue any subject that catches her attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T15:53:45-07:00","id":1243632,"title":"","content":"155) A Malkavian pharmacist and amateur psychologist, who operated in life during the latter years of the 19th century. As a mortal, he was staunchly atheist, see Faith as not merely a delusion, but an active impediment. When he became a vampire, his disdain for faith grew further, until he saw it as a disease.<br /> <br /> That was, until he came face to face with a mortal endowed with that most rare of traits in modern times: True Faith.<br /> <br /> Leaving him a sobbing wreck, the experience opened his eyes to new ways of thinking. So as he wiped the bloody tears from his eyes, he sat reevaluating the merits of the &quot;theistic disease&quot; he so often railed against. Being a man of science, he didn't have the passion nor the genuine fervor necessary to believe in Deities himself. But he began to wonder if there was advantages to faith, in those who could possess it. Both from a psychological angle, and from the plainly supernatural angle he experienced that night.<br /> <br /> So his current ongoing field of study is in the matter of belief. He runs experiments, studies faithful people, and tries to understand the mechanism that allows sincere belief to translate into positive results. At first his study was clinical, and he remains obsessively focused on the Scientific Method concerning his experiments. Unbeknownst to him, True Faith comes in many forms. He may soon discover that absolute conviction to an ideal - of any sort, not merely theistic - can foster True Faith. It's a change that is slowly beginning to take place inside him. Perhaps one night, he will become the paragon of Science, in the way that faithful mortal was a paragon of his religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T17:06:54-07:00","id":1243647,"title":"","content":"156) A Tremere programmer who first came into contact with Clan Tremere when he managed to crack techno-thaumaturgical defenses on a secure Tremere server. When the Clan tracked him down, they were impressed enough by his ability and his understanding of techno-magic that they embraced him, rather than just killing him. The higher ups - burned more than once by technomancers in their ranks - put him to work for a few years doing nothing but scanning important texts to digital backups. Not content to remain stagnant, he pursued his studies, and managed to graduate out of the dead-end assignment by effectively inventing a Ritual ward for an electronic copy of a text that mimicked the traditional one on its paper original. His encryption rituals are seeing adoption at many Chantries.<br /> <br /> Growing more ambitious by the day, he's started researching a new project. Combining his knowledge of Thaumaturgy and coding with the added power of finance, he aims to bake in a powerful magical effect into a Cryto-Currency of his own devising - something he's calling ThaumCoin - that will give Clan Tremere the ability to cast spells on any person who owns some of the currency. Given the fervor with which speculators collect any crypto-currency, in the hopes one of them will be the next BitCoin, he expects the project could be at least mildly successful. If nothing else, placing one of his ThaumCoins in the same cache as other crypto-currencies might be what's needed to pivot into larger financial control.<br /> <br /> At the moment, the project is in the research and planning stages. As such, he's in a bit of a rush to produce a viable product, before the crypto bubble inevitably bursts, and he loses his chance to exploit it. Clan Tremere, being skeptical of all technomancy, has refused to permit him working with fellow Tremere technomancers within the Pyramid, nor is he allowed to train or embrace researchers to his cause. Increasingly irked by these setbacks, he's begun to turn to technomancers outside the Pyramid, in secrecy. He might find like-minded spirits among Anarch technomancers, among tech-savvy Nosferatu, or even from non-vampire code wizards. All of these are potentially dangerous to involve on their own, and would certainly garner his sanction from the Tremere upper ranks if found out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T22:48:55-07:00","id":1246198,"title":"","content":"157) In the ultimate display of playing against type, a Scout Gargoyle (Lore of the Bloodlines, p. 36) that acts as a social butterfly. All clad in homemade <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lolita_fashion\" target=\"_blank\">Lolita Fashion</a>.<br /> <br /> Her first memory was awaking in a deserted car park, with her sire squatting on a fence nearby. Like all Gargoyles, the Embrace had stripped her of her living memories. Well, mostly. When she learned enough from her sire to survive on her own, she flew and sneaked about the cities. Wrapping herself in a cloud of Obfuscate, and looking for clues about who she was, and where she came from. One night, walking unseen amid the streets, she discovered a crosswalk that jogged a foggy memory. Following that wisp of recollection, she found a loft that seemed familiar. So she gained entry via a hatch on the roof.<br /> <br /> The occupant there was a young woman - a student of fashion - who stocked her loft (what the Gargoyle was almost certain was once her own) with rack after rack of clothing. Unable to be seen and intrigued, the Gargoyle perched herself on a ceiling support beam, and watched the human work. The Gargoyle observed the mortal for many weeks, then months, as the human toiled long into the night on frilly dresses and colorful cloth. When the human would pass out at her work bench, the Gargoyle would slip a blanket over her, then curiously read through foreign fashion magazines. The vampire came to understand this &quot;Lolita Fashion&quot;, and its emphasis on &quot;cuteness&quot; and &quot;youth&quot;. She also began to become energized by the enthusiasm - and dedication - with which the mortal plied her craft.<br /> <br /> Increasingly, the Gargoyle looked at herself in a mirror, and despaired. She wasn't cursed with outright hideousness, like some Gargoyles were, as she was a Scout. Nonetheless, while she could be construed as having cute qualities, she thought, she could not pass as human. Nor did she have the power, yet, to affect a more pleasing appearance. So her horns and granite-colored skin stood out, requiring her to go &quot;invisibly&quot; at all times. A fact which pained her markedly less, perhaps, than her own shoddy clothing; filthy pants and shirt plundered from a forgotten clothes line 100 miles and several weeks back. Having come to familiarity with more intricate, clean, and deliberate fashions, the Gargoyle became self-conscious about the way she presented herself.<br /> <br /> Making up her mind, the Gargoyle spent further time watching &quot;her human&quot;, this time not from a vantage of detached curiosity, but from the perspective of a student. She watched the human's deft hands working a sewing needle, and observed her work with sewing machine. When the human was asleep, the Gargoyle devoured (metaphorically) her stores of magazines, text books, and manuals. She taught herself to use the computer, so as to learn still more about the craft. Finally deriving a working understanding of the process, the Gargoyle &quot;borrowed&quot; a set of needle, thread, and scrap cloth, and took to a private perch on which to work. Her first several outfits were, predictably, awful and stumbling, but she remained persistent. And when she wandered the streets looking for sustenance, she listened to people converse, so she could practice social skills in private. When other Gargoyles were around, she practiced talking to them; others of her bloodline were baffled by her strange clothes, yet remained nominally supportive. Little ones had little enough to remain enthusiastic about, in this world dominated by more powerful vampires.<br /> <br /> The Gargoyle was working up the courage to reveal herself to her &quot;teacher&quot;, until she noticed the mortal growing pale. She thought it sickness, until the mortal collapsed when walking through her loft door. The Gargoyle, panicked, put her unconscious body to bed. As a vampire, the Gargoyle suspected the cause: another vampire was feeding on her &quot;teacher&quot;. She jealously watched over the mortal for nights, leaving only to feed, while the mortal's health improved. But the mortal knew something was wrong, ever since she passed out at the door, only to end up in bed. Eventually, her paranoia - and perhaps some Awareness - allowed her to pierce the Gargoyle's veil, for a moment. She cried out to whoever was hidden, imploring them to reveal themselves. So, reluctantly, the Gargoyle did, appearing with back turned, so her wings obscured her face.<br /> <br /> Getting over the initial shock, the human exhibited surprising courage, asking to see her mysterious benefactor's face, and complementing her on the outfit she wore. &quot;I want to see the front, if you wouldn't mind,&quot; the mortal said, almost as if to break the tension. When the Gargoyle turned around, the mortal seemed taken aback by the horns and the skin, but was further shocked as a realization kicked in. &quot;Sister?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Gargoyle did not have time to learn what the woman meant, as the mortal was suddenly struck by an irresistible urge to depart. The Gargoyle chased after - trying to stop the sister she didn't know she had - but had to cloak herself as the woman hit the streets. Following her for several miles, the Gargoyle lost her as they arrived at an aging brownstone, and the men at the door permitted the girl entry, yet seemed to notice and bar the way for the vampire. The were Ghouls, and old enough to see through a novice vampire's obfuscation. They commanded the neonate Gargoyle to leave, lest it make the Toreador Primogen angry. The Gargoyle knew enough of vampires to know that &quot;Primogen&quot; were powerful vampires, not to be trifled with or angered, and so could only watch as her sister disappeared into the building.<br /> <br /> The mortal never returned to her loft. Grief overtook the Gargoyle for a long time.<br /> <br /> Now, the grief is passed, and only a slow burning anger remains. Her only link to her past, stolen by an Elder. Probably dead - drained - or else made the Toreador's blood bound slave. Whatever the case, the Gargoyle cannot stand not knowing, nor can she allow this injustice to go unpunished. The Toreador Primogen had to pay. But a hasty attack would lead to Final Death, rather than answers or victory. To achieve her goals, the Gargoyle would need to take a more...subtle approach.<br /> <br /> Some time passed, and a new person waltzed into Elysium. A Gargoyle, as powerful vampires could tell, but one who wore ostentatious and ridiculous fashions (&quot;what a strange tableau of Victorian, Roccoco, and modern dress&quot;), and affected a chipper, outgoing demeanor. The harpies had their fun mocking her behind her back, but the Gargoyle seemed to both visibly notice and not mind. She seemed incapable of getting embarrassed. Realizing this one fell into the same sort of outrageous, shameless foolery as a Malkavian or Nosferatu, the harpies ran out of steam quickly. It wasn't so much fun to mock, when the subject didn't seem to care. Moreover, she was curiously outgoing, for a Gargoyle. She seemed to want to make friends with everybody. And she seemed to master the art of disguising herself as mortal, so her appearance could easily be ignored.<br /> <br /> While the ancillae and older neonates considered how best to use her as a pawn in their games, the Gargoyle remained focused under her childish mask. If she wanted to get a chance to destroy the Toreador Primogen and discover what happened to her sister (one way or another), she needed to insinuate herself into the vampire courts. No one told anything to the vampires who dwelt on the edge of vampire politics. Nor could one make friends and learn secrets about a Clan without really getting up in their business. So while the Gargoyle plied her craft and pursued social capital, she is always on the lookout for a chance to get close to the Toreador Primogen. Where better to slide in the knife, then standing in the same salon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 08-15-2018, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T21:43:18-07:00","id":1247283,"title":"","content":"158) A Ventrue who fancies himself a &quot;Grudge Eater&quot;, after his feeding restriction; he must feed on those who hold hatred in their heart, longing for revenge.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue keeps tabs on various parts of society. Every evening begins with a check through the news, looking for disasters and crimes. Those left behind after a car crash, or those who lost loved ones, may harbor animosity in their hearts for the ones responsible. Especially when those responsible - or who are thought to be responsible - appear to have escaped justice. The Ventrue keeps an ear to the ground in other ways, having Contacts in the courts, major businesses, and the criminal underworld. Layoffs, messy divorces, and gangland killings leave people behind. People who hold grudges.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness being a dangerous, disappointing place, there are no shortages of folks with axes to grind.<br /> <br /> Not content to merely let grudges form naturally - for no Ventrue in his right mind would leave his sustenance to chance - he will often get involved in the lives of his prospective vessels. If someone has reacted to personal offense with mere despair - or, worse, forgiveness - that's not so good for the Ventrue. So he will sidle up to his target and lend a sympathetic ear. One willing to affirm to the person what they'd never admit to themselves: that they hate someone or something, and want to go on hating them. The Ventrue nurses their hurt feelings (or rather aggravates them), so they maintain and deepen their grudge. Usually, he'll stop short of actually advocating or enabling revenge - they might come away satisfied (or dead) if they attempt as much, and that's also bad for him. On the other hand, he's seen tragedy and vendetta enough times to know that many mortals can harbor a lust for revenge that can <i>never</i> be satisfied. The pain - and the fury - doesn't go away, just because they vent it onto one person. These sorts of people - those whose grudge transcends their ability to resolve it - the Ventrue treasures above all others.<br /> <br /> Except, sometimes, he doesn't keep them poised on the razor's edge between having hate and acting upon it. Sometimes, when the whim takes him or the mortal's passion is great enough, the Ventrue will decide to help them get payback. Because the Ventrue is no perfectly detached vampire, dispassionately cultivating grudges for his consumption. This Ventrue had a vendetta, once. A vendetta born of tragedy. And because the object of his enmity suffered an unexpected demise, not by his hand, it left the Ventrue with no recourse, in a period of his life when his hate burned blackest. He'd had everything taken from him, including his revenge.<br /> <br /> Is it no wonder, then, that he'd wish, every once in a while, to help someone else achieve their's?<br /> <br /> Lastly, the Ventrue loves to ride the waves of danger, when it comes to vampire hunters. Many of these folk harbor an overwhelming hate, if they strive to hunt blood-drinkers. The Ventrue keeps an ear to the ground of the Kindred grapevine, for word of hunters operating in the area. Where possible, he leads these sorts into a trap, dividing their numbers and feeding from them individually. Those who hold no antipathy to vampires - rare, but it happens - he simply disposes of permanently. They are only a danger alive, while their deaths will drive the hunters either to despair (forcing them to retire), or to deepen their grudge. Where possible, he'll try to implant deep commands into such hunters, making them engage in actions that he can exploit.<br /> <br /> It's beyond dangerous, what he does with hunters. But he considers them a potent and persistent source of Vitae, to slake his thirst. Moreover, he simply adores the ability to stand over his defeated nemesis, making sure they know he's beaten them. He hopes to string some of them along for years to come.<br /> <br /> Moreover, unlike many of his Clanmates, this Ventrue has not skimped on Fortitude. You cannot make yourself a target and not take steps to ensure your survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-18T17:23:13-07:00","id":1255369,"title":"","content":"159) He was the host on one of those dime-a-dozen ghost hunter &quot;reality shows&quot;. His small crew would haul their recording equipment out to abandoned buildings, and pay people to fabricate &quot;witness testimony&quot; about supposed hauntings. He cut his teeth on acting from drama class and community theater, so playing the part of a stalwart expert on ghosts, braving spirit-wracked places came naturally. When a sufficient amount of footage and &quot;evidence&quot; got collected, he'd splice it together into a half-hour feature, and sell it off to networks to pad out broadcast slots. It took him all over the country, got him exercise, let him mug for the camera, and earned him a modest amount of money. Altogether a decent gig.<br /> <br /> Naturally, in a world full of real ghosts and other monsters, he was inevitably going to run afoul of something. His crew tackled a disused property on the edge of town, that came pre-packaged with rumors of hauntings and disappearances. The footage they captured throughout that night could have sold for a lot of money as a found-footage horror film, were it not for the whole crew being actually picked off one by one. Last one alive, he carried the camera valiantly (after the cameraman died horribly), staying in character to avoid breaking mentally. Apparently, the orchestrator of his misery - a Nagaraja - found his act amusing. Amusing enough to allow him to leave...just not as a living man.<br /> <br /> His new pointy teeth make him much less photogenic these nights. And the need to consume flesh weighs on him at times. Plus, he never did get the footage back, rendering all the horror and loss a complete waste. But he &quot;survived&quot;, after a fashion. Moreover, he has incredible supernatural power, and the chance to &quot;live&quot; forever. Some of his crew even persisted as wraiths, so he still has someone to talk to. At present, he's doing what he always did: traveling around with his crew, hunting ghosts, and trying to make a profit off said ghost-hunting. In this case, he does a lot less recording (though he still keeps a private video diary), for Masquerade reasons. But mortals still need intercession with the undead, and the spirits often have their own unfinished business they can trade for favors.<br /> <br /> And if nothing else, there are folks out there who are willing to pay for bound ghosts. The Nagaraja's old crewmates are growing progressively more uncertain of their future prospects, with this guy around...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T11:04:28-08:00","id":1283542,"title":"","content":"160) A Tzimisce that, in life, acted as a drug mule, transporting cocaine across the Mexican border to the US. At first, he started just moving drugs hidden inside his car. When border patrol agents became better at finding it, he lost his car and barely got away. In need of cash, he took to transporting small quantities of drugs inside his body, by ingesting balloons filled with them. Sooner or later, his luck was going to turn worse, and he ended up almost dying when a balloon burst and induced an overdose.<br /> <br /> That's when a Tzimisce found him, and saved his life with his blood. Becoming a ghoul, the mule was...&quot;convinced&quot; to work for the Tzimisce, in order to provide him with a steady stream of cash and/or drugs (because the Tzimisce had a hand in drug dealing). To &quot;make him more efficient&quot;, the Tzimisce flesh-crafted the mule's body, moving organs around to create a more accessible cavity that could hold more drugs. The physical changes and absolute servitude were distressing for the man, but he was enthralled, and furthermore had steady work. So that became the drug mule's life, for roughly ten years. He even mastered the rudiments of Vicissitude during that time, in order to change his appearance (an asset in his line of work) and provide minor alterations.<br /> <br /> Even this passed, and there came a time when ghoul and master were caught in a Camarilla attack. Both were riddled with bullets, and the Tzimisce master drained the mule of blood to restore himself. Immediately after, the poor drug mule woke again as an undead. The Tzimisce master intended to use the newly embraced whelp as a distraction to effect his own escape. This plan went awry, with the fledgling staked effortlessly by a Camarilla agent and the Tzimisce sire unceremoniously destroyed with fire. As he lay there on the ground, paralyzed and all-too-aware of his sire's demise, the fledgling thought himself thoroughly doomed. Was it really the end for him, after all he'd suffered?<br /> <br /> Not so, it seemed. The Camarilla agents took the fledgling back and interrogated him for information. Plying him with sweet, precious blood, and the promise for survival, at least, if he divulged all he knew of Sabbat activities. The drug mule knew enough about his sire's pack and contacts to be of use, to buy his unlife for the moment. Pressing his luck - having no loyalty to the sect that used and abused him, with the blood bond gone - he offered to act as a double agent for the Camarilla. The Camarilla were savvy enough to remain cautious, but knew an opportunity when they saw it. They agreed, but made sure to plant mental commands deep in his mind to keep him cooperative. He even had a method for dodging the Vinculum: he'd learned enough flesh-crafting to create a false &quot;pipe&quot; down his throat, so he didn't ingest the ritual blood.<br /> <br /> He returned to the Sabbat, who shrugged and brought him in. They needed more lackeys anyway, though this one was experienced and eager enough to please. They aren't (yet) aware that he's quite unbound by the Vinculum, though THEY are bound to the blood HE adds to the bowl. The mixture he would ingest goes into a vile, that he secrets back to the Camarilla, for use in arcane rituals when the need arises. Along with that blood, he carries all sorts of contraband. Usually information. But whenever his pack shares blood with other packs, at sect gatherings, he carries a generous helping back to his Camarilla masters. Lately, he's even been called upon to bring some blood with him to the Sabbat, hidden in his torso cavity, that he can add to the bowl. The Tremere say that he doesn't need to know what the blood will ultimately do to the Sabbat. He's smart enough not to ask too many questions. For now.<br /> <br /> In his line of work, it pays to be careful when to ask questions, and when to just listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T11:50:46-08:00","id":1283548,"title":"","content":"[For this Ravnos, I'll be using the Ravnos weakness from DAV20.]<br /> <br /> <br /> 161) &quot;Honest Andrew&quot; is a Ravnos descended from the medieval Phaedymite line, and sees himself as heir to those chivalric knights of old. Born to a British household in the fifties, he grew up hearing tales of King Arthur and his knights. In his university days, he established a student society devoted to emulating chivalry. Though the society eventually imploded due to internal strife and misfortune, Andrew's efforts brought him to the attention of a Phaedymite Ravnos - having recently woken from Torpor - who embraced him. Andrew laments his descent to a blood-sucking undead, but has resolved to carry on resolutely. He considers his current state a test of character, to be endured and used for the greater good.<br /> <br /> As his moniker implies, he has the particularly unfortunate pleasure of having Honesty as his inborn compulsion. He finds telling lies difficult, and his nature makes him disinclined to try. What keeps him from being a walking Masquerade violation is merely that he is not forthcoming about his vampiric nature. Nonetheless, Ravnos in general are despised and undesired at the best of times. An &quot;Honest&quot; one is simply intolerable for any society of vampires, and such individuals are often subject to proactive blood hunts as a rule.<br /> <br /> &quot;Honest&quot; Andrew considers this situation a challenge, if not an opportunity to do good. He travels from city to city, investigating and foiling the plots of particularly heinous Cainites, often of the Sabbat, Followers of Set, or Baali. Moreover, whenever he enters a city, he has a hand-written letter delivered to its rulers - Prince, Baron, Bishop, or other - formally announcing his presence in their territory. The mad scrambles to find and &quot;persuade&quot; him to leave are inconvenient, sure, but also virtuous. After all, if every Cainite in the city is trying to locate and put an end to the Honest Ravnos - &quot;if there can even be such a thing&quot;, the uninformed are quick to say - it just means they've diverted time, energy, and resources away from the Jyhad. Andrew avoids direct Masquerade breaches where able, so matters only sometimes result in a blood hunt forcing him out. Other times, his efforts to curtail Sabbat or Setite efforts are a boon to the locals, meaning requests for him to leave are sometimes even polite, if emphatic.<br /> <br /> Still, he's altogether too noble for his own good. Even relatively decent elders in a given Camarilla city will sink to vile lows for their own advantage. Too many have been on the receiving end of this itinerant knight's efforts for him to ever be fully secure, wherever he goes. Still, he wouldn't be a Knight Errant, ever questing for glory, if he stood in one place too long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T19:43:53-08:00","id":1285776,"title":"","content":"162) A former district attorney, turned Assamite Vizier, this woman acts as an itinerant advocate within the Anarch movement. She travels from territory to territory, acting as a lawyer in Anarch courts, where cases are judged with what passes for &quot;fair justice&quot; among the rebels and the damned. Her personal mania centers itself on the acquisition of knowledge pertaining to local Anarch law and movement-wide precedent. Whenever she enters a city, before even having secured shelter for the day, she busies herself with learning the letter and spirit of local custom. If there was a ruling made decades ago - even if most have forgotten about it - she's eager to learn it. It might be important. Or so she says.<br /> <br /> When she's learned all she can, she tackles cases with a thoroughness and professionalism that often surprises and intimidates other Kindred. As a Muslim woman of Arabic descent, living in the West, she HAD to learn to be twice as good at her job, just to break even with her white, male colleagues. That she's part of a distrusted minority as a vampire is thus hardly a change of pace. To her, helping the Anarchs come to a just - or at least well-informed - decision is its own reward. And when that decision leads to a mob of angry Anarchs, well, she's learned how to beat a hasty retreat.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it's like these people care less about their own customs and laws than she, an outsider, does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T02:23:23-08:00","id":1287002,"title":"","content":"163) In life, he was a mechanic and underground motorcycle racer. He lived for the thrill of the chase. Until one night, that is, when his bike was sabotaged by a rival motorcyclist, and he went careening off a bridge to his death. One spectator did not wish to see his talent disappear, though. So he was embraced as a Brujah.<br /> <br /> Since then, he's traveled cross country, continuing to pursue his love of technical mastery and great speed. For a time he was content participating in underground street races, as he'd always done. He soon bored of this unlife, however. He needed a new thrill.<br /> <br /> He got that thrill when traveling through the backwoods on his way between cities. Territorial Lupines took exception to his presence in their lands, and gave chase. A harrowing situation to be sure, but one that would have set his blood to pumping, were his heart not cold and still. It took every ounce of skill he possessed to maneuver the woods, and every horse of power his bike could produce to outpace his hairy aggressors. Truly a wild ride.<br /> <br /> Ever since then, starting chases - with himself as the bait - has been a favored goal of his. He's learned elementary Presence to make himself a more enticing target, Potence when he needs to carry his bike over impassible ground, and Celerity to give him the dexterity needed for riding maneuvers (as well as the ability to run if he's ever deprived of his ride). On the mundane side, he works to continue improving his mechanical skills, upgrading and fine tuning his ride for peak performance...and to add a few more unusual features. In practice, he uses these advantages to stay one step ahead of his targets. His favorite &quot;playmates&quot; are Lupines and Sabbat packs, both of whom can be easily riled into a pursuit. He's even made a few Boons, by acting as a decoy for the benefit of other Kindred.<br /> <br /> If there's anyone HE would chase, though, it would definitely be the man who sabotaged his bike, all those years ago. While he enjoys being a vampire well enough, he's got a score to settle. Which makes it a little awkward, since that rival motorcyclist, once big in underground gambling, has made some powerful friends. Not all of them human...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:31:37-08:00","id":1290689,"title":"","content":"164) A Moorish True Brujah, first Embraced in Iberia during the height of the Cordoba Caliphate. Son of a North African merchant and a minor Iberian noblewoman, he had access to Iberia's greatest libraries. His excellence in mathematics and other sciences of the day drew the attention of his sire. His love of Allah and the Prophet may have cooled following transition into a True Brujah, but he retained an intellectual belief in the cosmos as a work of divine craftsmanship. Even after centuries of political upheaval, he continued to study what would become the field of mechanical engineering long after the Muslims were driven from al-Andalus.<br /> <br /> It was his continued work in the area that caught the attention of certain members of the Order of Reason, namely of the Artificers. Prohibitions against consorting with the undead prevented him from working in person, but he maintained written correspondence with multiple Artificers for many years. Dispassionate like all True Brujah, he considered animosity towards living Mages to be an absurd impediment to the more important work of invention. After two hundred years, when members of the Cabal of Pure Thought had punished his allies and come to destroy him, he merely found it irksome that such bright minds were extinguished before their time (and that he would have to relocate his laboratory). Still, his long collaboration had borne fruit, as he'd developed a form of blood sorcery revolving around machines, making him one of the earlier vampiric technomancers. His main focus of study has been the learning of what he calls the &quot;Path of the Automaton&quot; (a modified Path of Ushabti, that uses clockwork robots instead of wax figurines).<br /> <br /> His subsequent travels saw him first in Northern Africa - where he paid his respects to the home of his African ancestors by paying for the construction of a school there (sadly long abandoned by modern times) - and then later to the Middle East, where he forged ties with many thinkers among the Ashirra. He provided clockwork servants for certain elder practitioners of Dur-An-Ki - what he considered a cheap service, in return for hospitality - yet he was surprised when they insisted they teach him a little of their own magic. He found many of their arts too mystical, except for the Music of the Spheres, which appealed to the fascination with music he held since his youth. There was something gratifying about interfacing with what he came to understand as the cosmic machine of creation. He didn't learn a great deal of this Path while he remained with the Ashirra, but continued to hone his theories on the subject ever since.<br /> <br /> Finally, his travels saw him returned to Ibera - now Spain - where he dug up his old laboratory and worked for a number of years. Sometime in the 18th century, the True Brujah fell into a sort of funk. A dry period where all progress stalled, and he couldn't focus on his work. Moreover, he found himself alienated in Christian Spain, centuries after he left, which made fitting in difficult. Resolving to sleep off his existential ennui, he entered Torpor, which lasted until the 1930s, when his basement lair was nearly bombed during the Spanish Civil War. Waking amidst fighting going on topside - fighting of a nature and ferocity he'd not seek the like before - he elected to flee, though with regret that he could only take so much of his library with him. Not liking any part of the present war - nor what he could well see was a yet larger war brewing elsewhere in Europe and the Middle East - he finally decided to travel to those &quot;American colonies&quot; they'd all made such a fuss about, last time he was awake.<br /> <br /> He currently maintains a new workshop beneath a university devoted to engineering. These new technologies - electricity, motors, and even computing - both daunt and intrigue him. He's had much to study - much to catch up on - and he's reconnected with members of his Bloodline. If he hasn't already, he considers Embracing his own progeny, so he has students to teach. And of course, there's that matter of his old haven, abandoned during the Spanish Civil War. Adapting to the times has taken all his attention, so he hasn't been able to travel himself. If he creates progeny, he may send them out to loot the workshop. However, he isn't against rewarding any Kindred who would return it for him...so long as they actually DO return his materials, rather than exploiting it themselves. If he found out about such a thing, he would positively HAVE to intervene. His work and research cannot fall into just any idiot's hands, now can it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 02-22-2019, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T21:00:09-08:00","id":1292060,"title":"","content":"165) Hanna White grew up with a very sick sister who lapsed into a coma. With her parents letting all the attention they got for being &quot;so brave and selfless in their dedication to her and their activism&quot; go to their heads, they let her sister stay in her comatose state when pulling the plug would be more humane. So Hanna pushed her unhappy feelings about her sister's suffering down and trained to become a nurse straight out of high school.<br /> <br /> When her sister died and seeing her parents take advantage of all the sympathy it made her snap. Too many people were suffering and wishing for death and she would be the one to secretly help them. Eventually, she got caught, was tried, and was about to be sent to jail if her sire (Brujah) didn't intervene by ambushing the van she was in and sneaking her out. Hanna sees her embrace as a chance to continue her work and bring peace to those who suffer and make sure those that benefit off of the sufferer feel that pain (like luring them to a Sabbat pack to be used in a ritual).<br /> <br /> Now what would be a good Path for her to follow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T05:05:01-08:00","id":1292733,"title":"","content":"[This might be cringe-worthy, but let's get Meta, shall we?]<br /> <br /> <br /> 166) The fascination with Japan and its culture was a completely genuine phenomenon in the 90s, not influenced by any vampires; mortals crave the novel and exotic. But if you want to know the origin of the practice among Kindred of carrying and wielding Katanas - in actual combat, on the streets of modern western cities - you're probably looking for the enigmatic vampire named David Blade (<a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/name/nm1563220/\" target=\"_blank\">no relation</a>). Or, as Katana enthusiasts among Kindred call him, &quot;Master David&quot;.<br /> <br /> He showed up one night in 1990, with stories saying he'd traveled to Japan, braving the lands of the mysterious eastern vampires, and returned with ancient knowledge of Japanese swordplay. When occasion had saw fit to see his skill witnessed by a group of Anarchs, they flocked to him, wanting to learn how to use the Katana. Within a couple years, it seemed like every young Lick was wielding a Katana and wearing trench coats (for the record, the trench coats arose on their own, though David himself cannot argue the utility that came from a long coat that can hide a blade). Most of these practitioners weren't his students, but rather the knowledge spreading around as he taught what he knew and those students then taught what THEY knew. He's even admitted that nothing would have stopped Kindred from adopting the Katana on their own; he was just the earliest in the west, and the one who advocated its use. He also taught his students how to best utilize their Disciplines in conjunction with the weapon...though often, such lessons centered on how not to accidentally break their weapon from excessive application of Potence.<br /> <br /> As the 90s transitioned into the Aughts, western culture lost its fixation on all things Japanese. Greater connectivity through the Internet meant that David's knowledge was no longer rare, and people (living or undead) began to explore other forms of melee combat, including European blade arts (helped by a series of Elders, who got motivated to teach their childer how to use a &quot;real&quot; sword). Plus, with the Japanomania wearing off, people started to see David Blade as kind of...problematic; an American running around, championing the merits of &quot;Glorious Nippon Steel!&quot; (though he himself hadn't used that phrase since the very early days) smacked of cultural appropriation. This also seemed to be the time frame when &quot;Master David&quot; both grew more tired of taking students and more adept at Obfuscate. So he faded from view. He currently wanders back and forth between America, Europe, and Japan, taking very occasional students or dispensing specific lectures.<br /> <br /> But the question of his origins and Clan still lingered, unanswered. He seemed skilled in the physical Disciplines, but seemed most adept at Auspex and Obfuscate. This lead many to assume he was either a Caitiff, or a Malkavian with a particular monofocus. No one knows for sure, as he doesn't speak of it.<br /> <br /> The truth is far stranger, but far more understandable when one learns that David Blade always wears a bandanna. He's a Salubri, specifically a Wu Zao (or &quot;Watcher&quot;), having been Embraced back in the eighties when he traveled to Japan. His dedication to learning traditional swordplay from old masters caught the attention of a Watcher, who saw potential both in the Gaijin's skill and in the prospect of getting more eyes out in the West. One would assume David's caste-defined monofocus would manifest around his love of Japan as a culture, but it seemed to latch on to the art and application of Japanese swords. That he returned wearing bandannas all the time was chalked up by Kindred to him being a Japanophile (what modern folk would call a &quot;Weeaboo&quot;), allowing him to pass unnoticed despite that it conspicuously masked his forehead.<br /> <br /> Since the teaching business slowed down, David Blade (for the record, that's obviously not his real name; then again, no Kindred bats an eye at Licks with assumed names) has continued his blood-driven interest in swordplay. He's sought out old masters (mortal, vampire, ghost, and in records), and even braved vampire-kind's instinctive fear of fire in order to begin learning the forging process. True to his Watcher roots, he's sought magical secrets concerning the Katana; ancient scrolls documenting old rites, and delving into tombs and ruins for cursed blades. He may end up trying to develop blood sorcery, focused entirely on channeling magic through his sword. These are all long-term goals.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, his activities have made and still make enemies among supernaturals. He's pissed off Mages of the Akashayana and Dreamspeakers, for stealing knowledge and Wonders. Many Elder vampires in the west despise him, for being the one who perpetuated an annoying trend among neonates, often leading to Elder final deaths. And naturally, the Japanese Wan Kuei despise him, both for being a bastard progeny of Zao-lot, and for being a filthy gaijin, coming into their territory and appropriating their traditional ways. Moreover, his (&quot;stolen&quot;) skill makes him a juicy target for swords-vamps, looking to test their own skill and increase their prestige by besting &quot;Master David&quot; in a duel. He walks these nights cloaked in obfuscation as much for his desire for peace as anything else.<br /> <br /> He's a divisive figure, to be sure, but some Kindred (even his opponents) think the modern nights are more interesting for his presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-01-2019, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T17:47:29-08:00","id":1292890,"title":"","content":"^^^^ I dig it!<br /> <br /> And I see David's affinity and practice of Japanese culture being more a case of assimilation and not appropriation. Big difference.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T21:02:18-08:00","id":1292930,"title":"","content":"167) A Toreador art forger. <a href=\"https://www.sleek-mag.com/article/art-forgers/\" target=\"_blank\">This character is inspired by some of the best known art forgers</a>. That an art forger would be a Toreador feel perfect. It becomes interesting if an elder buys a forgery, or something similar. However, this character takes it a step further. She forges Noddist and kindred (non-magical) relics and artifacts. Then she releases them, through back channels and anonymously, just to create confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T17:28:52-08:00","id":1293922,"title":"","content":"168) A Malkavian who is blind since birth or since she was an infant, and her derangement is that she refuses to believe that there is a world that you can see. She gets increasingly paranoid as people talk about sight and concepts related to sight, going from mild irritation to a downright frightening anger, frustration and sadness that everyone is always lying to her and that there's some kind of worldwide conspiracy to maintain the lie and keep her isolated and confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T17:32:06-08:00","id":1293924,"title":"","content":"169) A scary Malkavian that tries to make himself immortal by embracing suitable people and trying to make them into complete copies of himself through blood bonds, viccissitude, dementation, dominate, and twisted mental conditioning. Once he manages to create persons that both look and behaves like him, he is confident that it'll make him functionally immortal, as the divide between the self and the other will break down, and he and his clones will be the same person in the eyes of God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T17:39:30-08:00","id":1293925,"title":"","content":"170) A vampire that was on a Path of Enlightenment, but has found that he longs to feel true warmth, love and happiness in his heart again, and devoted himself to the herculean task of trying to regain his Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T17:45:01-08:00","id":1293927,"title":"","content":"171) The coolest player character in my current chronicle, a Rat Pack musician in 1960s Las Vegas who got embraced by a Nosferatu who adored his musical skill. He is still a gallant soul that loves to perform and get ovations from an adoring audience, but needs to reconcile this with the fact that he is now a wretched creature who'd make people flee in fear if his Obfuscate ever faltered. He is bitterly jealous of other talented musicians, who aren't hideous beasts, and tries to blood bind or bully them to suck up to him, as he desperately wants to be the biggest star.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T17:49:19-08:00","id":1293929,"title":"","content":"172) A formely Sabbat Lasombra who got taken prisoner or surrendered to the Camarilla when the city was conquered by them. The new prince has elected to keep her alive and roam relatively free, albeit blood bond, as she has many connections in the city that are useful to him, and furthermore can be used as a hostage against the threath from her powerful sire, who loves her dearly and is now forced to stay away. But will he truly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:40:08-08:00","id":1294867,"title":"","content":"173) A Toreador art researcher.They revel in the hunt for providence and ownership of art pieces. They were looking into what appeared to be sloppy paperwork showing a 150 year gap between transactions for a minor impressionist painting, everything showed the art was authentic, but during their research they uncovered an elder's art collection. They were embraced to solve this problem of people looking into things, by forging documents and histories. They hate what they have become, but being around such hidden masterpieces is intoxicating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24591-sparkeyg","name":"SparkeyG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T23:06:44-08:00","id":1295505,"title":"","content":"174) In life, he was a private detective in the most Noir sense. Complete with trench coat, hat, and smoking habit. And in the most Film Noir move imaginable, the chain of events that would kill him started with a pretty woman walking into his office. He learned later it was a Toreador, who hired him to investigate a missing person's case. The missing person, in fact, was the Toreador's prospective childe. The kidnapper was...the Toreador. And it wasn't a kidnapping.<br /> <br /> What the detective pieced together - but just too late - was that his entire investigation, including the descent into the seedy underbelly of the city, was the Toreador's attempt to determine how air-tight the childe's disappearance was to mortal society. To figure out exactly where the trail could be picked up by mortals, so she could come along and scrub that trail clean. He'd been a patsy to an absurd and useless plot, and now he was a loose end. He'd seen too much; he'd already figured out the whole &quot;hidden vampire conspiracy&quot; angle. So when he was cornered at gunpoint in the depths of a sewer, he was given the courtesy of one last smoke before he was riddled with lead.<br /> <br /> But while it was the end of his life, it wasn't the end of his story. His perforated body tumbled down a pipe and washed out to a gutter a quarter mile down the way, still barely alive.<br /> <br /> That's where his sire found him. A rotting carcass that stank worse than the sewer, but ambled on anyway. The Toreador wasn't the only one who followed the detective's case with interest.<br /> <br /> He's a Samedi now, but remains committed to the noir detective lifestyle. Unlifestyle. He works more night cases now, because of his particular condition. He relies on his Obfuscate to get him work, and his Fortitude to carry him through the fire and fury. He takes a special pleasure in freaking out Toreador clients, and shaking them down for all they're worth. He still stinks, and his clothes constantly need heavy laundering. But on the upside, he can look forward to a long career. AND he can smoke all he wants. His lungs already rot and grow back on the regular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T18:42:10-07:00","id":1295712,"title":"","content":"A different version of the noir character...<br /> <br /> 175) He's an investigator for the Tremere - looking into mortal cults, human reported sightings of the supernatural, faith healers, supposed shamanism, authors of popular occult books that seem know a little too much, etc. However, with in that he is a purely Sam Spade or Philip Marlowe type of character. Or was - the Tremere destroyed his ethical core. His standard operating procedure is to kill any one or anything with actual knowledge or real power that cannot be made to serve the Tremere. His own blood magic is modest, but he is effective at destroying anyone who does not suit the local regent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T09:57:06-07:00","id":1295859,"title":"","content":"176) Never came up with a name for the character, but he's one I mentioned to my table in a discussion about fun character ideas a few years back and got explicitly banned from playing. <b><i>Ever</i></b>. Let's call him, &quot;Chuck&quot;.<br /> <br /> Chuck was a restaurateur and cuisine savant, winning his first Michelin star at 23 and having been awarded three stars before the age of 30. After securing a book deal and several appearances on food shows and marrying an up-and-coming model and influencer, he was well on his way to celebrity chef and social media darling status when the unthinkable happened: a hit and run car wreck that left his young wife dead and him horrendously disfigured.<br /> <br /> Just kidding! A Nosferatu nailed his car, intending to kill him and Embrace his wife as a Cleopatra. It was pure happenstance Chuck had a bit much to drink that night, so she was driving when the Nosferatu slammed into the driver's side which killed her on impact. Having to improvise, the Nosferatu set the car on fire and fled. Learning later Chuck survived the wreck and fire, but was left disfigured which would be the end of his celebrity chef career, the Nosferatu stole into his home and Embraced him. Except, Chuck came out the other side...<i>wrong</i>.<br /> <br /> See, Chuck learned nothing from the &quot;humbling&quot; effect of the Nosferatu Embrace. His Obfuscate worked on camera, and worse, his blood lacked the foul properties of typical Nosferatu blood, and he had an uncanny knack for Dominate. His sire accidentally slipped early on he was responsible for the car wreck that killed his wife, and ended his rise to celebrity. This, understandably, caused him to develop an intense hatred for his own sire, and he rejected his own clan to strike out on his own.<br /> <br /> For now, Chuck retains his restaurateur status, capitalizing on his story of personal tragedy, re-branding himself as a connoisseur of all things alcohol, and changing his restaurants' concepts to invitation-, membership-, and reservation-only luxury gastro lounges that offer haute cuisine alongside the world's choicest alcohol selections, in cutting-edge decoration and weekly offerings of performance and visual art from around the world, and in an environment that allows relaxation and discretion in his most prominent clientele.<br /> <br /> Chuck excuses his behavioral &quot;eccentricities&quot; (i.e. only being out at night, etc.) as business choices and the consequence of emotional trauma, and justifies his rapid improvement in appearance (Mask) as reconstructive surgery and make-up. Otherwise justified questions about his business strategies (Why only be open at night? Why prohibit walk-in dining?) tend to get pushed down due to whacko Pizzagate-style conspiracy theories that Chuck and his most-trusted associates <i>may or may not</i> be anonymously propagating online to discredit critics. The occasional drop of blood in a key patron's food or drink, or subtle command here or there, doesn't hurt either. Neither does it hurt that competing restaurants, pubs, and lounges tend to get knocked down by strings of health code violations.<br /> <br /> Chuck's relationship with other Nosferatu is...<i>unique. </i>He really doesn't like his own clan, and as a result he tries to cozy up with, of all vampires, the <i>Toreador</i>. He's not <i>completely</i> hated by them, his social niche serves its purpose, and they're willing to deal when it suits their purposes. On the other hand he'll never be accepted by them, and Toreador being Toreador, look at him under the best of circumstances as a novelty or pet, but most of the time he's an unwelcome interlocutor with a profile high enough they simply can't get rid of him.<br /> <br /> Other Nos find this hilarious, and they love to egg him on by behaving as deplorably as possible around him while keeping him completely out of the loop on their own schemes; most expect him to come around, eventually, especially once his attempts to weasel his way into the Torries' good graces inevitably bite him in the ass. It doesn't hurt Chuck's case that he's found a way to muscle in on territory typically controlled by the Toreador, and that <i>really</i> sticks in their craw. They're not <i>too</i> worried about the Masquerade for the moment, since he has a good grasp on how to maintain it and keeps the environment surrounding him tightly controlled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 03-11-2019, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T20:53:55-07:00","id":1296030,"title":"","content":"[While the Bloodline as such is controversial, I'd like to take a crack at the DAV20 Niktuku. For extra points, one embraced in the modern day.]<br /> <br /> <br /> 177) He and his girl were the talk of school. She was the prom queen, him the handsome, self-styled bad boy. Until one night they were returning from the local drive in theater, when another car drove them off the road. He awoke at the wheel, a little banged up, to see a bunch of ugly sons of bitches - a pack of Nosferatu Antitribu - taking turns draining his girlfriend dry. He tried to stop them, but they were too strong. They stood over his beaten body, one of them prepared to &quot;do a number on that pretty face&quot; of his. He was only saved by the oncoming lights of a passing patrol car.<br /> <br /> The police figured it was a passing band of miscreants, but the people of their small town didn't trust him. He'd always been a &quot;bad seed&quot;. But they didn't get a chance to drive him out of town, before he made pursuit of his girlfriend's killers. From there, he spent two years traveling, stopping in small cities along the road and honing his skills as a vampire hunter. From backwoods folk, he learned to fire a bow; they were quieter than guns, and had a chance to stake the target outright if his aim was true. For a time, he mostly eliminated weak or small time licks; Caitiff and Thin Bloods, that he caught along the road. He wouldn't tolerate any of them to live.<br /> <br /> At last, he tracked the pack of Sabbat Nosferatu to their resting place. He flushed them out with fire, slaying three. He was unable to best the last survivor, however. The lick who'd threatened to cut up his face proceeded to nearly kill the young hunter. Timely application of a flaming board drove the vampire off, but unfortunately also let the creature escape. Dying, he screamed at the monster, demanding it come back so he could kill it. Cursing and vowing revenge, though he was fast bleeding out.<br /> <br /> Until a figure, as hideous as any Nos, appeared behind him, clapping in glee at the young mortal's cocksure display. This Niktuku had followed in the hunter's wake, admitting that he'd intended to kill the mortal (for robbing the Hungry bastard of potential meals). But seeing the young man's ferocity, tenacity, and beauty had stoked feelings in the Niktuku's cruel, dead heart. Feelings of admiration. &quot;What will you do, boy hunter?&quot; he said, a mocking grin made from behind a chapped, once-beautiful mouth. &quot;What would you trade to exterminate your foes? Would you give up your life? Your beauty? Your humanity? I can give you new life, after a fashion, and the ability to feed on their strength. Would you willingly become a vampire that hunts vampires?&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly, the old lick didn't need to ask. It was no question at all.<br /> <br /> The young man remains a wanderer, a hunter, and, for the moment, beautiful. He's just no longer alive, and pursues his prey with an intensity borne not of loss, but of hunger. In his private moments, when the trail goes cold, he laments how hard it is to remember <i>her</i> face. It's been decades now. He takes the slightest bit of solace, knowing that if he ever forgets her completely, it will be when he's become so ugly that she wouldn't want him anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T18:19:19-07:00","id":1297407,"title":"","content":"178) A career sailor - occasional privateer - who in life operated in the Caribbean, he held a particular passion for scrimshaw and bone-carving. His skill at etching scenes into bones attracted the attention of his sire: a Cappadocian refugee who'd finally been run out of his hiding place in Europe by the Giovanni. When the Elder took shelter in Haiti, he discovered the sailor's remarkable craft in the stall of a night market clerk, who pointed the Cappadocian in the sailor's direction.<br /> <br /> Turns out, it's not just Toreador who can appreciate good artwork. It helped first that it was bonecraft, and second that the sailor possessed a knack for conveying deep information in the carvings. It tickled the old scholar's love of history.<br /> <br /> Since his Embrace, the sailor has made it a personal journey to travel the oceans, learning as much as he can about the world, the Kindred in it, and the art of bonecraft. His sire instilled in him an appreciation for recording events; bones outlast paper, and are much harder to burn. He's left hundreds of pieces lying around, documenting in sculpture many movements of the Jyahd over the years. At least, such that the sailor is aware of. Many necromancers collect his works, both for the insight they may gain, and for the joy of possessing such unique, well-crafted pieces.<br /> <br /> He's also been known to study Kine, too. When he's had the occasion to befriend a mortal - because of his hunted &quot;bloodline&quot;, he watches but does not readily engage with other Kindred - he will learn their personal stories. Then, when that mortal passes on, he'll return years later and etch those stories on their bones. One last, final testament to the people they were. He's also been known to do this on bodies he finds that catch his interest. If he cannot learn about such persons second hand, he can always summon their spirits and learn about it from the most primary of sources.<br /> <br /> Whether it's to dodge the Giovanni, a desire for new stories, or simply personal preference, he is itinerant to a fault. He pilots a personal sailing craft from port to port, from South America to Africa, up to Iceland and the Mediterranean (though, for the Venetian necromancers, he doesn't stay there long), and down and around to India and Australia. Inheriting an animosity to the Camarilla Elders who betrayed his Clan, he has more sympathies for the Anarchs than anyone. Still, he'll play nice in whoever's territory he's in. No use rocking the boat. Not when he can fade into the background and watch events unfold.<br /> <br /> Currently, he's parked his boat out in Africa, carving the stories of the Libertatian Fleet into the bones of Atlantic sharks and felled Savannah beasts that come out from inland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T22:31:47-07:00","id":1299862,"title":"","content":"179) A Malkavian who fancies himself a neo-Socratic. Complete with toga.<br /> <br /> Originally a student of classical literature, this deep education into philosophy stuck with him following the Embrace. He travels from city to city, and hangs out at Elysium. There, he engages Kindred of all stripes - Elders and Neonates, Ivory Tower and Anarch, etc - in philosophical discussions. And like any good student of Socrates, he employs the Socratic Method. No statements of fact, merely questions. In the hopes of forcing them to examine their base assumptions, and realize how little they actually know.<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly, the reason he moves around so much is because of his penchant for pissing off the vampires in power. Multiple Domains have declared Blood Hunts on him, for no other reason than because his reasoned oration and insightful observations or questions have a tendency to make any and all vampires look foolish. However, that tendency to make them look like fools is often what saves him from Final Death. When a Prince calls for his blood, simply because he asked them questions, it often makes the Prince look bad, and/or incompetent. Not to mention that overreaction to the Malkavian - up to and including Frenzy - reflects poorly on any Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T10:13:18-07:00","id":1299991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1292060#post1292060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">165) Hanna White grew up with a very sick sister who lapsed into a coma. With her parents letting all the attention they got for being &quot;so brave and selfless in their dedication to her and their activism&quot; go to their heads, they let her sister stay in her comatose state when pulling the plug would be more humane. So Hanna pushed her unhappy feelings about her sister's suffering down and trained to become a nurse straight out of high school.<br /> <br /> When her sister died and seeing her parents take advantage of all the sympathy it made her snap. Too many people were suffering and wishing for death and she would be the one to secretly help them. Eventually, she got caught, was tried, and was about to be sent to jail if her sire (Brujah) didn't intervene by ambushing the van she was in and sneaking her out. Hanna sees her embrace as a chance to continue her work and bring peace to those who suffer and make sure those that benefit off of the sufferer feel that pain (like luring them to a Sabbat pack to be used in a ritual).<br /> <br /> Now what would be a good Path for her to follow?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think she did to her parents?<br /> Drama demands she did something to them. Or wishes of doing. Or will do.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> my next chronicle will definetly have a Samedi detective. I need a Samedi detective. Now I want to play a Samedi noir detective with a cool hat.<br /> <br /> 180) Sir Alfred of Winchester AKA Loki AKA Dance with Coyotes<br /> <br /> Born Alfred of Winchester in England in 1033 AD as the third son of an important noble family, he got &quot;educated&quot; about the unfairness of the world at large by a powerful Ravnos witch.<br /> Once a stalwart defender of the institutional order, his Clan Curse manifested in the vice of breaking the laws of societies.<br /> Traveling Europe in search of a land where he wouldn't be tempted to breaking its laws, he found out the problem wasn't in the law themselves but in the special <i>gusto</i> he felt in breaking the laws.<br /> After becoming an elder in XV century he adopted the name of the norse god Loki. He deemed it appropriate for himself, due to his mastery of illusions, his own growing ego and his penchant of causing &quot;mischief&quot; in every domain he visited. He was a well known troublemaker to every Prince of northern europe at the time, due to his temptation of breaking some vampiric traditions. But as a 7th generation elder he managed to survive and do what he wanted.<br /> When the Anarch Revolt exploded he was in truth envious of the rebellious faction that was actually shattering institutions reputed old as the world itself. He was very tempted to help them. He, in fact, did that and helped a few anarch packs destroy a few methuselah. But he was still an elder and the nascent sabbat was becoming increasingly diablerie-prone.<br /> He had to flee and sought new lands in the americas, one of the few kindreds to take that option.<br /> Some old feelings and desires resurfaced and he tried to live amongst the natives in search of a completely different society.<br /> Yet his vice hit again and again, tempting him into breaking the traditions of the american people. But he always tried to do so without killing and without violence, when possible. He sincerely enjoyed living amongst the natives, or at least as much as an old vampire can. He kept wandering from tribe to tribe, breaking local laws, but the population came to respect him as a wandering natural force of the night, who could talk with the animals, withstand any mortal weapon, and made dreams come true albeit for a mere moment.<br /> Amongst the emigrated europeans he still kept breaking the laws of the old world, and this new player, this new vampire society known as the Camarilla was... a funny plaything. With strongly enforced vampiric laws, Traditions. Laws to break. Alfred was descending into inhumanity, indulging in his vice too much. He wasn't violent of sadistic, yet. But it was a more subtle way for his Ravnos Beast to drag him down.<br /> Something changed when in following a new tribe of natives he met this shaman. He thought he was a shaman. What was surprising was not only he discovered Alfred was a Cainite, but that when he caught the vampire in the act of desecrating an important sacred ground in order to break very old traditions... The shaman joined him! He explained it was to teach the tribe a lesson. It was Coyote's idea, and that Alfred was acting his part as a trickster that must exist to subvert society's known and comfortable order and teach the people lessons. Or so the shaman, actually a rare werecoyote, believed. The Garou amongst the human tribe didn't. Outnumbered and on the run, the odd pair somehow ended up being vital for defeating a Wyrm creature brought to the americas by the Wyrmbringers that was hidden under the sacred ground and corrupting the humans slowly. The Garou thanked the Nuwisha and the Ravnos they called &quot;Dance with Coyotes&quot; (this legend still told amongst the Uktena). Alfred licked this new name and adopted it. He parted ways from the werecoyote a few months later, but he tried to learn more about this &quot;trickster&quot; role he talked about.<br /> In 21th century US he travels from city to city breaking Traditions. Being almost a millenia old there's nothing much anyone can do to stop him, but he's surely on a good path to enter the Red List and a few Archons actually wants his head. And some Sabbat people remember his face from his &quot;Loki&quot; days, and they're very old too now.<br /> But the trickster still wanders, and where he comes the unnatural order of society gets disrupted, new Ravnos get Embraced without permission, some minor Masquerade breaches happen without knowing who made them, some Kindred meet Final Death. But Dance with Coyotes is deceptive, quiet, careful, and powerful.<br /> No one knows how he survived the Week of Nightmares and maybe no one will, for he has no friends nor allies.<br /> He's not a person anymore. He's a natural force of the night, as the natives believed. Or so he fancies himself. He tricks himself into believing so. For the Ravnos Beast is a devious one and it will be what finally brings this old monster down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T20:05:54-07:00","id":1304381,"title":"","content":"181) A Malkavian technomancer who was Embraced at age 15 or so. As such, he calls himself &quot;the Eternal Boy Genius&quot;. Needless to say, his derangement is Megalomania.<br /> <br /> He just...showed up, one night, at a small domain. With his presence, the domain's Kindred population reached a nice, round half-dozen. Mostly, his &quot;peers&quot; are a handful of Anarchs and Caitiff, and one Autarkus with no apparent interest in politics. As such, when the &quot;Boy Genius&quot; came in and insisted on being recognized as the Prince, no one was in any position or inclination to argue. After all, he might have strange, technological blood sorcery, but he's still just one Neonate. If matters got really bad, they could all just leave.<br /> <br /> The source of the Malkavian's &quot;Science(!)&quot; is a mystery to everyone. Save an offhand remark, where he grumbled angrily that the &quot;Sons&quot; will rue the night they &quot;denied true brilliance&quot;. What is known is that, when angered he can spit lightning like the best of them. He's not mad enough to endanger the Masquerade, but he longs for the day when everyone - Kindred and Kine alike - can witness and recognize his greatness.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, he toils in his Haven, expanding his knowledge of technomancy. The place hosts a lab, and a handful of ghouled assistants, eager to please (and learn from) their master's genius.<br /> <br /> But his activities are not all contemplative or experimental in nature. The Malkavian has designs for the nearest Kindred population center. Like all good Megalomaniacs, he resents being relegated to the outskirts of vampiric civilization, desiring to gain the power and adulation he &quot;rightly deserves&quot;. So what if the Kindred in the big city have centuries on him? That just means they're horribly outmoded. Behind the times. Unfit to adapt to the age of technological wonders, as he is. They, too, shall fall, acting as stepping stones for his own glorious ascent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 04-15-2019, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:04:00-07:00","id":1306930,"title":"","content":"182) A Ventrue antitribu who, like his Bishop sire, suffers from the Flesh of the Corpse flaw (V20, p. 483). While his sire has weathered enough battles over the centuries that he must go covered in flowing robes and an ornate ceremonial helmet, the childe has only taken light damage that is visible on the face. Every night, he strategically applies band-aids and minor bandages, to appear as only lightly hurt. It's a serviceable cover for occasional mortal contact, but hardly a permanent solution. Which is unfortunate, given that the Ventrue is a member of the Order of St. Blase, who work closely with mortals on behalf of more inhuman Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Part of the character's desire to work in St. Blase is out of disgust for those same inhuman Sabbat. Every time he meets the more &quot;typical&quot; Cainite, they always give him shit for &quot;playing with his food&quot;, and for him not being a warrior like his sire. His sire mostly goes fully clad for the sake of pragmatism, not because he despises his appearance (also, he gets sadistic glee subjecting the unknowing to his horrid countenance). The childe, however, tolerates his condition much less. He was vain as a mortal, and his vanity rankles at the loathsome state of his body. Not just as it is, but that it will only ever get worse from here. Over a long enough time frame, he'll look just like his sire, eventually. He hates that fact most of all. That and his sire, who inflicted the fate on him. This is not what he signed up for when he was promised immortality.<br /> <br /> As such, he avoids combat like the plague. Any sort of danger, really. He invests highly in Fortitude, simply in the hope of mitigating or avoiding further damage. Keeps ghouled guards around, just to be safe.<br /> <br /> All the while, he burrows his tendrils into mortal society. Not content merely pulling strings on behalf of the Sword of Caine, he's interested in acquiring power. It keeps various packs off his back, and alerts him to Camarilla spies looking to put down roots in Sabbat-held territory. Most of all, though, he has his sights on his sire. That hateful, hideous creature who inflicted the defective curse on him. One night, that old bastard WILL pay. Everything else is negotiable, including the character's own sect loyalty...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T14:54:59-07:00","id":1307591,"title":"","content":"183) They call him Johnny Reb, because he considers himself the last true Confederate soldier. At least, the only one &quot;alive&quot; who still refuses to surrender to the hated Yankees.<br /> <br /> During the Civil War (the &quot;War for Sourthen Independence&quot; as he calls it), he served in the Confederate army for his home in Alabama. Not for anything like &quot;protecting slavery&quot; (though, on par with the time and place, he has no affection for African Americans), but because the Union invaded his home. After years of fighting - wherein he took many bullets at different times and survived - he finally seemed to meet his match during a black powder explosion. Burned over much of his body, he lay dying in a hospital tent. For that, though, the fire in his heart for the hated Northerners still burned, and he approached death still trying to get up and fight. This display of rage - of utter commitment to his cause - impressed a Brujah that stalked the tents to feed on the dying.<br /> <br /> To this day, Johnny Reb sports a Confederate uniform (though a reproduction; all the originals rotted away long ago). Of course, he's inclined to cover it with a long coat, when he must go under cover. When on the prowl against Northerners, however, he wears his gray openly. He wants to remind the &quot;damned Yankees&quot; that the South WILL rise again. For his crusade - and because he cannot bring himself to feed from Southern whites (Prey Exclusion, V20 p. 485) - Johnny Reb spends much of his time stalking the streets of states north of the Mason-Dixon line. When he cannot stomach Yankee lands anymore, he stays in the moldering house of his family's ancestral state. Feeding from impoverished black farmers, and quietly disposing of tourists and travelers stupid enough to come trespassing on his property. It's not HIS fault the city declared his house abandoned.<br /> <br /> Presently, he's back home, working with Camarilla forces to jettison the Sabbat from Alabama. Some of the Camarilla are damned Yankees themselves, but others are right and proper antebellum sorts, so they're alright with him. It's those Sabbat who are the problem right now, who come out from Mexico to try doing what the Union couldn't.<br /> <br /> Naturally, very few Kindred born in the last hundred years can stand &quot;Johnny Reb&quot;. Unless, of course, they are Southerners themselves. Especially the neo-Confederates. For his own part, Johnny Reb considers the modern acolytes of Dixie to be well meaning, but ultimately <i>failures</i>. &quot;They just sit in their homes, watching this 'RED Network' on the Idiot Box, and bitching about how miserable they are. So few want to do a damn thing but whine. Those that do spend more time lynchin' ******s than something productive. A god-damned waste. Makes me want to stab my guts and puke blood.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 05-16-2019, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T16:48:24-07:00","id":1307616,"title":"","content":"<b>184)</b> It started as a curiosity, a one in a billion chance of ever coming to pass. But one night, the stars aligned and a member of clan Ventrue decided to see what would happen if they gave the embrace to one of the low born street trash. How much success was due to the Ventrue's own merit, and how much of it was due to relying on the supernatural powers of their blood?<br /> <br /> If somebody who displayed no history of leadership qualities was suddenly inducted into the clan of Lords, how would they respond to the situation? Would they remain nothing more than a common miscreant, acting no better than an oafish thug? Would they act like a spoiled child and go mad with power after discovering what they were capable of? Or, would they lift themselves up from such meager beginnings and do something more productive with their lives?<br /> <br /> This particular fledgling is about to find out the answer to that question first hand!<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>185)</b> The wrath of a Koldun is not something one should ever brush aside lightly, but such lessons are wasted on modern kindred, who have rarely encountered such fury. Even worse is the fact Koldunic Sorcery is almost exclusive to the fiendish Clan Tzimisce, who have seen fit to let the art fade into obscurity.<br /> <br /> Which is why it is so surprising then, that this particular Koldun is a member of clan Nosferatu! The knowledge of how they acquired this power is perhaps not as important as the knowledge of how they wield it. Devoting themselves to mastering the powers of Earth and Spirit, the sewer rat can defend their warrens against the threat of the Niktuku like never before. Sensing their presence before they even have the chance to trigger their more mundane security measures. And since the Nosferatu love hiding underground so much, only a suicidal moron would dare to attack them head on!<br /> <br /> The only downside seems to be that their devotion to the study of Koldunic Sorcery alienates them from even their fellow Nosferatu. You don't just walk up to the Tzimisce and ask them for ancient power that they themselves turned away from, without offering them some kind of substantial payment in exchange. Plus, the Koldun's nightly meditation rituals, and neo-shamanism is off putting to those sewer rats who prefer to place their faith in more reliable methods of security. Yet, none can deny that the warrens have become a far safer and more productive place, since they started using their magic to shore up its defenses. And some among the clan have even begun to question the benefits of petitioning him for apprenticeship, so that other warrens might make use of such a rare and potent ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-24-2019, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T22:40:18-07:00","id":1307689,"title":"","content":"186) An amnesiac Caitiff, who awoke one night tired, hungry, and undead. He retains no recollection of who he was, how he got there, or how he became a vampire.<br /> <br /> He's not completely ignorant, of course. He knows language - five of them - and understands how to operate machinery, perform basic computer functions, and navigate the urban landscape. He knows the state of the world in general, current events, and, most especially, History. He could explain the sequence of events that lead to the French Revolution, the dynasties of China, and the theories about the Bronze Age Collapse. About his own life, he can say nothing.<br /> <br /> What he discovered quite early in his unlife, however, was that he was extremely physically capable. Highly skilled in Athletics (especially Parkour), Martial Arts (Soft Style), and fighting with sticks and staffs. He learned he knew them in his first nights, evading and repelling attacks by a Sheriff. Which was weird (not just for the obvious reason), because when the Sheriff elected to talk rather than hunt, the Caitiff learned that he was targeted for his face. A face shared by a mysterious malcontent and ne'er-do-well, who made trouble for Kindred and Kine alike.<br /> <br /> Adrift in the world and without other purpose, the Caitiff elected to track down his doppelganger. Their shared visage provides the only lead concerning who he was, and perhaps why he cannot remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T16:13:11-07:00","id":1308814,"title":"","content":"187) A Warrior Salubri who runs a series of fight clubs throughout the state or province. He brings dissatisfied men and violence enthusiasts together, where they beat the tar out of each other. He's built a mystique around the movement, citing the power of drinking a defeated opponent's blood. Which is why no one bats an eye when he partakes.<br /> <br /> Don't worry, kids, he only advocates taking small amounts of blood. He can't maintain his Herd - er, followers - if they are beaten and bled to death. That's both wasteful and disrespectful to one's opponent. Or something.<br /> <br /> Currently, the Salubri is just building up his following. But soon, he'll start introducing ideas into their heads about taking violence to the establishment. The apparatus of government and capitalism must be dismantled, he might say, as it's currently keeping them trapped in a system of banal office work and passive political engagement (in which they, as common people, don't have any real power).<br /> <br /> That these targets are often the instruments for Camarilla influence is left unstated. The mortals don't need to know that their anger is being co-opted by the Sabbat in their crusades. If some of the followers seem to possess special promise, the Sword of Caine could always &quot;promote&quot; them. The gift of Caine can do wonders to elevate someone to true greatness. Assuming they survive long enough to become True Sabbat. The Salubri himself is paying close attention to his men, to find those worthy of following the Warrior's path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T00:05:44-07:00","id":1309386,"title":"","content":"188) A Gangrel Mariner, embraced more or less in the usual Gangrel way. Her sire found her swimming at night, embraced her on a whim, then left her alone for months to see how well she adapted. Adapt she did, deciding to unlive in the ocean full time. For ten years, she pursued her great hobby: scouring the seabed for treasure. &quot;Treasure&quot;, in this case, being whatever materials she considered interesting or historically relevant. Fancy lures, sunken cargo, anchors, the occasional statue looted from a derelict ship, bottle caps, etc. She stored it all in the bulk of a yacht, sent to the seafloor by an errant storm. It wasn't the finest collection in the world, but it was hers.<br /> <br /> So imagine her ire when some divers came crawling around her hoard. She'd been away at the time, and only arrived in time to see the mortals hauling up the last of her treasures. She lashed out at one of them, clawing his face and ripping his goggles off. Alas, the humans managed to swim far enough towards the surface to reach the sunlit layer, where she couldn't pursue. It seemed as though her hoard was lost...except the goggles had the name of the diver written on them, identifying them as the man's property.<br /> <br /> With a name, the man could be tracked. It probably helped that he now sported a wicked set of facial scars.<br /> <br /> After a decade chilling under the sea, the Mariner reluctantly returned to the land. Warped by her Clan curse, she made landfall more fishy than when she'd left. But it wasn't a problem a stolen hoodie and other clothes couldn't hide. She's now tracked the man to a city, where he supposedly lives. Unfortunately, entering the city means she must now contend with Camarilla law, and the bothersome presence of other Kindred. So long as she continues her search, she had to play Camarilla games. She cannot wait to retrieve her things and leave, returning to the depths of the ocean once more. Until then, she makes her haven in a drainage pipe down by the river, where none but the Nosferatu would even notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T17:00:30-07:00","id":1309951,"title":"","content":"<b>189)</b> A Nosferatu who is adamant that they were embraced by the wrong clan. Refusing to spend eternity wading through the filth and shadows of the city, they have devoted their every waking moment to climbing the ranks of kindred society, until such a time as they see themselves sitting upon the Prince's throne. Using the term &quot;Sewer Rat&quot; when addressing this kindred is perceived as a grievous insult.<br /> <br /> <b>190)</b> A member of the Lasombra, who failed the clan's merciless training regiment and was declared too soft and cowardly to be worthy of membership. Before they could be destroyed for their weakness, they fled the Sabbat, eventually seeking shelter among the Camarilla. To allay suspicions of their motives, and make it easier to fit in with society, they have chosen to conceal the truth of their lineage, by posing as a member of clan Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-04-2019, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T07:01:51-07:00","id":1310032,"title":"","content":"<b>191)</b> A Malkavian, who's twisted sense of humor leads to some truly sadistic &quot;pranks.&quot; They spread pain, tragedy and terror for no other reason than to get a reaction out of people, finding their shock and outrage to be a source of great entertainment. Their favorite targets are those who live in blissful ignorance, never suspecting that their night could go horrendously wrong in the blink of an eye.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>192)</b> A Thinblood, who's sire attempted to embrace their immediate family members in a misguided attempt to sustain their relationship to them. Needless to say, the plan went to absolute shit, leaving the Thinblood as the only survivor. Now, they struggle every night to avoid the Camarilla's wrath, all while desperately looking for a way to improve their situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T10:53:18-07:00","id":1310319,"title":"","content":"<b>193)</b> A Gangrel Prince, who's time spent traveling abroad has lead them to many exotic places... like the jungle... where they spent a lot of time refining their in clan disciplines... Word of advice, the pair of tigers he keeps in his throne room aren't just for show.<br /> <br /> <b>194) </b>A Toreador, who was embraced as a child in a woefully misguided attempt by their sire to preserve their young acting career. With the expiration date on their celebrity status rapidly approaching, the young fledgling's life begins the tragic, downward spiral that so many child actors have succumbed to before.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T22:00:02-07:00","id":1311152,"title":"","content":"<b>195)</b> A high Generation Brujah, who wages peaceful protests in the hopes of bringing about a nonviolent revolution. Unlike their stereotypical clanmates, they focus more on mastering their Social and Mental skills, rather than those of the Physical variety.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>196)</b> A high Generation Ventrue, who's mortal lineage suffered a fall from grace and were forced to become part of the working class to sustain themselves. With the new powers at their disposal, they have vowed to help their family get back on top, so they might once again enjoy the privileged lifestyle of their forefathers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>197)</b> A Thin Blood, who became fascinated with the hermetic sorcery of clan Tremere, after witnessing it in action. They wish to study this power in greater detail, and are actively searching for ways in which to petition the clan for membership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T01:34:51-07:00","id":1311363,"title":"","content":"198) A Tremere who was Embraced for her ability as a Natural Linguist, as Hermetics highly value extensive knowledge of various languages. But when the Embrace took, she discovered she had yet another Merit to her name: Magic Resistance. On the upside, it protected her from Thaumaturgy and other magics. On the downside, it prevented her from ever developing skill in blood sorcery of any sort. Given that this is Clan Tremere, it was far more of a bane than a boon. Ensuring that she'd never be able to advance in the Pyramid.<br /> <br /> Not that she doesn't have her uses. Clan Tremere does not squander resources. In her early years, she was relegated to grunt work - keeping records, obtaining rare ritual ingredients, erasing inconvenient memories, and retrieving vessels on behalf of &quot;her betters&quot; (basically anyone with actual Thaumaturgy skill and a week of seniority over her). But eventually, her talents as a linguist were put to use translating Clan documents and magical texts. Because while most Hermetic sorcerers pride themselves on the ability to read books in their original language, this is not always practical. Especially in chantries stationed outside the English-speaking world.<br /> <br /> Because of her responsibilities - and the often sensitive nature of documents in need of translation - she travels extensively. Hopping from chantry to chantry, doing her work and then being shuffled off to a different region. It's a thankless job, because a good translation is invisible, while a bad translation leads only to scorn (at best). However, her job has advantages. Namely that, especially when it comes to hoary Old World Tremere who stubbornly refuse to learn the vulgar English tongue, she ends up being the pathway through which considerably important information is transferred. A great deal of knowledge of operations and magical theory must cross her desk and be subjected to her full attention. She can turn such information to her purposes, even if knowing how a ritual is cast does her no personal good. Indeed, it's because she's known to be incapable of blood magic that makes others ignore her. So long as she draws no attention to herself, she's practically invisible.<br /> <br /> Her mobility is also a hidden asset. Sure, she can't build up a local power base when so often on the move, but she can network like no one's business. She'd never be so foolish as to directly sell Tremere secrets to those outside the Clan, of course. That would be suicide. But she knows what she knows, as well as who else knows it. That networking comes in handy when allowing Tremere to get in touch with non-Tremere who might need their services, or vice versa. Not to mention how well she can network within the pyramid, since she knows lore that ambitious Warlocks would kill for.<br /> <br /> She's a woman who, by twist of fate, slipped through the cracks. But in slipping through, she found her own niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T06:23:55-07:00","id":1312929,"title":"","content":"199) I'm actually really tempted to try out a Malkavian with Sociopathy as their derangement.<br /> <br /> The balancing act between portraying them as a character who is single minded concerned with their own gratification, without using it as an excuse for being Chaotic Evil might be fun, if I can do it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-18-2019, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T15:05:46-07:00","id":1313023,"title":"","content":"Hello I\u2019m a new ST about to have my first session and wanted to join in on the community. It took forever for the forums to activate my account and in the mean time I\u2019ve been hanging around /r/vtm/ board. But now that my account is finally activated here I figure I would show off my first custom character for the Chicago by Night campaign I\u2019ll be running. I thought Gary needed it own Sheriff so I created one, let me know what you think. She is meant to be very scary and intimidating. I wrote this in the same style as the Chicago by Night book presents its characters.<br /> <br /> <br /> 200) Kate Summers (Stray Winfield) - Sheriff of Gary<br /> Clan \u2013 Lasombra Antitribu<br /> Concept \u2013 Runaway Sabbat<br /> <br /> In life Kate\u2019s family was well off enough and she had smarts that promised her a spot in a good school all in all things were looking good. But then it all came crashing down she was reject by her collage of choice and around the same time her parents were murdered. If that wasn\u2019t enough she lost all her inheritance because apparently her parents had a back log of unpaid taxes (though she never knew her parents to have tax troubles). Left with nothing and all her hopes of a future dashed away she found herself forced into prostitution. One time she sold her body for money one time and something in her snapped she swore that she would never ever again degrade herself like that. The world was a cruel and unfeeling place and she would have to be just as cruel to survive. It started with small things mugging shoplifting but gradually she worked her way up in the criminal underworld becoming more and more heartless her thinking being in this world your either the abused or the abuser so she might as well be the abuser.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s when she was approached by her sire all of Kate\u2019s misfortune had been no accident. In the Lasombra tradition Anastasio had destroyed Kate\u2019s life to test her, as he had many other test subjects. It was Anastasio who was responsible for her not getting into collage and her parent\u2019s murder and her losing all her inheritance and now after climbing the ranks to carve out a niche for herself in the criminal underworld he found her worthy of the embrace. At first she was delighted with what she had become thinking now she never be the abused always and forever would she be the abuser. But such fantasies quickly fall away as she realized not only was kindred society just as abusive as the kine's society but she was expected to be a foot soldier in some mad cult\u2019s holy war. Kate never much bought into the whole religion thing so fighting and dying (again) because of some shit some asshole wrote down in a book a gazillion years ago didn\u2019t sit well with her, \u201cCain and antediluvians my ass I know a cult when I see it\u201d. So she ran away abounding her name so as not to be found calling herself Stray.<br /> <br /> After many years she found herself in dump called Gary run by this guy calling himself Modius. Somehow he found out about her being a Lasombra and a former Sabbat despite her best effort to conceal those facts. Modius didn\u2019t really find out about these things himself it was Annabelle who found out and told Modius to offer her a position as his sheriff. It wasn\u2019t that hard to convince her after all the title appealed to her personality and Modius offered protection from the Sabbat. Really he will sell her out in instance if it will save his skin but protection is what he sold to her. Of course Stray returns the favor and will dump Modius should it ever become convenient for her but for now sheriff of Gary is a pretty sweet gig. The two Sabbat scouts in Chicago are under orders to kill her on sight but they think she is in Chicago itself rather than in Gary so they haven\u2019t found her yet. Stray doesn\u2019t yet know of the scouts existence but if she ever finds out she will rat them out to Modius, Lodin and anybody else that will listen (maybe she will even enlist the help of the players assuming their not trying to kill her as well).<br /> <br /> Sire \u2013 Anastasio Villanueva<br /> Nature \u2013 Bravo<br /> Demeanor \u2013 Loner<br /> Generation \u2013 8<sup>th</sup><br /> Embrace \u2013 1926 (born 1901)<br /> Apparent Age \u2013 25<br /> Physical \u2013 Strength 3, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> Social \u2013 Charisma 1, Manipulation 3, Appearance 3<br /> Mental \u2013 Perception 2, Intelligence 3, Wits 3<br /> Talents \u2013 Alertness 2, Athletics 1, Brawl 1, Intimidation 3, Streetwise 4, Subterfuge 3<br /> Skills \u2013 Drive 2, Firearms 3, Larceny 3, Melee 3, Stealth 3<br /> Knowledge \u2013 Academics 1, Finance 1, Investigation 3, Law 1, Occult 1<br /> Disciplines \u2013 Obtenebration 2, Potence 3, Dominate 2, Fortitude 4, Celerity 1<br /> Backgrounds \u2013 Retainers 2, Domain 2, Contacts 2, Resources 2<br /> Virtues \u2013 Conscience 2, Self-Control 3, Courage 5<br /> Humanity \u2013 4<br /> Willpower \u2013 6<br /> Blood Pool/Max Per turn \u2013 15/3<br /> Weapons carried on person switchblade and a Springfield XDM .45 ACP<br /> <br /> Image \u2013 A woman of average height with long black hair and permanent scowl on her face. Her piercing brown eyes have the oppressive look of a predator. She favors dark leather cloths so she can batter blend into the shadows and go unseen until it\u2019s time to strike.<br /> <br /> Haven \u2013 Dave\u2019s automobile (it\u2019s merely a front for a chop shop run by one of her ghouls).<br /> <br /> Roleplaying hints \u2013 unless somebody is in your way or Modiu\u2019s way be quiet and stick to the shadows you don\u2019t want anybody to find out you\u2019re a Lasombra ex Sabbat, be weary of reflective surfaces. However if do need to get involved be ruthless and tough it\u2019s the only way to survive in this world, mercy is used only by the weak who simply get stepped on. But never use your obtenebration in front of others unless you absolutely have no other choice. Avoid talking about your clan but if you have to give somebody an answer tell them you\u2019re Brujah.<br /> <br /> Secrets \u2013 B-<br /> <br /> Influence \u2013 as Modius\u2019s primary enforcer she has a great deal of pull in Gary (for what it\u2019s worth) and the other kindred of Gary give her a wide berth. As long as Modius is not after them and their not in her way she leaves them alone. But this influence does not extended beyond Gary and she has little influence past its borders, nor does she seek greater influence outside her niche for fear of her linage and former sect being discovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25317-brakenwagen","name":"brakenwagen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T00:43:10-07:00","id":1313080,"title":"","content":"201) He began as a comic book artist in the 1950s, working for a cheap horror anthology. He knew nothing about real supernatural creatures...until one of his readers arrived at his doorstep one night. It was a recently turned vampire who, after seeing (and perpetrating) too much horror, decided to greet the sun. But not before coming to the artist (a favorite of the fledgling's, and the only thing they had left after a cycle of horrors and loss), to reveal everything they knew about vampires. After having the painful truth of vampirism proven to him, the artist recorded the monster's last testament. As the vampire departed to die, the artist used his connections in the publishing industry to start his own company, with its own 4-color. He called its main book &quot;Vampires Are Real!&quot;.<br /> <br /> He filled the book with more or less accurate information about vampires, as he understood it at the time. The great conflicts between sects were unknown to him, but the mechanics of vampirism and the nightly unlifestyles of the undead were fair game. For a time, he ran under the radar. While the &quot;funny books&quot; weren't new by this point, they were often beneath the notice of vampires still. This, of course, would change (especially as public outrage over horror and crime comics increased), but the artist-turned-publisher remained hidden long enough for mortal hunters to take notice. He started getting letters from people who claimed to have seen or even hunted vampires. Some could be rightly written off as jokesters or the mentally ill, but others seemed genuine. He started depicting their stories in the pages of his comics, though with names changed to protect the innocent.<br /> <br /> Eventually, with more and more vampire hunters being galvanized by the cheap rags he put out, vampires began to notice. In truth, the man had always underestimated the total vampiric saturation of society. He'd actually thought he and his followers had made a sizable dent in undead numbers, when he was targeted for assassination. They cut his brake lines, and sent him colorful death threats. When he wasn't deterred, they came into his home, stealing information from his files and from his mind. Someone, somewhere, apparently decided against just killing him, for reasons unknown. Maybe they didn't want his death attracting attention, or making him a martyr. He didn't know how far they'd go, because he ran at the first opportunity and never looked back. Abandoned his old identity, to start a new one.<br /> <br /> The vampires, perhaps supposing they could prevent repeat offenses against the Masquerade, fed the fire of public outcry against &quot;sordid literature&quot; in comic books. The Comics Code Authority came down, destroying the mainstream horror comic industry. If they supposed that it would stop the artist, they were sorely mistaken. He entered the underground comics market, distributing small print runs of new material, under the heading &quot;Vampires Are Everywhere!&quot;. He'd learned his lesson, and started doing his own investigations. Contacts within hunter groups were supplemented with personal detective work, to learn as much about vampires and their stories as possible. With far more care than in the old days, he worked to keep the mags circulating and the hunters informed. Information on how to hunt vampires - the tools, techniques, and temptations of the trade - became more direct and explicit. He liked to think he created his best work in those days, both in writing and in his art, experimenting with the new underground styles.<br /> <br /> This, too, did pass. Vampires tracked him down again. And again, he was not outright destroyed. But only because his assailants - now thoroughly sick of his shit - wanted to subvert him. In a cruel irony, the Toreador leading them Embraced and Blood Bound him, and forced him to continue his work. By this point, the Comics Code Authority lost much of its bite, and horror titles gained mainstream acceptance. His master set him up with a new company, and bought up the rights to his own &quot;Vampires Are Real!&quot; comic, that had languished in rights hell for years. Set him to work, pumping out vampire stories. Except these were deliberately seeded with lies and disinformation, meant to get hunters killed. When people who knew things would send him more letters, he had no choice to pass them along to his master, who would track down their senders and silence them.<br /> <br /> Times change again, however. In a reversal of fortune, the artist's master perished in a Sabbat crusade. As the artist fled from their city, he felt the Blood Bond keeping him in check break down. He took charge of his master's ghouls, allowing him to completely control the assets of his company. By this point, of course, the company had struggled after the bursting of the 90s Speculator Bubble, which rocked most of the comics industry. But, after selling much of the physical assets, he made the transition into the digital age. He carries the rights to his comics, but now he put that work on the Internet. Learning to create webcomics with digital tools was a learning curve, but one he took to with enthusiasm. Despite being years dead, he'd never felt more alive. Free and learning new skills.<br /> <br /> And with the internet, he had the tools necessary to reach a far larger and more connected audience than he had before. He trawls message boards, looking for folks with vampire experiences, and pointing them towards &quot;interesting reading material&quot;. He might be one of them now, but he has no love for vampires still. So much ground was lost when he was a slave. It's time to catch up. His Embrace HAS given him new appreciation for the vampiric struggle, though. His first addition to the &quot;Vampires Are Real!&quot; website was a story he'd put off making for over fifty years: a dramatic retelling of his first encounter with the vampire who met the sun. He could understand it in the new light, and so figured it was important to create. Nonetheless, he used it as a teaching moment, both for vampire readers and mortal ones.<br /> <br /> That vampires suffered from their condition. For vampires, it was a call to hold fast to their Humanity. For mortals, it was a charge to put them out of their misery. Even with Empathy, he must keep perspective that vampires are all monsters. His readers must never be made to forget that, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T02:49:05-07:00","id":1313094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1313080#post1313080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">201)</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, this seems extremely unlikely to happen. Julius and Hatter from Bloodlines comes to mind when I read about this character. Any domain that allowed this kind of threat to survive for as long as it did is run by drooling imbeciles, who deserve to be put to Final Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-19-2019, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T03:41:49-07:00","id":1313097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1313094#post1313094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me, this seems extremely unlikely to happen. Julius and Hatter from Bloodlines comes to mind when I read about this character. Any domain that allowed this kind of threat to survive for as long as it did is run by drooling imbeciles, who deserve to be put to Final Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It IS weird. One could almost imagine there's more going on than the artist realizes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T09:32:44-07:00","id":1314309,"title":"","content":"<b>202)</b> Rowen Wolfe<br /> <br /> <b>Clan:</b> Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Hormone Crazed Steroid Abuser<br /> <br /> <b>Character Bio:</b> Some people take the muscle man fetish too far, and Rowen Wolfe is one such example. A competitive body builder in life, Rowen devoted his attention to getting as jacked as possible, and then flaunting his brawn for all the world to see. Had he stuck with basic training, he might have been a prime candidate for clan Toreador. But his lust for ever sicker gains drove Rowen to heavy steroid usage. After decades of abuse, Rowen's muscles had inflated to disgusting proportions and it was clear he did not have much longer before his body suffered a catastrophic backlash. That was when he drew the attention of clan Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Rowen's sire did not approve of the obscene vanity he placed on his muscles, and decided to punish him, as many Nosferatu are known to do. Even with his herculean strength (by human standards), he was no match for a potence infused kindred, and Rowen was forcefully embraced after a short struggle. <br /> <br /> Even by Nosferatu standards, Rowen Wolfe is shocking to behold. He has turned the stereotypical idea of the clan as a bunch of skeletal anorexics inside out, and become a hulking monstrosity that would inspire urban legends for any mortals who lived to tell the tale. He is obsessed with Potence, to the point where he focuses on improving it to the detriment of his other disciplines. He is also envious of the more <i>&quot;beautiful&quot;</i> clans which share this power, and is always eager for a chance to demonstrate his perceived superiority with its usage.<br /> <br /> The clan uses him like a blunt instrument. When stealth and espionage can't get the job done, they send in <i>&quot;the Behemoth&quot;</i> to acquire the information they're looking for. It's a thankless job, but it's one which Rowen Wolfe manages to excel at. That is until his Cleopatra attitude inevitably leads to him doing something incredibly foolish in an attempt to satisfy his vanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-25T21:27:49-07:00","id":1314456,"title":"","content":"203) A Ventrue Antitribu who served four tours of duty in the middle east. The exemplary record of service was what attracted his Camarilla Ventrue sire in the first place; the old leech had a fondness for soldiers dating back to the Napoleonic era. Back when folks still believed war to be a glorious adventure; a belief the sire held to unironically.<br /> <br /> For the veteran, of course, his experience in war was anything but glorious. A little PTSD, a little shrapnel embedded in his bones. Bad memories, and lingering health issues. He'd only joined the military to get a college education...which, thanks to the bureaucratic clusterfuck that is the Army, he never got. Nor did he get much help from Veterans Affairs, when it came to those aforementioned health issues. So by the time he heard about some rich guy, looking to hire him personally for some mysterious job, he was too in debt and too homeless to say no. Borrowed a suit and a shower from a friend, and took his night interview. While he was damaged, he had a good enough hold on his psyche to fake being more put together than he felt. Faked it so well, the Elder bought it, and gave him the Embrace.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, the Elder was fooling himself, seeing only what he wanted to see and hearing only what he wanted to hear. It was well into the veteran's grueling &quot;education&quot; - when the fledgling snapped more than once under pressure - that the old vamp realized he'd attached himself to &quot;damaged goods&quot;. He tried to reclaim the blood he'd given. Except, if nothing else, the service had taught the young vamp two things: 1) how to survive, and 2) paranoia. He took his sire's eye on the way out (not that it means much), and vanished to the streets. Trying desperately to blend in to the legion of other homeless veterans, before the Sabbat picked him up.<br /> <br /> See, the neonate had done some thinking. With Clan Ventrue digging its roots into every facet of international business, it wasn't a hard leap to assume that they had hands in the military industrial complex. The same circle of business interests and war profiteers that gobbled up government budgets, by selling them military hardware, leaving nothing for programs to take care of soldiers AFTER they returned from war. The Military Industrial Complex that lobbied politicians, encouraging them to go to war only the slightest pretense, then stay there indefinitely. How many Clan Ventrue bastards profited from America's Forever War in the middle east? How many folks like him - brave, patriotic, desperate soldiers - were ground up and spat out by a military machine, as a byproduct of Camarilla interests? Were they responsible for the poorness of Veterans Affairs, so they'd always have broken, homeless soldiers to feed on?<br /> <br /> Just thinking of it drove the veteran to Frenzy, on more than one occasion.<br /> <br /> The last thing he'd ever wanted, when his tours were over, was to go back to combat. But here he is, in a squad (pack) of his own. If the Camarilla wants unceasing conflict - if they want their Forever War - he'll give it to them. And he'll take the fighting right to their havens. Make them feel just a tiny fragment of the fear that kept him up at night when he was alive, and that troubles his daydreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T17:23:24-07:00","id":1315052,"title":"","content":"204) Heard of Reptillians? Plenty have. Also called &quot;Lizard People&quot;, they're one of the most infamous &quot;Secret Masters&quot; spoken of in conspiracy theory circles. The reality of their dominion of the earth and its leaders is espoused by notorious figures like David Icke. So widespread is the idea - if not belief in its truth - it's become a punchline for skeptics. But for some, the Reptillians are given as much credence as the Illuminati and the &quot;Elders of Zion&quot;, to the dismay of everyone else.<br /> <br /> Naturally, then, as heavily reptile-themed as they are, it was practically a no-brainer for some Followers of Set to get in on that action. That's where this Setite comes in.<br /> <br /> Strangely, he used to be a skeptic himself. A journalist and published author in the 70s and 80s, he sought to debunk belief in the ridiculous conspiracies spouted by theorists. This includes Reptillians. Unlike the average theorist, who was content never to look outside the bounds of mass media and conspiracy zines for their &quot;evidence&quot;, he made tracks in pursuit of such subjects, in the interest of proving them wrong. Until, that is, he got a lead on a man who supposedly encountered a Reptillian, before promptly winding up dead of overdose weeks later. The author tracked the man's apartment down, following clues that lead deeper and deeper into the criminal underworld.<br /> <br /> He only came to believe when he stood face to face with a scale-faced man. He didn't survive the encounter, though he did walk away from it.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Reptillian&quot;, of course, was a Setite, possessed of a Flaw that covered his face in scales. The old one was impressed by the skeptic's investigative skills, and Embraced him for the benefit of Set. The truth was revealed unto the fledgling and, after a period of indoctrination, he came to see it the Setite way. The world truly did suffer under the weight of Secret Masters - the Aeons - but the Setites were interested in breaking people free from their bonds. The reptile, not an oppressor, but a liberator.<br /> <br /> Now he trawls internet forums and social media, most nights. Keeping tabs on conspiracy theory circles. Separating the wheat from the chaff, to find those mortals who are most useful to Set. Starts dropping hints and leads, coaxing those who are not mere dabblers or totally useless into going beyond their comfort zone. Having them seek the truth...or A truth. Most will simply be pawns or cultists. But, perhaps, a few worthy of Set's blood will surface. Seekers of truth, ready to remove the blinds and take on the Aeons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T23:55:01-07:00","id":1315390,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I've been trying to think of an interesting way to run a character from the Children of Osiris for a while now. I think I found one.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> 205) These nights, he goes by the name Manish, called &quot;The Mouse&quot;. It's not hard to see why, as he will (very rarely) manifest rodential features after frenzy (to accompany his permanent buck teeth). Frenzy, of course, being something Manish avoids judiciously, as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> For his part, the <i>Child of Osiris</i> considers &quot;Mouse&quot; to be aspirational. A state of humility to be emulated, and a quiet (un)lifestyle to be practiced. The acolyte makes his haven in a farm just outside of town, where he raises rats. The blood goes to him - the power of Bardo allowing him to gain ample nourishment from a single rodent - while the bodies are butchered and sold to any of various local customers who appreciate the culinary value of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rat_meat\" target=\"_blank\">rat meat</a>. (Most are Chinese, Vietnamese, Taiwanese, and Thai restaurants and families, though a few West Virginians seem to enjoy clean fare for their rat stews). All in all, Manish considers his situation almost perfect, for the purposes of allowing him to pursue spiritual ends. Almost.<br /> <br /> Alas, the Mouse has more than ample baggage, and stacks of unfinished business that gnaw at him.<br /> <br /> Before he was Manish the Mouse, Child of Osiris, he was Rahgu, called &quot;The Rat&quot;, City Gangrel and soldier in the Sword of Caine. His early unlife was a blur of violence, skullduggery, and gluttonous excess. When the Sabbat needed answers, they called on the Rat to spy, unseen. When the Sabbat needed a knife stuck in the back of an enemy, the called on the Rat to get in close and wield that swift blade. And when the Sabbat required someone to contribute blood to create new recruits, well...rats are known for their fecundity, aren't they?<br /> <br /> Therein lies much of the vampire's current trouble. When he was Raghu, he sired many childer, participating in mass embraces often. Many failed to dig themselves from their burials, and remain interred to this night. Most others failed to unlive very long. But, still, progeny lasted beyond the lifespan of the average rat. Indeed, they outlasted The Rat's own life, in a manner of speaking.<br /> <br /> In time, Raghu could stomach the Sabbat unlife no longer, and grew ashamed of the blood on his hands. In a terrible moment - that moment when his pack perished and he had no more Vaulderie ties holding him down - he realized that his whole unlife had amounted to nothing but ruin. Ruin of the world, and his own soul. He abandoned the Sword of Caine, his wicked ways, and his own name. When he found the Children of Osiris (or rather when they found him), he converted without a second thought, seeking absolution and control. The Rat became the Mouse.<br /> <br /> But while he can no longer sire childer - thanks to Osiran ritual - it would not erase the progeny he already created. Their existence pains him now, both because of how he thoughtlessly cursed them, and because he unleashed blood-drinking monsters on the world. To complicate matters, his new dedication to Humanity ties his hands. He cannot, in good conscience, put down his ill-sired progeny. Even were he willing, they are difficult to find; the buried ones alone are scattered, and he cannot rightly recall where all the failed mass embrace targets could be found. Those up and about are fewer, but move around. For many of them, his hope is that they destroy themselves (as Sabbat often do, one way or another).<br /> <br /> One of them is a particular trouble, because he knows exactly where they are and what they do. The last of his childer abandoned the Sabbat before he did...to join the Followers of Set. So, on top of opposing the Setites for sectarian (and moral) reasons, Manish must contend with his own errant, corrupt progeny. The rodent must oppose the snake he created. All while upholding his virtues, and hopefully not exposing himself to either Setite or Sabbat agents, lest he be a target.<br /> <br /> It's a tough world, for a Mouse. But who said the road to Golconda was easy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 05-30-2019, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T02:14:22-07:00","id":1315406,"title":"","content":"<b>206) Artair Sutharlan:</b><br /> <br /> For the clan as a whole, the collapse of the Tremere's pyramid was a catastrophe. But for some individual members, it was the best news they'd heard in a long, long time. Upon hearing of House Carna's formation, Artair Sutharlan immediately severed any involvement he had with the main clan, and left to join her side of the now scattered remnants of the Tremere. A dabbler of hedge magic since before his embrace, Artair accepted the Tremere's recruitment offer under the pretense that he would be allowed to explore several human life times worth of arcane knowledge. Only to discover too late that his research opportunities would be severely curtailed by the hermetic elders who ruled the clan with an iron fist.<br /> <br /> With the pyramid collapsed, and the blood bonds destroyed, Artair is once again able to study magic freely, and House Carna is not nearly so oppressive, or narrow focused as the rest of the clan proved itself to be. He has turned his back on the hermetic sciences and adopted more pagan traditions, based on the celtic magic of his Scottish homeland. Runes and sigils are his particular specialty, and he is always eager to try new combinations in order to see how the enchanted language interacts with itself.<br /> <br /> When he isn't busy with his own magical research, Artair also has a keen interest in strengthening House Carna as a whole. He has adopted a far more casual set of standards towards giving the embrace to mortals, and believes that a genuine love for magic should be the highest concern, instead of focusing on whether or not the subject is talented enough to rise above their peers. He claims that magic should be available to all who wish to learn, and is not something to be hoarded by vain tyrants looking to feed their egos. This philosophy has lead to him becoming the leader of his own chantry, who's apprentices take inspiration from neo-shamanism and new age druids in their approach to magical traditions.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> In true celtic fashion, Artair is both equal parts warrior, as well as priest. His knowledge of rune magic works exceptionally well on the battlefield, and more than once, he has heard that his rituals bare a closer resemblance to those of the Banu Haqim, than that of the Tremere. As for appearance, Artair is a middle aged looking man of Scottish descent, with fiery red hair and bright blue eyes. He also has a full, thick beard which he keeps immaculately braided. His build shows signs of someone who took pride in physical exercise, before the Tremere forced him to focus on more intellectual pursuits. He stands at 6'2 in height, weighing 245 lbs, and has thick patches of body hair on his forearms, chest and shins. At the risk of potentially breaking the Masquerade, he is also known to carry around a broad sword, who's blade has been carved with runic glyphs along the side. When asked what the runes are for, he explains that they make it easier to use Blood Sorcery, since all he has to do is paint the blade with fresh blood to awaken the rune's power!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-30-2019, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T21:18:31-07:00","id":1316010,"title":"","content":"<b>207) Anthony Knight:</b><br /> <br /> Sometimes, even thin bloods can't escape the curse of their sire's lineage, and Anthony Knight would awaken into the world of darkness to find that he had a powerful urge to punish the wicked! Unlike most of his kind, Anthony was not abandoned at birth, but rather his sire took it upon themselves to train him in the ways of alchemy and assassination. For the first three years of his unlife, it looked like Anthony had a promising future among the Banu Haqim. But that all changed one night, when they received a visit from the local sheriff. It turns out that Anthony's sire was also a thin blood, and had embraced him with neither the prince's knowledge, nor permission. Anthony managed to escape the sheriff's wrath, but his sire was not so fortunate.<br /> <br /> Shortly after this incident, Anthony swore a vendetta against the Camarilla, who had succeeded in making his unlife magnitudes more difficult in their quest to hunt him down. He eventually fell in with the Anarch crowd, though only because he was smart enough to realize that he needed allies if he planned to survive any longer. In truth, Anthony would consider himself part of the Unbound. He cares almost nothing for the politics of kindred society, and works as a professional assassin simply because that is what his sire trained him to do. <br /> <br /> Anthony's long term goal is to kill the ones responsible for his sire's death, that being the sheriff who committed the deed, as well as the prince who ordered it. But even for all his training, he realizes that would be a suicide mission by himself. So, in preparation for carrying out his revenge fantasy, he has begun to assemble a coterie of like minded rebels, whom he feels trustworthy enough to wage war upon the Ivory Tower!<br /> <br /> Anthony was embraced early in his life. He is a young, white male in his early 20's with short, black hair and dark brown eyes. He was not particularly athletic in life, but had remained healthy enough that the occasional display of vampire prowess won't seem out of the realm of possibility. He stands at a height of 5'9, with a weight of 140 lbs. He has a habit of dressing in layers, which makes it easier for him to conceal weapons on his personage, as well as store ingredients for his alchemical formulas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Renegade Hunter<br /> <br /> <b>Clan:</b> Thin Blood<br /> <br /> <b>Generation:</b> 15<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Thin Blood Alchemist, Anarch Comrades<br /> <b>Flaws:</b> Clan Curse (Banu Haqim), Mortal Frailty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-03T18:19:12-07:00","id":1316346,"title":"","content":"208) One of the rare male &quot;Daughters&quot; of Cacophony, this man had dreams of being a country singer. After many rejections by record companies, however, he started to get discouraged. Desperate, even. In came members of the local mob, who agreed to pull strings to get his music career up and running. Naturally, this offer came with dire strings attached. After he'd gotten his big break, the mob would have him put on a private show for some VIP or another. In truth, the VIP was an enemy of the mob, and before he went on, he was handed a pistol, and told to gun them down during. No witnesses would be around to talk about what happened...but the act of assassination would be secretly recorded, the mob using it as further leverage to keep the singer in line.<br /> <br /> His stardom rose, just as his spirits sank. In time, he started to break. His last record saw him pour his heart out into songs of absolute sorrow, grief, and shame. Nothing specific enough that the mob would have words with him, but enough to convey the emotional weight under which he labored. It moved one heart, despite that heart being dead. His sire - a woman who had been a folk singer, in a previous life - was moved to blood tears (luckily, no one saw). Using Presence, she drew him out to a bar after the show, and convinced him to tell his story. When he'd finished, she offered to give him the power to visit retribution on those who had wronged him, and turned him into a killer. All it would take was death, of himself and his career.<br /> <br /> They say the last member of that organized crime syndicate begged on the phone from distant allies for help, before he was drawn away by &quot;that voice&quot;.<br /> <br /> The singer left his identity behind, but not his vocation. He travels from city to city, putting on shows for local venues under an assumed name. That's his &quot;day&quot; job. When he's not on stage, he's offering his services to Kindred who need a hired gun. He prefers to offer protection services, but he's not above being a hit man. Despite the sorrows he displayed in his breathing days, he's grown numb to dispensing death. His sad songs are about how easy it's become. Veterans seem to appreciate those tunes. He wishes he was as noble as them.<br /> <br /> At least he's useful to the Bloodline. By his reckoning, it isn't proper for ladies to get their hands dirty. &quot;Call it 'old fashioned',&quot; he says, &quot;but that's a burden the men-folk should take on themselves. And I am, as always, a helpful servant.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T10:15:32-07:00","id":1317615,"title":"","content":"209) A Goldsmith (a smithy in general, really), who uses this talent in order to get in good with the \u201chigher ups.\u201d They use this connection to gather information (eavesdropping, spying, etc) to use as currency with anyone interested in knowing more about what\u2019s going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3439-limeflavored","name":"LimeFlavored","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T00:19:03-07:00","id":1318808,"title":"","content":"210) A Nosferatu Anarch who works to undermine Camarilla institutions.<br /> <br /> <i>Literally</i>. With a pickaxe.<br /> <br /> A miner during his breathing days, this Nosferatu knows his way around soil and stone. Due to having lost his mortal employment to both outsourcing and mechanization, he's got a (pick)axe to grind with corporate interests. The Camarilla being highly involved in big business - including in manipulating economies to their own ends, no matter if it makes the little people suffer - he takes these lingering frustrations out on them.<br /> <br /> His years of experience with geology and practical earth-work allows him to spot where the foundations of a structure are weakest. Using Animalism, he coordinates teams of moles and other burrowing creatures, turning the ground beneath Elysiums and other Cam-vampire holdings into swiss cheese. Potence, meanwhile, allows him to use his pickaxe to devastating effect. While he can often be found helping local Nosferatu expand their warrens, he's committed to the cause of bringing Ivory Tower Kindred down a peg. Or, in this case, down a whole floor. To round off his skillset, Obfuscate allows him to come and go as he pleases, allowing him to survey targets and travel to places where his tunnels start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T21:55:48-07:00","id":1319001,"title":"","content":"<b>211)</b> Most Gangrel are known for their affinity for bats, wolves and occasionally rats. But in this particularly bizarre case, the vampire has developed a kinship with locusts. Like the insects they nurture, this vampire has an almost insatiable appetite. Always draining his victims down to the last drop, and then allowing the swarm to feast upon its fresh meat. It is no surprise then, that they would find themselves among the ranks of the Sabbat, for whom impulse control is already a precious rarity.<br /> <br /> As conspicuous as a swarming cloud of insects may be, the Gangrel has learned to wield it to their advantage. Concealing your presence is quite easy, when people are afraid of being eaten alive if they get anywhere near you. And stories of a gigantic insect hiding among the buzzing masses can easily be waved off as simple delirium brought on by stress and overactive imaginations. Unfortunately, the Second Inquisition is not so easily fooled, and it probably won't be long before the Sabbat starts seeing agents carrying around insect repellent on their next hunts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T02:53:04-07:00","id":1319239,"title":"","content":"212) Drawn from the ranks of domestic moonshiners and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homebrewing\" target=\"_blank\">homebrewers</a>, he was lured to the Followers of Set with promises of freedom from controlling powers (he'd never had much respect for governments or moral busybodies). The transition into vampirism, however, disrupted his ability to enjoy alcohol. As such, he pursued the power of Setite Sorcery, specifically to master Typhon's Brew.<br /> <br /> Some in the Followers of Set would consider this a poor - if not blasphemous - reason for learning Set's magic. He doesn't particularly care, and less orthodox Setites are just happy for another sorcerer to add to the Clan's power. Typhon's Brew has always been a major source of wealth and Boons, extracted from desperate Ghouls and nostalgic Kindred alike.<br /> <br /> But this Setite has considered himself not just a brewer, but an artist. An aficionado of liquor and beer, he spent much of his life learning different recipes. Yet Typhon's Brew has only so many variants and too few tastes, despite the thousands of years spent exploring the craft. As such, his current goal is to experiment, seeking out various beer and liquor making processes, and figuring how to adapt them to blood. Communicating with old Ahku masters, to mine them of their variants, or creating new flavors, textures, and aromas himself. If his work pays off, it could profit him greatly, as he provides not just bloody booze, but a variety of same. Allowing Kindred and Ghouls real choice in their fare, rather than settling for any vitae-enriched alcohol at all.<br /> <br /> There's a small hitch: not all who know Typhon's Brew are Setites. It is old magic, and thus has been traded (or recreated) from time to time. In the city where he makes his haven, an enterprising &quot;Old Skool&quot; Anarch sorcerer knows his own version of the Ritual. Naturally, this Anarch will take issue with someone moving in on his racket, with a new and better product (or products).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 07-01-2019, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T20:05:43-07:00","id":1321819,"title":"","content":"213) A Tremere vampire Embraced from the working classes, for his expertise in metal-working and carpentry (as a person working in THIS economy, he's had many jobs over the years). Turns out these skill sets are useful for many Rituals the Clan employs. From carving specialized wands and staves, to melting silver and casting jewelry, his skills are in his demand. He carved out a healthy niche in his city, employing the Brand Ritual in service to Anarchs looking to apply body art and prove their courage at the same time. He's not generally an academic (though he's hardly stupid; he wouldn't be Embraced if he wasn't above-average in Intelligence), so he's more approachable to members of the Movement. A factor that caused some Tremere to look down at him, but others to consider him a valuable asset. If Anarchs from working-class backgrounds see him as &quot;one of them&quot;, he can be used to lure them to Clan Tremere's services and away from wily Anarch blood sorcerers.<br /> <br /> So long as Clan Tremere kept him under its thumb, all would be well. Naturally, if House Carna and/or the loss of the Pyramid's inner circle are in play, it may be harder to keep him.<br /> <br /> Of other worrying note is his connections with mortal Mages. He was around during the Second Massasa War, and contributed to the Clan's defense. In the course of the conflict, he tangled with a member of Hermetic House Verditus. The two men saw in each other shared interests and a kindred spirit. Despite being on different sides of the conflict, they grew to respect one another, and one a few occasions avoided killing each other when they had the chance. With the conflict over and the uneasy peace between the Order of Hermes and Clan/House Tremere restored, they'd become occult rivals. Blending craftwork with their Hermetic arts, they compete to see whose work is greater. While this has the benefit of motivating the Warlock in his research, thereby enriching the Clan, this contact could result in messy entanglements between the Tremere and mortal Mages.<br /> <br /> If Pyramid control has deteriorated, the Warlock might only be emboldened in this area, as he's left unfettered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T02:07:00-07:00","id":1322576,"title":"","content":"<b>214)</b> A sympathetic Ventrue, who maintains the conviction that the mind is a sanctuary. Having rejected the powers of Dominate and Blood Bonds, they look for more humane ways in which to rule others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>215)</b> A ruthless Toreador, who maintains the conviction that self preservation justifies murder. Since the nights following their embrace, they have encountered many situations in which their continued existence is threatened.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>216)</b> A Thin Blood who was embraced more for their strength of passion, rather than their strength of body. Failing to manifest either the disciplines of Potence or Celerity, they instead focus on using Presence to win most of their battles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>217)</b> A Thin Blood who prides themselves on being the &quot;prettiest rat&quot; in the city. Ostracized by even the Nosferatu who sired them, they have to work extra hard to uncover the elusive secrets they so desperately crave.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T02:30:38-07:00","id":1324674,"title":"","content":"218) This Brujah is Strong. Like, really Strong. Like, &quot;do you even lift, bro?&quot; Strong.<br /> <br /> Growing up, this guy had been the stereotypical Gym Bro. An absolute Chad, who took Sick Gains to be the height of achievement, at least according to his hyper-masculine perception of reality. He oozed Toxic Masculinity. Weight lifting and boxing were his jam.<br /> <br /> Then, he received the Embrace. Except it was an illicit Embrace, given by one of his weight-lifting buddies who wished to share the gift, but hadn't known what the consequences of the act would be. The two had to bail, leaving the city and settling somewhere else. While his friend/Sire made connections with local Anarchs, he poured all of his effort into his Potence. Between this and his skill in Athletics and Brawl, he was a pretty archetypal &quot;Combat Monster&quot; Brujah (well, except he didn't invest in any Celerity; ONLY Potence).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, his great strength did little to help prevent his Sire from being killed, due to Jyhad shenanigans. Now this Brujah was never exactly smart. His friend and Sire had been smart; it's why that guy had been chosen by the Clan of philosophers. But <i>this</i> Brujah wasn't. He'd gotten into college through sports scholarships and a bunch of folks pulling strings for him (or just doing his class work for him, in the case of the nerdy kids he'd bully into helping him). But even he could understand that his one notable strength - Being Really Strong - was useless when dealing with vampires older, wiser, craftier, and better at manipulation than he was. And when he got a group of other Neonates together to maybe help him figure out what happened, he discovered that he could contribute little of worth. He wasn't smart like the Tremere, insightful like the Malkavian, sociable as the Toreador, convincing as the Ventrue, stealthy as the Nosferatu, or resourceful as the Gangrel. He couldn't track clues, do research, cover up the Masquerade, or any of that stuff.<br /> <br /> He was just Strong. Which doesn't matter as much in the modern world, full of its complex systems and many ways to approach problems.<br /> <br /> Understanding now that being Strong was a dead end, he has resolved to correct his deficiency. He's cracking open books and really applying himself. He's actually listening when other vampires talk about things like history or occultism. He's realized there's more to unlife than being strong. Though it might be hard, he's going to make himself better. Reevaluate his priorities, and try to understand the world as others see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T05:51:37-07:00","id":1324704,"title":"","content":"<b>219)</b> Reece Greene was having the time of his unlife, partying it up with the Sabbat. As a member of clan Gangrel, he took to the borderline demonic rituals and customs of the sect like a shark to bloody waters. He was powerful, he was terrifying, he was free! But that all changed one night, when the other members of his pack received The Beckoning.<br /> <br /> Out of nowhere, his priest and ductus suddenly thought it was a good idea for the pack to pull up stakes and take a one way trip to the middle east. No explanation given, just that they had to leave as quickly as possible! The fact that this sudden movement would have practically handed their territory over to the Camarilla on a silver platter didn't seem to cross any of their minds. Well, all except for Reece himself, who had surprisingly managed to avoid falling under The Beckoning's influence.<br /> <br /> Reece didn't go with the rest of the pack. A decision that he is almost certain has branded him a traitor in their eyes, but one which he will hopefully avoid the consequences of in the future. They seemed pretty convinced they were going to stay overseas for an indefinite period of time, so maybe they'll never see each other again?<br /> <br /> After losing his pack, and finding out he wasn't the only one facing such problems, Reece ingratiated himself with the Anarchs. Continuing to fight against the Camarilla's machinations, rather than roll over for them. For the most part, he finds it quite easy to cover up his past affiliations from his new allies. The Sabbat were the original Anarchs, after all, so as long as he makes an effort to hide his religious extremism from the public, most kindred assume he's just another in a very long list of violent thugs who find their way into the Anarchs' ranks.<br /> <br /> <b>Predator Type:</b> Alleycat<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>220)</b> Millie Marsh did not have a pleasant time during her early introduction into the world of kindred. As a devout believer in The Ministry's theological rebellion, her sire took pride in casting off the shackles of moral constraints and liberating herself from the oppression of false gods. As it happens, one of her favorite spiritual taboos was the targeting of children. To hear her sire defend themselves, they would tell you that mortals lock baby animals in cages for later consumption by the thousands every year. Why should doing the same to baby humans be seen as any more offensive, in a society that uses humans as a food source?<br /> <br /> Millie spent 5 long, grueling months chained up beneath her sire's haven, along with 4 other kids who had been abducted from their homes in the middle of the night. One by one, they were slowly drained of their blood, until Millie was the only one left alive. But by the time it was her turn to die, she had subconsciously absorbed enough of The Ministry's teachings to give her captor pause. Maybe it was the fear and desperation of the situation, but something in Millie compelled her to begin debating the finer points of Setite faith with the hungry vampire. And after an hour or two of doing so, they were impressed by her insight on the subject. So impressed, in fact, they decided to keep her around, and embraced Millie after draining the last of her blood.<br /> <br /> So now here she is, a fledgling Minister trapped forever in the body of a 14 year old girl. It was a difficult adjustment period, seeing as how most of the services that The Ministry provides catered to a more adult demographic. But after a while, she found her niche among the city's street kids. Orphans, runaways, gang members, young and impressionable minds who have become frustrated with society in one way or another. These are the kinds of mortals that Millie is able to reach out to, and indoctrinate them into the The Ministry's teachings.<br /> <br /> Her sire couldn't be happier with the situation, children are the future, as they say. And if some of them don't seem like they're cut out for long term service to The Ministry, well it's not like anybody is going to notice if these kids suddenly go missing!<br /> <br /> <b>Predator Type:</b> Cleaver","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T22:06:02-07:00","id":1324882,"title":"","content":"220) A discredited historian and archaeologist, made a laughing stock for his continued pursuit of &quot;ancient sunken civilizations&quot;. To him, Atlantis is just the tip of the iceberg, a cipher for greater and more varied ruins to be found beneath the waves all across the world. Delving into forgotten academic records, he looked for signs of underwater ruins that the scientific community may have dismissed or ignored. In time, he actually found something: records from a century prior that told of an explorer operating in Europe who found signs of a potential sight off the coast of Britain. (Modern archaeologists now accept that &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doggerland\" target=\"_blank\">Doggerland</a>&quot; was a real stretch of land that filled out that space around the island, connecting it to continental Europe, prior to the end of the last Ice Age).<br /> <br /> The researcher wasn't entirely circumspect about the trip that followed, as his inquiries into local rumors attracted the attention of parties interested in keeping certain buried civilizations buried. He ALSO attracted the attention of a Setite researcher, who wanted the truth buried, but also wanted it claimed for the Followers of Set. So the vampire struck up a friendship with the mortal, helping him uncover more evidence and clues (while making sure they wouldn't appear again after their journey concluded). They chartered a boat out into North Sea and weighed anchor, intending to dive down and look for where they thought it was.<br /> <br /> That's when the Technocracy hit squad arrived, trying to threaten the men into silence.<br /> <br /> An altercation occurred, and they were both shot. The Setite, of course, was minimally injured, falling into the water to escape capture. But so did his mortal protege, who would soon succumb to his wounds if drowning didn't do him in first. Not wishing to squander such a bright resource, the Setite embraced the mortal down there, beneath the waves. Their boat scuttled, the two descended to the bottom, and proceeded to continue their journey.<br /> <br /> They found a small ruin of algae-covered stone walls and buildings. Clearing away debris, they found an underground chamber, in which ancient carvings were preserved. The site was tiny, all things considered, but it implied greater things elsewhere. Before they could fully explore the site, though, they were forced away by aquatic <i>things</i>, down in lightless depths. The fledgling's sire later concluded that it was probably Mariner Gangrel, but the fledgling himself wasn't sure. Were they actually aquatic vampires? Or were they something different?<br /> <br /> In the years since, the historian has pursued many such leads, diving down to explore sunken, Cyclopean ruins. On more than one occasion, he's encountered fish-like humanoids, but in the night diving he must engage in, discerning their nature is difficult. Other Setites scoff at the idea that merfolk inhabit the seas. &quot;Even if they had existed, and weren't Cainite or Setite,&quot; they said, &quot;they'd surely be extinct by now.&quot; Nonetheless, he remains undaunted. He not only wishes to discover what time and the sea has forgotten, but what living creatures remain, under the waves. And why they seem so intent on thwarting him.<br /> <br /> (As is implied, the &quot;merfolk&quot; might, in fact, be Bygones. This Setite, however, doesn't know the significance of the term. Technocrats would, though, as would other Mages.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T11:43:13-07:00","id":1333710,"title":"","content":"221) One of the rare Cappadocians embraced in the modern age, this man was a student of micro-biology. He grabbed the attention of his sire when the two had a chance meeting in a swamp. The Cappadocian Elder seeking a cadaver suspected to be in the area, the student collecting pond water samples after a long day of classes. The two wandered for a time together, and spoke of microbes. The Elder still found the idea of micro-organisms to be strange, and so listened intently as the student explained what he learned. Eventually the two parted ways, but the Cappadocian kept tabs on the student.<br /> <br /> When the pressures of university life caused the student to burn out, the Cappadocian was there to pick up the pieces. The Elder didn't want the bright mind extinguished. As the Elder said, &quot;It's alright to pause here, your education can continue later, when you're ready. There is always more time.&quot; And indeed, there would be more time. Now the student has all the time in the world.<br /> <br /> Since becoming Cappadocian, the micro-biologist has bent the powers of Necromancy down, to that minute level. Germs are &quot;born&quot;, live, and die very rapidly. What more perfect environment exists for the task of unlocking the secrets of Life and Death? For still, after so many years of looking into microscopes, man and vampire still find <a href=\"https://youtu.be/oRmbWj2ZITM\" target=\"_blank\">Death quite mysterious on the microscopic level</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-07T08:45:40-07:00","id":1334353,"title":"","content":"<b>222)</b><br /> <br /> Helen (Lowndes) Goldsborough was born on the Eastern Shore of Maryland, to the town doctor, and the town librarian. Tilghman was a quiet, secluded town most of the year. Helen was a bit of a tomboy, and enjoyed wandering the fields and hammocks along the Chesapeake Bay. Alone in the yard, she would line up her dolls and preside over royal teas and courtly intrigues. She would gather seashells to make a crown, and a cattail for her scepter.<br /> <br /> Helen loved the quiet times of the year, when all you could hear was the tide gurgling in and out across the mudflats, dry leaves rattling on the trees, and, maybe, the rumble of a tractor hauling feed corn to the barns. In winter, the bay waters along the shore would freeze into a delicate lace of mud and ice, and the wind would try to pick her up and carry her into the sky. Spring was prosaically beautiful with more flowers than little Helen could count, and dragonflies swarming like an army of faeries. Spring was sad, though, because it meant the summer people would return soon.<br /> <br /> Every summer seasonal people would move into their weekend homes, hosting raucous parties on the marshy beach and careening fancy cars across Tilghman's one causeway to the mainland. (And, once or twice a year, off the causeway into the brackish water.) Helen came to envy and resent those Summer People. Truth be told, she feared them a little. The mothers wore such short skirts, and the men guffawed and slapped one another on the back when they had too many cocktails. Even their children seemed like strange aliens, with their foreign games and sports.<br /> <br /> Helen, at sixteen, gained a new appreciation for the summer people. One of them in particular, actually. She was courted by Henry Goldsborough, the son of a factory owner from Baltimore. They married after Henry returned from the war in Europe. Henry passed the bar, and Helen worked as a secretary in his thriving law office. By the time Helen had their son, William, they were able to have Helen stay home. Henry ran for, and won, a seat in the State Senate. They bought a rambling Victorian farmhouse on ten acres on the edge of town.<br /> <br /> Those were happy years for Helen. She grew prize-winning roses, and chaired the local garden club. She was president of the school board, and invested some of her inheritance in rental cottages. She opened a kennel and bred Papillons, winning best in show at the AKC nationals in 1967. Helen loved those dogs dearly, and they were a great comfort to her when William died in Viet Nam, and Henry died of a heart attack within six months of one another.<br /> <br /> Helen knew she had to pick up and carry on, so she got her real estate license and opened an agency, mostly managing seasonal rentals. She loved Tilghman so much, it was a true honor to help others make their homes there. Plus, it let her pick and choose the &quot;right sort&quot; of people and businesses to have in town. She wouldn't stand for any riff-raff or dirty people in her hometown, believe you me.<br /> <br /> By the time of her retirement, in 2003 at nearly eighty years of age, she was known around Tilghman as a tireless worker in making the town a better place, but also quite the busy-body. She snuck her nose into everyone's business. If a local husband was philandering, Helen would inform the wife, in gentle, sympathetic tones... while secretly reveling with glee over her own power. If a child was being abused, Helen was the first to call Child Services. If a movie with nude scenes or too much violence came to the local theater, trust Helen to write the editorial in the local paper decrying the decline of virtue. She served on the church board, and arranged the firing of at least three ministers over the decades for &quot;unorthodox&quot; content in their sermons, but always organized the clothing drive for disadvantaged youth. If a tosspot family came on hard times, Helen was quick to lobby for their employment at a local business... or else subtly push them out of town.<br /> <br /> Three Sabbat found Helen as she was walking her dogs along the fetid bay after the July Fourth fireworks. The ragtag pack was looking for cannon fodder to distract some Archons hot on their tails, and put her (and a summer family) through the creation rites. When Helen crawled out of her grave, she saw her attackers (&quot;Those hooligans!&quot;) fighting handsome young men in military outfits. Starving, Helen jumped onto one Sabbat after another, draining them dry in a cannibalistic frenzy. Finally sated, the Archons informed her she was a vampire.<br /> <br /> The nearest Prince, in Salisbury, Maryland, accepted her and determined her clan to be Old Clan Tzimisce. This caused some stir at the tiny Elysium, but what could they do? She had saved the lives of several Archons, and was owed multiple life boons. These have allowed her to keep the sect at arm's length, while claiming their protection when needed. (No one bothered to tell her about her soil dependence, but she has never slept outside her barn's root cellar in Tilghman, so remains unaware.)<br /> <br /> Helen has settled into semi-autarky in Tilghman. She works hard to make her little seaside village absolutely perfect. Visitors to Tilghman find a quaint and spotless town square, that looks like a back-lot set from a Disney movie. The parks are groomed like a golf green, and every home is in perfect repair. All the locals wear benign smiles, and all the children play quietly in a very expensive playground the town council just installed last year. Even the streetlights are cleaned regularly, and hung with seasonal flower decorations.<br /> <br /> Tilghman has become known for its charity and public-spiritedness. There have been carnivals to raise money for African famines, lobbying campaigns for environmental protection for the bay, and, at the monthly blood drive in the town hall, every adult in town lines up to help others in need.<br /> <br /> The only hint that anything is amiss are the animals. From slobbering Labradors to stray cats, from otters in the bay to seagulls in the sky... they all look at people with an unsettling gaze, as if there is an arcane intelligence within the beasts, critiquing the town and looking for flaws. These are Helen's secret police. They look for visitors with good genes who are introduced to local harlots, as part of Helen's eugenics program. Visitors with lots of money, brains, or good looks may even be Dominated into buying a house and relocating to Tilghman full time, taking the place of a less valued previous resident.<br /> <br /> Those locals who don't measure up are dealt with harshly. Those who are grumpy or impolite are corrected and assisted in becoming a more pleasant neighbor, with brainwashing of a cult-like efficiency. Anyone with true criminal or antisocial tendencies is fed to Helen's pack of ghouled Papillon, who buzz through the unfortunate like a pack of piranha. Last year, there were bad words grafittied on the back door of a local business. Helen found the miscreant and had his mother rip out the delinquent's eyes; the vandal was eleven years old.<br /> <br /> If you'd like an audience with Helen Goldsborough, just go to Tilghman and stroll along the brick lanes and peek over the white picket fences. She'll be the old woman in the big floppy hat, kneeling on a foam pad, pruning shears in hand. If you're polite and pleasant, she'll return the favor and invite you to help in her garden while you chat. If you are rude, however, well... you can help her garden in another way.<br /> <br /> Her hydrangeas get such a beautiful color when fertilized with vampire ashes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T12:23:54-07:00","id":1335933,"title":"","content":"223) An Old Clan Tzimisce, trained as both a tracker and detective. He calls himself &quot;Houndmaster&quot;, because he's never found without at least one large, trained hound by his side. Ever since his mortal youth, he found dogs more agreeable than people. On this, he and his sire were in accord, which is what attracted the latter to the former. That, and the youth's skill at finding creatures...and people.<br /> <br /> Skilled in Animalism and Auspex, he is sent forth to various cities, on a mission from his sire. That mission being to find Sabbat vampires (especially Vicissitude using Tzimisce), sniff out their havens, study their movements, and know their ways. Collect as much data on the Sword of Caine and the &quot;diseased&quot; main Clan Tzimisce, and report it to his sire. Other agents will know what to do with the information.<br /> <br /> He's only rarely met these other agents, in league with his sire. On occasion, he's needed to directly convey information or help them scout Sabbat havens. Or obtain and deliver body samples or favored objects, collected by birds or rodents (never his prized ghoul hounds). Who are these people, his sire works with? At first, he thinks Ordea League, looking to muscle out the Sabbat at last. Now, he's not so sure. These other agents are strange, and manifestly not Tzimisce, Old Clan or otherwise. They invoke strange powers, or have an unnatural air about them.<br /> <br /> Only once, he shook the hand of one such agent. Unconsciously, he derived an impression of them using Psychometry. It was dark, foreboding, and had the essence of the grave. Through the flood of stimuli, three words could be made out: &quot;True. Black. Hand.&quot;<br /> <br /> He doesn't know what it means. But he cannot help wondering. It won't be long before the urge to investigate this mysterious &quot;True Hand&quot; becomes overpowering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T12:31:48-07:00","id":1336926,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> <br /> <br /> I like #223 a great deal. OCTz make excellent spies and trackers. It's an excellent concept for a pc. It has a broad mission to fulfill, while operating more-or-less independently. Well done.<br /> <br /> Fun note: &quot;True. Black. Hand.&quot; is grammatically ambiguous. Is it a true version of the black hand, or a hand which is truly black? I think the sect planned it that way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T22:09:16-07:00","id":1337020,"title":"","content":"Well, I didn't use this for my PC, so I thought I might as well throw this in here.<br /> <br /> 224) Rack owners, Keepers of Elysium, and Harpies tend to be highly empathic, energetic, dynamic people with strong aesthetic sense and instincts for trends and popular culture...and as such they tend to be of passionate, driven, and humane clans like Toreador, Brujah, Malkavian, maybe even the more fun among the Gangrel and Ventrue. Not this one -- nope, this one's a <i>Tzimisce</i>.<br /> <br /> When the Camarilla moved in, this Tzimisce gave a message and an offer: they're neutral, pledged to neutrality, their domain is neutral, and anyone (other than Tremere) who obeys the <i>proper</i> etiquette is welcome to use their space to feed and negotiate. No competition under any circumstance will be tolerated, and will be met with the harshest reprisal. In exchange, the Tzimisce tracks prestation independently and stays out of city politics.<br /> <br /> Sure, some among the Camarilla and Anarchs made plays against the Tzimisce; surely enough the Tzimisce was good to their word, but never escalated conflict beyond turning would-be rivals into delicately-crafted &quot;do not fuck with me&quot; statements. The Tremere flipped their shit over it, but they had as much success dislodging this Tzimisce as anyone else. But once again, even in the face of Tremere fuckery, the Tzimisce remained good to their word.<br /> <br /> It may be a little weird having a member of the Camarilla's most avowed enemy clan, and a vampire who's still <i>technically</i> blood-hunted in the city, being the exclusive owner of the Racks and the Keeper of Elysium. But the reality is, pragmatism always triumphs, and it would be a bigger pain in the ass to get rid of this Tzimisce and deal with the fallout, than it is to just let them be. Honestly, the Tzimisce's a more effective and efficient administrator than any Toreador or Brujah could ever hope to be, and younger vampires certainly seem to appreciate its avowed and demonstrated impartiality, which has led to substantial gains against typically biased city leadership.<br /> <br /> For the Tzimisce, it's a cunning survival strategy based on weaponizing two personal quirks. The simpler to explain is they're privacy-obsessed even by Tzimisce standards, and can barely tolerate leaving their own domain let alone setting foot on others'; it's advantageous to curate one's own domain into a space others will choose to come, on the Tzimisce's terms, than leave. The harder to explain is the Tzimisce is obsessed with numbers, mathematics, and statistics; finances, social capital (prestation), gathering data about current trends, modeling and predictions, game theory.<br /> <br /> The Racks and Elysium are in the Tzimisce's mind one giant aquarium: watch, gather data, see if they can predict what happens next, and refine models for future predictive value. Tapping on the glass, or allowing others to do it, agitates the specimens, ruins data collection, and interferes with modeling behavior; something the Tzimisce will not tolerate. After decades (centuries?) the Tzimisce has grown quite skilled at observing and predicting mortal behavior and trends, and runs their domain with surgical efficacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T14:16:27-07:00","id":1337267,"title":"","content":"[Let's get a little silly, shall we?]<br /> <br /> <br /> 225) A Malkavian who dresses and talks like a pirate.<br /> <br /> Yes, really. Honestly, it's not even the strangest thing to come out of Clan Malkavian.<br /> <br /> However, he's not exactly a mindless stereotype of a lunatic with a gimmick. He only ACTS like he is. His madness is not that he's delusional, thinking he's a pirate. His madness is an obsession with a dream...and of revenge.<br /> <br /> In life, he worked for years to build and run a small pirate-themed amusement park. It had boat tours, sailing around the local lake, a couple roller coasters, a seafood restaurant, an arcade full of pirate-themed games, and a big stage for putting on shows, in the shape of a pirate ship. It wasn't the most extravagant place in the world, but it was the best the city had for a good long while. The kids loved it, and the teens came around because at the time there wasn't much else to do (and, again, it had an arcade). Most of all, it was HIS.<br /> <br /> Then the new highway came in, making it easier than ever to get from this city to the neighboring one. It just so happened that said neighboring city built a big, huge amusement park. Competition would have been difficult enough - for a while his place survived mostly on attendants who didn't want to drive too far - but then the recession hit. The big park could weather the downturn well enough. The small pirate park could not. He shut the gates after years of continuous service, heartbroken.<br /> <br /> He was wandering the empty park one night, half-drunk and contemplating suicide, when his sire found him. An out-of-towner, who took shelter in the defunct park. They got talking, he cried as he told his story, and the Malkavian offered him the Embrace. For what reason, no one can say. Pity perhaps? As a potential tool in the Jyhad? Because the Malkavian believed in this man's dream? Or simply on a whim?<br /> <br /> Whatever the case, the old park owner runs around town, decked in pirate costume from when the park was functioning. Talking like a pirate, including a thick wall of period-accurate lingo. Other Kindred rightfully consider him a non-threat...which is exactly how he likes it.<br /> <br /> See, this Malkavian has plans. He wants to not only get his old park up and running again, he wants to get revenge on that rival amusement park one city over. This requires both resources and connections. And the ability to come and go in that domain as he pleases, without arousing the suspicion of its resident Kindred. Ruining the reputation and operation of an amusement park requires time and effort, as well as the ability to get authorities in charge - safety inspectors, local news, parents groups, etc. - to pass judgement on that park, and find it wanting.<br /> <br /> Plus, that rival park is the domain of a different vampire. To prosecute his revenge, he'll have to wade knee deep into the Jyhad. But this ol' sea dog ain't afraid to get wet, y'arr!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T07:00:45-07:00","id":1337971,"title":"","content":"<b>226)</b><br /> <br /> Shirley Potts was born in Shaker Heights, Ohio, in 1930. Her father was a pharmacist, and her mother had been a high school math teacher before Shirley was born.<br /> <br /> Shirley's life changed forever in 1937 when Dr. Potts was struck by a streetcar and killed. Widowed during the depression, her mother had to go back to work as both a substitute teacher and a stocking clerk at Sears. Shirley spent many long hours alone after school waiting for her mother to return from work. Shirley kept the house, though that didn't take long, as it was a one room apartment over the garage of a distant relative. Every night, at nine-fifteen, her mother would trudge home up the bus stop, and eat the meal Shirley had made for her.<br /> <br /> During the long, quiet hours between school and dinner, Shirley read books leftover from their former lives. By the time she was 9, she had worked her way through Organic Chemistry and Calculus II. She got excellent marks in school, though her teachers barely noticed the shy, bookish girl. She never raised her hand in class, though she always knew the answers. Teachers never called on her, since they knew Shirley knew the answers. The teachers were too busy helping the students who needed help.<br /> <br /> By the age of 12, Shirley got permission from her mother to ride buses unattended, which allowed studying at the public library. She needed little time for her schoolwork, as she usually worked her way through her courses by October each year. No, she studied her own subjects. She would wander the stacks, running her hand along the book spines. She loved how every book had a Dewey Decimal number on it, so it could be in the correct place every time she looked for it. It was so neat and tidy. A whole world in straight rows, cross-referenced, and summarized in the card catalog. Soon, Shirley had exhausted the Shaker Heights library,and switched to the big library downtown.<br /> <br /> In high school, Shirley got straight A's, but really excelled in math. It was like the demimonde of a library: orderly and organized, but with fun back-currents and surprising interactions to find. She wanted to be an engineer, but her school only offered shop classes, mechanical drawing, and applied physics classes to the boys. Girls were relegated to home economics. Disappointed, Shirley applied to engineering colleges in he senior year, but lacking the background coursework she was not accepted. She adjusted her academic plan.<br /> <br /> Shirley graduated with a dual degree in Mathematics and Library Science from Western Reserve. That summer, her mother had a heart attack. Shirley would have to take a job offer from Cleveland city hall, organizing files, to pay the rent. Her mother wasn't the only one with a broken heart. Shirley had never really thought of marriage, but how could she ask a man to support her mother. She resigned herself to a life as an old maid.<br /> <br /> From 1952 to 1997, Shirley worked that civil service job. She became head of the records department, fanatically keeping all the data up to date and stored in the latest format. Whether with microfiche or mainframes, there wasn't a record in Cuyahoga County she couldn't find. Her co-workers knew her as a quiet boss, the sort who walks up behind you and startles you with a mistake she sees over your shoulder. She retired on a modest pension, and lived in a small brick house whose floors groaned under the weight of bookshelves, dusty computer equipment, and small appliances she was fixing for her neighbors.<br /> <br /> That's when the Camarilla decided to retake Cleveland. The Tremere had set up a provisional haven in an electronics store near Shirley's home. One evening she went there to buy a new rheostat for the widower Mr. Saluski's toaster oven. Her sire was behind the counter, organizing files on suspected Sabbat safehouses. Not noticing Shirley, he was startled when she said, &quot;That property on Quincy Avenue is labeled wrong. It's in Central, not Fairfax.&quot;<br /> <br /> She had assumed he was working on a real-estate search, and he was impressed she had caught the flaw from across the counter. After a week of polite examination of her skills, he ghouled her. After another week, he gave up trying to keep secrets from her. Given full access to Camarilla resources, she proved instrumental in the Camarilla's assault in Northeast Ohio. She combed through city, utility, and financial records to find likely Sabbat holdings. She cooked up reasons for daylight code inspections and utility interruptions.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla assault failed, but the sect decided to maintain a beach-head in Cleveland with a full Chantry under the library of Case Western University. Shirley was embraced and got to work researching the sect's enemies in town, and across the globe.<br /> <br /> She focused her development as a vampire on her disciplines. She uses Auspex to boost her ability to comb through records and find flaws in security systems. She insisted on learning Focused Mind as her primary path as soon as she heard of it. Her main weapons, though, are handful of rituals, including Bureaucratic Condemnation, Expedient Paperwork, and Deny the Intruder. She hopes to learn Technomancy and Conjuring.<br /> <br /> Shirley is not afraid of field-work, if she needs physical access to records. In fact, she finds it the best part of her job, going out to see how other people have set up their systems. Now, she just needs a coterie who can assist her in her missions.<br /> <br /> No record is safe with Shirley Potts on the job, whether it's repair requisitions for cemeteries damaged during mass embraces, or the health insurance records of vampire hunters. She may look like a little old lady, with a pen hanging on a lanyard around her neck, but she is a serious bureaucratic badass.<br /> <br /> Her main flaw? Mister Saluski is still waiting for his toaster oven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T08:11:43-07:00","id":1338461,"title":"","content":"#227 Caitff, embraced to be saved from the terrible car accident that could have cost his/her life. Learns how to be a vampire, how to hunt, how to hide.<br /> Finally his/her sire brings him in an hospital where he/she finds<br /> <br /> #228 His/Her Boyfriend/Girlfriend, in a coma since the accident. The ony chance to save him/her is Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T20:29:13-07:00","id":1338558,"title":"","content":"229) A Ravnos embraced as a little girl (~10-12 years of age), who specializes in Animalism and Chimestry. Always accompanied by her pet black cat - named Secret - that is missing an eye.<br /> <br /> Coming from an abusive household, the girl found a kitten one day and kept her in secret (hence the name) from her violent father. Inevitably, the cat was discovered, and the father tried to kill it. Hence, the missing eye. She ran away with the cat, sobbing and without a clue about what to do with her injured cat (or, indeed, where she would even go).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately (or fortunately), the scent of Secret's blood attracted a Ravnos that had fallen to Wassail. The girl tried to protect her cat, and was drained for her trouble. She died muttering &quot;it's not fair&quot;. Somewhere in the Wight's broken psyche, a shred of...something...stirred. Was it guilt, at having killed a child? Was it a memory of long-ago injustice? Was it merely a hint of whimsy? Whatever the case, the Wight embraced the child, and lingered only so long to see her rise as an undead.<br /> <br /> The girl's Ravnos weakness manifests as a drive to met out Justice. Her first nights as a vampire were spent haunting her father's house, using her way with animals and illusions to psychologically torment the man. Feeding on him when he slept (or lay passed out drunk on the couch), so he was perpetually tired. Having his food and possessions gnawed on by rats, and his car and windows defiled by birds. In the dead of night, he would see figments out of the corner of his eye, or hear noises he could not place. They wheeled him off to an asylum within months, and the girl was, at last, free to wander. Justice was served.<br /> <br /> Walking the streets at night, she is accompanied by her one-eyed cat ghoul. Her favorite hunting tactic is to have Secret hide, and then pretend to be a lost child looking for her cat. Those who offer to help, she leads on a performative search, before allowing them to &quot;find&quot; Secret, then letting the person leave unmolested. She can gather all the animals she requires, so the girl is never in danger of going hungry. Those who refuse to help, she stalks from afar, sneaking up and feeding from them; a just reward for callous indifference (also, the loss of the contents of their wallets). In the sadly not uncommon event that the individuals seek to take advantage of the little girl, she never goes without backup close at hand. Her favorite allies are alley cats, and flocks of night birds, ready to claw and peck assailants. It's almost a mercy for her to deliver the mind-numbing Kiss, taking their blood (and usually all their clothes and possessions) as punishment.<br /> <br /> Her innocence is a double-edged sword. She's not malicious by nature, but she's perhaps not cognizant of her potential for cruelty. The treatment of her father was (arguably) less terrible than it could have been (and equally arguably he perhaps deserved what he got), but it shows how much harm she could do, given the right motivation or lack of understanding. Here's hoping she either matures, or gains a Mentor who can guide her. If nothing else, Kindred society is loathe to allow an uncontrolled child vampire to run loose, unsupervised and dispensing &quot;justice&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, there's the matter of her Wassailed sire. The more she learns of vampires, the more she will realize how dangerous it is, not only for her to ignore her Humanity, but to allow that old Wight to unlive. Did it get put down already? Or is it still out there, waiting for someone to end it? Will that someone need to be her?<br /> <br /> Can judgement truly be passed down on a being who understands not what they do? And does that question apply more towards the Wight, or to her?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T15:34:54-07:00","id":1345342,"title":"","content":"I feel like taking a break from my usual &quot;block of text&quot;, character concept posts in this thread.<br /> <br /> Today's post is a lightning round. Very brief vignettes of stuff that, while fun, probably doesn't need so much depth. In honor of the Day of the Dead, I'm making a loose-knit pack of Sabbat residing in Mexico. Frankly, their stories could happen anywhere.<br /> <br /> (Usual disclaimer: this thread is over three years old. If I accidentally recycle an old idea which bubbles up from my subconscious, forgive me.) <hr />230) <b>The Terrified Attack Dog </b>Chato was raised in a crime-ridden neighborhood and had to front tough, since the time he was seven and his older brother broke his nose fighting over a snack cake. In truth, he was constantly, secretly, terrified. He joined a gang, rose through the ranks, leaving behind a trail of crazed, blood-splattered violence. A City Gangrel of the Sabbat embraced him. Chato has been True Sabbat for a few years, but feels left out among his clan. The rest have learned to take animal form, and make (cautious) fun of him for not running with them as a wolf, or bear, or cougar, or whatever. Last night, Chato finally managed to turn into an animal! He was so happy. Then he realized his fight form was a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pug\" target=\"_blank\">Pug</a> dog. His flight form? A fucking goldfish. He is considering walking into the sun.<br /> <br /> 231) <b>Pedo's Nightmare </b>Lydia, who was embraced at sixteen, is a Toreador antitribu, and sex worker on a mission. She spends her nights displaying her underage wares on the dance floors of the seediest tourist bars of Acapulco. She closes the deal out back by the dumpster. She really enjoys finding a married businessman looking for teenaged side-fun on vacation, and punishing him for his pervy sins. Usually she just feeds and leaves a hickey or two for him to explain to his wife. On occasion, she has bitten down a lot harder than she needs to for a simple feeding. Then the gringo can go explain what happened to an ER doctor sewing up the bloody stump.<br /> <br /> 232) <b>Chat Show Accuser </b>Jorge Osito was a household name in Mexico. With a cuddly dad-bod, sparkling eyes, and a boyish grin, no one minded when he picked some random person and exposed all their most personal trash on his daytime talk show. He started out as an investigative journalist with high ideals and nearly supernatural instincts for uncovering secrets. He wound up peddling everyone's deepest shames to pay for his mansion in Polanco and a fleet of fancy sports cars. He exposed husbands who weren't the father, mothers who slept with their sons, politicians who took bribes to ignore murder, and priests who rubbed little boys. About half of what he &quot;exposed&quot; was true, but, hey, what mattered was telling a compelling story to get ratings. In that department, he was king. After investigating a biker bar in Hermosillo, the owners decided they could use Jorge's detective skills. He is now a Nosferatu antitribu who digs up secrets on Camarilla and Anarch licks. Sometimes for blackmail, sometimes just to see what happens when he reveals them. He still wears designer labels and drives a Maserati, even if his looks are long gone.<br /> <br /> 233) <b>Reluctant Daughter of Privilege </b>Leona was a brilliant, but deeply insecure, PhD candidate working on a thesis about the social psychology of small working groups in NGO settings. Her sire accidentally embraced her while feeding on this random nerd. Not wanting to admit such a rookie mistake to the rest of the Amici Noctis, he claimed it was on purpose and tutored her as his prized pupil. Luckier still for Leona, her sire was Gratiano de Veronese. Her sire has left town and Leona is leading her own small pack. She is terrified of someone seeking out her blood. She desperately hides her lineage from others, but that's becoming harder and harder. Leona has been pondering her sect allegiance. The Camarilla seems to actually value those with pedigree...<br /> <br /> 234) <b>Woman, Taken by the Wind </b>Estrella de Rhiannon spent her days in the late 60s and early 70's wandering Mexico and the Southwestern US in a hippie van, telling fortunes for spare change, and discussing Carlos Castaneda while waiting tables in college towns. She was shovelheaded during the Festival de Avandaro, a 1971 music happening with hippies, bikers, and leftie students. Now a Malkavian antitribu, Estrella usually presents as a gently smiling hippie in flowing silk gowns, sewn thick with silver bangles. She sings a little Fleetwood Mac on street corners, reads a few palms, and firmly refuses to take part in any violence. She says, &quot;All violence is damage to the universe, and, so, damage to yourself. Why can't you see that?&quot; Every so often, however, when the spirit strikes her, she enters a week-long vision quest. These visions tell her of a person, mortal or vampire, who needs to die for the greater good. When these visions strike, she will do anything... anything... to complete her mission. She becomes a terrifying spirit of vengance, like something from a Greek myth, and is amazingly good at identifying targets. She has targeted secret hunters, Camarilla ghouls, and even a family of Spiral Dancer kinfolk who all needed killing. Now, she has had a vision of Pierre Bellemare, a powerful Sabbat of Montreal. In the past, her pack has always admitted (after the fact) that Estrella had chosen targets wisely, but killing a fellow Sabbat for no reason? It just isn't done.<br /> <br /> 235) <b>Should Have Kept the Receipt </b>Don Fredo trained as a plumber and a construction worker. He saved up his money and bought an apartment house. He fixed it up and bought another one. Then another, then another, then a strip mall, then an office building. By the time he was 40, he had become a rich man who commanded whole sectors of the economy. He had hundreds of employees and dozens of overseas bank accounts. He had a new wife every five years, and nothing but the best cocaine. Unfortunately, at 63, he was diagnosed with terminal cancer. He had long heard rumors of vampires in Mexico City, and sought them out for a cure. He was ghouled by a Lasombra fledgling, and bankrolled her pack for twenty years in exchange for vitae. The pack was destroyed by a pack of Garou, and Fredo was desperate. He found a vampire and begged to buy the embrace from him. He gave the vampire every penny he had for an eternal life of power and respect. It was only after the fact that Fredo realized he had been robbed. The sire had the most watery of blood. Now, Fredo is a penniless thinblood... a joke among real vampires. He despairs he will never be a True Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","user":"Nosimplehiway","date":". 11-01-2019, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T16:58:43-07:00","id":1345350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1345342#post1345342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His flight form? A fucking goldfish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I never realized this before, but a vampire fish probably wouldn't suffocate on dry land!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T22:33:08-07:00","id":1345529,"title":"","content":"236) A Nosferatu who is the secret controller of an architecture firm, with some ties to construction companies hired to put those plans into action. Of course, all vampires have angles, and his is to sneak in a variety of off-the-books additions to the floorplans. The blueprints that are logged - both in the firm's files and on municipal records - are not the blueprints handed to the builders, who just nod and do as they're told. The additions are usually subtle things. A crawl space here. A dividing wall slightly too thick there. In recent years, the Nos was able to score the contract to design the layouts for an entire suburban neighborhood, which he has seeded fully with a series of simple ways to enter and hide inside the homes. When a particularly flexible vampire (like the Nossie in question) can squeeze through these secret passages, a Herd is easy to cultivate. Especially when combined with the city's sewage and drainage system.<br /> <br /> <br /> 237) A Scout Gargoyle (see V20: Lore of the Bloodlines) who has carved out a niche for himself in a port town nearby to a small island. The island, notorious for the presence of smugglers, is a spot where a great deal of drugs come and go. So prominent is this smuggling, then, that authorities watch both the bridge connecting to the island and the surrounding bay. But neither the checkpoints nor coast guard boats pay much attention to the skies above the bay. An enterprising vampire with the power of flight can readily carry pockets of cocaine over from the island, and delivered via drop to distributors. Sometimes, he's even called upon to make deliveries to the tops of tall buildings, for the benefit of rich and important VIPs. Of course, as a Scout, he's also got plenty of experience with Obfuscate. Sometimes he sticks around - whether in drug dens or high rises - to learn what the recipients of his shipments are up to. To cover him, he's got a ghoul who acts as a liaison with his customers, who makes sure the product reaches its proper destination. The ghoul is aware that his boss isn't quite human (both because of chance partial slipping of Obfuscate during meetings, and inferred by the boss's ability to seemingly get anywhere), but keeps this to himself. The two enjoy a mutually beneficial relationship. However, the ghoul also knows things about their clients, and is starting to pay attention to signs of monsters hiding in plain sight. He has ambition, and would see his master obtain greater power in these modern nights. The Gargoyle is hesitant, but begins to wonder himself whether he doesn't deserve more than eking out an unliving on the fringes of Kindred society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T21:09:19-08:00","id":1346353,"title":"","content":"One of the coterie's member's mortal friends calls, hysterical that their child has disappeared after reciting cultish propaganda. The parents hired a private investigator who located the child on a commune in the middle of nowhere. But, the PI reports unbelievable accounts of members of the commune lifting the rear end of trucks by hand. <br /> <br /> Then, the stories of an energy drink from the commune that promises the strength of 5 men. Just make sure you drink 3 days worth for maximum effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T21:22:04-08:00","id":1346356,"title":"","content":"While out carousing The Rack, looking for an easy meal, the coterie runs into a typical sorostitute, asking for a ride home. <br /> <br /> On the way, they discover she's anything but what she appeaes to be, and is actually a capricious, powerful elder up for playing games with players for the night. Games that may end in diablerie. In her favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T09:13:34-08:00","id":1346475,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25666\" data-vbnamecard=\"25666\">Illuminostro</a> <br /> <br /> Awesome see somebody new on the forums who is eager to jump in. Welcome!<br /> <br /> Just a heads up. Traditionally when we post character concepts on this thread, we number them as we go. Makes for easier reference when discussing them later.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest using 238 and 239, maybe, for yours. Except... I'm not clear on what the character concepts are, or how many of them there are.<br /> <br /> Also, what exactly is a &quot;sorostitute&quot;? Is this slang for somebody whose car has broken down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T10:08:44-08:00","id":1346495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1346475#post1346475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what exactly is a &quot;sorostitute&quot;? Is this slang for somebody whose car has broken down?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's slang for a female college student who has many sexual partners. Sorority + prostitute. There isn't a male equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T10:25:35-08:00","id":1346501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1346495#post1346495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's slang for a female college student who has many sexual partners. Sorority + prostitute. There isn't a male equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh.<br /> <br /> Thank you, False Epiphany.<br /> <br /> A slang term that has no male equivalent is usually not a good sign.<br /> <br /> Sigh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T13:10:51-08:00","id":1350294,"title":"","content":"240) A con artist who managed to convince a borderline senile rich woman that he was her long lost son. He thought it would be an easy gig, insinuating himself into her good graces and living a life of wealth then on. What he didn't count on was that his con would work a little too well. Nor did he realize the old woman was a member of the family Giovanni.<br /> <br /> Plenty of the family were suspicious of this suddenly reappeared family member they barely remembered. But &quot;his mother&quot; had the ear of older Giovanni, who let it all slide. That the con artist had a keen eye for money and could sweet-talk people (whether potential customers, business partners, or members of the family) helped his chances. His new &quot;relatives&quot; started giving him business offers, while also testing his capabilities. Thinking he was just being probed as to his true identity - and liking the opportunities he was being given - he rushed headlong into family affairs (at least, the mortal ones).<br /> <br /> In time, he was judged sufficiently useful to warrant the Embrace, and was &quot;brought into the fold&quot; as it were. Immortality and supernatural power weren't exactly what he signed on for, but he's hardly complaining. To his thinking, he'd had it made...so long as his ruse held up.<br /> <br /> Trouble came from the fact that Clan Giovanni weren't just merchants, but necromancers. One of the Ancillae of the family - who never trusted this slick fast-talker - came to the con artist one night. He had the only evidence he really needed to expose the Neonate: <i>the summoned and bound ghost of the family member he was impersonating</i>. He was, indeed, a fraud, and this older vampire could make this fact known at any time.<br /> <br /> Yes, Extortion is the name of the game. Not only must the False Giovanni make tithe to the Clan in his own name, but also kick up plenty of money (or souls, if it comes to it) to the lick that has him dead to rights. That is, if he doesn't want a load of vampire necromancers to show what happens to a deceiver in their midst. For the moment he maintains a facade that everything is fine; in truth, though, he's on the verge of panic, hemmed in by threats of final death (or worse) and by financial strain. He needs to find ways to get a lot of money quickly, or he'll unlive to regret all his life and unlife choices.<br /> <br /> And here, he thought conning that old woman would make things <i>easier</i> for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T23:01:25-08:00","id":1351972,"title":"","content":"241) A fashion model in the seventies, she lived a life of parties and privilege. Until, perhaps inevitably, she fell into the orbit of a Toreador, who found her beauty exquisite. She was his blood doll for a time, before he embraced her in a fit of passion. Almost as soon as he turned her, he came to regret his decision. Over the next few years, her spoiled and needy personality wore on his every nerve. When he could stand her no longer, he tried to get rid of her in the manner customary for the time: sending her to Russia and beyond the Shadow Curtain. Plenty of ways in, no way out.<br /> <br /> If she was meant to perish to the innumerable dangers of the Soviet Union and the methuselah that ruled its nights, she didn't comply. Oh certainly, she tried to leave, to no avail. Nor did she - a Western Toreador Neonate in the heart of Brujah-dominated Russia - have many Kindred to rely on. Just doing as Baba Yaga commanded was challenging enough.<br /> <br /> But it is said that some people thrive under pressure, and that challenges allow even the indolent to awaken to their full potential. Her good looks, sexuality, and command of Presence was enough to keep her above water, so to speak. Knowing she needed more powerful friends, however, she wormed her way into the social circles of the local underworld. Criminal sorts that would come to be known as the Mafiya. A particular Mafiya boss of some small power was in decline due to a wasting illness; she had little to offer at first, but her Vitae could keep the man alive. That she turned him into a thrall only helped. Under his tutelage, she learned how to manage a gang, how to shoot, and how to speak the language of organized crime.<br /> <br /> The man perished in a gang dispute that escalated to bullets, when she wasn't around to save him. But he'd taught her enough. When the Shadow Curtain fell and Kindred trapped by Baba Yaga's spell poured out of the country en masse, she was in a position to arrive back home and establish her credentials with the local Mafiya crime syndicates (in a manner of speaking). She even brought a few allies with her - strong Russian boys who looked to the &quot;old man's apprentice&quot; for their fortunes.<br /> <br /> Now she was back home, and ready to make her sire pay for using and discarding her. &quot;It is said, 'Revenge is a dish best served cold'. Well, it is <b>very</b> cold in Russia.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T23:41:09-08:00","id":1351974,"title":"","content":"242) The Twilight Tremere: A thinblood who managed to learn and master blood sorcery and passes through kindred society posing as Tremere and often taking payment in favors and secrets. Its easier to protect your secrets when you have the secrets of others to hold over them. They use blood sorcery nightly to boost their blood potency to complete the disguise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:25:30-08:00","id":1354460,"title":"","content":"243) When Kindred of different cities must have direct dealings, the city mice must call upon the expertise of the country mouse. This Brujah is one such country mouse, with the ferocity of a lion when provoked. Some of this &quot;poorly insulated electrical wire&quot; temper is customary among Brujah. Some of it comes from his experience in war.<br /> <br /> Before being drafted into WWI, this French man worked as a sketch artist for periodicals and magazines, mostly concerning natural scenes of the French countryside. He spent much of the war driving supply trucks, learning how to observe the environment (even at speed), find shortcuts, outrun pursuit, and spot ambushes. During times when the lines needed bolstering, he would be sent to man the trenches. Others might have broken under the pressure or developed shell shock, but he simply became angry. Angry at the war, at its orchestrators, at the senseless destruction of human life and the natural world, and at himself for having participated in the whole affair.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it was that seething fury that attracted his sire's attention. More likely, it was happenstance and convenience. He was caught in a cloud of mustard gas, and was too slow in putting on his gas mask (which, being an early model, was of limited use anyway). The Elder found the mortal, coughing up blood and thoroughly doomed, and turned him then and there. The Elder needed someone to escort him away from the fighting, and vampires didn't need to breathe.<br /> <br /> Nothing is ever simple, though. While his &quot;life&quot; was saved that night, an error in his Embrace left him with a Permanent Wound. A parting gift from the Great War, that leaves him waking every evening to the feeling of having been struck by mustard gas all over again. Is it any wonder his disposition is terse and irritable? Healing his lungs takes Vitae; there are many nights when he just lets the wounds be, to save on blood. The frequent pain does no favors to his already shaky mood.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, his choice of career, post-WWI, has permitted him lots of time on his own, where he isn't expect to talk or tolerate people. Between both World Wars, he lost all affection for his native Europe, and moved to the US. There, he drives various vehicles through the spaces between cities and towns. Delivering messages, transporting goods, and ferrying vampire clients (among others) across the expanse of untamed wilderness that hosts all manner of dangers for a vampire. Sometimes, when waiting for a pickup or when he's sure he's alone, he tries his hand at sketching examples of the natural world around him, however limited his perspective due to the eternal darkness that is his unlife.<br /> <br /> Just don't ask to see what he's made. Not unless you enjoy enduring his intense, unfriendly stares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T19:20:31-08:00","id":1354848,"title":"","content":"I just came up with Izzy, a Pander in what's left of the Sabbat in Mexico City in 2019. This is in V5.<br /> <br /> Physically, she's just a cute, freckled 12-year old girl, but she was always ruthless, manipulative and bossy, and impressed a perverted Pander who got the mad idea to try and Embrace her. It actually succeeded, but Izzy is a literal genius, and quickly understood much more about the old, adult-looking vampires in her pack than they understood about her. They all underestimated her, in fact. She eventually got her sire's pack to turn against him, and help her diablerize him.<br /> <br /> That was back in 2004 or so. Now, 15 years later, Izzy's the head of her own pack, a bunch of sinister Path of Night devotees that haunts the suburbs of Mexico City, committing various atrocities to mess with the Camarilla in the city. But Izzy herself is calm, soft-spoken and cautious, leaving the fighting to the &quot;adult&quot; vampires, while she leads them (and goads them) from the back ranks. She loves playing them against each other, and has her aim set for a much higher position in the Sabbat eventually - she just needs to show the higher-ups that she can do a good job, make a proper, feared Sabbat pack, of the idiots she's stuck with for now.<br /> <br /> Because she's so small and weak, Izzy seldom hunts alone in the streets. Instead, she's become a Cleaver, feeding from mortal families that she infiltrates. She does this through her ghoul Ram\u00f3n, an adoption agency employee. He pays various middle-class families good money to take her in, claiming she's an orphan, and Izzy quickly takes control over the family through gaslighting, blood bonds and Dominate. She then uses them as blood-bags for a few months, until they expire or neighbors and friends starts asking too many questions. Izzy then moves on, utilizing her adoption agency contact to find a new family to parasitize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","user":"Natsymir","date":". 12-13-2019, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24830-natsymir","name":"Natsymir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T00:07:30-08:00","id":1364487,"title":"","content":"245) A Telyav Tremere who started life as a disgruntled urban botanist, trying to bring the natural world back to the cities, one unauthorized planting at a time. Basically, he started as <a href=\"https://youtu.be/vvtqKMxZ95s\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a>. That is, of course, until he ran into his Sire while planting protected plant species in a vacant lot (thereby preventing it from being legally cleared and made into a parking lot). The two got to talking about all things plant, and eventually bonded, working on a number of projects over successive months. Eventually, he was turned, the Sire seeing in the botanist a kindred spirit.<br /> <br /> After a crash course in both vampirism and the pagan Thaumaturgy practiced by the Telyavs, the botanist began to consider how he was going to develop a sustainable Herd. He settled on a plan that would combine his botanical work, his newfound mysticism, and his long-time love of social activism.<br /> <br /> He started a cthonic cult.<br /> <br /> Specifically, he &quot;obtained&quot; warehouse space in a largely empty area of the city, where the factories and office buildings were abandoned. Inside these he installed a complex hydroponics farm, using the latest in artificial sunlight (that, to his amazement, didn't even irritate his undead flesh), to grow vegetables for cheap. These he turned around and provided to poor local communities, who often don't have access to fresh fruits and vegetables. This drew people in, while he slowly set himself as the center of a cthonic mystery cult. He was their little god of life and death. He gave them life, and they let him get close enough to sup on their lives in turn. Moreover, whenever they urban poor in his care were threatened from the outside, he would do his duty as a death-god and deal with it.<br /> <br /> The cops still haven't found any trace of the officer who gunned down a few local children and received no legal or disciplinary action for it. His body fertilizes the soil of a fresh planting of native trees, and his blood is better served down the Telyav's gullet anyhow.<br /> <br /> Unlife is not without its problems. First, the Telyav has reason to believe some unclean spirits (read: Banes) are taking issue with his efforts. He hasn't stepped into the realm of Spirit Manipulation, but he thinks he might need to soon, which means tracking down where his Sire and magic teacher went.<br /> <br /> Second, his work to promote a cult has attracted the attention of certain religious forces. Namely a female pastor at a protestant church not too far away, endowed with True Faith. Now, Telyavic Tremere are especially vulnerable to True Faith, meaning the woman could be formidable, if the two come into conflict. At the moment, she is ignorant of the Telyav and his nature, but is aware that a &quot;heathen religion&quot; has taken root in the community. Her primary tactics include doubling missionary efforts, and to perform charity work (to take a bite out of the incentive to join the cult). She may become even more inconvenient, if she starts calling attention to his efforts among the wider religious and civil community.<br /> <br /> Third, the same Bloodline weakness that makes Telyavic Tremere weak to True Faith also causes him to recoil against Christian symbols. During a recent trip to another city - to pick up specialized plants, and to touch bases with neighboring Anarchs - he betrayed his repulsion by crosses and the like. This fact has made the rounds among Anarchs in the tri-state area, and therefore piqued the interest of Assamite and Salubri vampires. The Telyavic weakness is not dissimilar to that of the Baali, and so some have made the assumption that he IS one. That he's set himself up as the center of a cult doesn't help his case. He may soon find himself targeted by Kindred looking to remove his blight forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T07:11:01-07:00","id":1379474,"title":"","content":"246. Johnny Wilson was born an hour outside Chicago, in the boring little town of Dwight, Illinois. His dad died early on, and his mom had a moderately successful dental practice. He grew up in a nice Victorian house on the good side of town.<br /> <br /> Johnny was never the brightest light on the Christmas tree, but he wasn't quite &quot;challenged&quot; enough to get special classes or tutors. He just kind of wandered forward each year in school, with the lowest possible grades needed to pass the year. Johnny was quiet and loved to read, though it took him a long time to trudge through a book. Lovecraft, Percy Jackson, and Harry Potter were his favorites. He didn't always understand all the little details of the plot, but he loved the big picture of fantasy worlds where he could do things most people couldn't.<br /> <br /> Johnny graduated high school... barely... and got a job working the nightshift at the SuperFastGasMart out by the interstate. Every night, Johnny'd pick the cigarette butts out of the nacho cheese sauce pot, change the expiration stickers on the egg salad sandwiches, and settle in with a good book.<br /> <br /> Other than the homeless guy, Buddy, who lived in an old shipping container out back and used the station's bathroom, Johnny talked to almost no one. Everybody paid at the pumps, so only a few times a night a tourist or a trucker would come in for some cigarettes or lottery tickets. The job was perfect for Johnny.<br /> <br /> One night, half-way through Stephen King's Salem's Lot (which Johnny'd been struggling through for two months) the door buzzed and a really pale guy walked in. He was short, had shoulder length black hair that looked like it was cut with a butcher knife, and his face and chest was covered in red slurpee syrup. What the hell? Had he gotten to the slurpee machine before Johnny noticed him? Was that slurpee on the man's hands, too? Wait, no. It was ketchup. Yeah. It's ketchup.<br /> <br /> The man smiled at Johnny's slack jaw surprise, and said, &quot;Sorry, kid, but I have hunger.&quot; The next thing Johnny knew he was being pulled across the counter into the man's arms. There was a pain on Johnny's neck, as the man bit down. Johnny, thinking this was some weird sex thing, figured &quot;What the hell. It seems kind of fun.&quot;, and bit down, too.<br /> <br /> Johnny was awakened by the sound of the man burning rubber out of the parking spot on pump 12. Johnny was on the floor behind the counter, feeling woozy. And hungry. No... starving. He got himself together, and headed out back for some fresh air. His reflection in a display case showed ketchup on his face. Except, maybe... that isn't ketchup?<br /> <br /> After disposing of Buddy's body in the drainage pond out front and cleaning himself up in the restroom, Johnny went back to his reading. Two hours before dawn, he tidied up the store. An hour before dawn, the morning cashier arrived. They did their till exchange in silence, and nodded goodbye. Johnny walked home to his little apartment in his mom's basement, and went to sleep.<br /> <br /> That was two months ago, and Johnny kept expecting things to get weird, but they didn't.<br /> <br /> He figured out he was a vampire in the first week, and sent away online for a rabbit hutch for his backyard. He told his mom he wanted to sell rabbit meat for a business.<br /> <br /> Friday nights, he treats himself to a truckstop hooker. Brandi Jo is nice about his bitiness, and Johnny found he can lick the wounds and heal them.<br /> <br /> He still works overnights at the SuperFastGasMart.<br /> <br /> As expected, he has developed superpowers. He can make himself hidden if he stands completely still, which is hilarious when people come in. Boo!<br /> <br /> He can also make people like him a lot. They like him so much they tip him ten or twenty bucks just for selling them a corndog.<br /> <br /> There have been changes to his mind, though, and sometimes he thinks he's going crazy. He's developed a fear of crosses and stuff, like in the movies. When people come into the store, he gets a quick flash of some horrible thing they've done, like beat their dog, or cheat on their wife. He thinks he has just gotten really negative about people being assholes. Truth is, he can sense other's moral flaws.<br /> <br /> What Johnny really wants is to learn how to fly. He has broken his leg twice jumping from the roof of the store.<br /> <br /> No, wait, what he really wants is to have somebody around who he can be a real vampire with. He's getting awful lonely, and knows he doesn't know a lot of stuff about vampires. Anne Rice says there are vampires in New Orleans and LA, but that's really far. Maybe he'll go to a big city that's closer, like Bloomington, Kankakee, or Chicago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T18:01:06-07:00","id":1384967,"title":"","content":"247. Here's an idea. A Giovanni who knows the Path of Technomancy.<br /> <br /> She uses it for thread necromancy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T07:49:34-07:00","id":1385078,"title":"","content":"248. A young Ventrue Antitribu who managed to commit diablerie on a sleeping Methuselah. The ancient's soul could easily overtake the neonate, but chooses not to. He's fine where he is and instead chooses to guide his diablerist through unlife. Just exist as an advising voice in the back of the Cainite's mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 05-01-2020, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T16:55:25-07:00","id":1385321,"title":"","content":"249) Malkavian enforcer with police training. Worked as a SWAT officer for years. Not all the homes and buildings they were sent to raid had just criminals, though. On more than one occasion, they tear gassed, terrorized, and gunned down innocent people. Like that time their squad entered the wrong house, and killed a couple in bed, who only opened fire because a bunch of armed men broke in. Or when they personally cracked the skull of some guy playing video games, who had gotten SWAT called on them falsely by another internet user. Or that time they thought a child had a gun (it was, of course, a toy).<br /> <br /> All par for the course with the police, and their fellow officers tried to brush it off. The department shielded them from repercussions. But they could never be shielded from the guilt. For the sake of keeping sane, they forced the bad feelings down, putting them in a box. They couldn't afford to break down, not with a family. (Not that they got to see their spouse or children much; work kept them busy, or at least that's what they told them. They'd destroyed one more family in the line of duty to ever feel wholly comfortable at home).<br /> <br /> It all came crashing down on the night their squad got a direct order from the mayor's office to storm a run down building. The squad was told it was anarchists strung out on PCP. The mayor's office lied. The building was crawling with, of course, Sabbat vampires. Everyone died...except them.<br /> <br /> Apparently, the Malkavian Antitribu who looked like a little girl wanted to &quot;play with her food&quot;. She tricked them into a solitary area, and proceeded to psychologically torment them. Using Dementation and Auspex to tease out details of their guilt, then exploit it. With tensions artificially heightened, they broke down completely. Perhaps on whim, or to torment them further, the Malkavian Embraced the cop.<br /> <br /> Ever since then, they're haunted by hallucinations of the people they murdered. Ghosts of the past, never letting them forget. They can never go home again. Even if vampirism itself didn't make it a non-option, the visions wouldn't miss a chance to rear their ugly heads. It's only duty to the law - this time the law of the Camarilla - that keeps them from greeting the sun. They deserve to die again for what they did - their perpetual companions remind them constantly - but so do the vampires who abandoned their humanity, and make sport of mortals.<br /> <br /> They haven't yet killed an innocent while feeding. They haven't added anyone to the roster of poor souls dogging them. It won't be long, in vampire terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-04T21:03:46-08:00","id":1438066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1311363#post1311363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">198) A Tremere who was Embraced for her ability as a Natural Linguist, as Hermetics highly value extensive knowledge of various languages. But when the Embrace took, she discovered she had yet another Merit to her name: Magic Resistance. On the upside, it protected her from Thaumaturgy and other magics. On the downside, it prevented her from ever developing skill in blood sorcery of any sort. Given that this is Clan Tremere, it was far more of a bane than a boon. Ensuring that she'd never be able to advance in the Pyramid.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't a character like this have a third discipline that replaces thaumaturgy then? Perhaps Fortitude due to the Tremere's Salubri ancestors? Obeah would be a much more juicy story hook, but I don't see how the character could possibly prevent the third eye from being discovered and dooming her to being purged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T06:46:02-08:00","id":1438116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1364487#post1364487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">245) A Telyav Tremere who started life as a disgruntled urban botanist...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually a bit similar to a Telyav I played recently, so I'll throw in the character archetype too...<br /> <br /> 250) Felicity was, for <i>any </i>Tremere regardless of lineage or bloodline, an absolute dipshit (primary social, secondary physical, tertiary mental; primary talents, secondary skills, tertiary knowledges). As in, she made her money uploading nude yoga videos and doing livestreams on Patreon/Venmo and OnlyFans, and advertising herself as a life coach and life coach, and <i>actually thinking</i> she's not just uploading wank material. Otherwise, she was whole hog into the new age-y, hippie lifestyle; living off the grid, doing house and community garden shit, dumpster diving, community yoga classes, and the like.<br /> <br /> She was also high Humanity (I started with <i>eight</i>), and that was front and center with any interaction she had, so she was &quot;that guy&quot; in terms of being a general buzzkill for other vampires. Having Blush of Health and Sanctity really helped any and all of the above, so she was <i>extra</i> insufferable just to be around if you had fangs. In fact, the entire reason behind her Sanctity was she was simply too stupid, young, naive, and insular to be any <i>real</i> threat to any right-thinking, upstanding vampire and therefore not worth notice.<br /> <br /> Her thing was, she was part of an indie coven of Appalachian Telyavs, and sent to the city to keep tabs on some whacky supernatural shit going on and the local Tremere. She didn't use Thaumaturgy that much, and she had Celerity, so she could pass off easily as a Toreador and that was the reason for her Embrace. Nobody would ever suspect a hippie dumbass to be Stealth Tremere.<br /> <br /> They <i>would</i>, however, suspect her to be a Malkavian. Because her primary path was Spirit Thaumaturgy, and her first two secondary paths were Neptune's Might and Green Path. She didn't use Thaumaturgy <i>that</i> much, and when she did she was always very careful about it, but her propensity for talking to herself, staring into toilets and fountains, and having conversations with house plants was duly noted. Which actually turned out to be <i>really fucking handy</i> because Elysium in the course of the chronicle was moved to this new urbanist green/blue space with multiple fountains.<br /> <br /> She also had a Spirit Mentor in the form of a river spirit, which is where everything tied together neatly. Part of the pact with the river spirit was to help keep the local environment clean, and the downside of it was she had an Arcane Curse to always smell like fresh water and flowers, and she couldn't cross running water. That was where the Humanity came into play, because the pact would be broken if she degenerated or treated spirits the way most other spirit thaumaturges do -- meaning, she couldn't compel spirits to do what she wanted, but had to take the long route fostering Contacts and Allies that are spirits. Not an easy task, but made possible by having at least one local spirit that could vouch for her and her good intent.<br /> <br /> The character <i>really</i> came into her own when she discovered pattern spiders in her computer. I had her become instantly enamored by this new type of potential friend, and a few experience points and an online coding boot camp later, I raised her Technology and Computer ratings high enough to figure out how to lure them to her computer and communicate with them -- by coding text and flash games for them to play. At the point I had to stop playing the character (she eventually got found out by the Tremere and had to go on the run) I was close to being able to buy the first dot of Technomancy to complement her other paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T08:10:16-08:00","id":1438123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1438066#post1438066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't a character like this have a third discipline that replaces thaumaturgy then? Perhaps Fortitude due to the Tremere's Salubri ancestors? Obeah would be a much more juicy story hook, but I don't see how the character could possibly prevent the third eye from being discovered and dooming her to being purged.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire point of the character is that her Merit is at cross-purposes with her Clan, both in the sense of her as a vampire and in the organizational sense.<br /> <br /> If I wanted her to be a Tremere with Salubri traits, I would have outlined that character. You are free to do that character write-up and post it to this thread, if you want. That's just not what I did.<br /> <br /> I would also argue that her being a member of Clan Tremere in good standing, but with no opportunity for advancement, is just as interesting as one that is hiding a secret that would get her killed if revealed. It's a different kind of character arc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T09:37:50-08:00","id":1438133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1438123#post1438123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also argue that her being a member of Clan Tremere in good standing, but with no opportunity for advancement, is just as interesting as one that is hiding a secret that would get her killed if revealed. It's a different kind of character arc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That in itself is a sticky proposal. Sure, <i>formal</i> advancement in the clan (as in, movement up the Pyramid from apprentice, to regent, lord, pontifex, and councilor) is predicated upon thaumaturgical expertise, but thaumaturgical expertise alone doesn't make the Tremere. Least of all when it comes to that thaumaturgical expertise takes decades and centuries to build, and Tremere who focus exclusively on that are heavily reliant on support networks for having neglected other aspects of personal development. Tremere <i>do</i> embrace from non-occultists and non-intellectuals on occasion, when they need individuals to perform specialized roles for the clan for which thaumaturgy has few, if any, efficient or easy solutions.<br /> <br /> That invariably creates conflicts within the clan, and internal power struggles beyond the simple confines of vying for position within the Pyramid. A Regent may be the most thaumaturgically-skilled Tremere in a chantry, but would they be more powerful than a subordinate who commands the chantry's ghouls, acts as blood and reagent procurer, likely liaises with the other vampires in the city, does the external investigations and cleans up Masquerade-related oopsies, or handles mortal bureaucracy and finances for the chantry? Sure, most of that <i>can</i> be handled with a smattering of level 1-3 rituals, but is it the easiest or most elegant solution when compared to, say, sending a representative to blood bond or dominate a handful of mortals over the course of an evening or two?<br /> <br /> The most obvious and glaring example of which would be to ask what happens when a Regent is an ancilla or elder (as almost all are), and finds themselves in the position of relying on a neonate apprentice to handle the chantry's electronic transactions, whether that's as simple as paying the bills or as complex and risky as buying rare and almost certainly illegal reagents on the dark web.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T01:12:26-08:00","id":1438906,"title":"","content":"251) Hogarth Smith was born into old-money wealth, ensuring he would never have to work a day in his life. Spoiled and congenitally irresponsible, he was busy not attending the exclusive ivy league college his parents had paid for when he received word of the car crash that had claimed both their lives. Returning to the city of his birth, he dismissed the entire household staff and settled into the vast family manor for a protracted isolation. The young dilettente was exploring the surprisingly deep stone halls beneath the old mansion when he discovered a most curious thing: on a slab in a bare chamber, a dissicated corpse with the face of a demon frozen in mid-snarl. A wooden stake was driven deep into its breast. Following he knew not what impulse, Hogarth removed the stake and was immediately set upon by the frenzied Nosferatu. When the creature came to its senses, it decided to make use of the dying mortal and gave him the Embrace. After interrogating Hogarth about the state of the world, the creature vanished. For the newly-made Nosferatu, the existence of the undead and his entry into their ranks was the first of several revelations. From old journals found in the catacombs, he learned that back in the 1800s his namesake, one of the city's founding fathers, had been a prolific vampire hunter. Exploring the city by night, Hogarth discovered there were others like him---and that the elders among his newly adopted &quot;clan&quot; had less than fond memories of the elder Hogarth Smith. Not yet recognized by the Prince as he is without sponsor, Hogarth is aware he must begin making some moves quickly, or he will face Destruction, according to the draconian laws of these so-called Kindred. Fortunately, he still has his family's wealth and a vast haven in the form of his ancestral home. Not to mention his ancestor's effects, including a brutal two-handed blade perfect for severing undead heads. The question is whether to try and ingratiate himself with the city's self-styled Court, or seek refuge among the young kindred called Anarchs.... <br /> <br /> 252) A doom metal frontman with a devoted following, Brandon LaRue had it all: fame, fortune, and beautiful groupies throwing themselves at his feet. His true passion however, was the occult. Having absorbed the Satanic Bible at a young age, he quickly moved on from LaVeyan Satanism in search of real supernatural power. While filling his song lyrics with cryptic hermetic and gnostic references, he burned his wealth into acquiring expensive tomes and following their rituals. Nothing seemed to work, but Brandon slowly acquired a following of hardcore devotees, drawn in through his music, who would join him for weekly black masses and attempted summonings or ritualistic magickal workings. On one such night, a new face--a beautiful, pale woman--joined Brandon's cult of groupies and hangers-on for a post-orgy ritual attempting to commune with the spirit Yaldabaoth. When, as ever, nothing happened, Brandon fell into his usual sulk and angrily dismissed everyone from his penthouse apartment. The woman however, remained and, sitting beside Brandon, asked him if he was truly devoted in his quest for knowledge---and what was the worth of that knowledge to him? Surprisingly, the singer found himself entranced by the stranger, and answered her questions honestly---how he had never fit in anywhere, how he longed to bend the world to his will and sought power in hidden mysteries to do it. The woman smiled and suggested that if Brandon was serious, the only way to climb that summit might be to go below. If he truly sought power, she could show him a path, but he would have to start at the bottom. It might be many years before he could ascend to the heights of power he sought, if ever. With conviction surprising even himself, Brandon swore that for even a taste of real magic, he would pay any price, endure any service---he would do anything. The woman said she believed him, and suddenly Brandon was dying on the floor of his apartment as his life drained out of him. When he awoke, he discovered that he had changed: he was now one of the kindred, the world's true masters, and of a very special clan within that species: the Clan Tremere. Taken to the local Chantry, he endured the sneers of the so-called Regent, who chided his sire for her choice in childe. A musician, really? But her choice would be honored, and Brandon was brought into the Pyramid as an Apprentice of the lowest level. Although he is but a fledgeling of the Tremere, he still has his devoted following and wealth, and a voracious appetite to follow the cursus of Blood Sorcery. His ambition matched by unnerving conviction and dark charisma, he enters the Society of the Damned determined to let nothing slow his mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T02:37:03-08:00","id":1438913,"title":"","content":"253) Raymundo Elias Gonzalez (Ray) was an artist of a peculiar sort: his medium was comics, and he spent years self-publishing his opus on the internet slowly building a cult following. His comic, called The Underbarian, is a psychedellic fantasy epic following the titular hero through a melange of worlds and states of consciousness. Through the blend of prose and pictures Ray would pour his emotions onto the page, sending the Underbarian through dreamscapes of transcendent beauty or eldritch nightmare; transforming people from his life into a supporting cast of tyrants and tricksters, gods and monsters. By turns the Underbarian's picaresque wanderings would reel from the stuff of pulp adventure to meditative illustrated poems, following the hero on an endless quest for enlightenment. The comic was Ray's passion and release from a moribund life in which he was hampered by disability, living alone with high functioning autism and no regular employment. His sister, a tireless social worker, was his anchor and sole support. Aside from the Underbarian, Ray produced surreal dreamscapes on canvas in ink and oil, and it was at a gallery showing his work that he met the woman who would bring him into the night. Entranced by the kindred's otherworldly charisma, Ray found himself opening up to her and speaking about his art, the dreams that brought inspiration, and his belief in many lives and many worlds. After many nights spent together, the woman had one question: how did he <i>know?</i> Know what? What would happen next, the woman insisted. Ray's comics were more than fantasies; in esoteric ways and through artful symbology, they contained premonitions. Ray had a gift, one which his sire meant to serve the machinations of her Malkavian Brood and her own ambitions. Ray was embraced into the Clan of Seers, better known as the Lunatics, and immediately he found the lines between the world of flesh and the world he brought to life with his pen blurring. Events in his nightly existence would translate, quite unbidden, into events in his stories, which came to him in torrents of spontaneous inspiration; likewise a twist in the Underbarian's journies or a potent image would find clear resonance in the real world. A perilous sea journey in the comic would prefigure a dangerous trip through the City Barrens. An encounter with a knight errant would prefigure confrontation with a rapacious kindred. As his reality shifts and blurs, Ray finds himself the pawn of his devious sire, his predictions fueling her machinations, while his own life seems completely out of his control.<br /> <br /> In game terms, this Malkavian's derangement is Schizophrenia. His reality is filled with unbidden, symbolic revelations and it seems as if no matter what transpires, it was predicted in some way through his spontaneous art. Ray is compelled to keep creating, although the story has completely spiraled out of his control, and he knows he must overcome the disassociation that separates him from his fellow beings kindred and kine alike if he is to hold on to his Humanity. His concerned sister (now wondering what this &quot;new job&quot; is that occupies Ray's days) remains his best link to reality, but Ray knows that breaking the Masquerade would place her in mortal danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","user":"Ventrue Busboy","date":". 03-10-2021, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T14:22:39-08:00","id":1439032,"title":"","content":"254 There's a rather naive and amiable Malkavian living in a Camarilla city. by all investigation, he's a young 13th gen with an unknown sire and no significant contacts. That alone should make this kindred dead, and a witchhunt for the sire should have transpired, but this has not happened. This Malkavian, quite worryingly, claims to be Malkav, and though this claim is rediculous, nobody seems to be challenging him for it. No records can be found of his mortal existence. He seems to unsettle a few people, but there's no evidence he's capable of much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:11:58-08:00","id":1439160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/860617-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1439032#post1439032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">254 There's a rather naive and amiable Malkavian living in a Camarilla city. by all investigation, he's a young 13th gen with an unknown sire and no significant contacts. That alone should make this kindred dead, and a witchhunt for the sire should have transpired, but this has not happened. This Malkavian, quite worryingly, claims to be Malkav, and though this claim is rediculous, nobody seems to be challenging him for it. No records can be found of his mortal existence. He seems to unsettle a few people, but there's no evidence he's capable of much.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do the other Malkavians make of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:22:47-08:00","id":1439163,"title":"","content":"They have their own individual opinions, but don't like to talk about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T01:25:47-08:00","id":1439396,"title":"","content":"255) Winston Thuresby is a most unusual Brujah. Punctiliously dressed in expensive but tasteful clothing, slender and softspoken he is more at home in elegant clubs or an Elysium than the streets. No one has ever seen him frenzy. His method of hunting utilizes his good looks and sensitive mannerisms: frequenting university campuses or quiet cafes, he targets lonely young women, stalking and studying them before introducing himself seemingly by accident. Charming them is easy enough (&quot;please, call me Wynne&quot;), but Thuresby isn't interested in a quick dine-and-dash following a one night stand. Drawing the target into deep conversation, often over many nights, he slowly reveals what he is---an undead vampire, tormented by urges he can barely control and cloven from humanity by many years of immortality. The young women inevitably fall into his hands---declaring that no matter the danger, he too deserves love. The pitiless predator plays into their romantic fantasies, acting each time as if they have awoken something in him he thought lost. Once the kine is fully enamored of this duplicitous chameleon, they soon end up in his large herd. Although breaking the Masquerade carries a risk, Thuresby isn't above sharing his new Blood Dolls around with thirsty kindred to increase his prestation and influence. Hopelessly addicted to the pleasure of the kiss, they become his chattel, inevitably coming to tragic ends. The small Masquerade Breach having taken care of itself, the remorseless Thuresby moves on. Slowly losing his Humanity by drips and drabs, he nevertheless occupies an place of preeminence in the Domain, propounding the Traditions and his loyalty to the Camarilla in the salons while passing off his harem of victims to Licks on the down-low. Among Kindred he usually goes by the nomme-de-guerre of Mr. Thursday, a henchman of the elders and a caterer for kindreds' dark desires.<br /> <br /> The origins behind this sinister figure are as simple as they are pathetic. Born in the interwar period, Winston was a sickly boy unfit for military service. As a man he worked a dead-end job as a patent clerk and paid for his stymied ambition with disdain from his wife. The loveless marriage came to a sudden end the night Thuresby murdered his wife with an axe. The Brujah <i>antitribu</i> who would become his sire chanced across Thuresby at the edge of town while he was making a panicked attempt to hide the hacked remains. Amused with what he saw, the vampire gave the fumbling murderer a second chance of sorts, to see if he could make more of himself dead than he ever did while alive. As Mr. Thursday, Winston is determined to make good on that chance. His smoldering sadism parcel to his ambitions, he schemes to cement for himself a lasting place in the city. And if he wields the numerous boons owed to him smartly and manages to discredit certain rivals, he fancies a title as Herald or even Seneschal might be his for the taking.<br /> <br /> Note: The thread didn't specify, but this guy is definitely meant as an STC and hopefully a satisfying antagonist for the Player Characters to take down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","user":"Ventrue Busboy","date":". 03-12-2021, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T09:45:33-07:00","id":1454456,"title":"","content":"I'll necro this for an idea:<br /> <br /> 256) The Lasombra embrace is notoriously unforgiving, and even among the few mortals tested, fewer still thrive under the conditions forced upon them to earn the embrace.<br /> <br /> And very, <i>very</i>, rarely, it backfires.<br /> <br /> Such was the case when a young officer returned home after fighting in World War II, his exploits during the war earning acclaim and press in his hometown...and attracting the attention of a Lasombra <i>antitribu</i>. Soon, the officer found his attempts to get loans, GI Bill money, a good job blocked at every turn, and even his reputation impugned beyond repair as the &quot;truth&quot; behind the awards and medals he earned came to light. Left destitute, shunned, and homeless, the officer drifted for a time, finding impossibly-bad luck in every attempt to turn his life around.<br /> <br /> That is, until happenstance brought him to a dive bar in the middle of nowhere one evening, and he happened to see another vampire feeding on a victim. A fist fight that didn't go well for the officer and a molotov cocktail later, the officer stumbled away having caught a glimpse at the truth so long-hidden from mortals. The officer's prospective sire would have awarded the embrace then and there...but for the officer's quick thinking, a can of aerosol hair spray, and a cigarette lighter.<br /> <br /> From there, it didn't take long for the Society of Leopold to find the officer...and now out of the Lasombras' clutches, the officer went on to enjoy a long, violent, successful life of hunting the supernatural. The officer led hunters, grew older and no longer able to keep up with his younger colleagues, relegated himself to investigatory and clerical tasks, and eventually retired completely hoping to live his twilight years in peace -- a rare feat for hunters.<br /> <br /> Something that wasn't to be...the officer failed to kill his prospective sire from so long ago. That Lasombra would be excoriated by the Friends of the Night for creating a hunter instead of a childe, and his prospective sire's blood went to a <i>far</i> more capable Lasombra in short order. But in the meantime, the Keepers waited...and watched.<br /> <br /> And when the officer was too old and feeble to resist, he was <i>finally</i> &quot;awarded&quot; the embrace. Part revenge for a lifetime of hunting vampires, part ironic justice, part because this officer had paradoxically proven himself the most promising candidate for the embrace in a generation. The hunter had no choice in the matter, of course, and for the Keepers this was a no-lose scenario: a neonate forever locked in an elderly man's failing body with countless enemies among the undead, a lifetime insider's knowledge of the Society, who already had the knowledge necessary to survive among the Kindred. He would either be hunted and killed by his former Kindred victims, his former colleagues...or just as he had twice before in life, fight a war of impossible odds and <i>win</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T09:00:40-08:00","id":1473336,"title":"","content":"Time to do some thread necromancy. Two concepts for each Clan, let's go!<br /> <br /> Toreador:<br /> <br /> Helen Fairfield was chronically ill for the majority of her life, to cope with depression and pain she took to painting. The expressionist style was her favorite, blending dark colors to depict abstract representations of her experience with illness. She won a contest and entered a prestigious art school, and there she was Embraced by a Toreador enamored by the beauty of her work. The Embrace cured her illness and she found herself for the first time feeling truly alive. Painting was yesterday! She's now keen on enjoying all that pain and infirmity has denied her.<br /> <br /> Juan Costa is the heartthrob nurse who adores helping people, but more than that, he adores the attention. While he's genuinely nice, Juan practically feeds on the love he gets from his admirers, constantly hungry for more. He has an Instagram account with thousands of followers feverishly liking picture after picture of the hospital hunk in scrubs. His Embrace came from a Toreador who wanted to immortalise the beautiful and selfless man, but instead created a monster who hungers for attention almost as much as blood.<br /> <br /> Brujah:<br /> <br /> Blessed with a physique that could put most professional bodybuilders to shame, Fynn Murphy was nonetheless a gentle and kind soul willing to protect the weak. He always said he was born in the wrong era, vividly dreaming of a life lived as a knight in medieval times. He never grew out of this, and found a job as a bouncer that paid the bills while working part time as a performer in Renaissance fairs, fully immersing himself in the role of a knight in LARP events. One night, a woman approached him after he chased away a predator who didn\u2019t take no for an answer. He tried to tell her that he didn't want any favors. She shushed him and Embraced him into the Brujah, challenging his values and righteousness.<br /> <br /> Hong Li Xin, also called Lizzie. Crazy, attractive, will probably hand your ass to you in a fight. She bludgeoned her way into a fight club by beating up anybody who complained about a woman being in a brotherhood. The Kindred higher-ups didn't really care that much, and in fact found her promising. After a series of trials and challenges, she was Embraced. Now she is the firebrand preacher that doesn\u2019t believe in what she\u2019s selling, constantly searching for a new cause or a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T09:01:23-08:00","id":1473337,"title":"","content":"Banu Haqim<br /> <br /> Yousef Najjar always had a passing fascination with the occult. His grandmother on his mother\u2019s side was Syrian, grew up near the desert, and had the most fantastical tales of djinni and ifriti. So when he woke up dead and hungry as a ghul, a vampire, he believed himself abandoned by God and became a Sufi scholar to find answers. Yousef is a skilled blood sorcerer, a brilliant poet, and the perfect socialite, alas he refuses to get involved in Kindred affairs unless he finds the stakes worthy enough of attention.<br /> <br /> Azraa Al-Enezi was the youngest of 7 daughters in the Enezi family, her prospects slim as the good husbands, the sizable dowries, the attention and beauty were all held by her sisters. She instead became conniving, using her charms and politics to land herself a betrothal to a rich and foreign diplomat. Little did she know the man was but a mask of one of the djinn and he stole her away. The terrible need for blood was a small price to pay for the power she found in this new existence, and now she represents the Banu Haqim in Camarilla domains as a skillful emissary.<br /> <br /> (I will continue later haha I'm exhausted)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-16T14:36:31-07:00","id":1558901,"title":"","content":"<b>259. Matthew 'MT' Hart, the prodigal Pander</b><br /> A nomadic Cainite who treks across North America according to his own whims. Though MT's still known to perform odd jobs for the Sabbat, like moving caches of weapons between cities, the night they destroy him for being a liability draws dangerously near.<br /> Matthew was a teenage grave robber. Not out of poverty, being a middle-class kid. But just for some extra spending money. At night the boy drove out with his friends to the cemeteries of rural Texas. There they usually picked out the grave of some widow who'd been dead for at least a century. Matthew had found those were likely to be buried with at least their wedding band, if not some other jewelry as well. It was a lot of digging for a few pieces of gold. But he enjoyed the thrill of it, as a secret rebellion against his Baptist upbringing. Hence why those kids just kept grave robbing, and kept getting away with it too. Until that time Matthew discovered they weren't the only ones bumping in the night.<br /> As the youngsters were driving along the backroads they'd been unlucky enough to draw the attention of a local Sabbat coven, following them to the next cemetery. While Matthew and his friends were digging the vampires emerged from the darkness and attacked. The Cainites thanked them for bringing their own shovels as they buried the dying teens. Matthew was the only one who succeeded at clawing himself out again. Because his Embrace had been a messy affair, involving the vitae of multiple sires, he emerged from the dirt clanless.<br /> The fledgling shovelhead returned with the coven to their communal haven in El Paso. His mongrel heritage meant they treated him little better than a ghoul, assigning him thankless duties like body disposal. This unlife of drudgery continued for a few years until his coven joined the Miami siege. This was a gamechanger. He could finally prove himself to be True Sabbat. Though what was more important to MT; being rid of his coven-mates as they fell in battle. While feeling those Vinculi snap the Pander vowed to never allow himself to be enslaved again. From that moment onward he became a nomad who only occasionally belonged to a pack.<br /> It was while travelling alone, during the summer of 1999, that MT came across Caleb. He was a fledgling, of unknown lineage, left chained up in a vehicle. The older Cainite saw much potential in this wretch, who turned out to be of similar background. MT took Caleb under his wing and as a lover, alleviating his need for companionship in a controlled manner. Predictably it wasn't to last, as an act of betrayal ended their relationship. In a tight spot MT had attempted to sacrifice his companion's unlife to save his own. Caleb survived though and their subsequent confrontation nearly ended in Final Death.<br /> The last year MT has spent largely on his own again, which his Beast has taken maximal advantage of. The Cainite now realizes that any leeway he once had with the Sabbat has run out. They'll be coming for him. In response he has prepared his defection to the California Anarchs. However, MT refuses to leave before he can convince Caleb to join him.<br /> <br /> <b>Image: </b>The pallid skin of a low or no Humanity vampire has aged up MT's teen features. He also has trouble hiding his fangs. While his dark eyes blink no longer. The Pander's ragged clothing, smelling of dried blood, heavily contrasts with a clean-shaven face, and an auburn mullet appearing to be but a few hours out of an 80s hair salon.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> Though considered an unsettling presence by most kine, other Sabbat tend to appreciate your laid-back demeanor. On the road you easily join any Loyalist pack travelling in the same direction. Though you value your independence above all else. Hence why you're also quick to leave again, before any Vinculum ties could become too strong. Your lack of connection to other Sabbat is starting to take its toll though. You've wandered off your path, becoming a monster who kills arbitrarily. It's your hope that reconnecting with Caleb will help reign your Beast back in.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan:</b> Pander<br /> <b>Sire:</b> Unclear<br /> <b>Nature:</b> Rogue<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Dabbler<br /> <b>Generation:</b> 13th<br /> <b>Embrace:</b> 1989<br /> <b>Apparent Age:</b> Early 20s<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 3, Manipulation 4, Appearance 3<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 1, Athletics 1, Awareness 1, Brawl 1, Intimidation 1, Streetwise 3, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Drive 2, Etiquette 1, Firearms 2, Larceny 2, Melee 2, Stealth 2, Survival 2<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 1, Computer 1, Occult 1, Politics 1, Science 1<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex 1, Potence 2, Presence 2<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Contacts 4, Resources 1<br /> <b>Virtues:</b> Conviction 2, Instinct 4, Courage 4<br /> <b>Morality:</b> Path of Cathari 1<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 4<br /> <b>Merits/Flaws:</b> Language (Spanish + mother tongue English)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-17T03:48:27-07:00","id":1558910,"title":"","content":"<b>260. The Goblin King</b><br /> <br /> That's what he calls himself these nights. If he even remembers what his real name is, he's refusing to divulge it to even his closest allies. The only clue we have as to his original identity, is that he was embraced somewhere between the ages of 10 and 12 years old, by a rather sadistic Nosferatu. For reasons that should be blatantly obvious, he didn't have a snowball's chance in hell of being accepted by the Camarilla, driving him to fall in with the Sabbat crowd instead. His sire's pack mocked him, belittled him, and basically made his unlife a constant nightmare; all under the pretense of trying to <i>'toughen him up'</i> so he could be a proper vampire.<br /> <br /> Well, it worked... perhaps a little too well, because the Goblin King got his revenge. When a raid on enemy territory went bad, as is so often the case with haphazardly assembled Sabbat strategies, the abused fledgling seized the opportunity to diablerize his sire, stealing all of their power for himself. He would have loved to do the same to the rest of the pack, but the situation was growing increasingly more dangerous by the moment, so he was forced to bail and leave them to the Sheriff's men.<br /> <br /> <br /> While Nosferatu typically have a reputation for being tech savvy, the Goblin King is the opposite. He was far too young during his embrace to have any practical knowledge of computer and electrical systems, but destroying them is something that comes easily to him. In the time since his embrace, the Goblin King has become something of a domestic terrorist, focusing his attention on bringing down power grids, disrupting construction efforts, instigating wild animal attacks, and a host of other <i>'mysterious accidents'</i> that keep happening throughout the city.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Appearance: </b>A child sized monstrosity, who's posture remains hunched low to the ground. Instead of walking upright like a normal person, he lopes and skitters across the ground like a feral rodent. His skin has taken on a putrid yellow hue, while his ears are huge and tapered like those of a bat. His most outstanding feature is his nose, which is both comically long and abnormally thin. Hooking down over his mouth like some kind of withered carrot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Tips:</b> You are an agent of misfortune. Like the mythical creature from whence draw your namesake, you live to cause chaos. Your favorite method of spreading chaos involves ruining somebody's day without them even realizing you were present at the scene. In doing so, your reputation takes on a more mythical quality to it; you are the invisible monster spoken about in medieval fairy tales. The kind who is always to blame when something goes wrong, but never caught so you could face actual justice.<br /> <br /> Animalism is your primary discipline, as the power to control the city's animal population further solidifies your kingly status. Obfuscate comes second, as it assists you in evading capture or detection, while Potence remains your emergency last resort option.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clan:</b> Nosferatu<br /> <br /> <b>Sire:</b> Unknown (destroyed)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nature:</b> Child<br /> <br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Eye of the Storm<br /> <br /> <b>Generation:</b> 11th (formerly 12th)<br /> <br /> <b>Embrace:</b> 1999<br /> <br /> <b>Apparent Age:</b> 12<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-19T08:30:59-07:00","id":1558940,"title":"","content":"<b><b>261. Hermanus di Celano, the bookbinder</b></b><br /> Hermanus was the product of a marriage between a Giovanni maiden and the son of a Bavarian merchant family. The third child to be born of this arrangement, somewhere near the start of the 13th century. After a childhood spent in Munich, the pious youth left for an Italian monastery. No more than a year later Hermanus took his vows.<br /> When not in prayer the young monk spent most of his time in the scriptorium, copying books. A task he was neither the best nor the worst at. Certainly someone they could miss when the local lord asked the monks to be provided with a new scribe. Although he showed only obedience, Hermanus was anxious about this new assignment. It was the first time he'd left the monastery in years. The world outside its walls felt alien to him.<br /> He was quickly put at ease though. The castle and its inhabitants were quite welcoming. The lord's young wife proved to be especially affable. They soon became good friends. Lady Liviana had a warm personality and appreciated a keen mind to converse with. She found her often absent husband to be quite boorish. It soon became apparent his mistress was interested in more than just intelligent conversation though. Hermanus tried his hardest to hold on to his vow of chastity. But his thus far sheltered existence meant he had few tools to resist her feminine wiles. The start of a romance that would last for years.<br /> In time the entire household knew about the affaire, except for the lord himself. He spent too much time in other beds to know what was happening in his own. And yet one night the lord stormed into his chambers, sword in hand, catching the two lovers in the act. The last thing Hermanus saw before being run through with the blade was Liviana's head rolling across the floor.<br /> Hermanus who had expected to find himself in Hell, instead awoke in an underground crypt. Ermacora, a grandfather believed to be long dead, was watching over him. He informed the fledgling Cappadocian about the exact nature of this afterlife, and the Giovanni family's place in it. Augustus had recently decided to hold off on Hermanus' Embrace, until his untimely death had forced Ermacora's hand. The new Cainite let out a wail of great pain after being told saving Liviana hadn't been possible. Hermanus drank with great satisfaction from the bound lord, who was sobbing and begging, presented to him next.<br /> Soon after sire and childe left for Venice, where Hermanus would reside most of the following centuries. He proved to be an especially avid student of Necromancy, the art that could reunite him with his love. After never reaching that goal Hermanus in time lost all interest in the lands of the dead. However, not before accidentally developing a Necromantic ritual that proved of great value to the Clan. This rite permanently bound a soul to a book so it could act as its guardian. This involved binding the tome in the skin of the ghost's former body. In time many deceased mortal Giovanni have received this honor. More often than not by Hermanus himself.<br /> He has since mostly retreated from the affairs of his Clan. To them he's known as the mysterious bookbinder of Celano. Having made his haven under the ruins of the castle where he was once so happy. His only companion is Alda, a woman Embraced for her superficial physical resemblance to Liviana. She is neither the first nor the last to which he has done this. But the only one he hasn't destroyed soon afterwards.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> Over the centuries Hermanus skin has grown gray and rough, giving him a monstrous countenance. His dark soulful eyes are the only human feature left of the vampire's face. Despite his bookish ways Hermanus had grown tall and broad-shouldered in life. The robes and cloaks he commonly wears only increase his apparent bulk. Beneath which the vampire hides the sword wound through his belly and back. Another souvenir from his mortal years is the tonsure shaven out of his brown hair's top.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You've never enjoyed your unlife. It has been an existence of constant emotional and physical pain. And yet in your own detached way you perform your duty to your Clan and family admirably. It has provided you with a ghostly connection to nearly any Giovanni library in the world. Once your Clan's hold over the Underworld grows powerful enough to retrieve your lost love, you'll know about it and they'll repay their debts to you.<br /> You generally act somber and aloof. Only certain women can get a rise out of you. Passion cause they remind you of Liviana, often followed by fury once the brief illusion again dissipates.<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Hermanus di Celano<br /> <b>Clan:</b> Giovanni (Premascine)<br /> <b>Sire:</b> Ermacora Giovanni<br /> <b>Nature:</b> Celebrant<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Loner<br /> <b>Generation:</b> 6th<br /> <b>Embrace:</b> 1229<br /> <b>Apparent Age:</b> Indeterminate<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 4, Manipulation 5, Appearance 0<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 5, Intelligence 4, Wits 3<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 3, Athletics 2, Awareness 4, Brawl 2, Empathy 2, Expression 3, Intimidation 3, Leadership 1, Subterfuge 4<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Crafts (bookbinding) 5, Etiquette 3, Larceny 1, Melee 2, Stealth 3, Survival 2<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 3, Enigmas 3, Finance 1, Investigation 4, Law 1, Medicine 2, Occult 4, Politics 1, Science 2<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex 6, Dominate 2, Fortitude 2, Necromancy 5, Obfuscate 3, Potence 2, Presence 1<br /> <b>Necromancy Paths:</b> The Ash Path 2, The Cenotaph Path 5, The Sepulchre Path 4<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Domain 2, Generation 7, Spirit Slaves 5, Status 3<br /> <b>Virtues:</b> Conscience 3, Self-Control 1, Courage 5<br /> <b>Morality:</b> Humanity 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Merits/Flaws:</b> Language (German, Latin + mother tongue Italian), Open Wound, Sanguine Incongruity<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-25T14:19:54-07:00","id":1559019,"title":"","content":"Pre-gens I wrote for my upcoming wild west Giovanni game:<br /> <br /> <b>Ennio Putanesca </b><br /> As a boy you immigrated from Sicily to New York with your parents, and their undead master. Together they were supposed to build up a powerbase, for Clan Giovanni, among the city's burgeoning Italian community. Sadly the local Sabbat didn't take kindly to these efforts, killing your father a few years later. Subsequently you took his place, as a ghoul, at the Giovanni vampire's side. You turned out to be more business savvy, and all around shrewd, than your father had been. Your family managed to grow influential in the criminal underworld without antagonizing the city's ruling Cainites. A success for which you were rewarded with the Embrace. You're now assisted by your own trusty ghouls; the brothers Giorgio, Giuseppe and Guido.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A handsome Mediterranean man who was about 20 years old when becoming a ghoul. Except for a moustache your face is cleanshaven. A dark suit is your preferred attire. You usually also wear a red neckerchief.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You come across as a shrewd businessman. A true professional who's determined to build Clan Giovanni an American crime empire. Your heart isn't really in it though. Cause after all these years you're still haunted by your father's untimely demise. You want better for yourself. First and foremost you want to survive!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nicolasa Cort\u00e9s y Rossellini</b><br /> You grew up on a hacienda in the Central Mexican countryside. The Cort\u00e9s branch of the Pisanob family had fallen on hard times. There were no servants to work the land anymore. Instead it was you, and your siblings, who spent their formative years toiling all day. And yet you still found the energy to study Pisanob Necromancy deep into the night. Your efforts did not go unnoticed. A vampire, a great-grandfather on your mother's side, took you as his ghoul. A thankless existence assisting, and protecting, the Italian leech as he travelled the Americas. Though after years of loyal service this did eventually earn you the Embrace.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> An attractive woman, of mixed Aztec-Italian ancestry, in her early 20s. You're dressed for travel and action, like a bandida. This consists out of a simple blouse and ankle-length skirt, usually so dusty that you can't see the dried blood. Upon your belt you keep a revolver holstered. Your dark hair, on which rest a wide-brimmed hat, is tied in a single braid, hanging down your back.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> Eternally hard working and dutiful, with plain manners. No one appears to be more loyal to Clan Giovanni, and its Italian elders, than you. In truth you're just working inside the hierarchy hoping to destroy it. Your people should be their own masters, not beholden to European monsters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Margaret Dunsirn </b><br /> Born and raised on a family estate outside of Glasgow, Scotland. You first realized your kin were different when seeing Mother carve up a lazy maid's body in the kitchen. Besides learning about Dunsirn cannibalistic traditions, in time you were also informed about their links with Clan Giovanni. You were immediately enthralled by the possibility of becoming a vampire yourself. However, the Giovanni prized your family for little else except their talents at generating wealth. And unfortunately women couldn't legally own any property of their own. The exception would be a wealthy widow, which you made sure to become. After your husband's untimely demise you simply used his fortune to buy the Embrace from a lowly Giovanni vampire. You've since emigrated to the land of opportunity, hoping to make your own mark.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A fair emerald-eyed lady, appearing to be around 30. You let your ginger curls, held together by a bow, cascade down your back. No longer do you adhere to the fashions from Europe or the Eastern Seaboard. You instead dress as a frontier town's woman, in dresses that are plain, yet neat.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> The belief that the strong should consume the weak is deeply ingrained within you. Hence your continued striving to be the woman on top. Though you understand how off putting this can be within the misogynist society you're forced to operate in. So your level of ambition generally reads as appropriate for a good Christian widow who's just trying to make do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demetra Giovanni</b><br /> A child of Venice. You'd been told you're the cumulation of centuries of fine Giovanni breeding. Unfortunately that came with weak health. In your early teens you became infected with consumption, wasting away at a rapid pace. An undead grandfather stepped in with the Embrace, so that your potential wouldn't be lost. He didn't have permission from the family to do that though. For his crime you were banished to the New World. There you came under the care of Sister Virginia Maria, an aunt who'd been similarly disgraced.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A little young lady with dark eyes. Your pale features are stunningly perfect, like a porcelain doll. An innocent face framed by black curls, over which you usually wear a bonnet, tied under your chin with a bow. You wear a matching dress with hoopskirts underneath.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You've been hearing the dead whisper to you since birth, and yet you're still constantly overwhelmed by the supernatural world you were thrust into. You're more of a spoiled brat than an innocent child though. Cause the penitence you show, for your unsanctioned Embrace, is just a front. In truth you believe yourself to be a Giovanni of the highest caliber. You just need some help getting used to this undead existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gabriella Rosselini </b><br /> You grew up on a family estate back in Italy. From a young age it was clear you were a brilliant girl, who grew immensely knowledgeable in the dark arts. Unfortunately you weren't a pureblooded Rosselini, but a mere mortal destined to wither and die in just a handful of decades. Even as a young woman you feared this ticking clock, craving the eternal youth of the undead. Finally it was decided an elder from the Giovanni family's main branch was to Embrace you. They told you this was quite the honor. After the initial excruciating transformation you agreed with them. But by the next night it became clear something had gone wrong. You started to smell, your skin became discolored. You were decomposing! An irreversible process that continued for several more nights. Your eventual appearance made other Giovanni, kine and Kindred alike, uncomfortable. Which is why they shipped you off to America.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A cadaverous looking lady, like a week old corpse. Your milky, and glazed over, brown eyes are the least of it. Cause the outline of your skull is visibly protruding from beneath gray skin. This you usually obscure by dressing like a lady in deep mourning. Most importantly by having thick veils draped over your bonnet. Unlike a grieving widow you make heavy use of perfume, as to hide the smell of rot.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You present yourself as a font of knowledge totally devoted to your Clan. In truth you hate the Giovanni with a passion. It is they who subjugated your family, their cursed blood who afflicted you so terribly. As the Giovanni usurped the Cappadocians, you hope the Rosselini can do the same to Augustus and his get. You play nice with them only to help make this dream a reality. That one of your new coterie mates has a Rosselini mother seems like a possible opportunity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sister Virginia Maria </b><br /> You grew up in Venice, near your family's undead leadership. A legacy you desired no part in, turning to Catholicism instead. Unfortunately you were the most beautiful Giovanni of your generation, a young woman with many admirers. One of your cousins seemed particularly smitten. You took holy vows attempting to finally escape his advances. He eventually followed you to the convent though, more insistent than ever. In the subsequent altercation you stabbed him to death, damning your soul. As your punishment, because Clan Giovanni had earmarked him for the Embrace, you had to take his place in undeath. Furthermore you were banished to the American continent, settling in New England. More recently you were entrusted with the care of Demetra Giovanni, your niece, a child vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> You're always clad in the black and white garb of a Benedictine nun. This habit, veil and wimple cover nearly every inch of you except your face. But what an exquisite face it is; pale perfection further adorned by soft brown eyes. Your delicate hands are nearly constantly grasping at the silver rosary hanging down your chest.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You feel ashamed for your actions and the creature you've become. For these many sins you wish to suffer like the lord Ges\u00f9 Cristo on the cross. But you have a duty to your family to take care of little Demetra Giovanni. So you do your very best to hide your self-hate behind a motherly veneer.\u200b.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 03-30-2026, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-08T13:47:46-07:00","id":1559293,"title":"","content":"<b><b>268.</b></b><b> Mocel, Mesa Trueno's mistress</b><br /> A Tlacique who's claimed a mining town, far north of her bloodline's ancestral lands, as her personal domain. Other Kindred tend to assume she's a Gangrel. An impression she does nothing to dissuade. Though Mocel doesn't confirm this either, fearing how Outlanders would respond to such a deception. Cause in truth she's all on her own now.<br /> During the early 1800s Mocel grew up in the mountains of Central Mexico, belonging to an isolated community that had managed to defy the Church's conversion efforts. They still believed in the Aztec gods, powerful beings of darkness and blood. These weren't like the invisible Christian god, cause Mocel's kin had all seen these deities with their own eyes. Eventually, as a young woman, came the night she too met one of her gods. Mocel had broken a taboo, been careless lingering at a sacred shrine past dusk. Once the Tlacique emerged from the earth the girl's life was forfeit. They immediately pounced upon her like jaguars, taking all Mocel's blood as a sacrifice. However, to the young woman's surprise, she rose again. Those she'd once thought of as gods had made her one of their own.<br /> The fledgling soon discovered that her undead condition was no great honor. The Tlacique were in a war for their survival against the Sabbat. Mocel simply owed her Embrace, instead of being left an empty vessel, to the bloodline's great need for more foot soldiers. Unfortunately the brood had underestimated the betrayal their newest recruit felt after learning her people's gods were nothing but blood drinking parasites. So rather than fighting for them she fled at the first opportunity, mere nights after her Embrace.<br /> Mocel's flight brought her to the Mexican Republic's northern reaches, specifically the lands of the Akimel O\u02bcodham tribe. The Tlacique made an abandoned Spanish mission into her haven, at a place called Mesa Trueno. It wasn't a pleasant unlife, with only coyotes and rattlers as company. But at the time she was laying low, fearing the others were looking for her.<br /> No other Kindred came for her. Though eventually the Church sent nuns to reclaim the mission, forcing Mocel to trade in her haven for a nearby cave. Primitive surroundings the young Tlacique soon found an alternative for, as a mining camp formed in Mesa Trueno. While men dug the surrounding hills for gold, Mocel moved into the newly established brothel. There the vampire could hide in plain sight, feeding off sex workers and patrons alike.<br /> As more years passed the camp became a town, now part of the New Mexico Territory. One of the miners, a Frenchman named Henri Corbeau, had hit it big. A rich vein, in the mountain overlooking Mesa Trueno, made him a rich man overnight, who bought up all the other nearby claims, or sent outlaws to deal with anyone unwilling to sell. Though meanwhile he kept patronizing the local brothel. So as Corbeau used his newfound wealth to bring Mesa Trueno under his control, Mocel took the opportunity to enthrall the man.<br /> Under the guise of being Henri Corbeau's mistress the vampire became the true power in Mesa Trueno. She moved her haven yet again, to hidden quarters in the bowels of the massive mansion Corbeau built overlooking the town. Through secret corridors she had the run of the entire property. There Mocel dwells still. Though after her thrall's recent demise, during a devastating quake, her grasp on the domain's become tenuous.<br /> <br /> <b>Image: </b>A slender beauty of indigenous Mesoamerican extraction. Mocel's ebon curls fall halfway down her back. Around her neck she a wears gold pendant, set with a ruby. A gift from Henri Corbeau. Her overall attire is quite expensive, but considered too risqu\u00e9 for a lady. Because by 1863's standards Mocel's gowns are overly colorful, show too much cleavage, than what is thought proper. The image of a high-end sex worker is exactly what she's cultivating. This Tlacique now spends much of her time in the shape of a black jaguar though.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> Shook out of your complacency since Corbeau's death. You had learned to appreciate the finer things in unlife. And will now not shy away from violence to defend your privileged existence. Though when possible you prefer to rely on your feminine, and vampiric, wiles. While in dealing with Kindred machinations you're clearly out of your depth, from lack of experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan:</b> Tlacique<br /> <b>Sire:</b> Acatl<br /> <b>Nature:</b> Bon Vivant<br /> <b>Demeanor:</b> Gallant<br /> <b>Generation:</b> 10th<br /> <b>Embrace:</b> 1832<br /> <b>Apparent Age:</b> 22<br /> <b>Physical:</b> Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social:</b> Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Appearance 4<br /> <b>Mental:</b> Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> <b>Talents:</b> Alertness 2, Athletics 1, Awareness 1, Brawl 1, Empathy 1, Intimidation 2, Leadership 1, Streetwise 2, Subterfuge 2<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Animal Ken 1, Etiquette 2, Melee 2, Ride 1, Stealth 2, Survival 3<br /> <b>Knowledges:</b> Academics 1, Finance 1, Investigation 1, Occult 1, Politics 1<br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Presence 2, Protean 4<br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b> Allies 1, Contacts 2, Domain 5, Generation 2, Herd 2, Resources 1<br /> <b>Virtues:</b> Conscience 3, Self-Control 3, Courage 4<br /> <b>Morality:</b> Humanity 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Merits/Flaws:</b> Language (English, Spanish + mother tongue Nahuatl)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 06-13-2026, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-14T14:02:37-07:00","id":1564058,"title":"","content":"I'm starting a new Victorian Age Vampire/Wild West storyline soon. These are the sires I wrote for my PCs:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>269. Evica Mumir</b><br /> You grew up on the Serbian countryside, the daughter of peasants. This was around the turn of the century, when the land was still part of the Ottoman Empire. You fell in love with one of the Turkish soldiers garrisoned near your home. Against your parents wishes you converted to Islam and married the man. Tragically he was killed shortly after, in the Serbian Uprising against the Ottomans. You attempted to follow him, hanging yourself from a tree. However, an ancient Gangrel resurrected you with its blood. The elder had felt your pain, centuries earlier losing its mate to the vile Necromancers. You were to become the instrument of its vengeance, which eventually brought you across the ocean.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A brown-eyed, plain looking, young woman, wearing simple working class dresses. You keep your hair hidden beneath a bonnet, which you never untie in public. Not just for religious reasons, but because this hides your lupine ears. Your beast shapes are those of a pale wolf and a white butterfly.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You appear quite meek and softspoken. And yet most kine find you deeply unsettling because of your predatory stare. You try to be a good Muslimah to the extent the curse allows, hoping that when you're finally reduced to ashes you'll be reunited with your husband. Though you're almost equally determined to fulfill the quest bestowed upon you by your sire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>270. Wim Beceu</b><br /> You were born and reared, in rural Flanders, during the 1790s. The son of a country doctor, studying to follow in your father's footsteps. Until you chose to fight at Waterloo, on Napoleon's side. You fell in battle, but was raised again as a Brujah vampire. The lady who'd done so discarded you soon after. So you returned to the village of your birth, though not to your family. Instead you hid from the sun in barns, or submersed in ditches. An elusive presence who repaid the blood you took, from sleeping peasants, by completing their chores. Your existence became folklore, believed to be a ghost or fae creature. Until years onward a local priest was implored to drive you off. You left Flanders, feeling betrayed, stowed away on a ship to the United States. There you've since been eking out an unlife making yourself useful to the East Coast Camarilla. Currently by tracking down a diablerist Giovanni who escaped into the western frontier.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A plain looking man, in your mid-twenties, with a face covered in blond stubble. Your brown eyes radiate a quiet anger or frustration. You care little about how you look, wearing the practical clothing of a field laborer. Though beneath that unimpressive garb you have an athletic build.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You try to be a good man, following the example of your father. But the shame you once felt, for being an undead leech, has long since been replaced by something darker. You despise how humanity has rejected your intended kindness time and again. You seek to follow the example of more successful vampires; using the kine as pawns. Though at the moment you're still visibly struggling with your upbringing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>271. Mrs Yejide</b><br /> You originally hail from Central Africa. There you lived alone, in the jungle, cause your people suspected you of being a witch. In truth you never cursed anyone, but had learned much about such practices from your mother. Your sire's thoughts weren't even know to himself. But you assume he Embraced you to preserve all this knowledge. Once your mind was caught in the Cobweb you learned of the world's end. Though also how the demise of all things might be delayed. On impulse you crossed the ocean to America, hidden aboard a slavers' ship. The subsequent decades you survived travelling between Kindred domains along the East Coast, attempting to discover what had brought you to this land. Mere weeks ago you finally found your purpose here, when encountering a coterie heading west, to the New Mexico Territory. It's there you know you can make a difference.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> An African woman who was about forty at the time of her Embrace. However, across the sea you've chosen to walk in the guise of a white woman much of the time. A matter of survival, even for the undead, in a land where people of your race are often horribly mistreated. So your eyes appear blue, your skin light, though your dark curls remain the same. These are often covered by a bonnet, cause you complete your disguise by dressing as an American middle-class lady.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> Quiet and reserved, choosing to be an observer of the chaos around you. Staying out of the affairs of others, kine and Kindred alike, would be your preference. Self preservation is your only interest in postponing the end of the world. When you do speak it is slow and deliberate, hoping to hide any traces of an African accent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>272. Charles Moore IV, Adeptus Secundus</b><br /> You're the son of a smalltown lawyer, from New England, who followed in his father's footsteps. The difference being an adventurous spirit. When the California goldrush erupted you shipped out to practice law in San Francisco. This boomtown, which had people from all across the globe arriving, was an ideal place to pursue your passion for ethnology. You grew absolutely fascinated by the many Chinese conceptions of the afterlife. Eventually you realized there was a truth to them, after witnessing some unsettling phenomena. This supernatural expertise, coupled with your growing influence in local politics, caught the Tremere's attention. Once your health started failing a visiting Witch wasted no time administering the Embrace. In the decade since you've yet to truly prove your worth to the Clan. Perhaps this latest fact finding mission, into the western frontier, is your opportunity to shine?<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> A handsome middle-aged gentleman, with a neatly trimmed brownish beard and moustache. Sad eyes, azure in color, peer out from behind wire rim glasses. Your tailored suit does little to hide how emaciated your body is. A top hat only adds to how lanky you appear.<br /> <br /> <b>Roleplaying Hints:</b> You go through unlife as if it's a painfully unpleasant duty you're fulfilling. Cause your existence is no longer your own, belonging to the Pyramid. Though truthfully you do savor any time your knowledge is of use to Clan Tremere, glad to make up for your overall ineffectivity at studying Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}